How do you see Arisen interacting with Sin-Eaters or Geists?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that this answers that, but I gotta admit that the entire time I'm reading Mummy I've got natural necromancer vs natural necromancer conflicts popping up in my head.<br /> <br /> It does not help that Sin-eaters dealing with Temakhs while the Deceived are in a death cycle is <i>very fun</i> to think about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T17:21:54-08:00","id":1346622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1346609#post1346609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that this answers that, but I gotta admit that the entire time I'm reading Mummy I've got natural necromancer vs natural necromancer conflicts popping up in my head.<br /> <br /> It does not help that Sin-eaters dealing with Temakhs while the Deceived are in a death cycle is <i>very fun</i> to think about.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, this kind of makes me wonder as to how the Bound would see the Arisen... I'm largely thinking of what their Utterances could do with ghosts in the previous edition, but that included stuff like feeding ghosts to a chthonic horror in order to better control it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T19:11:35-08:00","id":1346635,"title":"","content":"I know that core books don\u2019t generally deal with crossover type stuff, but this is my first time delving into Mummy, and I can see plenty of potential points of conflict with Mages, Sin-Eaters, and the God Machine.<br /> <br /> However, I wanted to ask about cosmology for a bit. Is Duat the same place that all ghosts go? Does that mean the Judges are just a type of Geist? Or is this one of those underworlds, like the Inferno?<br /> <br /> ....or is Duat a Supernal Realm and the Judges are Supernal spirits?<br /> <br /> Or is it an entirely different area and I need to just expand my cosmology?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T19:16:47-08:00","id":1346637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1346635#post1346635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that core books don\u2019t generally deal with crossover type stuff, but this is my first time delving into Mummy, and I can see plenty of potential points of conflict with Mages, Sin-Eaters, and the God Machine.<br /> <br /> However, I wanted to ask about cosmology for a bit. Is Duat the same place that all ghosts go? Does that mean the Judges are just a type of Geist? Or is this one of those underworlds, like the Inferno?<br /> <br /> ....or is Duat a Supernal Realm and the Judges are Supernal spirits?<br /> <br /> Or is it an entirely different area and I need to just expand my cosmology?</div> </div> </div> </div>Duat is what Mages call a Lower Depth,Lower Depths are otherworldly realms that lack an aspect of the world and consume it.<br /> One Lower Depth might Lack Life,and be a world full of death. Another might Kack virtue and be a world full of sin<br /> Duat lacks Sehkhem","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T19:35:03-08:00","id":13466