ns would take offence. Starting with whatever angels use it as Infrastructure and ending with [REDACTED]. But it would be fun chronicle to see them try! XD<br /> <br /> And to be clear, that redaction is NOT for Mummy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T22:04:43-08:00","id":1346666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1346635#post1346635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, I wanted to ask about cosmology for a bit. Is Duat the same place that all ghosts go?</div> </div> </div> </div>Duat is a &quot;place&quot; where <i>souls</i> go. A ghost is a different beast.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does that mean the Judges are just a type of Geist? </div> </div> </div>No, and also that's not how geists work. A geist is a ghost that has drunk from the Rivers of Death, the first dead or buried at a site of deathly resonance to rise with its Avernian Gate, or a necromancer whose deathly power in life has translated through death into a broken mask and detachment from the singular concerns of Anchors. The Judges are cosmic forces that salt the earth and turn seas to blood with their scrutiny.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or is this one of those underworlds, like the Inferno? </div> </div> </div>It is, in practice, closest to the Inferno as far as the cosmology goes, though there was a circle that needed squared in the cosmology between what the Inferno was and what the label that referred to it wound up also referring to. See anon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ....or is Duat a Supernal Realm and the Judges are Supernal spirits? </div> </div> </div>For all that the trials of Duat notionally bear a strong resemblance to the confrontation with the self that characterizes a journey to Pandemonium, the Judges are an outside force rather than a manifestation of your weaknesses demanding you to master and claim them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or is it an entirely different area and I need to just expand my cosmology? </div> </div> </div>So Mage: Summoners came out some time ago, and it talked about creatures from the Lower Depths, alien creatures from realities even more divorced from Truth than our world of time and space and concrete phenomena; some of their denizens, when they're in a talkative mood, claim to pre-date the rise of ordered reality; the never-born chthonians that inhabited the Underworld before human ghosts arrived were speculated to know the deep roads to these realms in much the same vein as they were theorized to be Fallen Supernal beings, but that was a different matter.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing: at least as far as 1e ChroD cosmology went, the Lower Depths were the Inferno, that many-faceted Hell made from human imagination, invented structure, and the willing forfeiture of the bits of one's soul that committing dark and transgressive acts damaged. The Lower Depths that Summoners (and later, Left-Hand Path) discussed had little to do with the Great Unclean Ones of sin and demonology approached in Inferno and alluded to in Imperial Mysteries' <i>akathartoi</i> and the Elder Demons of Hunter: the Vigil.<br /> <br /> Whisperers, Diaboli, and Dominions were flexible, but there was only so far you could stretch &quot;demons are distinguished from other spirits by their capacity for empathy and their self-serving flexibility in relation to their defining sinful concepts&quot; toward the end of things like &quot;the Seers of the Throne found a thing in the desert that doesn't possess awareness but will reflexively consume the human sense of self&quot; and &quot;chthonians are at their most conversational when they've recently eaten a ghost and are so alien that reading their mind courts madness.&quot;<br /> <br /> The simple solution, of course, was to make the call that the Inferno was a subset of the Lower Depths, and very probably one of the closest ones to the Fallen World; demons may not be the only hungry creatures from the edges of reality warming themselves with stolen aspects, but you'll seldom need to seek out thin places in the world or wait for inauspicious confluences out in the wastes to find one. The category is still poorly-understood, but if a creature comes from a place you can't physically go to and return from, and it takes something from you or turns you into a way of taking something from the world, it's a fair bet that mages will call its home part of the Lower Depths.<br /> <br /> Where this gets tricky is with the beings the Arisen serve. Remember how Summoners says some things from the Lower Depths claim to have come before reality? The Judges are, if not such beings, then directly descended from them. Remember how the Inferno feeds on sin? The Judges are, in First Edition Mummy, the primordial beings who defined sins to condemn human souls to the Devourer's maw by their commission because Sutek objected to their starting offer of consigning a tenth of the universe to oblivion outright. Remember how chthonians knew the roads to Hell but might have fallen from Heaven? The Judges share a cosmological wavelength with an encounterable being (Anpu) who reads as &quot;all/none of the above&quot; when queried with magic as to whether he's a demon, a god, or a creature of death.<br /> <br /> tl;dr It's weird, but if you want to fit it into your maps of the cosmology, it's an empty place on the border of reality that most people can't go to safely, and its main agents harvest an aspect of the world in a way that tangibly removes it from consideration until and unless it's re-deployed elsewhere. The fact that souls can go here is distinct from the fact that Deathless magic is powerful and necromantically charged and may truck with ghosts or match the scope of Awakened sorcery.<br /> <br /> (It's a lot more straightforward in Geist, where the Underworld is a naturally-extant part of phenomenal cosmology that has been <i>heavily </i>broken by the debatably-extant Chthonic Gods and their servants, as well as the ghost-eating chthonians that hunt the Rivers and care not for the worshippers that sometimes follow them. The Great Below is a fair bit <i>wetter</i> than Duat is usually characterized.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-07-2019, 01:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T23:27:12-08:00","id":1346673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1346666#post1346666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(It's a lot more straightforward in Geist, where the Underworld is a naturally-extant part of phenomenal cosmology that has been <i>heavily </i>broken by the debatably-extant Chthonic Gods and their servants, as well as the ghost-eating chthonians that hunt the Rivers and care not for the worshippers that sometimes follow them. The Great Below is a fair bit <i>wetter</i> than Duat is usually characterized.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Not meaning to take away from your point... One of the mini-fictions available in the preview so far gives a description of an Arisen's first journey into Duat, and a river actually gets mentioned....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T00:29:52-08:00","id":1346678,"title":"","content":"There's a river in Duat as well, but I wouldn't call its waters cool or refreshing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T00:44:01-08:00","id":1346679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1346649#post1346649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Judges wouldn't be the shadows of the Law of Suffering if they didn't embody catch-22s now and then.<br /> <br /> Damned if you do, damned if you don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or to put it in shorter terms:<br /> <br /> The Judges of Death condemn you for your sin. The point of doing this is not to prevent people from sinning. It is because they want reasons to condemn you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T05:46:52-08:00","id":1346700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1346673#post1346673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not meaning to take away from your point... One of the mini-fictions available in the preview so far gives a description of an Arisen's first journey into Duat, and a river actually gets mentioned....</div> </div> </div> </div>There was a river on the road to Duat in First Edition as well. And of course, the central civilization upon which Mummy is built upon also has a river. Rivers are Kind of Important, BUT<br /> <br /> A river does not a desert unmake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T06:30:19-08:00","id":1346713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1346664#post1346664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> And to be clear, that redaction is NOT for Mummy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Motherfucker...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T07:10:39-08:00","id":1346717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1346673#post1346673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not meaning to take away from your point... One of the mini-fictions available in the preview so far gives a description of an Arisen's first journey into Duat, and a river actually gets mentioned....</div> </div> </div> </div>The most enduring parts of the Underworld's topography are streams of loss and tears forming Rivers of mystery and death forming an Ocean of fragments and dissolution. There is an Admiral who commands Ferrymen who crew vessels across the Rivers. There are port towns with fishing nets and fugu dishes. The most dangerous creatures there in general resemble marine life that track ectoplasm behind them when they cross the land. The passage of time has a direct impact on the inhabitants because if they can't or won't spend their point of Essence then they get absorbed into the walls a la the more reluctant crew members of PotC's Flying Dutchman.<br /> <br /> The Great Below is <i>wetter</i> than the protean wasteland of Arisen vision quests. It is a drowning place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T08:01:07-08:00","id":1346724,"title":"","content":"You know I wonder if any of the Shan'iatu, those alien beings that looked human but weren't, are still around. Like either a sect of them left Irem or something. <br /> <br /> I am also really looking to how Sekhem Sorcerers work. I hope they are a little more fun and powered then the version in Dark Eras.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T08:25:28-08:00","id":1346732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The hints we've had so far seem to err in the direction of about what you expect from the Dark Era but more powerful in the presence of the Deathless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, which to me is a bit unfortunate as I was underwhelmed by the sorcerer merit in Dark Eras. Especially considering some of the info and hints given beforehand about them. What we got was much less then what I would assume an actual sorcerer in the world would have access to.<br /> <br /> That said I will wait and see for full on judgement making.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T09:38:36-08:00","id":1346751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1346732#post1346732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, which to me is a bit unfortunate as I was underwhelmed by the sorcerer merit in Dark Eras. Especially considering some of the info and hints given beforehand about them. What we got was much less then what I would assume an actual sorcerer in the world would have access to.<br /> <br /> That said I will wait and see for full on judgement making.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on what exactly you found lacking in sorcerers, you may find that the new <i>benbenet </i>can fill the role. They're pretty potent fellows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T09:59:37-08:00","id":1346758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With the upticks in power that 2e has generally brought, I would not be surprised if Sekhem Sorcery even outside of the Deathless boost is a little bit more potent in a sense in 2e. But that said, I don't really want or need to be personally. Sekhem Sorcery fills a cosmic horror magician niche for me that things like Mage's brand of magic doesn't really do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that is why I am hoping that things get made a little more in 2e. As I am not a super fan of cosmic horror as a mechanical element I hope that sticks to fluff and the rules are broad enough to be used even outside of that. <br /> <br /> As I have said before I really like the Pillar and Affinity and Utterance system and such and that is why I hope player characters as mortals being able to use them is given mechanical support. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1346751#post1346751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depending on what exactly you found lacking in sorcerers, you may find that the new <i>benbenet </i>can fill the role. They're pretty potent fellows.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh, interesting. Are they posted already or is that a group in a later chapter of Mummy that we have to wait a bit to see. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T10:00:21-08:00","id":1346759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1346751#post1346751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depending on what exactly you found lacking in sorcerers, you may find that the new <i>benbenet </i>can fill the role. They're pretty potent fellows.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not LordHeru here, but I remember being optimistic about the Ritual Sorcerer Merit in Dark Eras, but on review finding it to be unusually loaded down with prerequisites and ritual components for very little payoff, to the tune of an expensive Merit with some of the highest Merit prerequisites giving a couple circumstantial bonus dice or the privilege of learning complicated means of human sacrifice. Generally I think things like the Rite of Seeding would have been better fit as examples of Open Rites to keep that option interesting and underline the Chronicles of Darkness as a place where occult correspondences exist and can be efficacious, while the Rite of Purity is the best fit given in Isireion for what a Closed Rite should be like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T10:26:19-08:00","id":1346767,"title":"","content":"Aaaand I backed the Kickstarter.<br /> <br /> Well, at least we now know what happened to the Iremite soldiers. I remember there was a discussion about it, once, with the main question being &quot;why would the Shan'iatu want to have a group of immortal soldiers they can't fully control that may very well end up turning against them, with a millennia of experience at killing people?&quot;. I think we found the answer for it.<br /> <br /> I must say that among the lesser guilds, the Wadjet-Itja are reaaaaally cool. Like, really. Kudos for their writer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T10:41:37-08:00","id":1346772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1346759#post1346759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not LordHeru here, but I remember being optimistic about the Ritual Sorcerer Merit in Dark Eras, but on review finding it to be unusually loaded down with prerequisites and ritual components for very little payoff, to the tune of an expensive Merit with some of the highest Merit prerequisites giving a couple circumstantial bonus dice or the privilege of learning complicated means of human sacrifice. Generally I think things like the Rite of Seeding would have been better fit as examples of Open Rites to keep that option interesting and underline the Chronicles of Darkness as a place where occult correspondences exist and can be efficacious, while the Rite of Purity is the best fit given in Isireion for what a Closed Rite should be like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, it wasn't so much the Rites being fairly underpowered that got me, it was the prerequisites. Which I suspect were done by multiple people, given how the sidebar immediately goes &quot;alternatively...you can do this instead.&quot;<br /> <br /> I get that a sorcerer is essentially someone able to use pen and paper to do accurate algebra after hearing it only described , but surely it doesn't need to be so basic? <br /> <br /> Really, I'd like it, if they just had saner requirements. Still, the fact that sorcerers get that way through initially mastering Open Rites gives me hope, as Open Rites are far more achievable by...people. It also makes the danger of sorcerous secrets leaking far more present, because that implies all you need is gumption and a little lore before you're able to stand cackling over a summoning pit of your very own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T11:18:43-08:00","id":1346786,"title":"","content":"Basically what both <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar522_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"522\" data-vbnamecard=\"522\">Stupid Loserman</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar180_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"180\" data-vbnamecard=\"180\">Leliel</a> say. In fact they said it much better than I think I would. That said, though not only is it the prerequisties but it is also the limitation of how many powers one can gain that I immediately noticed and was not a fan of. <br /> <br /> (I don't think saying 'the character can only have x + y dots of powers' is fun when directed towards PC characters. I instead think the set up should be some dots are freely handed upon the initial power purchase and other powers are gained by spending XP to gain new Merits.)<br /> <br /> Personally, I like the idea of there being one Merit that unlocks the potential and gives a certain special advantage and then additional other Merits can be purchased at various dot ratings to represent the gaining of individual powers. <br /> <br /> To be honest the sidebar about the other option and the note that there might be a lesser template of sorcerors using Sekhem, well, that is what I wanted, what I was hoping we were going to get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T12:48:20-08:00","id":1346820,"title":"","content":"So... Are Arisen able to explore the Underworld?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T12:51:37-08:00","id":1346821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1346724#post1346724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know I wonder if any of the Shan'iatu, those alien beings that looked human but weren't, are still around. Like either a sect of them left Irem or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>All but seven of the Shan'iatu are currently stuck in Duat eating ashes for having committed the Rite of Return. They may one day come back into power, but for now they're fucked.<br /> <br /> The other seven persist in the Deceived.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1346820#post1346820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... Are Arisen able to explore the Underworld?</div> </div> </div> </div>Last we heard, the Upper reaches are open game, but Anpu intervenes when you go to cross a River. We'll find out if that persists in Second Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-07-2019, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T12:53:05-08:00","id":1346822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1346820#post1346820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... Are Arisen able to explore the Underworld?</div> </div> </div> </div>If memory serves, no; Anpu, one of the gods of Irem, stops them from getting in. Or he might stop you from getting past the first River?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T12:59:40-08:00","id":1346823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1346822#post1346822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If memory serves, no; Anpu, one of the gods of Irem, stops them from getting in. Or he might stop you from getting past the first River?</div> </div> </div> </div>Anpu stops the Temakh from descending into the Underworld, but the Arisen could likely physically find access through a Cenote. But as for finding Duat... that part is much more unlikely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T13:01:54-08:00","id":1346825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1346821#post1346821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last we heard, the Upper reaches are open game, but Anpu intervenes when you go to cross a River. We'll find out if that persists in Second Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm hoping that changes... I'm fine with some stuff being &quot;forbidden&quot; and having consequences, but I really don't like a game telling me to use a god-like figure to flat out say &quot;NO&quot; to players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T13:23:14-08:00","id":1346832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1346821#post1346821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i><b>All but seven of the Shan'iatu are currently stuck in Duat </b></i>eating ashes for having committed the Rite of Return. They may one day come back into power, but for now they're fucked.<br /> <br /> The other seven persist in the Deceived.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure about it. Like, it was 100% true in 1e, but the Maar Kherit's writeup state that their guildmasters were disposed by the <i>other </i>Shan'iatu. So while we have seven Shan'iatu being broken into parts and bound to their servants and the vast majority being stuck in Duat, a certain number of Shan'iatu (not sure if seven) are MIA, unless the plague have truly taken them out... unless the plague was the Contagion, and then my oh my they probably wish they were dead.<br /> <br /> On an unrelated note- Sutek is the 43rd Judge, who &quot;will not judge and won't be judged&quot;, god of chaos and Will, the stranger. The Wedjet Itja's guildmaster was the 43rd guildmaster, who was like the Shan'iatu but not a Shan'iatu, whose guild were gamblers and charlatans, who was forever the stranger among the guildmasters. Coincidence? Am I reading too much into this? Perhaps, perhaps- but it could explain why the Shan'iatu were willing to tolerate the Oracles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T13:23:28-08:00","id":1346833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1346825#post1346825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm hoping that changes... I'm fine with some stuff being &amp;quot;forbidden&amp;quot; and having consequences, but I really don't like a game telling me to use a god-like figure to flat out say &amp;quot;NO&amp;quot; to players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Recontextualize it. This isn\u2019t about saying no to your players, it\u2019s about giving them a mystery (why aren\u2019t we allowed there?) and also a chance to speak to one of the most important figures in the cosmology of the game. Anpu bars the way; what do you say to him? What questions do you ask someone who knows the truths of the universe, and was already old when the first bricks of Irem were stacked together?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T13:28:17-08:00","id":1346835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They are talking about the information in Mutapa that talks about where Anpu prohibits Arisen from going. The Deceived( and their temakhs) don't have to &amp;quot;worry&amp;quot; about it since they are metaphysically incapable of entering any realm, being monsters of this world the universe says must be, forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>I missed that part, but it makes sense that he would bar passage along the Rivers.<br /> <br /> I wonder if Deceived who have become Fate\u2019s Champions still have that restriction, or if they can go to other planes of existence due to being chained to Fate rather than the Temakhs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T13:40:13-08:00","id":1346839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They were &quot;disposed&quot;. After the others found out that the Shan'iatu of the Restless Stars were going to use their name magic to make themselves Judges above the other Shan'iatu their ritual was hijacked and their temakhs shattered to pieces.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I know- I talked about the Maar Kherit's Shan'iatu, not the Deceived.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sutekh wasn't a Judge he was a god they created. </div> </div> </div>Only that the Judges did not created Sutek? He is a child of Atum and Khepera, a sibling to the Judges, according to Dreams of Avarice","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T13:43:17-08:00","id":1346841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It didn't bother me and wouldn't in 2e if we delve into it the right way. Which for me would be both an examination of Anpu in general(I've gotten some impressions that part of this is due to whatever supernatural legalism was put in place when Azar replaced him). As well as presented as a mystery. IE perhaps there is something down there the Judges don't want the Arisen to find.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To me, that's better expressed as being &quot;forbidden, with consequences&quot; rather than have the wall of a deity that Arisen can't really do anything about. It feels like a dead-end for stories for me and I just don't like that.<br /> <br /> Onyx Path games have always felt best to me when they present open-ended story hooks, suggestions of what to do and where things can do. And the previous implementation of Anpu just... seemed contradictory to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T13:46:25-08:00","id":1346843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1346839#post1346839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I know- I talked about the Maar Kherit's Shan'iatu, not the Deceived.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that, being a minor guild, the Maar-Kherit didn't have any Shan'iatu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T13:49:23-08:00","id":1346845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given the limited word count I am not surprised it didn't go far into explanations.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And while a reason, it still left me with what I felt was problematic content that I just didn't know how to make use of. My fingers are crossed that Anpu's implementation in Second Edition is better. ^.^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T13:51:57-08:00","id":1346846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1346843#post1346843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought that, being a minor guild, the Maar-Kherit didn't have any Shan'iatu.</div> </div> </div> </div>That what I too thought- but the writeup says &quot;the other Shan'iatu disposed of them&quot;. Even if we were to disregard the part about the Shan'iatu taking part in the Guild, and them, unlike the other minor Guilds other than the Deceived, having relics of their own, and them being described as &quot;esteemed Guild&quot; (all which hinting towards them being originally a main Guild), the word &quot;other&quot; means that their Guildmasters were, in fact, Shan'iatu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T13:55:58-08:00","id":1346848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1346846#post1346846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That what I too thought- but the writeup says &quot;the other Shan'iatu disposed of them&quot;. Even if we were to disregard the part about the Shan'iatu taking part in the Guild, and them, unlike the other minor Guilds other than the Deceived, having relics of their own, and them being described as &quot;esteemed Guild&quot; (all which hinting towards them being originally a main Guild), the word &quot;other&quot; means that their Guildmasters were, in fact, Shan'iatu.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You know... You're right, that is very suggestive of that. Solid catch there!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T16:55:05-08:00","id":1346893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1346825#post1346825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm hoping that changes... I'm fine with some stuff being &amp;quot;forbidden&amp;quot; and having consequences, but I really don't like a game telling me to use a god-like figure to flat out say &amp;quot;NO&amp;quot; to players.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worth noting Anpu did make exceptions when presented interesting cases. I never read it as a NO so much creating a way for STs to wrinkle the setting while having more fun with the second most personable God along his role as a psychopomp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T17:16:39-08:00","id":1346900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1346893#post1346893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's worth noting Anpu did make exceptions when presented interesting cases. I never read it as a NO so much creating a way for STs to wrinkle the setting while having more fun with the second most personable God along his role as a psychopomp.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I get that. I remember that line in that section. But what I really appreciate from Chronicles of Darkness books is where they provide multiple examples of what can be done with an idea. I find those incredibly helpful to me as they give me places to either make those ideas my own or help inspire me to make my own ideas. But an open ended statement of &quot;interesting cases&quot; gives me nothing to really work with as to what Anpu might consider &quot;interesting&quot;. I guess that could be read as &quot;Whatever the ST and Players find interesting&quot;, but that's the situation to begin with, and so what Anpu finds &quot;interesting&quot; is completely meaningless then.<br /> <br /> And I don't want to read content in these books and think, &quot;Well, that's completely unhelpful to me.&quot;<br /> <br /> Maybe it was helpful to someone else, but I can only speak to my own experiences and preferences. And my preference is for an implementation of Anpu that is more useful to me and less, to my eyes, a wall for Arisen to smack into and not being able to do anything about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T19:03:55-08:00","id":1346915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1346900#post1346900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I get that. I remember that line in that section. But what I really appreciate from Chronicles of Darkness books is where they provide multiple examples of what can be done with an idea. I find those incredibly helpful to me as they give me places to either make those ideas my own or help inspire me to make my own ideas. But an open ended statement of &amp;quot;interesting cases&amp;quot; gives me nothing to really work with as to what Anpu might consider &amp;quot;interesting&amp;quot;. I guess that could be read as &amp;quot;Whatever the ST and Players find interesting&amp;quot;, but that's the situation to begin with, and so what Anpu finds &amp;quot;interesting&amp;quot; is completely meaningless then.<br /> <br /> And I don't want to read content in these books and think, &amp;quot;Well, that's completely unhelpful to me.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Maybe it was helpful to someone else, but I can only speak to my own experiences and preferences. And my preference is for an implementation of Anpu that is more useful to me and less, to my eyes, a wall for Arisen to smack into and not being able to do anything about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I can\u2019t stress enough that meeting one of the gods is a lord goldmine for the players. If I run into a deity blocking my, I don\u2019t think \u201cwow, the ST is an asshole,\u201d I think \u201cwow what the HELL is going on?\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T19:12:58-08:00","id":1346920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1346915#post1346915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, I can\u2019t stress enough that meeting one of the gods is a lord goldmine for the players. If I run into a deity blocking my, I don\u2019t think \u201cwow, the ST is an asshole,\u201d I think \u201cwow what the HELL is going on?\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;Meeting one of the gods&quot; isn't what is being talked about, though. It is <i>explicitly </i>not what is being talked about.<br /> <br /> And if you're thinking &quot;what the hell is going on?&quot; Well... That's my problem. I, as the ST, don't know either! And the books aren't helping with that as far as I can see.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping that Second Edition is a lot more helpful to me than First Edition was. Which... First Edition was very much not helpful to me. However, Second Edition seems to be doing a lot better with completely blowing me away with the first chapter, so I'm pretty hopeful!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T00:03:35-08:00","id":1346953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Was on mobile on the way to work so going off memory(and salent part being he was a god created.) Given the lore I would personally hate making him a Judge but that is what toolboxes are for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for what that it worth, Sutek is not a &quot;Judge' in the conventional sense of the word (hence why I mentioned him in the original context). He is their antithesis, representing Will over Law and standing against the Judges, Ammut and Suffering in support for the world. He is the good guy in the story, more or less- the Judge Who Will Not Judge And Won't Be Judged. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1308896-a-totally-serious-and-surprisingly-sober-summary-of-iremitie-mythology-and-history\">Arc summed it up really good, IMO</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T07:55:56-08:00","id":1347024,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/339646881/mummy-the-curse-2nd-edition/posts/2676818\" target=\"_blank\">FYI, balance and burden have been previewed on the Kickstarter!</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 11-08-2019, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T09:17:35-08:00","id":1347046,"title":"","content":"Stretch Goal achieved!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T10:42:13-08:00","id":1347063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now for that sweet sweet minor Guild action. Do we know yet if that is technically going to include the Deceived or are we saving the artists for something else?<br /> <br /> Also I have not delved deep into 2nd edition yet so I feel like I don't necessarily have the direct play experience to comment deeply on what all Burdens and Balances bring to the table compared to Vice and Virtues, but given how fairly limiting Vices and Virtues could be I have to imagine that opens some things up.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, Virtues and Vices are themselves opened up now, the list is gone; your Virtue is what you do when behaving selflessly, your Vice is what you're like when you're being dickish or otherwise uncaring.<br /> <br /> Balance and Burden...really isn't that much of a switch. Which makes sense, as an Arisen's basic instincts are still the same as the person they were before the Rite of Return. The major change is the cosmic duty the Judges entrusted them with before they went back to the mortal coil. That changes the context of it, even if their own internal rewards system is the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T10:56:29-08:00","id":1347067,"title":"","content":"I must say that I'm not a big fan of the name &quot;Burden&quot;- it immediately sends my mind towards Geist's lexicon. I would have also preferred something which takes more part in Mummy's concepts and cosmology. Like, &quot;Balance&quot; and &quot;Will&quot; could have worked better, IMO, the first pointing towards the Judges and Maat and the second towards Sutek, and also emphasis the concept of duty vs self. A minor detail, I know, but kinda feel like a missed opportunity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T13:28:45-08:00","id":1347090,"title":"","content":"So, are any of the backers ready to guess which decrees were written by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> and which were written by me? I think the only hint that\u2019s been given so far is that Second Chances wrote all of the decree unique Affinities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T13:32:31-08:00","id":1347093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1347090#post1347090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, are any of the backers ready to guess which decrees were written by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> and which were written by me? I think the only hint that\u2019s been given so far is that Second Chances wrote all of the decree unique Affinities.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've absolutely no idea which of you wrote which Decrees, and I view that as a really good thing. Consistency can be very hard to match between different writers and you both smashed it outta the park with the descriptions. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> did a really good job with the decree unique Affinities.<br /> <br /> ...Um... I gotta ask though... Is it intended for Arisen to be able to <i>change </i>their Decree?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T14:32:09-08:00","id":1347102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1347093#post1347093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I've absolutely no idea which of you wrote which Decrees, and I view that as a really good thing. Consistency can be very hard to match between different writers and you both smashed it outta the park with the descriptions. <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> did a really good job with the decree unique Affinities.<br /> <br /> ...Um... I gotta ask though... Is it intended for Arisen to be able to <i>change </i>their Decree?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. If anyone wanted to do that, it would need to be under very unusual circumstances, which is really the domain of a group\u2019s chronicle rather than a standard option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T14:46:25-08:00","id":1347105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1347102#post1347102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. If anyone wanted to do that, it would need to be under very unusual circumstances, which is really the domain of a group\u2019s chronicle rather than a standard option.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Okay... The sidebar in Chapter Two titled &quot;The Rite of Return when Arisen&quot; gives a very contradicting message to that.<br /> <br /> In fact, that sidebar confuses the hell out of me, considering it says that Arisen can &quot;request&quot; a particular Pillar from Judges...?<br /> <br /> I don't know what to make of this sidebar... But then a lot of Chapter Two just confuses me...<br /> <br /> Edit: To be clear, from my understanding of what I'm reading, it is very explicitly talking about Decrees in this context, since this sidebar is showing under the section of &quot;The Five Pillars&quot; and the first paragraph in this section states: &quot;By then, the mummy knows which of the five Pillars is their decree.&quot; So, to me, it reads as explicitly talking about the trials that determine what decree an Arisen is of. So, an Arisen can just ask a Judge to be a Falcon? This really doesn't make sense with the Decree section in Chapter One... These don't match up at all...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","user":"Paradim","date":". 11-08-2019, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T15:53:01-08:00","id":1347117,"title":"","content":"Just a random thought I had-<br /> <br /> Currently, we have five main Guilds- but it seems that in the time of Irem, both the Deceived and the Maar Kherit were equal to them in standing, giving us seven Guilds. The Maar Kherit were the &quot;sister Guild&quot; of the Su Menet, while it is clear that the Akhem Urtu had strong connection to the Sesha Hebsu. That makes me think if there are, perhaps, other such &quot;sisters&quot; to the remaining Guilds. As we are left with three such Guilds, it is likely that two of them may have had similar connections like the other couples. If that's the case, I would bet that it would be the Maa Kep and the Tef Aabhi, as their works complete each other (the later plans the monuments, the first supervise the slaves who build it), even though that following the stereotypes, it feels like it should be the Tef Aabhi and the Mesen Nebu (which could also make sense- the Alchemists have the vision, the Architects have the blueprints. The one works represents the future, the other the past. Yeah, it works). That would mean that either the Maa Kep or the Mesen Nebu are left without such &quot;sister&quot;. Sure, we still have two more Guilds, but the Kher Minu are not a true Guild, while the Wadjet Itja don't have relics of their own, and their whole standing is kinda shaky. If the Oracles are indeed the missing &quot;sister&quot;, they could work with the Mesen Nebu, as both of them focus of the future with different perspectives, even though I think that the Maa Kep would be a better coupling (as both focus around manipulation and control- the one through authority and secrecy, the other through prophecies and manipulations- and both are really good liars, after all). If not, than maybe there is yet another minor Guild hiding out there, either lying in the ruins of the past and waiting to wake up, or hiding in the shadows of the Deathless society.<br /> <br /> Just a thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T16:59:04-08:00","id":1347133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1347105#post1347105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Okay... The sidebar in Chapter Two titled &amp;quot;The Rite of Return when Arisen&amp;quot; gives a very contradicting message to that.<br /> <br /> In fact, that sidebar confuses the hell out of me, considering it says that Arisen can &amp;quot;request&amp;quot; a particular Pillar from Judges...?<br /> <br /> I don't know what to make of this sidebar... But then a lot of Chapter Two just confuses me...<br /> <br /> Edit: To be clear, from my understanding of what I'm reading, it is very explicitly talking about Decrees in this context, since this sidebar is showing under the section of &amp;quot;The Five Pillars&amp;quot; and the first paragraph in this section states: &amp;quot;By then, the mummy knows which of the five Pillars is their decree.&amp;quot; So, to me, it reads as explicitly talking about the trials that determine what decree an Arisen is of. So, an Arisen can just ask a Judge to be a Falcon? This really doesn't make sense with the Decree section in Chapter One... These don't match up at all...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll make sure it's clarified by the final version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T17:11:12-08:00","id":1347136,"title":"","content":"So, given the expanded descriptions of the Judges in Dreams of Avarice and the 2E previews, would there still be room for something like the Book of Going Westward that the 1E kickstart had as a stretch goal that wasn't unlocked? I really regretted that it wasn't made, because the Judges really are one of those interesting elements that make the world feel bigger and more complex.<br /> <br /> Edit: Just started reading the preview so this may be answered later:<br /> <br /> In the glossary, under the entry for Shuankhsen: is the shadow they have fallen to at all similar to Sheut, (perhaps the pillars having grown in what they represent) or still She with Teeth of Mountains?<br /> <br /> Edit 2: Sort of a behind the scenes question, but what references do you use for discovering and romanizing the various (I presume) egyptian terms? When I look them up they are often rendered differently if I can find them at all. Though that may be due to the antiquity (hah) of the free hieroglyphic dictionaries and the like online.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 11-08-2019, 08:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T17:26:33-08:00","id":1347139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1347133#post1347133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll make sure it's clarified by the final version.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you for that!<br /> <br /> Honestly, something I've come to appreciate from these previews of non-finalized manuscripts through the various manuscripts I've seen from Kickstarters that Onyx Path has done, is that there is a LOT of work that goes into one of these books. Not just from the writers, but also from tying the different chapters together from different writers, working the manuscript to read as one single piece, and then there's all the work involved with editing, layout and geez, then there's the entire artwork thing! I could see how it could be kind of painful to see people looking over work that you don't really feel is &quot;Done&quot;.<br /> <br /> I really do enjoy these looks &quot;under the hood&quot;, so to speak, that Onyx Path Publishing allows with their Kickstarters. I love the confidence you guys have in what will be the final product, and that confidence is very infectious. I never hesitate to back a Kickstarter from OPP because of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T18:11:48-08:00","id":1347147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1346288#post1346288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No.<br /> <br /> The Kher-Minu already have copyright on that.<br /> <br /> (I'm praying that it turns out their programmed bloodthirst doesn't shut down their minds too bad, because they are awesome on toast. Really, all the Minor Guilds are, including the Deceived in that, but the Kher-Minu are the kind of thing that would have their own gameline in another universe.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Death Knight you mean","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T20:19:06-08:00","id":1347163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1347147#post1347147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Death Knight you mean</div> </div> </div> </div>Death Knights are Paladins. Just the cthonic kind.<br /> Which is just how the Shan'aitu like them.<br /> I do not speak for the Judges, only express their Will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T21:11:27-08:00","id":1347164,"title":"","content":"I just wanted to pop in and say that I really dig the Kheru in this edition. Although I had nothing against them before, the Lion-Headed never really grabbed me in the same way as they do now. Their description alone has already inspired me to an interesting character concept I'd love to play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T23:13:04-08:00","id":1347174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1347164#post1347164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just wanted to pop in and say that I really dig the Kheru in this edition. Although I had nothing against them before, the Lion-Headed never really grabbed me in the same way as they do now. Their description alone has already inspired me to an interesting character concept I'd love to play.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m glad you like them! I hope you\u2019ll share your character idea once you gain more information as the previews continue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T07:13:29-08:00","id":1347234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1347163#post1347163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Death Knights are Paladins. Just the cthonic kind.<br /> Which is just how the Shan'aitu like them.<br /> I do not speak for the Judges, only express their Will.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, calling a Death Knight a Paladin is like calling a Blackguard a Paladin.. technically correct, but it feels wrong.<br /> <br /> But it\u2019s a good enough comparison, all things considered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T08:51:08-08:00","id":1347250,"title":"","content":"So with the recent update with the story element I can't help but think that if there is going to be a campaign arc where my mummy character uncovers a Relic from Irem that not only is bound to him but made by him in olden days there needs to be something that can be done to allow for him to craft that item anew. Especially when mortals can do it and a mummy is so much more. (I don't accept that relic creation is a lost never to be returned to the world art either.) <br /> <br /> Also there is no way I would have a mummy character destroy a relic that he created in his mortal life, no matter what the Judge's say, and so I hope there are storyteller guide for such decisions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T09:07:11-08:00","id":1347254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1347250#post1347250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So with the recent update with the story element I can't help but think that if there is going to be a campaign arc where my mummy character uncovers a Relic from Irem that not only is bound to him but made by him in olden days there needs to be something that can be done to allow for him to craft that item anew. Especially when mortals can do it and a mummy is so much more. (I don't accept that relic creation is a lost never to be returned to the world art either.)<br /> <br /> Also there is no way I would have a mummy character destroy a relic that he created in his mortal life, no matter what the Judge's say, and so I hope there are storyteller guide for such decisions.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't lost. It has been rediscovered or reinvented countless times by countless occultists since the fall of Irem. However, without the teaching, guidance, and oversight of the Shaniatu, these later works have also been lesser works. Mortals have worked in alone or in small groups isolated from each other, stumbling in the dark without the support of an empire to collect resources and provide servants and infrastructure.<br /> <br /> <i>Mummies</i> are the ones who can't make relics because their current state does not allow it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T09:11:15-08:00","id":1347256,"title":"","content":"I hope they do something like they did in Mage 2e, where supernaturals that serve the Exarchs gain supernatural perks related to Magic. Can you imagine a werewolf or a vampire joining a Iremite Cult? What kind of Devotions or Gifts would they get? The possibilities!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T09:15:49-08:00","id":1347257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1347256#post1347256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope they do something like they did in Mage 2e, where supernaturals that serve the Exarchs gain supernatural perks related to Magic. Can you imagine a werewolf or a vampire joining a Iremite Cult? What kind of Devotions or Gifts would they get? The possibilities!</div> </div> </div> </div>Chapter two of the preview does talk of vampires joining a mummy's cult and it being something beneficial for both parties...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T11:16:54-08:00","id":1347288,"title":"","content":"I know this is probably too early to ask about this, but I just now wondered about something I vaguely remember from the Dark Eras Companion. It mentioned that Sekhem Sorcerers would not become mages if their powers increased, rather they would elevate their sorcery to a higher level or become a full-on Sorcerer Supernatural template on its own. Is that going to be addressed in the mummy corebook or maybe in a stretch goal supplement?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T11:23:51-08:00","id":1347290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1347256#post1347256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope they do something like they did in Mage 2e, where supernaturals that serve the Exarchs gain supernatural perks related to Magic. Can you imagine a werewolf or a vampire joining a Iremite Cult? What kind of Devotions or Gifts would they get? The possibilities!</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf Sadikh anyone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T11:32:11-08:00","id":1347295,"title":"","content":"I have an idea in my head for like the ultimate weird crossover game where a sin eater krewe, a changeling motley/court, a werewolf pack and a Mummy's cult merge into one organization <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. That can only lead to great things!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8100,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","user":"Caedus","date":". 11-09-2019, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T12:06:30-08:00","id":1347303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;My time with The Motley Krewe Kult.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I actually remember in WTF The Pack Second edition it talked about a mummy being the totem of a pack of ghost wolves","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T12:26:01-08:00","id":1347311,"title":"","content":"As real history is often more fantastic then fiction I need to do some research on what is the oldest school and corporation in the world. This would come in handy as it would give a historical basis for a Mummy affiliated institution and such. It would also come in handy as it would allow for a reoccurring organization in a time hopping campaign. <br /> <br /> Of course nothing says that a player couldn't have a Mummy character who has memories of the modern world couldn't create an organization in say the 800s or even older somewhere in Europe that would survive the test of time through his preparations so that he can always have its aid. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T16:17:43-08:00","id":1347339,"title":"","content":"The cult section is awesome. I love that at this point there could be a game with cultists of all kind - from Mummy, Geist, Beast, Demon... - where the big template supernatural beings just stay in the background.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T22:28:22-08:00","id":1347406,"title":"","content":"Sooooooooooo I'm going to risk a derailment with this comment, buuuuuuuuut<br /> <br /> So I haven't really been able to read the preview up till now, so I'm just now really reading the Judges annnnnd boy howdy, my assertions that the closest game to the horror in the magical girl genre is Mummy the Curse just got a whole lot more affirmed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T03:03:57-08:00","id":1347432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1347406#post1347406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sooooooooooo I'm going to risk a derailment with this comment, buuuuuuuuut<br /> <br /> So I haven't really been able to read the preview up till now, so I'm just now really reading the Judges annnnnd boy howdy, my assertions that the closest game to the horror in the magical girl genre is Mummy the Curse just got a whole lot more affirmed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you unpack that a bit for those of us who've only picked up the magical girl genre through pop-culture osmosis? (or point to where you've done it before)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T03:53:47-08:00","id":1347438,"title":"","content":"Here's a character creation session for Mummy:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/GJIEAEAx2MY\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.