e-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1347600#post1347600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well now I'm curious.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was making some comparisons between the text and Madoka, but felt better of it since I was quoting from an unpublished source. Cosmic law and unknowable entities imposing their will and such. Also the image of a mummy hitting up Blessing of the God King by screaming &quot;Azar Power, Make up!&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T19:33:05-08:00","id":1347603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1347601#post1347601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I was making some comparisons between the text and Madoka, but felt better of it since I was quoting from an unpublished source. Cosmic law and unknowable entities imposing their will and such. Also the image of a mummy hitting up Blessing of the God King by screaming &quot;Azar Power, Make up!&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>*nods, enjoying the notion*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T03:14:36-08:00","id":1347849,"title":"","content":"So Immortals now have Sekhem rating? Cool","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T03:33:59-08:00","id":1347851,"title":"","content":"Also, just to clarify- if an Arisen has their body destroyed, all canopic jars ruined and no Inheritor alive, that would mean permanent death?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T04:08:54-08:00","id":1347853,"title":"","content":"Okay, this preview: Ritual Sorcerer might need to be dropped from four dots to three. I like the less stringent requirements, but if you're going for it, you're already giving over a significant portion of your life to scholarly pursuits; might allow just a tiny bit more flexibility.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, looking good! Just read Merits, and wow, I love how Cults are shaping up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T04:20:00-08:00","id":1347856,"title":"","content":"Sad there doesn't seem the purified aren't returning. But that's honestly not surprising, since they have so little to do with mummy's theme or lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T04:45:35-08:00","id":1347861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1347856#post1347856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sad there doesn't seem the purified aren't returning. But that's honestly not surprising, since they have so little to do with mummy's theme or lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their not returning <i>yet.</i> We also haven't got our stretch goal book yet and I can see the Purified ending up in there along with more Affinities, Utterances, minor Guilds, ghosts/Spirits etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T05:03:11-08:00","id":1347864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1347856#post1347856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sad there doesn't seem the purified aren't returning. But that's honestly not surprising, since they have so little to do with mummy's theme or lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was said that the Blood Bathers, Eternals, Body Thieves and Reborn would get a full coverage in this book, while the rest will get a short one. Hopefully once we will go through the current stretch goal, one of the future ones would be expansion for other immortals (Purified, Visitors, Harvesters, Wardens and Patchwork People). The Purified were mentioned in the previous preview as one of the less &quot;friendly&quot; Immortals, even though that as immortals they would seem to be related to Sekhem by the virtue of being Timeless, so we should expect some revision in their writeup from 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T05:07:50-08:00","id":1347865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1347853#post1347853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, this preview: Ritual Sorcerer might need to be dropped from four dots to three. I like the less stringent requirements, but if you're going for it, you're already giving over a significant portion of your life to scholarly pursuits; might allow just a tiny bit more flexibility.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, looking good! Just read Merits, and wow, I love how Cults are shaping up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m glad you\u2019ve been enjoying the Merits. If you think Ritual Sorcerer should be three dots, I\u2019d recommend mentioning it whenever the feedback sheet goes out. I made the requirements less strict to allow starting characters to have a reasonable chance of pulling it off without being severely limited in their available builds, and that would follow the same logic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T05:45:01-08:00","id":1347871,"title":"","content":"Now that the preview with the powers has dropped, I can tell this story. It amuses me enough that you\u2019ll probably hear it more than once, especially since it will be copy and pasted rather than typed again each time.<br /> This is definitely the most \u201cmeta\u201d story I have to tell (I believe meta is the appropriate word here). I was hired to write one of the Utterances, specifically the one that would become Invoking Tempest\u2019s Fury. This occurred after it first appeared in the prologue game Matthew Dawkins ran for Red Moon Roleplaying. That means that for our delightful game of nonlinear time, everyone got to see an Utterance I wrote used in play broadcast before I was hired to write it or even gave it a single thought. Mundane explanation? Sure. But I find this far more amusing than I probably should.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T06:45:33-08:00","id":1347881,"title":"","content":"Reading through the Merits has absolutely thrilled me; I got character concepts just from individual Merits alone. The inflexibility of Scorpion Cult Initiation is kind of &quot;meh.&quot; It's easy enough to use Mystery Cult Initiation, and that changes basically nothing. Hell, the second and fifth dots wouldn't even need to move, unless I could come up with something better.<br /> <br /> I must admit that compared to the Merits I was a little... underwhelmed with the generic Affinities. Most of them seem to be one-to-one repeats of 1e Affinities <i>and </i>they keep the clunky target number reduction mechanic as opposed to, say, dice tricks like 9-again or 8-again, which basically end up accomplishing the same thing but without tweaking the base system of every CofD game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T07:41:20-08:00","id":1347893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1347881#post1347881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading through the Merits has absolutely thrilled me; I got character concepts just from individual Merits alone. The inflexibility of Scorpion Cult Initiation is kind of &amp;quot;meh.&amp;quot; It's easy enough to use Mystery Cult Initiation, and that changes basically nothing. Hell, the second and fifth dots wouldn't even need to move, unless I could come up with something better.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m glad you liked the Merits. I wrote most of the new ones, so I take it as a point of pride that they\u2019re inspiring character ideas.<br /> SCI wasn\u2019t one of mine, but I don\u2019t believe it\u2019s intended to be inflexible. I thought it permitted adjustment, but only gave one example. If it\u2019s indicating that it is the only possible way, that might need to be addressed when feedback collection begins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T08:24:20-08:00","id":1347904,"title":"","content":"Read the mechanics chapter. Still taking it all in, but in a good way. Will comment more later after the full taking it all in thing occurs. That said, couple of quick comments.<br /> <br /> I love the chapter organization. I think its quite organized and efficient. Sections roll from one area to another.<br /> <br /> That said, question, why is Sekhem at the end? Wouldn't it make more sense to be before Pillars and such. It still is the power source.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Sekhem, I don't get the Pillars/Turn row. (Either now or in 1e) if the Turn part of Pillars/Turn always remains 1 then why even bother putting it in, it doesn't change.<br /> <br /> While I am still not a fan of Sekhem going 10-1 rather than 1-10 the fact that everything else seems really awesome, and Sekehm was at the end so I got all happy reading everything else, does make it less annoying and more just a bother.<br /> <br /> Anyway, there is much to like. Character creation and the descriptions in it. The Merits are awesome. The Pillars are fantastic. The Utterances are amazing. The way things develop and flow and the writing style. Its similar in purpose to 1e but less rambling, more direct, more focused. (Good example is the area on Pillars, it is nicely formatted.)<br /> <br /> Oh, and on Affinities, I REALLY like the fact that there are no lines limiting the number of Affinities a Mummy can have. Which is good as I thought that was out of place.<br /> <br /> On Merits, I like everything. There were numerous Timeless ones that had me going AH HA! AWESOME. Same with the regular merits, and also the supernatural ones.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, I really wish that the Ritual Sorcerer stuff didn't artifiically limit spells to Resolve or Occult. Why couldn't it be that they get a couple 'free' equal to Resolve and anymore need to be purchased as an individual Spell with Merit dots. That way you are still slowing growth but without giving it a limit that well limits character play.<br /> <br /> But so far so good, there is much to like here. Especially, the areas that I can see were rewritten a bit in comparison to 1e.<br /> <br /> Also I too would really like the Purified to come back as a full template. Though I hope they don't start adding restrictions and limitations and internal horror elements to it just because even though they aren't there in the Immortals book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T08:33:04-08:00","id":1347908,"title":"","content":"The Purified don't receive a big profile in this book, no, but if we hit some more stretch goals, I think we'll get to see Purified, Patchwork People, et al.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T08:33:58-08:00","id":1347909,"title":"","content":"While I greatly enjoyed most of the chapter, I was a little underwhelmed by the Utterances, they don\u2019t feel as biblically powerful as they seemed to be in 1e, and all of my favorite Utterances were cut from the list, though I\u2019m sure they will appear in later books. Now I do like how some were tweaked, like Blessed is The God-King and Power of Re, the changes feel right to me.<br /> <br /> But all in all, I\u2019m a little disappointed in the lack of my favorites and the fact that there is only one new Utterance, not Counting the 1.5 ed Utterances from DE ( but hey, that\u2019s word count limits for ya!).<br /> <br /> That said, I love the direction everything is headed, and I can\u2019t wait to see what the other previews will show us!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T09:33:51-08:00","id":1347926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1347904#post1347904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, and on Affinities, I REALLY like the fact that there are no lines limiting the number of Affinities a Mummy can have. Which is good as I thought that was out of place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't sure whether that was coming back or not. In case it is, when Second Chances wrote the unique decree Affinities, it is intended that those do not count against the maximum. Those are a happy little bonus for declaring that decree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1347904#post1347904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On Merits, I like everything. There were numerous Timeless ones that had me going AH HA! AWESOME. Same with the regular merits, and also the supernatural ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I wrote most of the new Merits appearing, I take this as a personal compliment. Thank you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1347904#post1347904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of which, I really wish that the Ritual Sorcerer stuff didn't artifiically limit spells to Resolve or Occult. Why couldn't it be that they get a couple 'free' equal to Resolve and anymore need to be purchased as an individual Spell with Merit dots. That way you are still slowing growth but without giving it a limit that well limits character play.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are multiple Merits that play off of the Ritual Sorcerer Merit, allowing access to more rites in one way or another. If the limit is particularly bothersome for your games, you can easily houserule that once your Occult is up to 5, you can continue purchasing dots of Sorcerous Knowledge beyond the 5 dot mark. I don't think that would really break anything, beyond making the Forbidden Rites and Sorcerous Prodigy Merits less useful.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T09:50:06-08:00","id":1347932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1347908#post1347908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Purified don't receive a big profile in this book, no, but if we hit some more stretch goals, I think we'll get to see Purified, Patchwork People, et al.</div> </div> </div> </div>Argh, as if deciding between money and Mummy wasn't difficult enough, you have just made it worse...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T10:01:47-08:00","id":1347934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1347932#post1347932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Argh, as if deciding between money and Mummy wasn't difficult enough, you have just made it worse...</div> </div> </div> </div>How is that a difficult choice? Eating is for the living! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T10:05:40-08:00","id":1347936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1347934#post1347934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How is that a difficult choice? Eating is for the living! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not if you are Shuankhsen :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T10:19:31-08:00","id":1347943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1347926#post1347926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't sure whether that was coming back or not. In case it is, when Second Chances wrote the unique decree Affinities, it is intended that those do not count against the maximum. Those are a happy little bonus for declaring that decree.</div> </div> </div> </div>It totally makes sense that the bonus Affinity from decree is beyond the normal limit. That said I am really glad there doesn't seem like there is a limit as there really shouldn't be. (I mean nobody says to a Vampire you can only have x number of Disciplines, etc etc)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1347926#post1347926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I wrote most of the new Merits appearing, I take this as a personal compliment. Thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>You should yeah. They are very awesome. While some of them 'just' sound cool to use others make me WANT to purchase them as I could see them being very important for a campaign or a character. There are too many to comment on but some of the immediate thoughts I had were: <br /> <br /> The one that has me going YESSSSSSSS!!! immediately is Resonant Lifetime. I mean it sounds perfect for the character who thinks he is more connected to a particular culture or time period then he is lost Irem. The idea of having it be a life from say the modern world in the current time would totally aid in making it so that even if the game is set in the distant past or the far future they get their memories from late 1990s early 2000s America first. Its perfect. <br /> <br /> Institional Lives seems perfect for random time period play, which is brilliant. I also like the whole if a group has it then they wake up together. (I could see having certain campaigns where all mummy characters get said Merit for free)<br /> <br /> Balanced and Overburned are brilliant. I could see times where taking them would be fun for characters. <br /> <br /> Sandglass is a very nifty ability. I like how it works for both mundanes and mummies. <br /> <br /> Scorpion Cult Initiation to me showcases how there is much potential for a mummy to basically have something like this for their own cult. Which could be very useful and fun for certain campaigns. <br /> <br /> As a note before going into my comment before I like the idea of chain merits and so would totally approve of others coming that have that. I also like the idea of Merits that vary based on who takes them, or what guild or degree or whatever said character has. Such variances are fun. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1347926#post1347926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are multiple Merits that play off of the Ritual Sorcerer Merit, allowing access to more rites in one way or another. If the limit is particularly bothersome for your games, you can easily houserule that once your Occult is up to 5, you can continue purchasing dots of Sorcerous Knowledge beyond the 5 dot mark. I don't think that would really break anything, beyond making the Forbidden Rites and Sorcerous Prodigy Merits less useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like how there is basically a chain of Merits that start from Ritual Sorcerer and expand in certain ways. That is very cool. So I wouldn't want to remove the potential for those merits as they are pretty fun. <br /> <br /> I guess whether I need to change the way those merits work or not depends on whether there is a template version of the Sekhem Sorcerer. Because if there is then there being a limit to what a non-initiated mortal could gain access to is fine for me. Especially if the idea is once they reach said height the only way to go forward is to become something else, something more, which is the template. <br /> <br /> Otherwise yeah, I would just remove the whole limit as you say. <br /> <br /> That said, wouldn't it be interesting if Open Rites and Closed Rites had their own dot level. So that way to gain a third dot Closed Rite one would need to purchase a third dot Sorcereus Knowledge merit. <br /> <br /> That said, I will wait and see for when we get to the chapter with some Open Rites and Closed Rites listed (which I assume there are) before making up my mind. <br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> I have to admit I am not so much a fan of Drawbacks in Merits. Thankfully most of them are more fluff then forced mechanics so its easy to ignore. <br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> Some other thoughts : <br /> <br /> I think some Affinities using Pillar Points would be fun, especially if its for high end super special highly powerful effects. <br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Still reading things, and taking it all in, so will comment again later. hehe <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But yeah, as I said, I really like the writing and the formatting and the structure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T10:33:15-08:00","id":1347949,"title":"","content":"Pardon me for a moment but I need to yell and squee in delight. <br /> <br /> I ABSOLUTELY LOVE LOVE LOVE LOVE NON-LINEAR TIME AND THE NATURE OF IT! IT IS SOOOOOOOOOO GLORIOUS. `<br /> <br /> *cough* <br /> <br /> Right. Pardon me. <br /> <br /> But yeah, the way non-linear time works is just so cool. So cool. <br /> <br /> I don't think I could gush enough about this element.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T10:40:01-08:00","id":1347952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1347949#post1347949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pardon me for a moment but I need to yell and squee in delight. <br /> <br /> I ABSOLUTELY LOVE LOVE LOVE LOVE NON-LINEAR TIME AND THE NATURE OF IT! IT IS SOOOOOOOOOO GLORIOUS. `<br /> <br /> *cough* <br /> <br /> Right. Pardon me. <br /> <br /> But yeah, the way non-linear time works is just so cool. So cool. <br /> <br /> I don't think I could gush enough about this element.</div> </div> </div> </div>This pleases me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T11:58:43-08:00","id":1347979,"title":"","content":"Just skimmed the new Preview, liking what I saw. A question about Sahu Repair though it says &quot;Once per turn, mummies may sacrifice dots of Sekhem to fully heal aggravated damage at a rate of one Sekhem dot per one box of aggravated damage.&quot; Is that intended to be, &quot;Spend one Sekhem, heal one aggravated&quot; or &quot;Spend one Sekhem, heal your Sekhem dots in aggravated&quot;. I ask because the former seems like a really awful use of Sekhem...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T15:31:36-08:00","id":1348027,"title":"","content":"Minor complication in the Affinities: While the description of raising Physical Attributes in the Pillars section has the more detailed Dexterity vs. Strength/Stamina differentiation in the Sekhem section to inform it, Divine Countenance and Wisdom of the Ancients allude to using the Dexterity rate without actually saying so by simply saying they work like the Physical Attribute boost does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1347881#post1347881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The inflexibility of Scorpion Cult Initiation is kind of &quot;meh.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's explicitly a sample version. It's MCI with the additional effects specific to mummy cults thrown in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1347979#post1347979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ask because the former seems like a really awful use of Sekhem...</div> </div> </div> </div>Aggravated damage is a big deal and most beings don't get the option of instantly healing it as an innate power. They've already got &quot;spend a Pillar point to just straight-up not die for a few turns while you heal lethal and bashing damage&quot; going for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T16:01:31-08:00","id":1348032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It feels, along with some other things as a bit baffling and simply copy pasta straight from 1e to 2e. It has some uses in a pinch technically, but the ratio is so terrible for the cost that I struggle to think it was something that should have simply been transferred directly over from 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I struggle to think if I ever saw it used in first edition. I think my players ended up concluding that it was better to die. Worst case scenario in a Death Cycle was that you might lose two dots of Sekhem (the second being reasonably likely but not guaranteed), but when you woke up you'd have healed half of your health in Aggravated damage. I haven't had a chance to look at the mechanics chapter yet, but if the Death Cycle rules remained more or less the same in their relation to the Descent then it's a pretty poor choice unless you're in a really time sensitive situation and are only barely on the cusp of death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T16:23:40-08:00","id":1348047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It feels, along with some other things as a bit baffling and simply copy pasta straight from 1e to 2e. It has some uses in a pinch technically, but the ratio is so terrible for the cost that I struggle to think it was something that should have simply been transferred directly over from 1e.<br /> <br /> Somewhat relating to that, I am veeeeeeeery slightly surprised that Sealing the Flesh transferred over the same, but it's always been a strong effect relatively speaking so I am not all that surprised.</div> </div> </div> </div>TBH I'm kinda shocked by how similar most of the mechanics are to 1e. Don't get me wrong, Mummies are still potent as always, but next to the buffs other Splats picked up they feel a little underwhelming. Not that I'm trying to make this a cross over fight or anything. <br /> <br /> I would have at least expected the kinda cludgy Pillar/Utterance system to see a rework. All the prerequisites and caviats struck me as trap mechanics, systems that demand a fairly comprehensive understanding of the value and rewards of certain investments that non-crunch oriented players can get screwed over by. Sahu Restoration being a perfect example, I can easily see a player getting spooked by aggravated damage and wasting an excessive quantity of Sekhem. Of course that's something a good Storyteller should stop, but alas not all storytellers believe in helping their players. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T16:26:45-08:00","id":1348048,"title":"","content":"1 Sekhem should heal all damage. The finished text will clarify this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T18:28:30-08:00","id":1348096,"title":"","content":"The Secretive Merit kind of puzzles me....<br /> <br /> If Cult members can only know other Cult members that are equal to their rank or lower... ...Who's giving them orders? How do they not know the person that is saying they can be ordered about has the authority to do so?<br /> <br /> Edit: Oooh wait a second. They have masks or badges or stuff.... It's not that the lower Cultists don't recognize a higher ranked Cultist... they just don't know who exactly that person is...<br /> <br /> Sorry! Having a little sake while reading and that's slowing my reading comprehension a little! ^.^;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","user":"Paradim","date":". 11-12-2019, 09:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T19:51:58-08:00","id":1348125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348048#post1348048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1 Sekhem should heal all damage. The finished text will clarify this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome! I knew something was up when I read it, heading agg isn't THAT special.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T20:01:25-08:00","id":1348127,"title":"","content":"@TyrannicalRabbit<br /> Tier 3 of Tempest\u2019s Fury doesn\u2019t automatically have the effects of Tier 1or 2, but it does boost those effects if they\u2019re used together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T20:21:41-08:00","id":1348135,"title":"","content":"Bah! Blessed Catalyst didn\u2019t make the jump! I really liked that Affinity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T21:15:21-08:00","id":1348148,"title":"","content":"I will say this: Looking at the Timeless Conditions in the Appendix makes me <i>really </i>excited to see how Feeling the Flow works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T22:29:50-08:00","id":1348160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348135#post1348135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bah! Blessed Catalyst didn\u2019t make the jump! I really liked that Affinity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, now that I realize which one that is I'm now sad. That Affinity to me was a brilliant way to provide Mummies with some alchemical abilities. Which is something I super enjoy letting them have. (Alchemy is a form of magic item creation and I like the presence of such powers.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T22:33:33-08:00","id":1348161,"title":"","content":"Interesting effects...<br /> <br /> Guardian Statue Affinity allows you to create a small statuette of someone that becomes enchanted so that the next time that person would take damage, the statuette breaks instead.<br /> <br /> The statuette is not required to be kept on the person. This means an Arisen can keep a shelf full of statuettes dedicated to the cultists he seeks to protect, and if one breaks, he'll know that they're in immediate danger. Even if across the world.<br /> <br /> Handy!<br /> <br /> Edit: Admittedly, Nest of Dolls would probably be better for that kind of information.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","user":"Paradim","date":". 11-13-2019, 01:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T23:01:41-08:00","id":1348168,"title":"","content":"Does a Disembodied mummy whose Ba and Ren or Ka and Sheut are both 0 still have an effective Finesse or Resistance of 1, given that they're Attributes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T23:45:37-08:00","id":1348173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348148#post1348148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will say this: Looking at the Timeless Conditions in the Appendix makes me <i>really </i>excited to see how Feeling the Flow works.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn\u2019t think any of my stuff was in this week\u2019s preview - missed the Appendix with Conditions.<br /> <br /> I think people will like mummies and time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T01:52:05-08:00","id":1348188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The tantalizing possibilities in the Appendix were honestly one of the few things I liked in this otherwise let down of a preview.<br /> <br /> Edit. Going to try to comb carefully over Affinities before work tomorrow, but a glance so far feels like a lot of the same. Affable Aid has awkward wording on one of it's effects relative to normally spending Willpower, Grip of Death inexplicably doesn't let you defend against ranged weapons anymore,etc. This feels like a really bad copy paste, without actually examining the issues of 1e Affinities and Utterances so far.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd appreciate it if you avoid use of the term &quot;copy and paste&quot; as it implies the writers literally copied text from one edition to the next. If you find a place where that is definitely the case, drop me a message.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T02:44:52-08:00","id":1348193,"title":"","content":"Edit: nevermind, found the answer to my own question. Enjoying the preview so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10272,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","user":"Daigotsu Max","date":". 11-13-2019, 06:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T04:20:03-08:00","id":1348211,"title":"","content":"I am happily wrong about no purified. Thank you all for informing me that we may see it in stretch goals. Even if that's very far away from now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T04:43:17-08:00","id":1348223,"title":"","content":"While not as bothered by it as TR, I do share concerns about the Affinities now that I\u2019ve looked them over a second time. Copy and Pasted they clearly aren\u2019t, but several do seem quite out of place for being adapted for second edition due to their effects not really evolving or getting expanded upon like other similar abilities from other lines. It\u2019s not an overly huge thing, but it is odd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T05:15:31-08:00","id":1348233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348223#post1348223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While not as bothered by it as TR, I do share concerns about the Affinities now that I\u2019ve looked them over a second time. Copy and Pasted they clearly aren\u2019t, but several do seem quite out of place for being adapted for second edition due to their effects not really evolving or getting expanded upon like other similar abilities from other lines. It\u2019s not an overly huge thing, but it is odd.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My opinion too. I thought target number manipulation wasn't a thing anymore, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T07:36:09-08:00","id":1348256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348233#post1348233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My opinion too. I thought target number manipulation wasn't a thing anymore, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. I thought that was going to get cut for sure. Especially now that &quot;target number&quot; refers to a <i>different</i> thing in the system (extended actions, which are mentioned in the same preview).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T10:07:00-08:00","id":1348284,"title":"","content":"The writer and I agreed that retaining target number manipulation was a fun way of making mummies distinct, but we're listening to what you're saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T10:15:20-08:00","id":1348287,"title":"","content":"Not to start a number but I thought the idea of Mummies manipulating target number was cool. Its basically saying they have an in with the universe and thus for them certain tasks are just all around easier. (Target Number still being the whole instead of 8 being a success it is now 7, right.)<br /> <br /> Looking at things I see the fact that there are less Utterances as more an issue then the fact that target numbers are modified.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T10:22:56-08:00","id":1348289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348284#post1348284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The writer and I agreed that retaining target number manipulation was a fun way of making mummies distinct, but we're listening to what you're saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that\u2019s perfectly fine, that\u2019s not an issue. I just was hoping to see some new iterations of the Affinities that build upon the manipulation of Fate that makes them so unique<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. <br /> <br /> Like how level one in Protean became an expansion on how Haven Of Soil operated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 11-13-2019, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T10:23:03-08:00","id":1348290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348284#post1348284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The writer and I agreed that retaining target number manipulation was a fun way of making mummies distinct, but we're listening to what you're saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mind target number manipulation, it's easy to understand and conveys their tie to fate nightly. But as per Tessie's point the term Target Number refers to something different in 2e.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> <s>Reading through the Utterances in more detail I see a number of them have Pillar Clauses that are the same as their Pillar Prerequisite, for instance: Tier 3 of Awaken The Dead has the clause &quot;The Arisen with a Ren Pillar rating of 5 is the true master of this tier, those raised by her can remain at liberty for Memory + Sekhem days, instead of hours.&quot; But the Arisen must already have Ren 5 to use the effect. Why waste the words and space on clauses that are essentially guaranteed?</s><br /> <br /> Nvm, read the Utterance Rules again and I see that you can use them without their Pillar requirements. Love that change! Though, as others have said the Utterances can feel a tad toothless without their Pillar clauses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 11-13-2019, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T10:39:38-08:00","id":1348295,"title":"","content":"It's not a deal breaker for me personally, but I'm a bit disappointed that it's included when another dev (who wrote for MtC 1e but not for MtC 2e) pointed out shifting target numbers as one of the mechanical failings of the game, and it's just going to be so messy combining it with other dice tricks, especially in roll-heavy groups like mine.<br /> <br /> It is, however, a deal breaker for my group. They're all oWoD veterans and never ended up playing MtC 1e because of shifting target numbers because of their experiences with oWoD difficulty. Now they're no longer interested in backing the book and I'll probably never end up playing it. So I guess it becomes a deal breaker for me too, in that regard.<br /> <br /> <i>If</i> shifting target numbers are removed, I would very much want the decision to be posted before the KS ends.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=960966#post960966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He also thought shifting target numbers were a good idea. I love mummy, I wrote on mummy, but it is not exactly overflowing with mechanical greatness.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 11-13-2019, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T10:52:07-08:00","id":1348299,"title":"","content":"Still taking the chapter in, hehe, but looking at the current note about Affinities I would like to make two comments.<br /> <br /> 1. The way the shifting target numbers work from 1e to 2e is a much broader and 'simple' way, which is good. The whole speciality dice pool thing seems to add more micromanagement. Maybe just have own the affinity, pay a willpower, and the target number for that scene and the attribute category is reduced by one. Just sayin. <br /> <br /> That said I do wish that Pillar Points could be used as a fuel stat for Affinities in addition to Willpower. I think it would add a nice variability to power use. <br /> <br /> 2. I miss the whole fluff sentence that gives a sort of ambiance to the affinity. I ENJOY that descriptive phrasing and wish it was still there. How a power looks and what it represents is just as fun as a mechanical effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 11-13-2019, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T11:16:46-08:00","id":1348305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348287#post1348287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to start a number but I thought the idea of Mummies manipulating target number was cool. Its basically saying they have an in with the universe and thus for them certain tasks are just all around easier. (Target Number still being the whole instead of 8 being a success it is now 7, right.)<br /> <br /> Looking at things I see the fact that there are less Utterances as more an issue then the fact that target numbers are modified.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same here, though I can agree another term might be better if &quot;target number&quot; is used for something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T11:34:39-08:00","id":1348309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348295#post1348295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a deal breaker for me personally, but I'm a bit disappointed that it's included when another dev (who wrote for MtC 1e but not for MtC 2e) pointed out shifting target numbers as one of the mechanical failings of the game, and it's just going to be so messy combining it with other dice tricks, especially in roll-heavy groups like mine.<br /> <br /> It is, however, a deal breaker for my group. They're all oWoD veterans and never ended up playing MtC 1e because of shifting target numbers because of their experiences with oWoD difficulty. Now they're no longer interested in backing the book and I'll probably never end up playing it. So I guess it becomes a deal breaker for me too, in that regard.<br /> <br /> <i>If</i> shifting target numbers are removed, I would very much want the decision to be posted before the KS ends.<br /> <br /> Edit:</div> </div> </div> </div>In fairness, just because Dave doesn't like them, doesn't mean we need to eliminate them. In any case, we're discussing how attached we are to them, but you probably won't hear our decision before the Kickstarter concludes as we'll have to review feedback on the whole text before making decisions. Sorry if that means your friends don't get to back the game, but there's always Backerkit if they change their minds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T13:13:37-08:00","id":1348322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whilst this section did not let me down the way that Utterances did, I still feel problematic overall about it. With the Affinities losing their cool flavour text from 1e, and I do understand that word count is a tough beast, the strange omissions that certain 1e Affinities had and the overall feeling that this isn't any significant change from 1e. It just kind of falls somewhat flat in places for me.<br /> <br /> I counted around twenty Affinities that were in the 1e core not here. Now it should be said, some of those are now either redundant or were not all that stand out in 1e. But among them are a number of arguably thematically and mechanically important effects to cover a base of supernatural power you would expect from a core book. Right now it feels like practically half a book in terms of giving you a good baseline for what your supernatural powers are in a core book. Since we will be looking to get more in the Companion I am tempering myself on the matter. But the powers section as a whole just feels stilted and uninspiring for me.<br /> <br /> I really hate to sound so negative on the matter, and I don't even consider myself a crunch guy. But yeah, just not feeling it. 1st edition had issues in places in a disconnect between how the setting describes the potency of the Deathless and the mechanical expressions of that. So far this feels like more of the same on that front.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah... This is kind of how I'm feeling. The change of the powers section from 1st Edition Werewolf the Forsaken to 2nd Edition Werewolf the Forsaken were... mind blowing to me. Not only did W:tF give the Uratha an effective range of powers, but the text slammed home how these powers are thematic through predator/prey and hunter themes, hitting several times ideas of horror movie monsters from the perspective of the monster. I loved it.<br /> <br /> And I'm not a Vampire: The Requiem fan... It's not that I hate it, it just doesn't grab me. But I can see the change from 1st Edition to 2nd Edition as being a really big improvement for the game, with powers becoming more evocative of their vampire nature.<br /> <br /> I was... kind of hoping for a similar kind of upgrade for Mummy: The Curse. Worse, actually, I kind of feel like Mummies are.... not doing good here. With the decision that there wasn't enough word count available to have the powers Mummies have over death in being able to manipulate and command ghosts, I understand the reason. But it still means that a lot of the powers Arisen had in 1st Edition that were extremely evocative, scary effects, just aren't represented here. <br /> <br /> It's effectively half of their power set just not there. I feel like this is a problem.<br /> <br /> And here's something else I'm noticing... The Eternal Legend Affinity. This kind of got disassembled to become a basic feature that all Arisen enjoy, being able to re-establish their Cults from beyond the grave. But something from the 1st Edition Eternal Legend Affinity is missing. And I can't find it.<br /> <br /> The power Eternal Legend Affinity gave you to have your Cultists use your name as a blessing to invoke your divine power to make their next action more successful if it's something you think would benefit your goals. Where is it? Did I miss it?<br /> <br /> Cause I'm gonna have a LOT of sad here if it's just gone. That kind of power is just too awesome not to have around... x.x","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T13:28:01-08:00","id":1348324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The sort of everyday use powers of Affinities would not be improved in the slightest by having them cost an already strangely tiny resource that already has a list of important uses.<br /> <br /> I am okay in general with the idea of more restrictive and different kinds of mechanical expression for a &quot;fuel stat&quot;. but Mummy's feels TOO restrictive. If in actual play, with new ways to regain Pillars,etc it doesn't actually feel like that I will be the first person to be delighted and glad to be wrong on the matter.<br /> <br /> -skip-</div> </div> </div> </div>Just wanted to comment on this, since you quoted me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> Though it might have sounded like it, and if so my bad, but I wasn't so much saying that this particular use of a power should cause Pillar Points, more that Mummies should have the ability to fuel their Affinities with Pillar and Willpower. That their fuel stat should be made available in some ways to activate powers. <br /> <br /> That said, I agree with you on not having an everyday use power having such a cost. Honestly, I would prefer it if TN reduction was more &quot;buy a power and gain TN reduction automatically&quot; (Like say how a Psion in Aeon would go from TN 8 to TN 7 upon becoming a Proxy.) The less nitpicky and micromanagey the powers are the better in my estimation. <br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> As a general thing I can't help but think that the whole non-linear time element of Mummy is totally the best way to handle being something ancient and yet relateable. It is just such a fantastic way to go about representing the nature of the mummy. <br /> <br /> ----------<br /> <br /> Hmmm. A thought. Maybe there can be an Utterance that could let a mummy more easily fit in to a time period upon awakening. Have it be related to his Cult and the knowelge that those bound to it feed him. That way it can be explained how a Mummy so easily fits into worlds quite different from the one he experienced beforehand. <br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> Another thought that is more a question - I wonder if there is a way to make it so that a Mummy upon being forced awakened won't automaticaly resort to violence (that is kill those who woke him) but rather act in dominance, that is basically showcase his godking ambience and make a minion of the person who woke him. That could be an interesting awakening act.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T13:51:46-08:00","id":1348328,"title":"","content":"I've been looking at the Affinities from 1st Edition and comparing them to the preview Affinities and... I think I'm noticing some things. First, I'm noticing that there doesn't seem to be any... entirely new Affinities. Same names, same general ideas involved, less evocative text. Second, I think I'm noticing that the Affinities that granted Merits have had that feature stripped out of them. For example, Enlightened Senses in 1st Edition gave you the Common Sense and Meditative Mind Merits. The Preview removes that and instead says you're immune to surprise attacks.<br /> <br /> Now... I'm just guessing here regarding the motivation for this, but I think it's under the idea of &quot;If someone wanted those Merits, they can just pay experience for them.&quot; But something I've noticed in my games is that those Merits tend to be... undervalued, relative for experience costs, in relation to supernatural powers for players. &quot;Why spend my precious experience points on something that seems so mundane as Common Sense, when I can pick up a power that lets me beast-mode on enemies?&quot; That kinda thinking. And I appreciated how 1st Edition Affinities wrapped up Merits into powers for the Arisen, or powers they grant to Cultists because it's an nice way to build up power that doesn't add a lot of text. And make more use of those Merits.<br /> <br /> But, this got exchanged with a flat immunity to surprise attacks and... I'm not sure how comfortable I am with that. It seems to be doubling up a bit on what the power provides, since it adds +Ren dice to perception checks, presumably you'd be adding +Ren dice to checks to notice surprise attacks. But instead, it just completely nullifies a mechanic from the game. I'm not sure how I feel about that, and I'm wondering what I'm forgetting from powers other supernatural creatures have in regards to having immunity to surprise attacks...<br /> <br /> Edit: To be clear, I think there might be some new Affinities for the Guild Affinities, even though there are only three listed for each Guild... I would need to go through the Guildhalls of the Deathless book I think.... But I'm pretty sure at least Nest of Dolls is completely new.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","user":"Paradim","date":". 11-13-2019, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T14:16:37-08:00","id":1348332,"title":"","content":"That surmises how I feel pretty well. Not as strongly as some, but like I said before, while I greatly enjoy the chapter, there are a notable number of... quirks with Affinities and the lackluster feel to the Utterances makes me not quite as hyped for Mummy The Curse as I was originally. But like before, everything else shows huge promise, especially regarding the lore and flavor blurbs between chapters. I love the MTC mythology a hell of a lot, and it is tied with Promethean at being the best gameline never played for me.. so i am still optimistic.<br /> <br /> Now assuming no one fucks up the antagonist or storytelling chapters, this will be fantastic! But seeing Matt\u2019s love for antagonists, I am confident there is no danger of that happening <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T14:18:57-08:00","id":1348333,"title":"","content":"Yeahhh, I'm... kinda in the same boat on a lot of this, in regards to the powers. Things feel missing, and many of the things that are still present feel... tamer than they maybe ought to be, stripped of tone in spots, weirdly more laser-focused in a couple cases than one might expect for the Arisen, and... we have precisely four Affinities and one Condition carrying over a mechanic that seemed on the chopping block in the edition shift. Granted, God King's Scepter at least feels like a good use of it if it's going to be anywhere, but... it doesn't feel worth keeping the mechanic around like this if it's only in such a limited capacity and on a small handful of powers, tops. Something less... clunky could easily slot in there in place of it. 9-Again, a die bonus... something <i>rooouuughly</i> statistically similar that doesn't bring back a weird (if at the time more plentiful and flavorful) mechanical quirk from Mummy 1e just because it was there.<br /> Not saying it has to necessarily go away though. It's been a long while since I read through Mummy 1e and I'm away from the PC with all my PDFs, but were there any effects that cursed others with <i>increased </i>Target Numbers under specific circumstances? That would have been a neat way to carry forward the effect into 2e while expanding it if it wasn't present before (well, the Dead Dreamer Condition in the Appendix preview applies the &quot;increase Target Number by one&quot; effect when not following the assigned task, so that's <i>one</i> use). Or spread the weird fate-bending around, blessing cultists in their presence, things like that. I guess the point is, if more powers played with it and in more ways than just &quot;three of effectively the same power on the Physical-Mental-Social axes, plus one for all uses on their own cultists&quot;, it might feel like a more natural fit, at least as far as literal fate-bending can feel natural. Add it to <i>more</i> Affinities outside those four, give another Utterance or two a horrible, personal curse that fucks over the victim's target numbers in different circumstances or <i>improves <u>others</u></i>' target numbers when working against them... something along those lines. There <i>is</i> <i>room</i> for it if it's gonna continue to exist.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the other hand, the merits list is cool, liking the options across the board. The fact that the Arisen can start their Descents with lower Sekhem depending on context is also fun in a way, though I can honestly see a number of tables dropping that for simplicity and Bigger Numbers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T14:50:42-08:00","id":1348337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sconce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348333#post1348333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeahhh, I'm... kinda in the same boat on a lot of this, in regards to the powers. Things feel missing, and many of the things that are still present feel... tamer than they maybe ought to be, stripped of tone in spots, weirdly more laser-focused in a couple cases than one might expect for the Arisen, and... we have precisely four Affinities and one Condition carrying over a mechanic that seemed on the chopping block in the edition shift. Granted, God King's Scepter at least feels like a good use of it if it's going to be anywhere, but... it doesn't feel worth keeping the mechanic around like this if it's only in such a limited capacity and on a small handful of powers, tops. Something less... clunky could easily slot in there in place of it. 9-Again, a die bonus... something <i>rooouuughly</i> statistically similar that doesn't bring back a weird (if at the time more plentiful and flavorful) mechanical quirk from Mummy 1e just because it was there.<br /> Not saying it has to necessarily go away though. It's been a long while since I read through Mummy 1e and I'm away from the PC with all my PDFs, but were there any effects that cursed others with <i>increased </i>Target Numbers under specific circumstances? That would have been a neat way to carry forward the effect into 2e while expanding it if it wasn't present before (well, the Dead Dreamer Condition in the Appendix preview applies the &quot;increase Target Number by one&quot; effect when not following the assigned task, so that's <i>one</i> use). Or spread the weird fate-bending around, blessing cultists in their presence, things like that. I guess the point is, if more powers played with it and in more ways than just &quot;three of effectively the same power on the Physical-Mental-Social axes, plus one for all uses on their own cultists&quot;, it might feel like a more natural fit, at least as far as literal fate-bending can feel natural. Add it to <i>more</i> Affinities outside those four, give another Utterance or two a horrible, personal curse that fucks over the victim's target numbers in different circumstances or <i>improves <u>others</u></i>' target numbers when working against them... something along those lines. There <i>is</i> <i>room</i> for it if it's gonna continue to exist.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the other hand, the merits list is cool, liking the options across the board. The fact that the Arisen can start their Descents with lower Sekhem depending on context is also fun in a way, though I can honestly see a number of tables dropping that for simplicity and Bigger Numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, there certainly were powers that increased Target Numbers.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm someone who was never bothered by the TN mechanics in 1e. They're implemented in a very different way to oWoD, limited to the usage of specific supernatural abilities, and weren't too hard to grok. I like that they're back, but feel like their identity has been confused. The first Tier of Blessed is the God King was enormously popular in my game, and I think changing it to be Rote Action both makes it feel less special <i>and</i> means that there are now multiple different mechanics representing the manipulation of Fate, which makes that side of the game weaker as a whole. Pick a mechanic for representing Fate and stick with it. I'd honestly prefer the mechanic to be Target Number reduction (in the sense of reducing what you need to roll for a success, not in the case of Extended Actions, I'm honestly not sure which one of those the 2e Affinities are meant to be referring to), but consistency would be good.<br /> <br /> And I'm going to add to the others saying that the Affinities and Utterances feel lacking. The core mechanics of Arisen too. I was seriously expecting Sealing the Flesh to match the <i>Garou</i> for healing prowess, there's something that feels a little wrong about the fact that the average Mummy might struggle against the average Werewolf. I don't really do crossover in my games, but odds are my players will be coming to Mummy from Werewolf and I think it'd be a shame if their firsti impression waking at Sekhem 10 with power raging within them was... disappointment. And I'm a little surprised that some of the Utterances that made the cut were some of the weakest from 1e. The first edition was beautifully balanced. My group spent a lot of time with that book, and the consensus at the end was that there were only two &quot;dud&quot; Utterances in the game. Waters of Life and Death and Seeds of Life, if I remember right. They were interesting, but were just too unlikely to be relevant in a game to worry about, and it's weird seeing Waters, for example, brought across without much to seriously spice it up. I'm really surprised that some powers, Blessed is the God King, Power of Re (Tier 3, Tier 1 feels like an improvement), Grip of Death, and a few others actually went backwards in scope, and a lot of the most evocative powers from 1e don't seem to have made the cut.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T14:50:51-08:00","id":1348338,"title":"","content":"Am I imagining things, or that the number of backers goes up while the total pledged earnings go down?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T15:07:29-08:00","id":1348341,"title":"","content":"Chiming in on powers - target number modification I was surprised to find, but since it's only of one type and for a few powers I don't think it's an issue. As said above, it does make the mummies distinct.<br /> <br /> As for Utterances, maybe it's because I don't remember the 1st edition as well, but I don't find them lacking or underpowered. Some of these effects are seriously huge, and they can all be available from character creation, possibly including the bonus depending on pillar values. And they're all pretty evocative, which is what I look for in abilities.<br /> <br /> Also, I feel we're missing Relics and Vestiges to get a full picture of a Mummy's abilities, but time and previews will tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T15:08:11-08:00","id":1348342,"title":"","content":"I didn\u2019t think of it until now, but looking at it AGAIN, I\u2019m surprised to see that Azahul is right, several are some of the weaker Utterances to boot, which probably adds to that feeling I have. ( Not that I\u2019m surprised that he\u2019s right, more that I didn\u2019t catch it)<br /> <br /> It makes me really Miss Revelations Of Smoke and Fire, and all of the the Words Of Dead Fury/Glory/Hunger, though I admit you could probably merge all three together into a single Utterence now, Words Of Dead [Insert epic or biblical sounding Adverb or Noun here]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T16:00:48-08:00","id":1348352,"title":"","content":"Utterances puzzle me a bit... The Cosmic keyword is terribly under utilized.... and confusingly used. Cosmic only shows up for the Tier 3 Awaken The Dead utterance which lets you temporarily bring a person back to life. And it doesn't show up on either the Utterance that lets you hit an area with an Earthquake, a Meteor Shower, or Storm.<br /> <br /> When it's meant to be used to denote an Utterance that can change the chronicle.... I feel like I'm not understanding what the criteria for that is.<br /> <br /> ...Anyone else finding that weird?<br /> <br /> Edit: ...Actually, why is this a Keyword at all? What purpose is it serving?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T16:42:17-08:00","id":1348357,"title":"","content":"My thought at this time is primarily this: I'm disappointed at how conservative the changes and overall enhancements to a Mummy's power are. I don't feel like as currently presented a freshly awaken Mummy is the terrible 'wake up surrounded by dead grave robbers' threat that we were promised. It was a problem I had with 1e, and it was the problem I was hoping 2e would correct and am currently disappointed to find is not the case.<br /> <br /> I have confidence in Matthew Dawkins as a developer, and in our current team of writers, that they have the awareness and desire to make this game the best game it can be. Already I have heard some corrections and clarifications that please me, and I content myself with the knowledge that at least some concerns will be addressed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T17:04:52-08:00","id":1348359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's somewhat why I was worried about the constant reference to things like the meteor shower Utterance in lead ups. Utterances are more self contained than some other powers in the cofd but right now mummies just feel like the earthquakes and meteor shower splat and that carries a lot of problems for a number of reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I need to nitpick the Earthquake power. Because for me it is <b>by far </b>the biggest letdown. The text pitches this as a miraculous power of vast destruction, which is certainly is, unfortunately the time to cast it is measured in DAYS. Even with good rolls you are looking at a 48 hour period to cast this Utterance (which, IMO, kinda goes against the Words of Power feel of Utterances). Not only that, but you have to be at the center of the quake, so there's no using this to shake down an adversaries lair from afar. <br /> <br /> Powers like this worry me because of how punishing they can be for a player who picked them. Having to wait out your character's big Utterance moment can be really disappointing, especially when the other players are calling down meteors, driving people insane with the winds and reviving Ghengis Khan. Seriously, I have run CofD for ten years now, hundreds of hours, dozens of stories all with different scales and tones, and I cannot think of a single time at which the story or characters could stand sit still for the 48+ hour cast time.<br /> <br /> This power has got to be the poster child for the &quot;breaks on&quot; feel of Utterances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T17:09:19-08:00","id":1348360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't speak for others but I dropped my pledge down for the time being and I am seriously considering bowing out entirely at this point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm leaving room for Mummy to surprise me, but as it currently stands, I am hovering around here. I would say that for my money, I'm disappointed at how conservative the changes to Mummy <i>in general</i> have been. Your mileage may vary, of course, but I considered Mummy to be one of the weakest of the 1e gamelines, despite respecting some bold choices it made like the unique relationship of the Arisen to their Sekhem. The nonlinear relationship to time is a cool new wrinkle the new edition adds, and I respect the added attention to cults and the demolishment of the wall between player and Storyteller knowledge (and, arguably, Storyteller and developer knowledge) 1e had, as well as the addition of fiends from the Duat that seems to be implied by the Appendix. But I think the basic structure of the Mummy template and experience needed a reenvisioning and focused overhaul on the level of Geist 2e's Bound or moreso, and what I see so far is more of an update and a little polishing. Some nice appetizers added to the menu, but little change to the recipe of the main dish.<br /> <br /> I don't really expect this to be a popular position on the Mummy subforum, of course, but I just felt one post of feedback was worth being heard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T17:12:52-08:00","id":1348362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348359#post1348359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, I need to nitpick the Earthquake power. Because for me it is <b>by far </b>the biggest letdown. The text pitches this as a miraculous power of vast destruction, which is certainly is, unfortunately the time to cast it is measured in DAYS. Even with good rolls you are looking at a 48 hour period to cast this Utterance (which, IMO, kinda goes against the Words of Power feel of Utterances). Not only that, but you have to be at the center of the quake, so there's no using this to shake down an adversaries lair from afar.<br /> <br /> Powers like this worry me because of how punishing they can be for a player who picked them. Having to wait out your character's big Utterance moment can be really disappointing, especially when the other players are calling down meteors, driving people insane with the winds and reviving Ghengis Khan. Seriously, I have run CofD for ten years now, hundreds of hours, dozens of stories all with different scales and tones, and I cannot think of a single time at which the story or characters could stand sit still for the 48+ hour cast time.<br /> <br /> This power has got to be the poster child for the &quot;breaks on&quot; feel of Utterances.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Earthquake power is great in every way except the time it takes to cast, yes. It was my first and immediate complaint when I saw it. It's worse because 'call down a shower of meteors from the sky' takes basically no time at all by comparison. Same with the capstone tier of the new Utterance, Invoking Tempest's Fury, where the casting time is a mere 3 turns that you can use in the middle of a fight if you were so inclined.<br /> <br /> The only way to use an earthquake in a reasonable timeframe is to commit suicide and watch the devastation from Neter-Khertet, waiting it out while your death cycle resolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T17:24:16-08:00","id":1348366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348362#post1348362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Earthquake power is great in every way except the time it takes to cast, yes. It was my first and immediate complaint when I saw it. It's worse because 'call down a shower of meteors from the sky' takes basically no time at all by comparison. Same with the capstone tier of the new Utterance, Invoking Tempest's Fury, where the casting time is a mere 3 turns that you can use in the middle of a fight if you were so inclined.<br /> <br /> The only way to use an earthquake in a reasonable timeframe is to commit suicide and watch the devastation from Neter-Khertet, waiting it out while your death cycle resolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have succinctly captured my thoughts. Thank you.<br /> <br /> That said! I don't want to come off as a total downer. As Daigotsu Max pointed out, to a newcomer I'm sure the powers fall well within the jaw dropping range. The fact that we've been conditioned to expect considerable power increases from the 2e reimaginings may be tainting my PoV. And for what it's worth I think most of the Utterances are nicely squared away in the &quot;holy shit&quot; zone of power. Hell, feeling a little disappointed with the powers might well be within Mummy's &quot;powerful, but not powerful enough&quot; themes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T18:01:48-08:00","id":1348375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348357#post1348357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My thought at this time is primarily this: I'm disappointed at how conservative the changes and overall enhancements to a Mummy's power are. I don't feel like as currently presented a freshly awaken Mummy is the terrible 'wake up surrounded by dead grave robbers' threat that we were promised. It was a problem I had with 1e, and it was the problem I was hoping 2e would correct and am currently disappointed to find is not the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this regard I think they had a difficult job in front of them. A newly awakened Mummy must be terrifying enough that no group of mortals would ever dream of standing their ground against it, while not so overwhelming that a plucky Brendan Fraser &amp; Rachel Weisz cannot mount a daring escape. That's a tough line to walk. Most 2e lines resolve the Mortals vs Monsters problem by rewarding ambush tactics, the far off sniper for the mage, the house fire for the vampire, etc. This straight up does not work on Mummies, whom for the most part are unkillable by mortal means (save fire, and even that'll at best knock them into a cycle). So in that regard Mummies are fairly special, they won't necessarily kill you on contact, but you absolutely cannot stop them.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>Thaaat said, I certainly wouldn't <i>complain </i>if the devs decided to rip off the brakes and make the Arisen outrageous (like Gauru form. 1e: heal a lethal each turn! 2e: HEAL EVERYTHING! EVERY TURN! AND PEOPLE JUST DIE! RAAAAAWR!!!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 11-13-2019, 09:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T18:07:30-08:00","id":1348376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree in parts and agree in parts. Themetically it wasn't the weakest game line. It knew what it wanted to be and the collective books under the at the time limited book run format realized it's internal mythology.<br /> <br /> Even the understandable complaints about the insularity of Mummy were not really about Mummy's world itself but about trying to use it's bits with other things. In comparison things like Werewolf and Vampire laboured under the shadows of the WoD before breaking out spectacularly in 2e. I admit some bias. After all it was one of the if not the favourite 1e line for me. But I think at times criticisms of it fail to touch on problems of it's infrastructure rather than the clash of preference and presentation.<br /> <br /> Where I think 1e Mummy had it's pitfalls are elsewhere. The well mentioned st player knowledge separation. It's tendency to talk about in world things and never following up on them like the Scroll of Ages, Cosmic keyword, Sekhem Sorcery, etc.<br /> <br /> Some of the above was mechanical in addition to being setting retalization failures. But even beyond them there were mechanical issues. Vice and Virtue from 1e fit Mummy extremely poorly. Memory being both it's own thing and a morality stat. The power of Affinities and Utterances fluxated wildly with a few having three straight tiers of &quot;Why ever take this.&quot; etc. Even Decieved which continued the corebook and Guildhall's fantastic flavour work for things like Utterances and Affinities had a few. Or in some cases had things like Affinities that looked like something that should have been core utility effects for all mummies that were cut for space from the core. And I'd still argue an incredibly restrictive fuel stat in Pillars that gets spread far too thin regardless of if you are newly awake or about to sleep. And even where we see potent powers done in a relatively satisfying way<br /> It tends to highlight even more so where it trips up. In my experience this can lead to players feeling like things are xp sinks and traps.<br /> <br /> 2e is bringing some amazing things but where it is tripping over itself it feels like it's following in the footsteps of where 1e did.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would ever so slightly disagree on the variance in Affinities and Utterances. There were a couple of Utterances I would never use, but in the context of Chronicles of Darkness games, 1e and 2e alike, that number was honestly perishingly low. Mummy 1e did an excellent job of balancing its grand powers I think, making very nearly every Utterance a compelling choice. Affinities were more hit and miss, but still erring towards the solid I thought.<br /> <br /> But yes, I agree that where 2e appears to be going wrong is that it is mostly reproducing the more niggly problems from 1e, and compounding that by having perishingly few new ideas of its own. I have a player from my Mummy game who has been pretty excited to hear about the new character creation options in 2e, and I... honestly feel like I have to tell them that they could frankly be better off building a character with the 1e Corebook. You get more Utterances to choose from (let alone once expansions get factored in), some of them are honestly stronger than their new versions.<br /> <br /> It gets worse from a meta perspective. In 1e, where the other splats were tamer, Arisen felt <i>dramatically</i> more impressive than they do in 2e. I'm looking at what a Sekhem 10 Arisen can do upon waking and generally feeling like a new Werewolf or Promethean character could be built to cover most of the same bases. Sure, they won't be throwing meteors or summoning Earthquakes, but those are just two powers on the list and what if you don't want &quot;city wide destruction&quot; to be the only selling point of your splat?<br /> <br /> This is a random tangent, but are we meant to be impressed by the meteors from Secrets Ripped From Skies doing Sekhem in Aggravated damage to structures? Won't buildings typically have well into the double digits in Structure? I can't help but feel like this number would need to be a great deal higher to actually level a building.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T18:27:02-08:00","id":1348379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348376#post1348376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would ever so slightly disagree on the variance in Affinities and Utterances. There were a couple of Utterances I would never use, but in the context of Chronicles of Darkness games, 1e and 2e alike, that number was honestly perishingly low. Mummy 1e did an excellent job of balancing its grand powers I think, making very nearly every Utterance a compelling choice. Affinities were more hit and miss, but still erring towards the solid I thought.<br /> <br /> But yes, I agree that where 2e appears to be going wrong is that it is mostly reproducing the more niggly problems from 1e, and compounding that by having perishingly few new ideas of its own. I have a player from my Mummy game who has been pretty excited to hear about the new character creation options in 2e, and I... honestly feel like I have to tell them that they could frankly be better off building a character with the 1e Corebook. You get more Utterances to choose from (let alone once expansions get factored in), some of them are honestly stronger than their new versions.<br /> <br /> It gets worse from a meta perspective. In 1e, where the other splats were tamer, Arisen felt <i>dramatically</i> more impressive than they do in 2e. I'm looking at what a Sekhem 10 Arisen can do upon waking and generally feeling like a new Werewolf or Promethean character could be built to cover most of the same bases. Sure, they won't be throwing meteors or summoning Earthquakes, but those are just two powers on the list and what if you don't want &quot;city wide destruction&quot; to be the only selling point of your splat?<br /> <br /> This is a random tangent, but are we meant to be impressed by the meteors from Secrets Ripped From Skies doing Sekhem in Aggravated damage to structures? Won't buildings typically have well into the double digits in Structure? I can't help but feel like this number would need to be a great deal higher to actually level a building.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Utterances need a buff; Arisen are all gods, not just war gods. Whatever they are called to do, they should be effective at.<br /> <br /> That being said, a single gander at the Appendix tells me that most of the new ideas are to do with the Cult itself; all mummies are fundamentally leaders of men, hence why they all know Dreams of Dead Gods. I like that thematic; in the character archetype, they're the pet class, their power comes from their ability to augment and serve as force multipliers with their followers. I'm going to spit in the eye of Kenemti here and say that's a really good thing; mummies are fundamentally creatures of civilization and the vessel of human faith, and the most lonesome Arisen still has a corps of trusted followers; there are no Unbound mummies. But the game is only partly about cults; you are their god, you should feel like them. So, go a little more wild with the powers, the rest of the setting has.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 11-13-2019, 09:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T18:30:36-08:00","id":1348382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348379#post1348379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. Utterances need a buff; Arisen are all gods, not just war gods. Whatever they are called to do, they should be effective at.<br /> <br /> That being said, a single gander at the Appendix tells me that most of the new ideas are to do with the Cult itself; all mummies are fundamentally leaders of men, hence why they all know Dreams of Dead Gods. I like that thematic; in the character archetype, they're the pet class, their power comes from their ability to augment and interact with their followers. I'm going to spit in the eye of Kenemti here and say that's a really good thing; mummies are fundamentally creatures of civilization and the vessel of human faith, and the most lonesome Arisen still has a corp of trusted followers; there are no Unbound mummies. But the game is only partly about cults; you are their god, you should feel like them. So, go a little more wild with the powers, the rest of the game has.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I would've really appreciated more powers that focus on empowering their Cultists, honestly...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T18:35:32-08:00","id":1348383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348382#post1348382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I would've really appreciated more powers that focus on empowering their Cultists, honestly...</div> </div> </div> </div>We dunno what being an Inheritor does yet, and we do know that Sadikh can borrow Utterances. That latter bit is not a small thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T18:46:37-08:00","id":1348384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348379#post1348379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. Utterances need a buff; Arisen are all gods, not just war gods. Whatever they are called to do, they should be effective at.<br /> <br /> That being said, a single gander at the Appendix tells me that most of the new ideas are to do with the Cult itself; all mummies are fundamentally leaders of men, hence why they all know Dreams of Dead Gods. I like that thematic; in the character archetype, they're the pet class, their power comes from their ability to augment and serve as force multipliers with their followers. I'm going to spit in the eye of Kenemti here and say that's a really good thing; mummies are fundamentally creatures of civilization and the vessel of human faith, and the most lonesome Arisen still has a corps of trusted followers; there are no Unbound mummies. But the game is only partly about cults; you are their god, you should feel like them. So, go a little more wild with the powers, the rest of the game has.</div> </div> </div> </div>As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar851_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"851\" data-vbnamecard=\"851\">Paradim</a> says, sure, totally cool as a focus, but I would like to see more Utterances that support your Cult. There's just not a lot that feels appropriate to invoke at a cult ceremony, or to bless warriors of the cult before going into battle. One of my favourite 1e Utterances was Guildhalls of the Deathless's Inscriptions Upon Flesh, specific to the Sesha-Hebsu, that could be used to turn your cultists into eagle-headed warriors with Physical attributes through the roof. Awesome stuff, allowing you to make these doctor-ritualists who hang back and let their supernaturally infused cultists take to the field, that 2e hasn't displayed much of.<br /> <br /> I also think it's relevant to note that &quot;pet classes&quot; are harder to make work in Chronicles of Darkness than, say, D&amp;D. Just looking at combat, but I feel like without the visual component of having another model on the field it becomes pretty hard to track whether Cutlist #4 is locked in a melee duel with the Amkhat or taking cover behind the ruins of the old coffee shop, or whether Cultist #2 is dangerously close to the Inferno spilling out from the meteor's impact site. They just become names on a checksheet and bog down combat without really the same aesthetic element that a miniature using game might have (and pet classes in those RPGs are still known for bogging down combat). You end up feeling compelled to shift to Down and Dirty Combat, but for players that enjoy playing out their fights that can feel like a point of failure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T18:48:20-08:00","id":1348385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348383#post1348383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We dunno what being an Inheritor does yet, and we do know that Sadikh can borrow Utterances. That latter bit is not a small thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's true, but I'm talking of support through Affinities. Like... I'm kinda on the fence about Radiant Lifeforce's changes.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh, Sadikh could borrow Affinities or Utterances in 1st Edition as well...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T18:51:09-08:00","id":1348386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348383#post1348383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We dunno what being an Inheritor does yet, and we do know that Sadikh can borrow Utterances. That latter bit is not a small thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly. I considered bringing up the Horse and the Rider Utterance from Rio as another fantastic cult-orientated Utterance from 1e, but left it off because I fully expect elements of it to be incorporated into how Cults work now. I don't think that allowing any Utterance to come from/be used by a cultist under the right circumstances is enough though if the focus is intended to be leading a cult. I'd like to see more powers that explicitly interact with the Cult mechanics, for example, or that augment your followers in some way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T19:03:32-08:00","id":1348389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348376#post1348376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a random tangent, but are we meant to be impressed by the meteors from Secrets Ripped From Skies doing Sekhem in Aggravated damage to structures? Won't buildings typically have well into the double digits in Structure? I can't help but feel like this number would need to be a great deal higher to actually level a building.</div> </div> </div> </div>More importantly, do we need to bother tracking damage to structures? Like, when does that even come up? I think most storytellers would just narrate that the roof is blown off and the walls are sputtering fire, I certainly don't want to track the health of my condo.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>All this talk of Mummy powers being too weak might run too close to splat comparison, I think what we really need to do here is check them against inspirational material. Fortunately, that's an easy pick. So without further ado <b>How do Mummies in 2e match up against Imhotep from the 1999 Universal action film The Mummy</b>?<br /> <br /> <u>FEATS OF IMHOTEP</u>:<br /> <br /> <b>Summon murderous scarabs that burrow into people's brains</b><br /> Check. Mummies can absolutely do this via Right of the Sacred Scarab. They don't eat people <i>quite</i> as quickly as the ones in the movie, but we can forgive leaving out a touch of death effect.<br /> <br /> <b>Endure five men with automatic weapons blowing the shit out of him at point blank range</b><br /> This one requires a touch of math. Lets assume the men in question are working with a well above average 10 dice each (since that makes the math easy). That's about 3 successes a head plus an additional ~2 from rerolled 10s. So 17 damage total, plus the innate weapon damage so that's another 10. Even if Imhotep had 1/0 armor and 10 health levels (drops it to 22) he's looking at a 2 agg rollover. That said, Seal Flesh and Sahu Restoration do cover the 'shaking off overwhelming damage' section fairly well. So our Mummies can do it, but it'll cost them.<br /> <br /> <b>Turn into sand and flow through a keyhole, then into a sand twister, then later into an entire sandstorm with his face</b><br /> Wrathful Desert Power covers the last two precisely, down to the description. Weirdly turning into sand to pass through things wasn't in any of the Affinities, but regardless Mummies can do it.<br /> <br /> <b>Rain blood/frogs/locusts on Cairo</b><br /> Invoking the Tempests Fury. Again, almost exactly from the movie.<br /> <br /> <b>Cause a complete Solar eclipse</b><br /> No. Though this doesn't seem to do much in the film, so I can understand the omission. Still, this definitely falls under &quot;effects that deserve the cosmic keyword&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Drop, like, a thousand meteorites on Cairo</b><br /> Yep, Secrets Ripped From Skies Tier 3 with the kicker does exactly this. Albeit at great cost. A side note why doesn't this have the Cosmic Keyword? Certainly laying waste to Cairo is chronicle altering.<br /> <br /> <b>Turn many if not all of the residents of Cairo into zombie-esque slaves</b><br /> Gift of the Golden Ankh kinda scratches this, as does Awaken the Dead's 2nd Tier, but neither really accomplishes it. There are shades of it Invoking the Tempests Fury's Madness effect, but without a way to direct said madness it's not quite right.<br /> <br /> <b>(Nearly) resurrect the body of his dead lover using a living human vessel</b><br /> Awaken the Dead can do this for a little while. But this is understandably not the domain of Utterances.<br /> <br /> So it turns out you can be a pretty good Imhotep. You'd need most of the Pillars at 4+ and looooots of experiences, but it's totally doable. This has actually been a reassuring experiment.<br /> <br /> <b>Double Edit!: </b>Yay, more Utterances is a stretch goal now!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 11-13-2019, 10:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T19:42:40-08:00","id":1348392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348389#post1348389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More importantly, do we need to bother tracking damage to structures? Like, when does that even come up? I think most storytellers would just narrate that the roof is blown off and the walls are sputtering fire, I certainly don't want to track the health of my condo.</div> </div> </div> </div>For sure. Part of the problem is that we don't have any reasonable guides on what aggravated damage to structures means. Does dealing 6 Aggravated with a Meteor mean that you broke the windows on the cottage, or that the whole cave is caving in? My inclination is a bit towards the former, though the damage being aggravated probably means it's severe damage even if it is only in a localised area. With the way the game approaches buildings having health as a whole, it's just numbers on a track at the height of abstraction. I know that as a GM, I've always done exactly what you described. &quot;You unleashed meteors on the warehouse district? Ok, now you're running through burning streets and dodging collapsing walls.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's a weird extra, particularly in the second edition era right? Isn't this what Environmental Tilts are for? You've got the Inferno Tilt, but something equivalent to a localised Earthquake Tilt as well for those inside a structure hit by a meteorite probably wouldn't go amiss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T20:11:19-08:00","id":1348395,"title":"","content":"New Stretch Goal added <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#282828\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">At $47,000 in funding \u2013 </span></span></span><b>ADDITIONAL</b><b>CONTENT: New</b><b>Utterances.</b><span style=\"color:#282828\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Due to fan demand, Onyx Path will add a dozen new Utterances to the </span></span></span><b>Mummy: The Curse </b><span style=\"color:#282828\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Second Edition core book.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T20:11:49-08:00","id":1348396,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar148_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"148\" data-vbnamecard=\"148\">PenDragon</a> Don't forget that Dreams of Dead Gods is something everyone gets, so you can do the chanting crowds thing with the third tier by casting either Ruin or Grandeur on yourself with it. Depending on if you consider the crowd more Broken or Awestruck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T20:25:56-08:00","id":1348399,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar148_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"148\" data-vbnamecard=\"148\">PenDragon</a> your post referencing common mummy ideas in fiction and then seeing how they can be done in Mummy the Curse is brilliant. It was a fun read. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The whole element that mummies are lords of civilization is a brilliant idea. For all the fact that they seem purely like monsters upon waking up the truth is they are so much more. And it is that more that comes shinning into the night once they get a hold of where they are and what is going on. <br /> <br /> Though as a mortal they were middle managers in the time after becoming a mummy they are now kings!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T20:38:15-08:00","id":1348401,"title":"","content":"I'm really impressed with everything presented so far, honestly, and I don't expect powers to necessarily get a boost from edition to edition when we already have a lot of setting changes too, with time travel and Immortals and Judges to name a few. Plenty of powers in D&amp;D remain pretty much the same from edition to edition and it doesn't hurt the game.<br /> <br /> Basically, I'm a bit surprised people are talking about reducing pledges based on the content of one chapter. Onyx Path have shown they listen to fans and the rest of what we've seen and heard about this game so far has been excellent, so maybe we should exercise some faith?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3241-stannis","name":"Stannis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T20:40:56-08:00","id":1348402,"title":"","content":"<br /> I'm really thrilled to see this finally going forward. I had some comments provided below, and I'm looking forward to the final product. Thank you for all the work that's gone into it so far.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>I\u2019d really like to see a stretch goal that addresses the remaining Judges, perhaps in a supplemental pdf. I\u2019d also be interested in knowing if the reduction to 7 judges in the book was primarily a page limitation decision, or if its\u2019 intended to feed into the premise of the game.</li> <li>A note about pillars in general: I was surprised that pillars retain the same basic mechanics as before. It feels like a missed opportunity to tie their progression character development, particularly in a way that can buoy either memory or power progression (with the consequences inherent in choosing either). I always liked that the 2e version of Renown in W:tF required character development and pillars seem ripe for something similar.</li> <li>Cult is under the Timeless Merit section, but it seems that it could also apply to a cult let be non-immortals, given the right circumstances. There isn\u2019t anything inherent to its benefits that require supernatural immortality.</li> <li>Dead Celebrity \u2013 Elvis has entered the building.</li> <li>Dead Flesh \u2013 it\u2019s an interesting idea, and feels like a gorier version of the 1e use of bandages to reconstitute a dead Arisen. It\u2019s not terribly clear exactly what\u2019s involved, however. Are you literally ripping flesh off corpses and slapping it on your body, replacing missing limbs, or what?</li> <li>Funerary Text \u2013 without most of the mechanics available, it\u2019s hard to assess, though the appendix preview gives some idea of the consequences of the Trials. I look forward to seeing how this interacts with the Descent. It fits a nice theme of Arisen adapting to overcome the limitations of hardships of their existence.</li> <li>Resplendent Soul/Tenacious Eternity \u2013 I like this pattern of a single merit having different benefits for different types of immortals. I\u2019d love to see more of this explored in the stretch goal pdf.</li> <li>Tomb \u2013 the use of the Tomb merit makes sense, but it seems as though it may portend the loss of the greater variety of sacred geometry in CN:Rio.</li> <li>As an organizational note, mixing the general merits with the cult only merits is a bit confusing, and it might make sense to give them their own section.</li> <li>Merits were one of the two strongest parts of this chapter, with a lot of customization opportunities for the Arisen and their menagerie of cultists. I really liked how this was explored, particularly with regard to the options for cults, which leads to\u2026</li> <li>Cults were the best part of this chapter. For a fundamental element of the Arisen existence, these received shamefully short shrift during 1e. Arguably, we knew more about cults among the Deceived than among the Arisen, and this section goes a long way to making these more vibrant and flexible options for play. I\u2019d really love to see a book on designing and running cults at different times and places in history.</li> <li>Cult Archetypes: one thing I\u2019d have like to have seen is a greater variety of archetypes, or the ability to create multiple layers, such as a tribal family that operates through the ownership of major corporation that the members control, with different benefits (or cult initiation characteristics) defined by where in the cult you\u2019re located.</li> <li>It seems as though dots applied through the cult merit should be able to purchase cult merits, in lieu of increasing Reach or Grasp. This would be especially useful in the context of a shared cult.</li> <li>Recovering Pillars: pillaging a vestige feels like it should be more rewarding. One point per dot (and unrenewable at that) seems excessively limiting, given that vestiges presumably play a role in the lifeweb.</li> <li>Physical Attribute Boost: As a point of clarification, are you boosting all physical attributes with one pillar, or one attribute per pillar spent?</li> <li>Utterances and Affinities: I\u2019ll echo some of the other sentiments shared here regarding the underwhelming nature of these sections. I like some of the changes put in place for several of these, including the Power of Re and Sacred Scarab, but several others felt like missed opportunities. With a large number of affinities and utterances missing (Night Creature is a personal favorite), I would feel better if I had some reason to expect future supplements that will fill in the gap. 1E had some great supplements, but not a huge number of them. Perhaps this is something that could be included as a stretch goal?</li> <li>Specifically to Affinities, you list prerequisites for the various soul affinities as \u201cPillar 1\u201d. This seems unnecessary, given that they\u2019re all one. Organizationally, have you considered separating them into sections of affinities associated by pillar, it would save a bit on word count without losing any information.</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2096-willywonka","name":"willywonka","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T21:05:33-08:00","id":1348403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stannis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348401#post1348401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, I'm a bit surprised people are talking about reducing pledges based on the content of one chapter. Onyx Path have shown they listen to fans and the rest of what we've seen and heard about this game so far has been excellent, so maybe we should exercise some faith?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm with you here, but at the same time &quot;shockingly conservative&quot; has been the refrain re: most of the powers in relation to 1e for a reason.<br /> <br /> I can certainly understand that, for example, if there isn't sufficient wordcount to include adaptation of the ghost-related Utterances in the corebook then there certainly isn't room to wax quite as poetic as 1e did with the descriptions of Affinities and Utterances, but at the moment my enthusiasm for Mummy 2e is more pinned on what looks to be strong core ideas and interesting new content than seeing much of the powers from 1e carry over largely free of changes that might reflect those refinements.<br /> <br /> I've little doubt the edition's new take on timelessness and the intercession of the Judges will capture my imagination, but Affinities are still mostly just <i>there</i>, in contrast to other Second Editions' more engaged twists on their predecessors' main powersets; Utterances being learned through Investigation and having a descriptive rather than prescriptive relation to Pillars is neat, but as the more starkly metered form of magic available to mummies they're not going to be able to do quite as much of the heavy lifting re: &quot;what magical powers does your mummy have?&quot;<br /> <br /> There <i>has</i> been the distinct impression, from the incidental mentions of various subsystems, that Second Edition is still going to be focusing on the big-picture impact of the Arisen on a setting in less dramatic terms \u2014 temporal weirdness, geomancy, the various tides of civilization that the Guild writeups mention them tracking, etc, but the fact remains that in the immediate sense, there doesn't currently seem to be too much to say about one of the Arisen that you couldn't say about them in First Edition, and that <i>is</i> a problem for drumming up enthusiasm when the last three ChroD gameline Kickstarters have all had a very solid thematic angle to how their power structures relate to what kind of monsters they were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T21:08:38-08:00","id":1348404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>willywonka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348402#post1348402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]Dead Flesh \u2013 it\u2019s an interesting idea, and feels like a gorier version of the 1e use of bandages to reconstitute a dead Arisen. It\u2019s not terribly clear exactly what\u2019s involved, however. Are you literally ripping flesh off corpses and slapping it on your body, replacing missing limbs, or what?</div> </div> </div> </div>Whichever you\u2019d prefer, really. The intent was to get some of the feel of the Dead levels from 1e with this Merit, where the mummy could have their pieces wrapped or stapled back into place to help with resurrection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T21:28:54-08:00","id":1348405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348404#post1348404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Whichever you\u2019d prefer, really. The intent was to get some of the feel of the Dead levels from 1e with this Merit, where the mummy could have their pieces wrapped or stapled back into place to help with resurrection.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Note to self: Have an Arisen expecting to go into battle become fascinated with a staple gun and bring it with them.<br /> <br /> Cultist: &quot;My lord! Do you need aid?!&quot;<br /> *chunkchunkchunk*<br /> Arisen: &quot;This tool serves me well.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T21:38:48-08:00","id":1348406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stannis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348401#post1348401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really impressed with everything presented so far, honestly, and I don't expect powers to necessarily get a boost from edition to edition when we already have a lot of setting changes too, with time travel and Immortals and Judges to name a few. Plenty of powers in D&amp;D remain pretty much the same from edition to edition and it doesn't hurt the game.<br /> <br /> Basically, I'm a bit surprised people are talking about reducing pledges based on the content of one chapter. Onyx Path have shown they listen to fans and the rest of what we've seen and heard about this game so far has been excellent, so maybe we should exercise some faith?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a few other niggles that are bothering me outside this chapter, but I should note that the chapter on character mechanics is from my perspective the most important chapter in any roleplaying game. I can always invent my own lore and setting. I can always just write my own story too, if it comes to that. What makes this a <i>game</i> is the presence of my players, and what defines the scope of the game is what those players can do.<br /> <br /> It is a seriously big blow to me that 1e actually has <i>more</i> player focussed content than 2e. Sure, tons of cool new setting ideas, but I'm going to be coming at this with a group of players who have played Mummy before and at the moment if asked the question &quot;Well what can we do now that we couldn't do before?&quot; I... I don't know that I have an answer? Nonlinear time is the main hook, but I'm still waiting to see the precise mechanics of that because I have very serious concerns for how it interacts with player agency, and ultimately it's still kind of just setting stuff. I could run a 1e game worked around the ideas presented in 2e (Sothis Ascends even had ideas on nonlinear time so even that isn't wholly new) and give my players more options of what to do with their characters. The fact that there are numerically fewer options wouldn't even be so much of a bother if those options that remain weren't primarily similar to or even just direct transfers of 1e powers.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, at the table, there is only one GM. Everyone else is a player, and this Chapter is the most important because it will be the vehicle through which the majority of people will experience the game. And if it's weaker than 1e's equivalent, just giving fewer options and being less compelling outside of a few choice Merits, that is probably the biggest stumble a new edition could make. Mechanics interlock with the narrative of a game on a fundamental level, they are the setting and story in a game, so all the amazing ideas in Minor Guilds and time travel and expanding on the Judges really don't amount to much if they come at the cost of what players can do.<br /> <br /> I have not reduced or rescinded my pledge, for what it's worth. But I am worried. This is my favourite RPG, bar none, but I'm struggling to see how I could excite my group of Mummy veterans who have literally seen most of what this chapter has to offer before, and that's definitely damaging my own excitement. I definitely understand people being turned off by this. Kickstarter is already a leap of faith, and Onyx Path is great for the transparency they provide through these drafts. It's like a safety net of sorts... but that safety net works by telling backers that this game might not be for them, and if that's the impression they get then rescinding their pledges is absolutely the right call.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T00:00:05-08:00","id":1348422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348295#post1348295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a deal breaker for me personally, but I'm a bit disappointed that it's included when another dev (who wrote for MtC 1e but not for MtC 2e) pointed out shifting target numbers as one of the mechanical failings of the game, and it's just going to be so messy combining it with other dice tricks, especially in roll-heavy groups like mine.<br /> <br /> It is, however, a deal breaker for my group. They're all oWoD veterans and never ended up playing MtC 1e because of shifting target numbers because of their experiences with oWoD difficulty. Now they're no longer interested in backing the book and I'll probably never end up playing it. So I guess it becomes a deal breaker for me too, in that regard.<br /> <br /> <i>If</i> shifting target numbers are removed, I would very much want the decision to be posted before the KS ends.<br /> <br /> Edit:</div> </div> </div> </div>Oi!<br /> <br /> Kindly don't quote something I said three years ago about 1e, before this edition was started, and make it look like I'm commenting on the new team.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T00:02:36-08:00","id":1348424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you're going to say something at least have the courtesy of addressing them. I think Azahal already put it very well and I've already articulated at length so far of what things I have and have not enjoyed. And why in actual detail beyond a simple &amp;quot;I no like-ie.&amp;quot; It has nothing to do with having or not having faith but with using the apparatus of Kickstarter and the benefits of that and previews to be able to gauge if it is a product a person wants to or does not want to pledge to. And ultimately it's based off an appreciation and complement to many other 2nd edition core books. Those books have set a standard of quality of life improvements,tools for player and storyteller empowerment,etc.<br /> <br /> In particularly,this quote hits on a very important thing. <br /> <br /> It's not really about any sort of artificial splat balance mmo-ish notion or raw power fantasy. It's about how mechanics inform the context of a setting and help to emulate it. And part of the reason we play a particular game and don't play another is due to an emotional investment in the setting and the things within it that appeal to us.There is a long and storied history that is fundamental to what ttrpgs are where mechanical implementations can either enhance or detract from immersion and context in a particular setting. If someone feels that the way a certain game expresses certain things mechanically is actively distracting or detrimental to their enjoyment of the setting, that will probably mean they wont be playing it for much longer. Doesn't mean things wont change, and we've seen so far that people have been very constructive in their assessments, and that is part of the advantage of Kickstarter. So, just let the process work itself and maybe not worry so much about what other people are doing eh.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry I'd didn't realise I wasn't being courteous. <br /> <br /> My feeling is that the upset over a lack of powers for Mummy is premature. This edition has been signposted as containing sorcerers and Immortals and making them playable, which triples the options of playability. They may be variations on mortals, but they make the game more complete to my mind. If this edition were just more mummies with more powers it would feel like a 1.5 edition over a 2nd edition, at least to me. I'm getting shades of D&amp;D5 and V5 from what I'm seeing so far: redirecting the game by cutting away the dross and opening up in a fresh direction.<br /> <br /> In short, I'm excited! It's perfectly fine for others to feel this edition should be more Mummy Mummy Mummy, but I'm glad it's not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3241-stannis","name":"Stannis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T00:15:51-08:00","id":1348427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's a non sequitur. Ultimately the game is called Mummy, not Sekhem sorcerers, or Blue Book Template immortals. For that matter it's also besides the point because multiple people, myself included have praised that part and talked about why it's an important addition(sekhem sorcerers in particularly) because it was something that was lacking for a very long time in 1e. That however is not any argument about why multiple people have been iffy about the preview.<br /> <br /> See the above, that has nothing to do with people's misgivings, and it's not even clear what that actually means.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If you're going to intentionally mis-characterize people's statements then there is no reason to discuss things further.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm really sorry. I'm not trying to mis-characterizs anything. My point is I don't feel the game is any weaker for having fewer Mummy powers or even due to their adjustments. If anything, I think Mummy + viable cultists is a much richer game. Different tastes!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3241-stannis","name":"Stannis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T00:31:05-08:00","id":1348429,"title":"","content":"Well, only $2k shy of new Utterances. That's some good support there!<br /> <br /> Curious when we will see them though!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T00:33:24-08:00","id":1348431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348429#post1348429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, only $2k shy of new Utterances. That's some good support there!<br /> <br /> Curious when we will see them though!</div> </div> </div> </div>We'll start writing them as soon as we hit the goal, so probably as backer updates after the Kickstarter concludes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T00:51:22-08:00","id":1348433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stannis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348427#post1348427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm really sorry. I'm not trying to mis-characterizs anything. My point is I don't feel the game is any weaker for having fewer Mummy powers or even due to their adjustments. If anything, I think Mummy + viable cultists is a much richer game. Different tastes!</div> </div> </div> </div>How I view it... Is that the Arisen are the star of this show. Now, every star needs a strong supporting cast, and because of that, I'm happy to see new inclusions. But if the star of the show isn't actualized because of cut space for new material? Then everything falls apart. If the Arisen aren't awesome (original meaning of the word, inspiring of awe, that is admiration, reverence and fear), then what is the point of making Mummy: The Curse?<br /> <br /> Consider that there is an entire major Guild that has a theme of being necromancers. The contrast as to how much support the material provides an entire Guild's worth of characters between 1st Edition and 2nd Edition is looking kinda stark.<br /> <br /> Now... I think the reasoning is that including those kinds of powers necessitates having the structural support of having Ghosts in the rules and that eats up even more word count. And I see that, yes, it does. Now, sure, second-guessing... hind-sight is 20/20... easier to arm-chair or backseat drive... Whatever, so take this with a grain of salt, sure. I'm kinda come to think that maybe a virtue should have been made of needing rules for Ghosts for better supporting necromancers, and make ghost-like entities that are more of a viable antagonist that make use of those rules, so less word count is needed for other engaging antagonists, as well as showcasing Arisen seeing ghosts as cultists too (I really do like the idea of an Affinity or Utterance that lets Cultists who die, come back as ghosts in your service), so you hit the points of Ally/Enemy that help provide that robust supporting cast for your stories.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, I haven't mentioned anything about changing my pledge either, for a couple of reasons. I want to see where this goes. We haven't seen the entire manuscript yet, and maybe there are things that really do deserve significant word count... My best guess on what this might be is the Trials of Duat thing we've seen mentioned several times now, which seems like an actual mechanic that gets engaged in between Deaths and Descents. You usually need to see the work as an entirety for things to click. ...the other reason is that I'm just at the PDF pledge because that's all I can really afford ^^; I don't want to take away what meager support I can provide. I'll be honest, I can't really see what the developer could even DO that would get me to remove my pledge. ...Mr. Dawkins, please sir, don't take that as a challenge... x.x","signature":"","edited":{"userid":851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","user":"Paradim","date":". 11-14-2019, 04:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T03:18:33-08:00","id":1348447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348422#post1348422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oi!<br /> <br /> Kindly don't quote something I said three years ago about 1e, before this edition was started, and make it look like I'm commenting on the new team.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't. I quoted you on the mechanics of the first edition, expressing disappointment that they returned in second edition. If anyone thinks you commented on the team that works on 2e, then they've both misread the topic and the edition. I also specified which editions you worked on or not as to prevent other misunderstandings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 11-14-2019, 06:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T04:48:36-08:00","id":1348457,"title":"","content":"The latest backer update is encouraging at least, though I hope some attention is paid to the Affinities as well as Utterances. They feel just as problematic on the &quot;same as 1e, but with fewer options&quot; front.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T05:11:29-08:00","id":1348461,"title":"","content":"That is good news.<br /> <br /> Either way, everything else is still really cool and promising so I\u2019m confident everything will be A-okay!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T05:21:28-08:00","id":1348462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348447#post1348447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't. I quoted you on the mechanics of the first edition, expressing disappointment that they returned in second edition. If anyone thinks you commented on the team that works on 2e, then they've both misread the topic and the edition. I also specified which editions you worked on or not as to prevent other misunderstandings.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point is that, while he\u2019s been a cherished vocal and engaged member of this forum community, Dave isn\u2019t the end all, be all representative of Onyx Path\u2019s writers and developers, and his opinions, while admittedly based on many years of experience, aren\u2019t axiomatic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T05:40:14-08:00","id":1348469,"title":"","content":"Agreed! Though Dry as he can be while on podcasts at times( no offense Dave, I\u2019ve just fallen asleep a couple times listening to you explain the premises of a couple game lines xD. That said, i think it was more of a relaxed ASMR thing instead of boredom), he\u2019s not one to really throw shade on people or throw them under the bus for mechanical issues.<br /> <br /> But I understand where Tessie is coming from, it\u2019s just not something that seems to be applicable now. <br /> <br /> Personally, I like the target number manipulation thing, but neither here nor there xD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T06:03:44-08:00","id":1348473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348431#post1348431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We'll start writing them as soon as we hit the goal, so probably as backer updates after the Kickstarter concludes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you good sir! Looking forward to more good work from your team <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T08:13:43-08:00","id":1348481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348433#post1348433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How I view it... Is that the Arisen are the star of this show. Now, every star needs a strong supporting cast, and because of that, I'm happy to see new inclusions. But if the star of the show isn't actualized because of cut space for new material? Then everything falls apart. If the Arisen aren't awesome (original meaning of the word, inspiring of awe, that is admiration, reverence and fear), then what is the point of making Mummy: The Curse?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So, does that make The Contagion Chronicles the <i>Friends </i>of the CofD?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T08:14:06-08:00","id":1348482,"title":"","content":"Mummies strike me as very good at causing an apocalypse, if they want to be murderously destructive towards the civilian populace (not really the kind of PC I want to have in my chronicle), but they don't have much packing oomph in a fight in any kind of timely fashion. Contrast this with beasts, deviants and changelings, who can just... melt everybody with environmental tilts if they want, but they have actual combat powers they can use 1v1.<br /> <br /> Beast has a nice system where you can impose environmental tilts on an area, usually without a roll. This can kill most encounters by itself. Then you can use an Obcasus rite to extend the effects to the city (with an advanced Obcasus Rite), or to a region (Kingdom of Nightmares). This feels like an ideal model for the more general sort of tier 1, tier 2, tier 3 effects of calling down apocalyptic temper tantrums on a region, though for beasts, its more aimed at preventing escape than killing everyone.<br /> <br /> Beasts also have a system where you have very small power pools, and can expend them fast and in a fury if you absolutely need to defeat an opponent; while you still have a lot of powers open to you. For mummies, its less that they can expend their power pools fast to deal with foes well and more that that's about all they have as an option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T08:20:21-08:00","id":1348483,"title":"","content":"I think the lack small scale offensive powers might be to encourage support and use of the mummy's cult<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T09:16:10-08:00","id":1348491,"title":"","content":"Another data point for feedback - my group is a lot like Tessie's, in that target number manipulation is a hard no for us.<br /> It's certainly true that it makes Mummies distinct, that point is definitely not in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T10:15:08-08:00","id":1348508,"title":"","content":"See, this is why a sidebar of &quot;Don't like Target Number changes? Use this instead.&quot; wouldn't be bad","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T10:56:53-08:00","id":1348525,"title":"","content":"Since there's only a few powers with the variable target numbers, and so many people have complained, I wouldn't be surprised if the mechanic never makes it to the final draft.<br /> <br /> While I, too, don't like it, I also believe the reaction to the mechanic is sometimes a little over the top. It's only referenced in about three powers, and nothing fundamental to the splat like Descent, Memory, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T11:35:34-08:00","id":1348528,"title":"","content":"I posted this on the kickstarter but I wanted to share the thought. - <span style=\"color:#282828\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Soooo does a mummy interrupted in his tomb automatic have to go all death spiral on the people or can he go 'I am now your master bow before my majesty!&quot; Because I think the idea of taking the tomb robbers and making them say the core of the descent's cult a very interesting idea.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T11:35:44-08:00","id":1348529,"title":"","content":"I'd contend that the mechanic's very limited presence is precisely <i>why</i> it either needs to be removed, or spread across the game <i>more</i>. Four Affinities and one singular Condition is... really not a lot, to the point it raises the question of why it was carried forward in such a diminished capacity in the first place, but <i>that in turn</i> raises the question of whether it &quot;ought&quot; to be broadened or completely stripped out. My vote's for &quot;remove&quot; purely since it'd be easier to retool those five bits than to rework an uncertain additional quantity and potentially see it wedged in awkwardly where it might not work, but it ain't my call.<br /> <br /> We'll see what happens with the retooled and new Utterances when they're ready to be discussed. I'm cautiously optimistic at least... particularly if some of the &quot;new&quot; ones (but certainly not all, nor even necessarily most) bring forward some of the missing highlights from the 1e list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T11:53:13-08:00","id":1348534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348525#post1348525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since there's only a few powers with the variable target numbers, and so many people have complained, I wouldn't be surprised if the mechanic never makes it to the final draft.<br /> <br /> While I, too, don't like it, I also believe the reaction to the mechanic is sometimes a little over the top. It's only referenced in about three powers, and nothing fundamental to the splat like Descent, Memory, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hear Hear. Let's not forget the fantastic first two chapters, and every other good bit of the character creation chapter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T17:22:43-08:00","id":1348583,"title":"","content":"So this was posted on the Mummy the Curse thread on the Rpg.net forums<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"color:#9F6FCD\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?goto/post&amp;id=22937120\" target=\"_blank\">Evil Midnight Lurker said:</a></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">...so is it viable for the group to awaken for the first time in the modern day, run afoul of an ancient conspiracy that aims to destroy everything the guilds stand for, and as they experience awakening after awakening across time -- encountering and struggling against this conspiracy at every turn, learning more about them, eventually coming to wonder who the real villains are...<br /> <br /> ...and finally discover that their own eventual selves, in the deep past, <i>are</i> the conspiracy?</span><br /> </div><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">@Leliel If you've done it right, the reaction, both IC and OOC is:</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">&quot;Dude! We're </span></span></span><i>awesome </i><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">in the future! Our future! Their past! Whatever, let's just send some tips back through the time portal and buy up Memory so we don't have to be lost next time.&quot;</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>I am posting it here because of HOW AWESOME the idea is to me. I mean damn, can you imagine the fun in said scenario as the players and the ST all begin meeting up in events. That's so cool.<br /> <br /> Non-linear time is gonna be EPIC!!!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T17:51:47-08:00","id":1348589,"title":"","content":"As a note, going over the manusacrift appendix and I noticed Memory Bleed. That is an awesome and PERFECT way to represent something like the soul transformation upon taking the body of a cultist or something else. It totally could aid in explaining why a mummy identifies more with say the modern world then that of lost Irem. <br /> <br /> I point it out because I love finding little nuggets like this that give me mechanical oomph to something that I had randomly thought about while reading the other available chapters. <br /> <br /> Same thing with the awe conditions. They totally fit with the whole concept of a mummy overwhelming someone with his sheer presence and making them submissive as a result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T20:52:52-08:00","id":1348609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348583#post1348583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So this was posted on the Mummy the Curse thread on the Rpg.net forums<br /> <br /> I am posting it here because of HOW AWESOME the idea is to me. I mean damn, can you imagine the fun in said scenario as the players and the ST all begin meeting up in events. That's so cool.<br /> <br /> Non-linear time is gonna be EPIC!!!!!</div> </div> </div> </div>This is absolutely something that can happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T04:57:42-08:00","id":1348645,"title":"","content":"So, we got a gander at Cult rules today on the Kickstarter, and - well, I didn't expect emanations to show up so readily.<br /> <br /> Don't know why I didn't, but that one rule about &quot;no second chances before meeting with the boss&quot; really hammers in just how willing the Judges are willing to yank on the leash - and why Wayward Cult is such an attractive Merit, because it removes that particular sword hanging over the head of a mummy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T05:19:35-08:00","id":1348647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348645#post1348645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, we got a gander at Cult rules today on the Kickstarter, and - well, I didn't expect emanations to show up so readily.<br /> <br /> Don't know why I didn't, but that one rule about &quot;no second chances before meeting with the boss&quot; really hammers in just how willing the Judges are willing to yank on the leash - and why Wayward Cult is such an attractive Merit, because it removes that particular sword hanging over the head of a mummy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I *think* that's worth some clarification of the text, as I <i>believe</i> the intent is not that any doctrine violation automatically causes a manifestation, but that it always gives the trigger needed if the Judge desires to use it.<br /> <br /> It's the equivalent of giving your murderous boss a loaded handgun. Better hope he's in a good mood.<br /> <br /> I'll query it and make sure I've got the right end of the stick :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T08:30:25-08:00","id":1348672,"title":"","content":"So, just to make sure I have things clear: the mummy's body good through time in a linear fashion: it does in Irem, rises during the first Sothic Turn, returns to the grave, maybe arises again in-between Turns when the Cult summons it or a grave robber disturbs it, arises again during the second Sothic Turn, and so on and so forth. <br /> <br /> But the mummy's consciousness goes through time nonlinearly: after visiting Duat for the first time, it arrives in, say, the Fourth Sothic Turn before returning to Duat and then arising in the Second Sothic Turn, etc. <br /> <br /> So if you show up in the Fourth Sothic Turn in your original body, that means that it survived all the way through history from the fall of Irem, and your subsequent Descents in earlier time periods will all be in your original body?<br /> <br /> Or is it that you don't ever know if it's your original body, and it's always possible that something happened somewhere earlier in the timeline that altered which body you inhabit?<br /> <br /> Is it possible that the process of Arising transforms your body, such that even if you never have to replace it, you can still go through a Descent in a drastically different form than you were in for a chronologically earlier Descent? Something vaguely similar to Doctor Who's Regenerations?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T09:24:35-08:00","id":1348679,"title":"","content":"On the above I honestly think its a bit of both and neither at the same time. I think that while the body itself flows through time in the normal way if the soul does something special then the soul gains primacy. Thanks to the Rite of Return and the power of Sekhem. <br /> <br /> So basically timey whimey and all Doctor Who Regenerations. (By the way the fact that this allows for something like playing out the Doctor's life is really cool. hehe)<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> On an unrelated point, I like how what dot of Sekhem a mummy might arise with may vary based on reason for awakening. That is nifty. <br /> <br /> That said I still wished the first descent had them at Sekhem 1 and that they rose it over time like other groups, especially as the non-linear nature of Mummy existence means that this does actually work to represent super powerful immortal timeless beings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T10:21:50-08:00","id":1348685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348672#post1348672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, just to make sure I have things clear: the mummy's body good through time in a linear fashion: it does in Irem, rises during the first Sothic Turn, returns to the grave, maybe arises again in-between Turns when the Cult summons it or a grave robber disturbs it, arises again during the second Sothic Turn, and so on and so forth. <br /> <br /> But the mummy's consciousness goes through time nonlinearly: after visiting Duat for the first time, it arrives in, say, the Fourth Sothic Turn before returning to Duat and then arising in the Second Sothic Turn, etc. <br /> <br /> So if you show up in the Fourth Sothic Turn in your original body, that means that it survived all the way through history from the fall of Irem, and your subsequent Descents in earlier time periods will all be in your original body?<br /> <br /> Or is it that you don't ever know if it's your original body, and it's always possible that something happened somewhere earlier in the timeline that altered which body you inhabit?<br /> <br /> Is it possible that the process of Arising transforms your body, such that even if you never have to replace it, you can still go through a Descent in a drastically different form than you were in for a chronologically earlier Descent? Something vaguely similar to Doctor Who's Regenerations?</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s complicated, but no, you have that wrong. The mummy\u2019s body and mind go through time non-linearly. The mummy who wakes up for his first Descent in 2019 literally hasn\u2019t been anywhere or when else yet. But from the point of view of more limited creatures who are trapped in time, they may have encountered the mummy in 2005. (Or 1505, for immortals.) This doesn\u2019t mean that the mummy has just been waiting for his body to catch up. <br /> <br /> How to put it another way? Say the mummy in 2019 barely survives a powerful supernatural effect that leaves horrible scars that will slowly fade over his next few Descents. The person he knew in 2005 remembers him being horribly scarred and wonders why the 2019 mummy is unblemished, but then experiences the event alongside the mummy in 2019 where he gets the scars. <br /> <br /> The immortal who knew the mummy in 1505 remembers that he had fading scars back then and wonders why they\u2019re so much worse in 2005. He then wonders how they\u2019re non-existent in 2019 after being so much worse just 14 years ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T10:31:58-08:00","id":1348686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348685#post1348685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It\u2019s complicated, but no, you have that wrong. The mummy\u2019s body and mind go through time non-linearly. The mummy who wakes up for his first Descent in 2019 literally hasn\u2019t been anywhere or when else yet. But from the point of view of more limited creatures who are trapped in time, they may have encountered the mummy in 2005. (Or 1505, for immortals.) This doesn\u2019t mean that the mummy has just been waiting for his body to catch up.<br /> <br /> How to put it another way? Say the mummy in 2019 barely survives a powerful supernatural effect that leaves horrible scars that will slowly fade over his next few Descents. The person he knew in 2005 remembers him being horribly scarred and wonders why the 2019 mummy is unblemished, but then experiences the event alongside the mummy in 2019 where he gets the scars.<br /> <br /> The immortal who knew the mummy in 1505 remembers that he had fading scars back then and wonders why they\u2019re so much worse in 2005. He then wonders how they\u2019re non-existent in 2019 after being so much worse just 14 years ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the point is that any time- dependent effect that is related to the mummy moves &quot;non linearly&quot; with time, but if I were to stay around the mummy from the time of Irem until today, I would just see them wake up every time the stars are right, and from my point of view it would just be as if the mummy serves as an oracle or prophet of some sort, bringing dread prophecies about the future and recalling lost knowledge from the past? Sounds cool. Really in theme.<br /> <br /> In that case, if one were to terminate a mummy's existence (which, as I understand, requires destroying all of its four canopic jars, killing all Inheritors, scattering the cult and burning its body to ash then scattered in the wind), the mummy could still awaken to past events, but can't progress any further than that point of time?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T11:10:34-08:00","id":1348693,"title":"","content":"So there isn't a mummified corpse in a sarcophagus somewhere when they're not in a Descent?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T12:08:21-08:00","id":1348699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348693#post1348693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there isn't a mummified corpse in a sarcophagus somewhere when they're not in a Descent?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually intensely curious about this as well. Because on part there has to be, otherwise being woken up by tomb raiders wouldn't work. <br /> <br /> That said I really like the idea that the body of the mummy is just as non-linear as the mind and soul of the mummy, so that is a nice touch. <br /> <br /> On a personal level I guess one way to think about it is that the corpse in the sarcophagus is just a material thing and only becomes the mummy upon the awakening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T12:28:28-08:00","id":1348701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348699#post1348699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm actually intensely curious about this as well. Because on part there has to be, otherwise being woken up by tomb raiders wouldn't work.</div> </div> </div> </div>And it\u2019s kind of central to the concept of \u201ca mummy\u201d.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said I really like the idea that the body of the mummy is just as non-linear as the mind and soul of the mummy, so that is a nice touch. </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d hate that for the aforementioned reason. There\u2019d be no reason to still call the game \u201cMummy\u201d if they\u2019re physical time hoppers instead of mummified bodies that rise in tombs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T12:55:46-08:00","id":1348711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348685#post1348685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It\u2019s complicated, but no, you have that wrong. The mummy\u2019s body and mind go through time non-linearly. The mummy who wakes up for his first Descent in 2019 literally hasn\u2019t been anywhere or when else yet. But from the point of view of more limited creatures who are trapped in time, they may have encountered the mummy in 2005. (Or 1505, for immortals.) This doesn\u2019t mean that the mummy has just been waiting for his body to catch up. <br /> <br /> How to put it another way? Say the mummy in 2019 barely survives a powerful supernatural effect that leaves horrible scars that will slowly fade over his next few Descents. The person he knew in 2005 remembers him being horribly scarred and wonders why the 2019 mummy is unblemished, but then experiences the event alongside the mummy in 2019 where he gets the scars. <br /> <br /> The immortal who knew the mummy in 1505 remembers that he had fading scars back then and wonders why they\u2019re so much worse in 2005. He then wonders how they\u2019re non-existent in 2019 after being so much worse just 14 years ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>So if your body is destroyed and you have to take a cultist\u2019s body in, let\u2019s say, 1905 - from the perspective of linear time trapped beings, your original mummified corpse throughout its history would sometimes adopt two different sahu when it rises before 1905, depending on whether that event was before said destruction and possession from the mummy\u2019s pov.<br /> <br /> And similarly, linear post-1905 the new dessicated corpse adopts the old sahu when it rises before said event from the mummy\u2019s pov?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T13:05:10-08:00","id":1348713,"title":"","content":"RIP target numbers. I\u2019ll miss you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T13:09:43-08:00","id":1348716,"title":"","content":"This is the way I see it. Your corpse is there, at all times. Without you in it, though, it\u2019s just a mummified corpse. Once you\u2019re in, it becomes the sahu, filling out and shaping it with magic. It is tied much to the mummy\u2019s self image, so it will closely match their original appearance during \u201cearly\u201d Descents. Now, say they incarnate into the body of Roman gladiator cultist (hell, we\u2019ll give the mummy the Resonant Lifetime Merit for good measure). From that point on, the mummy will likely look like the Roman gladiator every time they get up going forward, as the sahu will be shaped that way by the mummy\u2019s soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T13:11:08-08:00","id":1348717,"title":"","content":"This is the sort of thing I was wondering about. As well, when you take someone else's body, whether you're a Deathless whose body was destroyed requiring you take the body of one of your cultists or you're a Body-Hopper (eagerly waiting for Chapter Five, BTW), your physical stats change. That's why I was thinking along the lines of Doctor Who's Regenerations \u2014 though perhaps a better analogy would be a caterpillar's cocoon: there's a body in the bandages, but over the centuries it slowly changes so that each Descent potentially features a different form, whether or not the Arisen's body is destroyed in any given Descent and regardless of what order those Descents take place. <br /> <br /> I think I'd much prefer that to \u201cthe Deathless physically travels to Duat between Descents\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T13:20:16-08:00","id":1348721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348693#post1348693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there isn't a mummified corpse in a sarcophagus somewhere when they're not in a Descent?</div> </div> </div> </div>There usually is, but it\u2019s not really \u2018you\u2019 until \u2018you\u2019 are there. That\u2019s why it\u2019s complicated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T17:46:10-08:00","id":1348760,"title":"","content":"There's a corpse, and it's sorta you but it's a soulless husk connected to the Rite of Return until you're there, and then it's whichever you has arisen from Duat to inhabit it in that moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T22:49:06-08:00","id":1348793,"title":"","content":"Looks like we hit the Stretch Goal for the additional Utterances! And that means we're just nearly $3,000 away from the Book of Lasting Death Stretch Goal! ^.^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T22:57:37-08:00","id":1348794,"title":"","content":"So, seeing the latest update.... It's looking like the shifting target numbers thing to represent Fate is being removed from the game, and they're going to be using Advanced Actions and something new called Blighted Actions to serve the place shifting target numbers were used. Advanced Actions show up in W:tF 2nd Edition, and it lets you roll for an action twice and to take the better result. I presume a Blighted Action will be to roll for the action twice and take the worse result....<br /> <br /> I'm fine with that, honestly. I don't really see how this actually changes anything, how it makes things better or worse or whatever... But I mostly just want consistency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T23:57:32-08:00","id":1348799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if that will end up meaning we'll see those crop up more then. Wasn't something I hated but if expands a mechanic from 2e that will be fun.<br /> <br /> I remain skeptical but we'll see how it all turns out.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'll admit, I'm kind of amused as to how counting a number as a success is somehow a terrible thing, but doubling how many times you roll dice is... better?<br /> <br /> I don't get it, but whatever. I don't really think it matters in the long run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T00:14:43-08:00","id":1348801,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the pushback always felt to me like it was driven by oWoD veterans who didn't quite understand that the mechanic was reserved to specific supernaturally influenced rolls, as opposed to their own memories of it being a universal thing in oWoD.<br /> <br /> Not exactly the biggest problem in the game as it stands that I'd like to see addressed, but the fact that some Fate-related mechanics got changed and others didn't was bothering me. Hopefully they'll be consistent in how this is applied, otherwise I'm already having nightmares about Blessed is the God-King Tier 1 combined with an Advance Action mechanic...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T00:21:36-08:00","id":1348802,"title":"","content":"I think the idea is that Advanced Actions at least have precedent in the current edition (and thus set precedent for Blighted Actions). Whereas uh, target number shifts only have precedent in exactly one gameline - Mummy 1e - and the idea of introducing an entirely new mechanic for precisely four powers and one condition is... kind of weird and arguably unnecessary.<br /> <br /> I'd've been fine with it being around if it got used more, but I guess if that was the line of thought behind the scenes, it was deemed easier to swap in another existing mechanic rather than try to push this one into more Affinities/Utterances/Conditions.<br /> <br /> That, and (while I'm not in the mental space to try and crunch the numbers right now) Advanced/Blighted Actions <i>might or might not</i> have more potential for a bit more statistical impact while still feeling very Fate-Screw-y; lowering/raising target numbers by one isn't <i>nothing, </i>far from it (TN-1 shifts a two-die pool from a 51% success rate to 64% if I'm doing the right thing in my head, and only gets better with more dice), but... yeah. If someone else wants to run the numbers on that and/or correct my groggy maths?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T00:31:48-08:00","id":1348804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348794#post1348794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, seeing the latest update.... It's looking like the shifting target numbers thing to represent Fate is being removed from the game, and they're going to be using Advanced Actions and something new called Blighted Actions to serve the place shifting target numbers were used. Advanced Actions show up in W:tF 2nd Edition, and it lets you roll for an action twice and to take the better result. I presume a Blighted Action will be to roll for the action twice and take the worse result....<br /> <br /> I'm fine with that, honestly. I don't really see how this actually changes anything, how it makes things better or worse or whatever... But I mostly just want consistency.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s actually better, for the chance of success, than shifting the \u201ctarget number\u201d. And better than just adding a die.AAs are somewhere between 8-again and rote, probability-wise, which is why Stew invented them,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T00:41:43-08:00","id":1348805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348804#post1348804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It\u2019s actually better, for the chance of success, than shifting the \u201ctarget number\u201d. And better than just adding a die.AAs are somewhere between 8-again and rote, probability-wise, which is why Stew invented them,</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly, that's irrelevant to me. Having a useful mechanic that is flavorful for it's purpose is what I'm concerned about. I'm not specifically looking for a mechanic that makes it more likely you'll succeed, versus other mechanics that will make it more likely you'll succeed (say adding dice, adding 8-again or 9-again, etc).<br /> <br /> So, from where it was originally as a mechanic designed to represent something specific in the setting.... It's now a mechanic that's available with other games, but also a mechanic that is very similar with Dungeons and Dragons, so it doesn't seem particularly inspiring for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T02:41:28-08:00","id":1348818,"title":"","content":"Fate/fortune/luck/whatever isn't a good reason, in my view, to add a mechanic that changes the way success TNs are counted, because fate/fortune/luck stuff is there in at least vampire (strix), mage, mortal+, changeling, mage, demon, deviant and doubtless others. They all have some grounding to be viewed as special, as well.<br /> <br /> That they get the additional successes and what they do with those successes is what matters, in my view.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T03:18:50-08:00","id":1348823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sconce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348802#post1348802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That, and (while I'm not in the mental space to try and crunch the numbers right now) Advanced/Blighted Actions <i>might or might not</i> have more potential for a bit more statistical impact while still feeling very Fate-Screw-y; lowering/raising target numbers by one isn't <i>nothing, </i>far from it (TN-1 shifts a two-die pool from a 51% success rate to 64% if I'm doing the right thing in my head, and only gets better with more dice), but... yeah. If someone else wants to run the numbers on that and/or correct my groggy maths?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not being a maths and crunch fella my curiosity is mostly along the lines of how drastic of a difference it makes on success or failure. Beyond that I share in not getting it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was actually curious myself, so I spent some time running the numbers (having just spent a bit of time earlier to add Advanced Actions to my WoD/CoD/Exalted 2e general dice probability calculator).<br /> <br /> My assumption here is that there's three things that matter in a dice trick, in descending order of importance. First, how it affects your odds of rolling at least one success (important for succeeding at any action at all), second how it affects your odds of rolling at least five successes to get an Exceptional Success, and finally how it affects your mean successes rolled (important for extended actions, contested rolls, resisted rolls).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/e/2PACX-1vQZdnSdn_mZ_zEec9iQRn7vn4mcw4mWWGV1vu7rP3BPhp9Z_XJXjHhUom986tiU00cL62sGnxRHAx5D/pubhtml\" target=\"_blank\">Here are the results for those three actions, comparing a normal roll, a roll where 7s count as successes (referred to as TN7), and an advanced action roll.</a><br /> <br /> Each sheet has a number of dice from 1 to 20, either the odds of hitting the specified success count, or the mean successes gained from the roll. Further each sheet has the two dice tricks' effective base dice (how many dice you would have to roll without dice tricks to get the same results)/expressed in terms of base dice (so a relative value of 1.4 means &quot;as though having 40% extra base dice&quot;). This analysis assumes no other dice tricks are used).<br /> <br /> Based on that we see the following:<br /> <br /> For 1 success, Advanced Actions give a much better result than TN7 does. TN7 is equivalent to adding approximately 44% dice to your dice pool. Advanced Actions, in the meanwhile, just straight up doubles your dice pool, make it equivalent to the Rote Quality (for this purpose at least).<br /> <br /> For 5 successes, Advanced Action is slightly better at very low dice pools than TN7. However, the advantage of TN7 climbs quickly past that value, doing better from 3-18 dice (thus the vast majority of rolls even for very potent mummies). Finally, at 19 dice and beyond Advanced Action beats out TN7 again.<br /> <br /> For mean successes, Advanced Action initially does better than TN7. However, TN7 benefits from the fact that it gives a very constant return in the extra number of successes (always adding 1/3rd) whereas Advanced Action has sharply diminishing returns (since the more dice, the less likely you are to get a result that's very far from the mean). Starting at 8 dice, TN7 does better than Advanced Action.<br /> <br /> (Personally I am very happy with the removal of Target Number manipulation, since my location ensures I can only ever play online and adding extra flags and additions to dice rollers for a very limited group of things is a hassle and a half).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23896-mirthless","name":"Mirthless","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T05:30:04-08:00","id":1348833,"title":"","content":"I can't say I'm much of a fan for advance actions either, but at least it means my group is far more likely to play the game, and thus that I get to play the game.<br /> <br /> While flavourful mechanics are certainly important to make a game stand out, the by far most important part is that it's <i>fun</i> when playing the game.<br /> X-Again and Rote Action increases the fun by making you reroll specific dice (turning failures into successes, or successes into more successes).<br /> Advance Action is less fun because you reroll your dice pool again (i.e. just feels like more rolling, even if it's in your advantage).<br /> Shifting difficulty means you need to recalibrate your brain to calculate it different from other rolls, and, in combination with how rare it is, is thus much more likely to make you mess up the result.<br /> <br /> Anything that increases the complexity of figuring out the result (which shifting difficulty does more than other dice tricks) without outweighing that drawback by increasing the enjoyment of the game is bad design.<br /> Now whether shifting difficulty is fun to use is subjective. My experience was that most people didn't think so, but this thread leans the other way. Make of that what you will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T05:53:25-08:00","id":1348836,"title":"","content":"I mean, shifting the Target Number is such a small thing (&quot;Hey, for this one roll which I specifically made the choice to use a power on, I should count the 7s as Successes too&quot;) that I really can't believe it's considered any harder than Rote Action's &quot;Roll a set of the dice again&quot;. Neither of them are enormously disruptive, and both of them are active choices engaged in by the player. Arguably rerolling dice takes a bit longer to resolve. And honestly, Advance Action feels like a good bit more mental gymnastics, since you have to actually record your first result and then reroll and calculate the new result while holding the first result in your head to compare and contrast. Still not a large mental load, but surely larger than just remembering to count another number as a success?<br /> <br /> Personally, I think Blessed is the God King Tier 1 has been the biggest loser in the game transition. There was some grandiose about the way it worked in first edition. In the current iteration, if you roll poorly you can choose to reroll a bunch of your dice, and maybe you get lucky this time. In first edition, with it retroactively making 6s and 7s successes, you got to actually see in advance what your new result was going to be. &quot;I've got two successes, but if I trigger this power now it'll make the four sixes and sevens into successes, bringing my total to 6 successes.&quot; That just felt right. It made the result seem <i>inevitable</i>, like Fate had decreed it thus. Compared to Advance Action or Rote, that turns Fate in the Mummy context back into being equivalent to the fortune and luck that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11876\" data-vbnamecard=\"11876\">Deinos</a> equated it to. In First Edition, I never felt like Fate in Mummy had anything to do with Luck. Sometimes, the universe in Mummy simply decreed that something Would Be, and Arisen had the power to influence that decision.<br /> <br /> Of course, only Blessed is the God King of all Mummy's First Edition rules had that retroactive capacity, the rest of the rules applied the modifier beforehand. But I loved watching my players play with that Utterance, it always felt like asserting Fate in action.<br /> <br /> Still, at least it'll be consistent going forward. Target Number manipulation worked in Mummy 1e because there were a large number of powers using it, and any power involved with Fate tended to use it. Second edition has carved out whole Utterances and Affinities that used to manipulate Target Numbers in different ways as part of the whole halving the number of powers thing, reducing the number of Fate-related powers to a pretty small number, and then had the mechanics used amidst that number be inconsistent. At minimum, making the remaining Fate powers consistent will be an improvement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T11:37:41-08:00","id":1348892,"title":"","content":"I like the change. I never cared for shifting target numbers, but I love the idea of Mummies screwing around with probability and Fate. On that front, I'm really happy to see the Advanced Action quality get some love. It was a cool idea from the first edition World of Darkness core that was never,<i> ever </i>used* before 2E <b>Werewolf</b>.<br /> <br /> * Apart from rules reprints in <b>Innocents </b>and <b>Mind's Eye Theatre</b>, a cursory search reveals it was only ever referenced twice, in <b>Mirrors</b> and <b>Spirit Slayers</b>. There's your CofD trivia for the day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 11-16-2019, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T12:02:49-08:00","id":1348896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348805#post1348805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Honestly, that's irrelevant to me. Having a useful mechanic that is flavorful for it's purpose is what I'm concerned about. I'm not specifically looking for a mechanic that makes it more likely you'll succeed, versus other mechanics that will make it more likely you'll succeed (say adding dice, adding 8-again or 9-again, etc).<br /> <br /> So, from where it was originally as a mechanic designed to represent something specific in the setting.... It's now a mechanic that's available with other games, but also a mechanic that is very similar with Dungeons and Dragons, so it doesn't seem particularly inspiring for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is for mechanics to have the desired flavor, they have to actually have the desired consequence in play. TN shift in CoD rules really don\u2019t. So to me it\u2019s the difference between something that sounds interesting and evocative on the page and something that actually carries that out at the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T12:16:00-08:00","id":1348900,"title":"","content":"Speculating on the Utterances we might hope to see...<br /> <br /> I love the degree Mummies are Biblical-Miracle-Monsters, and toward that end I\u2019d love to see<br /> <br /> - Command the Beasts<br /> - Kiss of Apep<br /> - Revelations of Smoke and Flame<br /> - Seeds of Life<br /> - Word of Amanuensis<br /> <br /> make a come back! Seeds of Life could use a conceptual rewrite, focusing on various possible powers with the magic fruit (probably tied to Pillar ratings for options), one of which can be magic human fertility, but that isn\u2019t the sole Tier 3 power.<br /> <br /> Word of Amanuensis could alternately be saved as a Scribe exclusive Utterance.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In terms of original Utterances, one idea I had was a Lunar counterpart to Power of Re. As Khonsu is associated with time, I figure it could bend the locational passage of time. The light from the Utterance could also impact werewolves (since Power of Re can impact vampires).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T12:22:48-08:00","id":1348901,"title":"","content":"I wouldn\u2019t mind seeing some Utterances from Book of the Deceived, but perhaps easing off the Ren prerequisites a tad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T12:37:13-08:00","id":1348903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348901#post1348901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn\u2019t mind seeing some Utterances from Book of the Deceived, but perhaps easing off the Ren prerequisites a tad.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t know how to justify Nomenclature without Ren requirements through the roof - but then I guess with how Pillar requirements now just make Utterances stronger, they could lessen the base powers and make the Ren requirements necessary for the full powered effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T12:46:41-08:00","id":1348907,"title":"","content":"I think it\u2019s been indicated that Guild-the attic Utterances might be a companion stretchgoal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T19:44:21-08:00","id":1348982,"title":"","content":"Looking over the Merits again and there's one... Observance... that says &quot;Cultists participating in these rites gain the Inspired Condition, and add 1 to a cult action attempted within a number of days equal to the Cult's Dominance.&quot; I'm not sure what that &quot;1&quot; being added is.... +1 die, basically? That's my guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T19:54:56-08:00","id":1348985,"title":"","content":"As another question... What does the Resources Merit mean, in regards to a Cult having it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T20:16:53-08:00","id":1348991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1348985#post1348985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As another question... What does the Resources Merit mean, in regards to a Cult having it?</div> </div> </div> </div>It means you may or may not have money of your own, but your cult is potentially loaded and totally down to spend it on... um... luxury linen bandages, or whatever the well-to-do mummy is into these days.<br /> As far as the other goes, I\u2019ll need to look over it again, but +1 sounds like it was probably what was intended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T22:07:25-08:00","id":1349000,"title":"","content":"The Akhem-Urtu are dedicated to the secrets of Nomenclature and overridden by the Ren of their Temakh.<br /> <br /> The Shaukenashen are left with only their Sheut<br /> <br /> <br /> So do the the three new \u201cMinor\u201d Guilds complete the set as Pillar perversions?<br /> <br /> As tomb guardians the Kher-Minu have a clear Ka association.<br /> <br /> So which of the other two are Ba and Ab?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 11-17-2019, 05:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T00:49:55-08:00","id":1349016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349000#post1349000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Akhenaten-Urtu are dedicated to the secrets of Nomenclature and overridden by the Ren of their Temakh.<br /> <br /> The Shaukenashen are Sheut-eatten<br /> <br /> <br /> So do the the three new \u201cMinor\u201d Guilds complete the set as Pillar perversions?<br /> <br /> As tomb guardians the Kher-Minu have a clear Ka association.<br /> <br /> So which of the other two are Ba and Ab?</div> </div> </div> </div>Akhem-Urtu, and the Shuanksen are kind of just eaten-hell, the only thing they might have left <i>is</i> their shadow.<br /> <br /> If the Shuanknhsen were a guild and not a bunch of poor bastards who got the double whammy of being slaves and becoming the gnawed-upon consumers of reality, and the Akhem-Urtu weren't labelled a Minor Guild merely because No One Wants to Remember How Major They Were, it would probably stand to reason that the Minor Guilds were more mirrors of the Major Guilds-but that's not the case.<br /> <br /> Edit: Unrelated, and the point I'm about to comment on was from pages back and therefore not relevant, (And also I'm <i>still</i> reading the first preview, my life has been busy y'all) BUT<br /> <br /> Cosmic does not mean Really Fucking Big, it means This Power Changes The Shape of the Game. The one and only example was an ability that let you travel back and forth in time before 2nd Edition made that the default experience of reality, and thus was the only power in First Edition that let you go and change history as the present experienced it.<br /> <br /> In concept, Cosmic Utterances are akin to Wish in DnD (or, actually, wishes in Chuubo's, that game's casualness with it be damned)-It's a power that allows the player to grab the reins of the setting from the Storyteller and change it to something else within it's confines.<br /> <br /> Now granted, the apocalyptic nature of a lot of Utterances had that potential anyways, but Cosmic took it a whole 'nother step up. It's one thing to level a city, another go back to 551, introduce Mohammed to Rin from Fate, come back to 2012 and discover Islam's been replaced with the Best Girl Reich.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-17-2019, 04:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T01:31:13-08:00","id":1349025,"title":"","content":"Did the Tomb mechanics get moved to where the default template abilities ended up?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T01:34:26-08:00","id":1349027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349000#post1349000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So do the the three new \u201cMinor\u201d Guilds complete the set as Pillar perversions?<br /> <br /> As tomb guardians the Kher-Minu have a clear Ka association.<br /> <br /> So which of the other two are Ba and Ab?</div> </div> </div> </div>Great observation. My guess is that the disease guys will be corrupted Ab.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T14:52:41-08:00","id":1349174,"title":"","content":"Sadikhs appear more resilient to damage that mummies. Is this just a discrepancy between writers or holdover from 1e, or is it intended?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T15:09:41-08:00","id":1349177,"title":"","content":"Is anyone else kinda bothered by the fact that the Judges are mentioned rewarding Memory and taking it away? Offending the Judges causes Memory breaking points, and there have been occasions where it has mentioned the Judges gifting both Memory and Sekhem in the same breath.<br /> <br /> I mentioned this over in reseru's topic, but there's this troubling dilution of the first edition's central themes with respect to slavery and the power of the self. My original concerns there have been somewhat addressed, or at least put on hold, by the statement that the Judges being able to reshuffle your Pillars between descents is apparently a line that will be removed or otherwise clarified, but now instead of the 1e relationship of Memory and Sekhem being relatively opposed stats that push players into a tug-of-war between exploring themselves or advancing the cause of the Judge, now they appear aligned in the same direction with both going up as the Arisen obeys their Judge and falling when they disobey.<br /> <br /> I get that people complained about Memory being used as a morality stat in the first edition (though I never really minded it, the violent behaviours that the Judges kind of implicitly like would drive down your Memory by making you a better servant of the Judges, it kinda worked), but I'm not sure the fix was to throw out that central relationship between Memory and Sekhem. At best it kind of makes one stat feel a bit redundant, since they end up meaning much the same thing.<br /> <br /> There is every chance that this is jumping the gun, and I am waiting to see the preview that actually explores Memory in more detail, but I'm already quite concerned about where second edition is going thematically and this is another change that might seem small on the surface, but has pretty huge ramifications on Mummy's themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T16:56:27-08:00","id":1349202,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Memory Loss: Reflexive action. The act of creating a Sadikh offends the Judges, causing any mummies of Memory 6 or higher to roll their Memory rating as a Breaking Point, to determine if their Memory decreases by a dot.</span></span> </div> </div> </div> There's no explanation of why creating a Sadikh offends the Judges, or how or why it affects Memory. Shouldn't it be straight Sekhem loss or Descent roll with a penalty?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Also </span></span>If a Sadikh dies, a Judge would presumably want the body's Sekhem, and disapprove of resurrection. If a mummy resurrects, a penalty similar to creating the Sadikh should apply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T17:04:03-08:00","id":1349204,"title":"","content":"The idea that some other being can remove the character's memory while they are active in the world is not something that I am a fan of, nor is it something that I would EVER use as a ST. So yes, I am also very much bothered by this. Very bothered. <br /> <br /> Also the idea that the mummy having a servant that can aid him as he goes through time is bad from the judge's perspective is not something I find logical. As the power of the Sadikh entirely depends on the mummy they are bound to there is no threat from them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T17:13:05-08:00","id":1349209,"title":"","content":"I'm not as bothered, I just thought that the Judges controlled mummies' Sekhem, not Memory, so the mechanic didn't make sense to me. I also don't understand why Judges dislike Sadikhs. A happier mummy with more powerful help would seem to be a more effective servant for the Judges (particularly since Sadikhs are current more resilient than mummies).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T17:34:23-08:00","id":1349216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349204#post1349204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea that some other being can remove the character's memory while they are active in the world is not something that I am a fan of, nor is it something that I would EVER use as a ST. So yes, I am also very much bothered by this. Very bothered.<br /> <br /> Also the idea that the mummy having a servant that can aid him as he goes through time is bad from the judge's perspective is not something I find logical. As the power of the Sadikh entirely depends on the mummy they are bound to there is no threat from them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would assume that the reason the Judges don't like Sadikh is because the Sadikh acts as an anchor for the Mummy's memory, making it easier for them to recall aspects of themselves and who they are. In 1e this would bother the Judges, because the Judges didn't like Mummies having Memory and would prefer them to be mindless automatons without personality or recall. In 2e, the implication I get is that the Judges use Memory as a reward for their Mummies, so the lines are a bit more blurred. If anything, a Sadikh is arguably a perpetuation of the same cycles of slavery present in the Arisen, so it should gel well with the Judge's view of the universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T17:41:29-08:00","id":1349218,"title":"","content":"The Judges' controlling or affecting Memory contradicts the material in the preview.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Judges may control a mummy\u2019s Sekhem, but Memory recovery and loss is something only the Arisen are responsible for. Sekhem and Memory are often at odds. Regaining a sense of self sometimes means ignoring or outright disobeying the Judges. Following their orders can lead to actions that a mummy begs to forget. </div> </div> </div>Preview #2, p. 85","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T17:54:48-08:00","id":1349222,"title":"","content":"If having a Sadikh aids in a mummy gaining independence, then yes, I can see how the Judges might frown upon this. I could also see them making it so that by having one the Sekhem rating a mummy wakens up with is one lower than normal, all other things being equal. It affecting Memory is not logical, so that sentence would be ignored. <br /> <br /> The idea that a Mummy can do something, then stop and shudder as their memory is taken while they are standing there sounds incredibly bad to me, like really bad. I could potentially see the process of Duat effecting things but not while they are active and awake. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar618_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"618\" data-vbnamecard=\"618\">branford</a> nice find. I hope that is accurate and the other elements of the Judges effecting memory are oopsies. <br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> I wonder, hope, that at some point we see a Merit which allows a mummy to have an automatic boost to minimum Memory. This could have some flaw (though I personally dislike negatives on merits and will probably ignore most such elements, in both this and in Trinity where I see some have them as well) but in general the idea of automatically waking up with a bit more memory is cool to me. <br /> <br /> Most especially as it is a high Memory character that I would want to play. That low memory sounds un-fun and nasty and is not something I would enjoy. Its the same thing with serving the Judges as a mindless obedient peon or becoming one's own master - unless I see something in the text that makes the service actually enjoyable from a player's perspective it is not something I will focus on. <br /> <br /> BUT all this said so far it sees that Judge actions are very much ST fiat stuff rather than on character sheet limits and bonuses like say Decrees are. Which means its easy for an ST to be like &quot;nope&quot; and not use those elements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T17:56:04-08:00","id":1349223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349218#post1349218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Judges' controlling or affecting Memory contradicts the material in the preview.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Preview #2, p. 85</div> </div> </div> </div>There is this reference in the first preview though, which reads as though the Judges are able to reward loyal Arisen with Memory:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> She will not recognize the Judges\u2019 manipulations overtly, but she will feel an innate pull toward a certain place or certain task, despite being asked something else by her cult. If she obeys her inner voice, she receives Sekhem or Memory, but this will mean neglecting and possibly angering or losing her cult. </div> </div> </div>Preview # 1, page 71.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T18:05:59-08:00","id":1349225,"title":"","content":"The contradictions on whether Judges can affect Memory needs to clarified. I prefer they don't, but want consistency in either scenario.<br /> <br /> The mechanic about a Memory penalty for creating a Sadikh is just once sentence. It shouldn't be too difficult to fix.<br /> <br /> I similarly hope Sadikh don't remain tougher than mummies.<br /> <br /> These issues seem like matters that will hopefully be resolved with some thorough editing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T18:08:37-08:00","id":1349226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349223#post1349223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is this reference in the first preview though, which reads as though the Judges are able to reward loyal Arisen with Memory:</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the thing: that same reading suggests they're able to directly increase a mummy's Sekhem in the field. Does <i>that</i> seem more likely to you than the more prosaic &quot;doing work for the Judges might lead you to find secrets about Irem or your past or future Descents, or opportunities to cannibalize relics&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T18:14:35-08:00","id":1349227,"title":"","content":"Leading a mummy to things that help his Memory as a reward is not the same thing as <i>directly</i> improving or decreasing Memory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T18:30:30-08:00","id":1349233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349227#post1349227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leading a mummy to things that help his Memory as a reward is not the same thing as <i>directly</i> improving or decreasing Memory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Literally one page ago it was acknowledged that we were told the thing about Judges reshuffling Pillars would be clarified \u2014 not changed, <i>clarified</i> \u2014 so you'll have to pardon me if I have more confidence in the idea that a sentence is not expressing the idea it means to convey clearly than that <i>the entire dynamic of how supernatural power works in this game</i> contradicts the previous edition, the rest of the previewed text for the draft of the new edition, and the basic thematic gist of a game where you're immortal and both your power and your identity have a habit of slipping through your fingers like the desert sands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T18:43:41-08:00","id":1349235,"title":"","content":"Even if the Judges don't reward memory directly, the idea of the Judges even encouraging memory gain is still weird to me. Memory is all about attaining a sense of self, and the Judges are all about denying that sense of self to their servants because they just kind of want the Arisen to be tools they can take out and put away as they desire, and a tool that can have a personal objection to being used in a way is a bad tool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T18:49:43-08:00","id":1349238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrBreaksIt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349235#post1349235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if the Judges don't reward memory directly, the idea of the Judges even encouraging memory gain is still weird to me. Memory is all about attaining a sense of self, and the Judges are all about denying that sense of self to their servants because they just kind of want the Arisen to be tools they can take out and put away as they desire, and a tool that can have a personal objection to being used in a way is a bad tool.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Think of it as balancing stick and carrot. The Judges want enough Memory for their slaves to be useful, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T19:16:57-08:00","id":1349241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">My other concern with this preview is the use of Affinities and Utterances by Sadikh. Affinities are not an issue as Willpower is generally the resource there and Deathless seem to many many ways to regain Willpower. However, Pillar pools are tiny, unnecessarily so in my opinion, and now we have ANOTHER thing tugging on that string.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I wonder if it would be more interesting, and fun, to increase the amount of Pillar points a mummy has. I don't know what multiple to use by even twice or three times the dot rating of the Pillar in maximum points could be useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T19:25:52-08:00","id":1349243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349238#post1349238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Think of it as balancing stick and carrot. The Judges want enough Memory for their slaves to be useful, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Memory 0 Arisen is arguably the perfect tool, becoming an automaton beholden to their Judge's wishes.<br /> <br /> On the Pillar front, honestly I'd rather that the powers just be strengthened so that they're seriously worth the Pillar points. Make even Tier 1 Utterances relatively spectacular, and make Affinities strong enough that you don't feel like your abilities are limited if you're out of Pillars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T20:00:54-08:00","id":1349252,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't it be equally productive to just make recovery of Pillar points a little easier rather than increasing the number of points?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T20:23:54-08:00","id":1349256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349243#post1349243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Memory 0 Arisen is arguably the perfect tool, becoming an automaton beholden to their Judge's wishes.<br /> <br /> On the Pillar front, honestly I'd rather that the powers just be strengthened so that they're seriously worth the Pillar points. Make even Tier 1 Utterances relatively spectacular, and make Affinities strong enough that you don't feel like your abilities are limited if you're out of Pillars.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Kinda disagree with that. Not sure Judges want to be micromanaging individual Arisen?<br /> <br /> From a game design perspective, if Memory is something that Judges can manipulate, then there needs to be reason given as to why they don't force Arisen into being automatons. Otherwise, I don't think they should be able to manipulate Memory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T20:35:26-08:00","id":1349258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349256#post1349256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Kinda disagree with that. Not sure Judges want to be micromanaging individual Arisen?<br /> <br /> From a game design perspective, if Memory is something that Judges can manipulate, then there needs to be reason given as to why they don't force Arisen into being automatons. Otherwise, I don't think they should be able to manipulate Memory.</div> </div> </div> </div>We have absolutely no clues one way or the other when it comes to the Judges' views on micromanagement, the subject hasn't been explicitly discussed anywhere I can think of. They do appear to be a good deal more involved in this edition though, with those references to the cacophony of roared instructions that sometimes filter down to Arisen consciousness. And in 1e the fact that Arisen had Memory at all seemed to be considered a troublesome side effect of the Rite (or more accurately a representation of the Will as a fundamental Law of the universe, thanks Sutek), from the Judge's perspective. Those Arisen who degraded their own Memories to the point where they would just mindlessly follow their Purpose to completion were the perfect tools, and we can see that such behaviour is still possible in 2e.<br /> <br /> But yes, to be clear, I vehemently believe Judges have no place messing with Memory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T20:41:08-08:00","id":1349260,"title":"","content":"....I'm thinking about this a little more... And I'm kind of uncomfortable thinking about it now. I'm hoping that this is something that the game clarifies out, because I think it seriously needs the intent spelled out for Storytellers to know how to use appropriately... Because I can see some very inappropriate uses here. While I know that a game can't control what people choose to do with it.... Without up front talk about why things are set up as they are, I can see some bad situations arise. Basically, while mechanics can't stop abuse from happening, mechanics can definitely encourage abusive situations even without meaning to.<br /> <br /> Certain topics really deserve careful attention and consideration, and I see mechanics designed to impact player agency as being one of those topics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T22:35:11-08:00","id":1349284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">My other concern with this preview is the use of Affinities and Utterances by Sadikh. Affinities are not an issue as Willpower is generally the resource there and Deathless seem to many many ways to regain Willpower. However, Pillar pools are tiny, unnecessarily so in my opinion, and now we have ANOTHER thing tugging on that string.</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding is that Sadikh can use Utterences with the Arisen's permission, spending the Arisen's Pillars. So it is either another origin point for an Utterence (if the Arisen is needed somewhere else) or a way to pull off two Utterences using more Pillars than allowed to spend by current Sekhem.<br /> <br /> Not great, but not awful.<br /> <br /> As for Sadikh being more durable, is occurs to me we haven't seen the Arisen's default abilities yet. If the Deathless get the 'all non-magic, non-fire damage is bashing' thing, then they get a lot more of the awe-inspiring toughness coming back that people complained was missing from Sealing the Flesh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T23:07:52-08:00","id":1349288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349284#post1349284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My understanding is that Sadikh can use Utterences with the Arisen's permission, spending the Arisen's Pillars. So it is either another origin point for an Utterence (if the Arisen is needed somewhere else) or a way to pull off two Utterences using more Pillars than allowed to spend by current Sekhem.<br /> <br /> Not great, but not awful.<br /> <br /> As for Sadikh being more durable, is occurs to me we haven't seen the Arisen's default abilities yet. If the Deathless get the 'all non-magic, non-fire damage is bashing' thing, then they get a lot more of the awe-inspiring toughness coming back that people complained was missing from Sealing the Flesh.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Deathless do take damage that way. Unless you have a Relic weapon or a flamethrower, you can shoot them, stab them, slash them, bludgeon them, crush them, chop them, and kick them in the shins and it\u2019s all bashing until you manage to wrap it around into lethal. Their natural regeneration helps hold that off, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T23:11:41-08:00","id":1349289,"title":"","content":"We've already seen the default standard resilience and healing abilities for all mummies, Preview #2, pp. 49 (Seal the Flesh), 85, 91-92.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T23:13:20-08:00","id":1349290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349288#post1349288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Deathless do take damage that way. Unless you have a Relic weapon or a flamethrower, you can shoot them, stab them, slash them, bludgeon them, crush them, chop them, and kick them in the shins and it\u2019s all bashing until you manage to wrap it around into lethal. Their natural regeneration helps hold that off, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. That is good to know. I appreciate the gift of knowledge for my birthday.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T23:25:34-08:00","id":1349291,"title":"","content":"There are differences between Mummy and Sadikh resilience, and my guess is that it's because two different writers wrote the relevant sections.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 Resilient Body: Sadikh convert all damage to bashing damage, except for magical / supernatural attacks, which are treated as lethal. They do not die when their Health track is filled with lethal damage, instead falling into a repose and waking when the mummy next wakes.... </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Damage Sources Mummies don\u2019t take injury in the same way living bodies do. They receive the following changes to basic sources of harm (p. XX): ... \u2022 Mummies suffer bashing damage from firearms, blades, and melee weaponry. \u2022 In addition to basic sources of aggravated damage, mummies suffer aggravated damage from fire and vessels in the form of weaponry </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T01:09:33-08:00","id":1349299,"title":"","content":"Plus, iirc in 1e sadikh were slightly more durable than the arisen itself, though my memory may have faltered between that cycle and this one.<br /> <br /> I do have a question though. Why were Grasp and Reach kept from 1e, rather than updating to the 2e standards followed by Krewes and Conspiracies and such? Granted, it isn't hard to align, as the two match nicely to Power and Finesse, but we lack Resistance. I'm not sure if they're balanced to interact with the other types. It's just weird they took all of the rest of the standard group rules, I wish they used the PFR rules. Especially since I have a major faction that is a mix of mummies, sineaters, necromancers, vampires, and all the undead (the black lantern corps).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T12:10:21-08:00","id":1349394,"title":"","content":"Personally, if I was going to add TN shifting to a ChronD game, rather than saying something like \u201cyou subtract 1 from the target number\u201d or whatever, I\u2019d call it 7-Success and add a description in right under the 9-Again in the rules chapter that says \u201cOn this roll, you also count 7s as successes.\u201d Maybe also include a note that 6-Success includes 7-Success, if you want to modify TNs by 2.<br /> <br /> That seems like it might be simpler to describe it? <br /> <br /> (I apologize if that\u2019s what they did. I haven\u2019t gotten to that section yet.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T06:30:11-08:00","id":1349573,"title":"","content":"The next update is out, and I'm really digging the Vestiges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T06:47:37-08:00","id":1349575,"title":"","content":"This might be for the eventual errata thread, but I've always found it strange how social maneuvering rules outside of the core CoD book don't have the passage on forcing Doors open.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T07:26:25-08:00","id":1349580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349243#post1349243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Memory 0 Arisen is arguably the perfect tool, becoming an automaton beholden to their Judge's wishes.</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole purpose of mummies is to shape human society into forms that replicate Irem, so that their art falls in line with Iremite paradigms. They cannot do that as undead Terminators.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T07:29:25-08:00","id":1349582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349573#post1349573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The next update is out, and I'm really digging the Vestiges.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite. I really dig how every vessel is linked to powerful memories now. They can be happy, or they can be tragedies, or nightmares (I don't think anyone who sees the Stalker's Knife as something that only has positive use as fuel is begrudged), but yeah. Sekhem is born from people and follows people. Also, love the fact an Eternal's soul relic always contains the memory of their death. Very lich-like, very Dorian Grey, while remaining firmly morally neutral (it is literally not their soul or life in there, just their delayed mortality, and it ages because of that).<br /> <br /> Digging how Inheritors get Decree benefits, and how Cults work.<br /> <br /> EDIT: When I get a chance, I'm starting up the Geistblatt (the Whispering Blade) from Reliquary as a Regia or Amulet (not sure which) that enhances combat skills and tactical ability at the cost of having the blade try to replace your Aspirations with it's own pacifistic agenda. What makes it so valuable is that the Geistblatt is intelligent enough to work with people who already want to end fights; people who can stand its distracting whispering and already wanted to end a war often don't notice the difference, and so it's got a situationally weaker curse for a vessel of its use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 11-19-2019, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T07:37:43-08:00","id":1349583,"title":"","content":"Also as somebody who's obsessed with frogs I'm so happy to see a frog Relic <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T07:45:53-08:00","id":1349586,"title":"","content":"Cults and tombs are cool. I can see fun potential in both. <br /> <br /> Vestiges and relics are very cool. I like how its blatently called out that a) Sorcerers create relics and b) the Arisen specifically can't because of the bounds to a Judge. So yeah good stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T08:19:09-08:00","id":1349593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349583#post1349583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also as somebody who's obsessed with frogs I'm so happy to see a frog Relic <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I, too, like frogs. And this Relic was one of the reasons I was so happy to keep the Psychokinesis Merit in the book. I can say that now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T08:27:11-08:00","id":1349594,"title":"","content":"I'm a little unclear on what the Mortal Decree portion of the Rite of Investment does; does it grant the Decree's unique Affinity? a Favored Attribute dot? both?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T11:16:43-08:00","id":1349631,"title":"","content":"I assumed it gave the mortal a way to recover their Pillar point if they spend it.<br /> <br /> Speaking of that, being able to use cultists as Pillar point batteries is great. It makes them a slightly less scarce resource at the &quot;cost&quot; of getting you more involved with your cult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T12:47:40-08:00","id":1349650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349580#post1349580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The whole purpose of mummies is to shape human society into forms that replicate Irem, so that their art falls in line with Iremite paradigms. They cannot do that as undead Terminators.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd beg to differ, but we're getting into Assassin's Creed-esque &quot;the right meteor at the right time could shape the course of human civilisation&quot; hypotheticals and they're probably a tad specific for this conversation.<br /> <br /> Suffice to say, the concept of the Judges wanting their servants to rediscover Memory and their sense of self feels like a strange direction to go in for Mummy thematically, at least for me, and let's leave it at that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T13:00:31-08:00","id":1349652,"title":"","content":"Power: Returning a Vessel to the Judges releases its curse out into the world. Mummies who hope their work will protect people from Sorcerous doom are toiling in vain. This beautiful bleakness I just what I hoped for.<br /> <br /> Curse: While the importance of recovering Vessels is repeated within the book, this piece of information is easily missed. Many juicy tidbits are scattered around the bulk of the text, requiring a reader to do a diligent read-through. Potential buyers flipping through the book might miss important points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":7593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","user":"Teatime","date":". 11-19-2019, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T13:22:09-08:00","id":1349662,"title":"","content":"&quot;MY MASTER AWAKENED MEEEE!!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T13:24:44-08:00","id":1349664,"title":"","content":"In the Pyramid section on cultists in chapter 2, the Sorcerer entry says &quot;Once a mortal has learned the sorcerous rites of controlling Sekhem, they become better able to channel a mummy\u2019s soul, <b>and further empower the Guild Affinities of the Arisen</b> (see p. XX).&quot;<br /> <br /> I can't find anything in the Guild Affinities rules that makes reference to this. Unless Mortals with only one pillar invested don't count as Inheritors I don't see what advantages Sorcerers provide in regards to Guild Affinities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T14:23:28-08:00","id":1349687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349650#post1349650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd beg to differ, but we're getting into Assassin's Creed-esque &amp;quot;the right meteor at the right time could shape the course of human civilisation&amp;quot; hypotheticals and they're probably a tad specific for this conversation.<br /> <br /> Suffice to say, the concept of the Judges wanting their servants to rediscover Memory and their sense of self feels like a strange direction to go in for Mummy thematically, at least for me, and let's leave it at that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to agree: what would make more sense in my opinion would be if Memory is something the Judges didn't anticipate, and would eliminate if they could. <br /> <br /> Which reminds me: I haven't seen any mention of Apotheosis so far in 2e. Has it been removed from the game? I ask because the new nonlinear nature of time for the Deathless leads to some severe difficulties in this regard: if Apotheosis is possible, and is discovered by the Arisen in his first Descent in 2019, but isn't achieved until his final Descent in 2371 BCE, what happens in 910 BCE? (The connection is that Apotheosis is fundamentally rooted in Memory, which appears to be more of a \u201chow much Independence from the Judges have I achieved?\u201d trait.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T14:32:41-08:00","id":1349690,"title":"","content":"I, too would <i>really</i> love some clarification about how the concept of nonlinear time works with a mummy's Finale Death, falling into Shuankhsen or achieving Apotheosis. Each represents some sort of an &quot;end point&quot; for the Arisen's existence, and understanding how they work in the frame of nonlinear time feels kinda important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T14:51:03-08:00","id":1349693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349687#post1349687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I tend to agree: what would make more sense in my opinion would be if Memory is something the Judges didn't anticipate, and would eliminate if they could.<br /> <br /> Which reminds me: I haven't seen any mention of Apotheosis so far in 2e. Has it been removed from the game? I ask because the new nonlinear nature of time for the Deathless leads to some severe difficulties in this regard: if Apotheosis is possible, and is discovered by the Arisen in his first Descent in 2019, but isn't achieved until his final Descent in 2371 BCE, what happens in 910 BCE? (The connection is that Apotheosis is fundamentally rooted in Memory, which appears to be more of a \u201chow much Independence from the Judges have I achieved?\u201d trait.)</div> </div> </div> </div>There has been mention of Apotheosis, in a sidebar in the first preview that was pretty dismissive of the idea. Page 62 (the title falls on page 61), &quot;The Apotheotic Movement&quot;, describes Apotheosis as &quot;appearing&quot; to be the greatest threat to the Judges, but really no threat at all. That sidebar is another large part of my concern for where Mummy is going thematically.<br /> <br /> It also has a brief mention in the Glossary in terms closer to 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T14:51:10-08:00","id":1349694,"title":"","content":"Why should those elements be effected by the non-linear time? After all they are non-linear. If a mummy achieves final death or gets eaten or achieves Apotheosis in their 73rd descent but which is in say 975 BCE it doesn't change the fact that they had 72 descents from his soul's perspective beforehand. All it does is either stop (in the case of finale death) or change (in the other cases) the nature of descent 74 and on. <br /> <br /> In this I look towards something like the Doctor from Doctor Who. What the Doctor has personally done is something that is fundamental and thus is written into the very universe. Unless something is able to reach into the Doctor (or the mummy's) personal non-linear timestream then its near impossible to break things. <br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> I think Memory being an oopsy that is entirely out of the hands of the Judges (beyond normal means that anyone else can manipulate) is how I would go about doing it. <br /> <br /> I also like the idea that upon say achieving Apotheosis the Sekhem gets reset to 1 and the now free Mummy has to raise it in the way that everyone else has to - one point at a time. But I would also make it so that its not bought with individual experience but rather raises upon accomplishment or gaining experience thresholds. I would still keep them to the whole cycle of the descent, except there would be a bit more influence over it (I would like to see the Roman Empire, so you awaken somewhere where there is the Roman Empire, whether it is the historic one from early CE or even the Eighth Great Roman Empire in the far far future, it still is the Roman Empire). <br /> <br /> I will admit to waiting to wait for the rules and fluff on Duat before I make full comments on the details, but I do think there is much potential for the fun benefits that non-linear time provide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T15:01:00-08:00","id":1349697,"title":"","content":"This is mainly what I was getting at with my earlier question about the body in the tomb: if you achieve Apotheosis during the First Sothic Turn, where did the body that Arises during the Second Sothic Turn come from? <br /> <br /> Again, assuming that Apotheosis is even possible in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T15:28:08-08:00","id":1349705,"title":"","content":"As a random aside the whole note that the various bits of advanced technology we see in the past is a Mummy who had lived in the modern day trying to bring about certain developments is a brilliant one. I mean I could totally see a mummy saying to their cult &quot;Here are the details behind tech x, now I want you to use it within the cult but please keep it secret&quot; and then things happen and archeologists untomb them centuries later. Heck, I could totally see archaeology being a field that the Cults are heavily involved in. I mean if I was a mummy I would want people in my pay constantly working to find things that are mine through the centuries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T16:04:15-08:00","id":1349712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349705#post1349705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a random aside the whole note that the various bits of advanced technology we see in the past is a Mummy who had lived in the modern day trying to bring about certain developments is a brilliant one. I mean I could totally see a mummy saying to their cult &quot;Here are the details behind tech x, now I want you to use it within the cult but please keep it secret&quot; and then things happen and archeologists untomb them centuries later. Heck, I could totally see archaeology being a field that the Cults are heavily involved in. I mean if I was a mummy I would want people in my pay constantly working to find things that are mine through the centuries.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like the idea of OOPArts being the work of mummies who miss the conveniences of previous Descents","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T16:47:41-08:00","id":1349724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349697#post1349697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is mainly what I was getting at with my earlier question about the body in the tomb: if you achieve Apotheosis during the First Sothic Turn, where did the body that Arises during the Second Sothic Turn come from?<br /> <br /> Again, assuming that Apotheosis is even possible in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every single STARFALL section with the Guilds is basically addressing why Mummies seek Apotheosis, I think it's pretty safe to expect it to play a big part in the game due to its importance to the themes and be addressed in a later chapter, and in more detail than 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T16:53:23-08:00","id":1349726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349687#post1349687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to agree: what would make more sense in my opinion would be if Memory is something the Judges didn't anticipate, and would eliminate if they could.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind the Judges didn't create the Arisen. The Shan'iatu did, and the Shan'iatu had some rather different ideas than what the Judges have. They're the ones who wanted their empire's culture to be eternal.<br /> <br /> I find it not at all a paradox for Memory being a feature rather than a bug - it's just that their current masters really, really don't like that feature.<br /> <br /> There's a reason that &quot;Judge does not want you revived&quot; is a dice penalty that's likely neutralized by your cult just going about the normal Calling ceremony and doing it in your Tomb. Which is a really cool detail.<br /> <br /> Speaking of:<br /> <br /> <i><b>Geistblatt, </b></i><b>the Whispering Blade (Amulet ****)</b><br /> <br /> It was never meant to be a relic. The warlord who contracted the forging of the saber wanted a terror weapon, a pocket of Hell to eternally torture those slain with it. He was almost as shocked as the smith when he grew a spine and made the tyrant its first victim - and then the spell-smith even more shocked when the memory of noble treason gave it a soul.<br /> <br /> <b>Power: </b>The saber's telepathic mutterings include the knowledge of all those it has slain, and their skill. When activated, the bearer gains the rote benefit on all rolls meant to plan a battle strategy before conflict with a known enemy, and 8-Again on all Weaponry rolls when facing enemies these strategies anticipated. In addition, the Damascus steel within the blade is sharper than diamond and more resilient than titanium when the Sekhem within flows through it; it ignores up to four points of Durability and Armor when active, cutting through barriers and men with ease.<br /> <br /> <b>Curse: </b>The sword has a mind of its own, forged in betrayal of a madman and the best-intentioned murder. It desires to end conflicts, in as efficient and final a way as possible, not start them, and it will unleash the memories of all those it has slain on bearers it dislikes. While the sword is active, one of its bearer's Aspirations is replaced with one based around ensuring the battle at least attempts to both be considerate of collateral damage and to ensure it isn't repeated; &quot;Kill the aggressors&quot;, &quot;Evacuate the area of my loved ones&quot;, and &quot;Force my rival to the negotiating table&quot; are all valid. Betraying this Aspiration causes the sword to unleash its memory of violent and brutal conflict on its bearer, inflicting a breaking point with a -3 penalty; failure not only causes the bearer to lose a dot, but develop an Obsession based around making amends for the battle or become Fugued with grief and horror (player's choice) for the rest of the story, though the Arisen do not lose a Memory dot. What makes <i>Geistblatt </i>such a notorious node of (ironic) conflict is that the sword's mind is rather shrewd; it prefers to replace Aspirations with versions that are more akin to edits of its bearer's actual intentions or behave in ways that are both ethical and tactically sound (as opposed to &quot;hard men making hard decisions while hard&quot;; it can tell when the real reason the violent option is chosen is because it's really the easier one rather than the effective one, the sword <i>hates </i>torture for this precise reason); many bearers don't notice the difference, and even if told, don't see it as a curse. In this, the Whispering Blade becomes one of the most valuable mystical weapons in the world; the price it asks is fair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 11-19-2019, 07:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T17:01:46-08:00","id":1349727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349726#post1349726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Keep in mind the Judges didn't create the Arisen. The Shan'iatu did, and the Shan'iatu had some rather different ideas than what the Judges have. They're the ones who wanted their empire's culture to be eternal.<br /> <br /> I find it not at all a paradox for Memory being a feature rather than a bug - it's just that their current masters really, really don't like that feature.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it would be more accurate to say that it was always going to be impossible for Memory to not feature in the Rite, regardless of the wants and wishes of the Shan'iatu, the Judges, or even Ammut. The Will is a foundational component of Mummy's cosmology. You can bind and enslave ten thousand souls with the trappings of power and stack the deck against them as much as you'd like, but the laws of the universe demand that there be some way in which those souls could break their chains.<br /> <br /> At least, that was the 1e justification.<br /> <br /> I would also note that the Shan'iatu and Judges <i>both</i> want Irem's culture to be eternal. The Judges sent the Shan'iatu to birth civilisation because the laws intrinsic to said civilisation needed to exist so that humans could inevitably break them and be consigned to the Devourer's Maw. The Arisen perpetuating the strictures of Irem is something I imagine the Judges are more than happy with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T17:08:45-08:00","id":1349729,"title":"","content":"I know I said this before but I like the thematic nature of Vessels, and its subordinate Vestiges and Relics. I like how Vessel covers anything with Sekhem. I like how Vestiges are somewhat crude magical items, an art from both before and after Irem, and something that even modern Sorcerers can create. That said, I also like how Relics are special, they are a refined Vestige that makes use of certain secret teachings of Irem. That while sometimes new Relics can be made in general the methods used for such pure creations is super uncommon - especially because the one group with 'easy' knowledge of them are strictly prohibited by the very bounds that tie them to and empower them by the Judges. That, well that, is really really cool. <br /> <br /> I did just notice that Vestiges don't have power powers (just some small special effects), which while making sense is 'sad' to me. That said, its not a super big deal as its clearly mentioned that there is potential for surpassing things. <br /> <br /> On being effected by the Curses of Vessels, honestly, I wish the Arisen were immune to all Relics, gained a bonus when using a Relic of their Guild, and only faced half the penalty for curses of Vestiges. The whole idea that the pure, overwhelming potency of their inner Sekhem overwhelming the Sekhem in a Vessel to me means that the curses should not be able to stand the light of the Arisen. (Honestly, I wish the curses weren't even there, but at the same time I get why they are so its not a shocking existence for them.)<br /> <br /> On the nature of the Call, wouldn't such a roll only come into play when the players are the cultists rather than the Arisen themselves. Because if the players are the Arisen then as a ST I would basically just say &quot;its 1920 when you wake up and your cultists Called you using these three Relics, which you cannot use this story.&quot; But I would never really make a roll. <br /> <br /> The Relics described are very cool. I really like the format. A sentence or two with an evocative description, then a section on power and a section on curse, very very nice. To me this is a perfect way to write them out. So thumbs up to that. <br /> <br /> Tyler's Robot is sad, I totally awwwd on it. <br /> <br /> That said the mix of things is very nice. I like the general variance of the Relics. Its broad enough to give a sort of idea of what can be done without being limiting. <br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> As I am doing this I might as well make my other comments on the chapter. <br /> <br /> The sections Forgotten Skills, Skills and Dark Eras, Pre-Modern Skills, and Getting Ahead of the Times are all brilliant. Love the ideas. Love the way that it allows a player to always fit in with what is going on, and that is fun. <br /> <br /> On Dice Pool Permutations if you are going to allow modifying the success rate then it might be easier to just make a rule called 7-Success which clearly leads to knowing that upon using said rule dice that come up 7,8,9 or 0 are all successes. Just a random thought. <br /> <br /> Cult rules are really cool. They are like a side character on their own, but in a good way. I like the stats for them and the way that they can be personalized and enhanced. Dominance is nifty. Cult Actions are very cool. I could totally see a mummy player (or group) upon waking up saying &quot;right, so let us figure out what our cult did while we were asleep&quot; and such. <br /> <br /> The Descent section. On this honestly I am just going to have to nod and move on. While I don;t mind the idea that the time period a mummy is awake is limited the nature of how that limit is achieved is not something I am a fan of. So the first chart, with the story and the time, is great. But the chart where even saying &quot;screw the Judge&quot; leads to a descent roll has me going &quot;nah, that's not fun!&quot; Same with automatically raising memory, not going to automatically cause that to force a roll. Not gonna do it!<br /> <br /> Sybaris. Its very interesting. I like how on the short term it leads to a reduction in mortal efficiency while aiding the mummy but if it experienced too much then the mortal can basically push past the feeling to get angry or something. Its a good system. I like it. (I was afraid it was like the wasting thing of Prometheus, something that causes mortals and the world to have issues with the mummy, but it being what it is is fun for me, so that's cool.)<br /> <br /> Rite of Investment. Interesting. Question on Affinities, do Soul Affinities still exist? I mean the Affinity list just has regular and guild. <br /> <br /> So when you invest a Pillar you use up the Point right, which means your max for that Pillar is say 4 rather than 5. With how few points a mummy has that seems less than fun. Couldn't it be something like the max is a mummy's Pillar Rating but while they use a point to activate the rite they regain it as normal. Just my opinion. <br /> <br /> That said LOVE the Utimate Sacrifice bit. I mean its totally nasty and not 'good' in anyway but its fun. hehe<br /> <br /> Sadikh are awesome, though I wish there was a way to make them timeless too. That way the Sadikh found in 2020 can still be available when the mummy rises in 200 BCE. <br /> <br /> Timeless and Experience. The reshuffle of character sheets is AWESOME and AMAZING. I like this sooooooo much. <br /> <br /> The idea of having a flashback to a scene a thosuand years ago where the player gains 1 XP and then coming to the present point of the campaign and having 1XP to spend is sheer BRILLIANCE. <br /> <br /> Tombs. Not much to say but tombs are cool. I like the idea of being able develop and enhance them. So yeah, very cool. <br /> <br /> Then we get to Vessels which round out the chapter. But as time is non-linear that is something we already covered. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T17:11:15-08:00","id":1349731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349724#post1349724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Every single STARFALL section with the Guilds is basically addressing why Mummies seek Apotheosis, I think it's pretty safe to expect it to play a big part in the game due to its importance to the themes and be addressed in a later chapter, and in more detail than 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why they seek it isn't the question I have. What happens when they achieve it in a time period chronologically earlier than some of their Descents is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T18:41:40-08:00","id":1349745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349731#post1349731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why they seek it isn't the question I have. What happens when they achieve it in a time period chronologically earlier than some of their Descents is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Simple. The future changes.<br /> <br /> That may sound off, but a rule since Demon at least has been that in the Chronicles of Darkness, time paradoxes don't matter. If you kill your parents before they met, you still exist, it's just that the future you go back to doesn't remember you. The universe won't stop you from making a mistake you can't fix - but neither will it stop you from setting right what once went wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T19:28:54-08:00","id":1349755,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349729#post1349729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did just notice that Vestiges don't have power powers (just some small special effects), which while making sense is 'sad' to me. That said, its not a super big deal as its clearly mentioned that there is potential for surpassing things.<br /> <br /> On being effected by the Curses of Vessels, honestly, I wish the Arisen were immune to all Relics, gained a bonus when using a Relic of their Guild, and only faced half the penalty for curses of Vestiges. The whole idea that the pure, overwhelming potency of their inner Sekhem overwhelming the Sekhem in a Vessel to me means that the curses should not be able to stand the light of the Arisen. (Honestly, I wish the curses weren't even there, but at the same time I get why they are so its not a shocking existence for them.)</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1e, the Vestiges didn't have powers at all. The decision to give them powers and make their curses more obvious was made to make them a bit more flavorful in this edition.They're intended to be less impressive magical objects than Relics, which is why they hold to the list of basic ability options. I added situational benefits/penalties for extra flavor.<br /> Mummies are more curse resistant in 2e than they were in 1e. Mummies only suffer a reduced curse for Relics outside of their guild, experiencing no curse for guild Relics or Vestiges. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349729#post1349729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Relics described are very cool. I really like the format. A sentence or two with an evocative description, then a section on power and a section on curse, very very nice. To me this is a perfect way to write them out. So thumbs up to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. We wanted to keep things a bit shorter this time around, both to save word count and to make it easier for people to make their own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349729#post1349729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tyler's Robot is sad, I totally awwwd on it.<br /> <br /> That said the mix of things is very nice. I like the general variance of the Relics. Its broad enough to give a sort of idea of what can be done without being limiting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad you liked them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349729#post1349729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So when you invest a Pillar you use up the Point right, which means your max for that Pillar is say 4 rather than 5. With how few points a mummy has that seems less than fun. Couldn't it be something like the max is a mummy's Pillar Rating but while they use a point to activate the rite they regain it as normal. Just my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was clarified on the KS recently. You invest a point in your cultist, not a dot (though in my games I'd count that point as a &quot;dot&quot; rating for the cultist). You can regain that point like usual after enacting the Rite, and the cultist still holds on to it. Your rating doesn't decrease. This Rite basically allows a mummy to effectively double their available Pillar points with proper preparation, if they're willing to yoink them back from their Inheritors at a critical moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T21:33:02-08:00","id":1349779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349745#post1349745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Simple. The future changes.<br /> <br /> That may sound off, but a rule since Demon at least has been that in the Chronicles of Darkness, time paradoxes don't matter. If you kill your parents before they met, you still exist, it's just that the future you go back to doesn't remember you. The universe won't stop you from making a mistake you can't fix - but neither will it stop you from setting right what once went wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. I figured that Mummy doesn't necessarily work by the same rules about time that Demon does; and there have been hints in the comments that Mummy tries for a single consistent timeline (talks about how it's possible to tell a story where a chronologically earlier Descent can affect your current Descent, for example); but if it turns out that Mummy's policy is similar to Demon's, I won't object.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T23:50:25-08:00","id":1349790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349690#post1349690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I, too would <i>really</i> love some clarification about how the concept of nonlinear time works with a mummy's Finale Death, falling into Shuankhsen or achieving Apotheosis. Each represents some sort of an &amp;quot;end point&amp;quot; for the Arisen's existence, and understanding how they work in the frame of nonlinear time feels kinda important.</div> </div> </div> </div>In what way? Final Death - they die in whatever period and don\u2019t awaken again. This does nothing to erase the awakenings they\u2019ve already had, even those that occurred in the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T00:01:02-08:00","id":1349791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349779#post1349779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair enough. I figured that Mummy doesn't necessarily work by the same rules about time that Demon does; and there have been hints in the comments that Mummy tries for a single consistent timeline (talks about how it's possible to tell a story where a chronologically earlier Descent can affect your current Descent, for example); but if it turns out that Mummy's policy is similar to Demon's, I won't object.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mummy\u2019s approach to how time works is both and neither. Sometimes a timeline is consistent, sometimes it isn\u2019t. The Storytelling chapter goes into more detail, but the short spoiler answer is that time is a lot, *lot* bigger than any other splat understands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T00:19:41-08:00","id":1349797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349790#post1349790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In what way? Final Death - they die in whatever period and don\u2019t awaken again. This does nothing to erase the awakenings they\u2019ve already had, even those that occurred in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>My question about death is that could a mummy awaken in a period after her body was destroyed, if they have no Inheritors, canopic jars and their body was burned to ash. I accept that they can wake up in the past, but how could they have another Descent in a time after such destruction if they have no body to awaken into?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T00:31:00-08:00","id":1349800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349797#post1349797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question about death is that could a mummy awaken in a period after her body was destroyed, if they have no Inheritors, canopic jars and their body was burned to ash. I accept that they can wake up in the past, but how could they have another Descent in a time after such destruction if they have no body to awaken into?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the Rite of Return doesn\u2019t really care about anything like that?<br /> <br /> If a mummy is killed in a way that they can never come back, then they\u2019ll never come back, in future or past. If the mummy is killed in a way that wouldn\u2019t prevent them coming back, then they\u2019ll come back.<br /> <br /> If you\u2019re still interested, remind me to talk more about it after the ST chapter drops.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T00:39:28-08:00","id":1349802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349705#post1349705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a random aside the whole note that the various bits of advanced technology we see in the past is a Mummy who had lived in the modern day trying to bring about certain developments is a brilliant one. I mean I could totally see a mummy saying to their cult &quot;Here are the details behind tech x, now I want you to use it within the cult but please keep it secret&quot; and then things happen and archeologists untomb them centuries later. Heck, I could totally see archaeology being a field that the Cults are heavily involved in. I mean if I was a mummy I would want people in my pay constantly working to find things that are mine through the centuries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, thank you. I held my breath for a day or two knowing my section was about to get to the public, so it's great to know someone liked a chunk of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T01:32:50-08:00","id":1349810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349800#post1349800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because the Rite of Return doesn\u2019t really care about anything like that?<br /> <br /> If a mummy is killed in a way that they can never come back, then they\u2019ll never come back, in future or past. If the mummy is killed in a way that wouldn\u2019t prevent them coming back, then they\u2019ll come back.<br /> <br /> If you\u2019re still interested, remind me to talk more about it after the ST chapter drops.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be a great help. It seems that most of my confusion is that I'm not sure how far do I need, as a ST, to go in order to kill a mummy. While I'm not a supportive of the concept that &quot;the GM's job is to kill the player characters&quot;, I want to know that I do have the means to do so, and what are they. Currently, I have no idea what could actually threaten a mummy outside of making the Judges angry.<br /> <br /> I hope that the ST's chapter would clarify things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T02:08:44-08:00","id":1349815,"title":"","content":"By the way, I hid a not-so-subtle Indiana Jones reference in Chapter 4.<br /> <br /> Whoever finds it first wins a trip to Duat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T02:36:32-08:00","id":1349821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349810#post1349810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could be a great help.</div> </div> </div> </div>Happy to help. I have reasons and answers and descriptions of how it works, but need to wait until we get to the right backer previews so I can avoid the NDA ninjas. \ud83d\ude09<br /> <br /> And I\u2019ve added to the writer group feedback that we could consolidate the \u2018permanent-death\u2019 conditions for mummies so people have an easy reference. But be aware that there\u2019s not a lot of ways you can permanently eliminate a mummy*. It\u2019s not the kind of game where that kind of death is the problem. The horror comes from death not being the end.<br /> <br /> * From a game point of view, if you\u2019re not playing different time periods or a chronicle that will jump around, then the usual methods to temporarily kill a mummy are as good as permanent death for that game. They won\u2019t be coming back to the table if you kill them in this time and that\u2019s all you\u2019re playing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T02:37:22-08:00","id":1349822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349815#post1349815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whoever finds it first wins a trip to Duat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ll pass, thanks. \ud83d\ude2c","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T08:37:50-08:00","id":1349862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349815#post1349815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, I hid a not-so-subtle Indiana Jones reference in Chapter 4.<br /> <br /> Whoever finds it first wins a trip to Duat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would it be a certain Sample Tomb Trap that makes would-be thieves pray there are grooves in the floor they can throw themselves flat in?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> My own questions about the non-linear time thing:<br /> <br /> What happens if a Sadikth created in the past lasts long enough to overlap with one that exists in the future? Say a Mummy awakens in 2000 and creates one. Then they awaken again in 1999, find they don't have one, and make a new one. Is this one guaranteed to die before the new year? Is the Arisen guaranteed to be dead before their previous awakening begins?<br /> <br /> Given the way memories and appearance can fluctuate through the process, do cults ever suspect they raised the wrong mummy? If a mummy just went down, the hierophant realizes they forgot to ask what color of fuzzy slippers should be waiting new time, and they perform the Call immediately (assuming they aren't all murdered) what do they think when who rises has different gender, race, skills, and remembered history?<br /> <br /> There has been mentions of prior descents in the relative future. Are there going to be any suggestions for players bringing knowledge of the future back to the modern era of play? Or is that more an ST call with regards to what they will allow?<br /> <br /> Other questions:<br /> <br /> Can the Tier 3 effects of Gift of the Golden Ankh be applied to multiple people with the same unleashing?<br /> <br /> Can a cult choose not to drain some of the vessels in the Lifeweb when performing the call?<br /> <br /> Can Wanderer's Clay assume the form of complex items? Can it be reinvoked to make a different object or is it fixed once used? (I recall there were one(ish)-use regia like that wine that could only be recovered by pressing it out of a body.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 11-20-2019, 12:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T10:20:12-08:00","id":1349882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349650#post1349650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd beg to differ, but we're getting into Assassin's Creed-esque &quot;the right meteor at the right time could shape the course of human civilisation&quot; hypotheticals and they're probably a tad specific for this conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That only removes artforms from the world's artistic paradigms. It's an incredibly blunt hammer, when what you need is the soft and insistent shaping of mummies and cults providing consistent artistic, imperial, and cultural pressure over centuries and millennia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Suffice to say, the concept of the Judges wanting their servants to rediscover Memory and their sense of self feels like a strange direction to go in for Mummy thematically, at least for me, and let's leave it at that. </div> </div> </div>This is the crux of the misunderstanding, I think: no, the Judges do not want their servants to rediscover Memory and a sense of self. The Shan'iatu, in creating and encoding the Rite of Return, recognized that a <i>certain amount </i>of Memory <i>could be </i>situationally preferable to the raw might of Sekhem, especially when it comes to that all-important human interaction that is necessary for shaping artistic paradigms in the mold of Irem. They didn't anticipate Apotheosis; they knew that any recovered Memory would be eroded by the waves of Sekhem after the conclusion of the Descent. But the rising and falling pattern of Memory is a feature of the Arisen, not a bug.<br /> <br /> The Arisen are thinking slaves kept in rising and falling states of ignorance for eternity, not perfect automatons, and that's by design.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T10:27:04-08:00","id":1349884,"title":"","content":"Do we have an answer yet in what happens to your 2115 Descent you had if you then achieve Apotheosis in 2019 during your Fourth Turn?<br /> <br /> Does it just not occur from a linear POV, but still occurred in terms of the Mummy\u2019s personal experience?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T10:32:02-08:00","id":1349885,"title":"","content":"Talking about not expecting Apotheosis makes me REALLY hope we get something more meaningful and most importantly fun and interesting out of it in 2e, as compared to the its not really anything to write home about that we got in 1e. For example, I hope that they keep the Timeless element of non-linear time but gain more influence over it. I also hope that their Memory remains strong, with zero rising and falling. But even more I hope that though their Sekhem may start at 1 it can be raised over time. I want it to be a potential achievement of importance over a long campaign OR maybe even a starting point for a new campaign that is taken in a new direction. <br /> <br /> Its the same for Sekhem Sorcerer, which I really wish is a minor template rather than just a few mortal merits. (Mortal merits which are a great starting off point by the way, I just think it would be cool that after taking said merits or having a background where such merits are taken, a sorcerer finds themselves tapping into something greater and in a more controlled way.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T10:36:01-08:00","id":1349886,"title":"","content":"I really think the non-linear nature of mummy existence totally fixes any sort of issue that might occur. If you are a mummy that has gone through 40 previous descents then those 40 descents are 'canon' from your present version's mindset. The fact that one is in 2019 and another is in 8332 CE and another is 321 BC doesn't matter as they are all you. If your 41st Descent sees you go through Apotheosis and thus free, it still doesn't change what came before it just modifies what came after. Even if that descent is in 1320 BCE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T10:43:48-08:00","id":1349888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349885#post1349885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But even more I hope that though their Sekhem may start at 1 it can be raised over time. I want it to be a potential achievement of importance over a long campaign OR maybe even a starting point for a new campaign that is taken in a new direction.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>&quot;For the master's tools will never dismantle the master's house. They may allow us temporarily to beat him at his own game, but they will never enable us to bring about genuine change.&quot;</i> - Audre Lorde","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T11:28:24-08:00","id":1349892,"title":"","content":"Did I miss Advanced/Blighted Actions in this last systems chapter? They don't appear to be detailed there...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T11:34:20-08:00","id":1349893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349886#post1349886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really think the non-linear nature of mummy existence totally fixes any sort of issue that might occur. If you are a mummy that has gone through 40 previous descents then those 40 descents are 'canon' from your present version's mindset. The fact that one is in 2019 and another is in 8332 CE and another is 321 BC doesn't matter as they are all you. If your 41st Descent sees you go through Apotheosis and thus free, it still doesn't change what came before it just modifies what came after. Even if that descent is in 1320 BCE.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do people keep saying this like it remotely addresses the questions I\u2019ve asked?<br /> <br /> The mummy has achieved apotheosis and is no longer going through Descents. He is up and about 10 years later when he previously had a Dedcent. So now is there somehow a second him at the same point in time, or does the previous Descrnt not occur from a linear perspective?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T11:58:35-08:00","id":1349895,"title":"","content":"I personally really liked the message that Apotheosis had in 1e- that in the end, it is better to be a free person and not a bound god. Freedoms means you give up on your power, but you regain your soul in exchange- and when the whole world is doomed to feed the ever hungry Devourer and suffer eternally under the Law, what more could a person ask other than freedom?<br /> <br /> So for me, Apotheosis is not about becoming like the Judges- it is about putting yourself above them. That was the goal of the Shan'iatu- that's why they envied humanity, and why they sacrificed Irem. They tried to have the cake and eat it- being gods who stole the prize promised to mankind. That's also why they failed. You know what they say about the virtues and flaws and angels and humans. <br /> <br /> I don't know, people may say that Mummy is a fatalistic game where everything is doomed to be eaten by the Devourer, but I don't think so. I find it really hopeful. They say that A'aru is barren, with only two souls shinning in its starry wastes. I see that against all chances an in spite of the wrath of the Judges, the hunger of Ammut and the envy of the Shan'iatu, humanity managed to put two souls up in the heavens, where they are eternal. A proof that humanity exist. And how wonderful is that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T12:01:49-08:00","id":1349897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349892#post1349892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did I miss Advanced/Blighted Actions in this last systems chapter? They don't appear to be detailed there...</div> </div> </div> </div>They made the change in the Kickstarter, which means after the manuscript was put together. They'll have to re-write things to put in the Advanced/Blighted Actions. So, we may get that later in the Kickstarter, or it may come after.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T12:47:20-08:00","id":1349902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349888#post1349888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>&amp;quot;For the master's tools will never dismantle the master's house. They may allow us temporarily to beat him at his own game, but they will never enable us to bring about genuine change.&amp;quot;</i> - Audre Lorde</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont get this. Just because the tools were owned by the master at one time doesn't mean that in my hands they cant be used against him. The tools are tools and are not bound in loyalty. <br /> <br /> I guess its a way of looking at the world but I don't see it this way. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349893#post1349893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why do people keep saying this like it remotely addresses the questions I\u2019ve asked?<br /> <br /> The mummy has achieved apotheosis and is no longer going through Descents. He is up and about 10 years later when he previously had a Dedcent. So now is there somehow a second him at the same point in time, or does the previous Descrnt not occur from a linear perspective?</div> </div> </div> </div>Still not seeimg the issue. Old you from a previous descent is doing stuff and so is new you. So there are two of you at once, okay, that's fine. Time can handle that. Especially as new current you is free while old previous you was not. <br /> <br /> Also, are we sure there is no contimued Descents upon Apotheosis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T14:02:58-08:00","id":1349911,"title":"","content":"Oh, on the Master's Tools quote I have this quote to add <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That means Lorde is right, though: the master\u2019s tools won\u2019t destroy his house, because they\u2019re only his tools so long as he controls them. Once they are reclaimed, they belong to all of us. And our tools can do anything. <br /> <br /> Nathan J. Robinson </div> </div> </div>(I looked up the quote to see where it was coming from and I have to say it is a very interesting, thought provoking, philosophic idea.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T14:13:10-08:00","id":1349912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349731#post1349731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why they seek it isn't the question I have. What happens when they achieve it in a time period chronologically earlier than some of their Descents is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was mostly addressing your earlier inquiry of &quot;is Apotheosis in 2e&quot; by pointing at places that lend it relevance by name. Misleading post to retort to, sorry!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T14:43:15-08:00","id":1349921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349902#post1349902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dont get this. Just because the tools were owned by the master at one time doesn't mean that in my hands they cant be used against him. The tools are tools and are not bound in loyalty. <br /> <br /> I guess its a way of looking at the world but I don't see it this way. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Still not seeimg the issue. Old you from a previous descent is doing stuff and so is new you. So there are two of you at once, okay, that's fine. Time can handle that. Especially as new current you is free while old previous you was not. <br /> <br /> Also, are we sure there is no contimued Descents upon Apotheosis?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would kind of defeat the point of Apotheosis if there were. The whole point is to break the chains of slavery that keep pulling you back down rather than letting you live on your own terms.<br /> <br /> The issue is Mummy bodies don\u2019t time travel. It\u2019s the corpse hanging out in linear time when the Arisen is in the Duat. So the mummy from different points in their own timeline would be trying to occupy the same corpse in your description.<br /> <br /> Can someone involved in the game please clarify this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T14:51:08-08:00","id":1349924,"title":"","content":"I assume that they are waiting for the Storyteller chapter to drop in order to speak about the subject. NDA ninjas and all of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T14:53:27-08:00","id":1349925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349821#post1349821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* From a game point of view, if you\u2019re not playing different time periods or a chronicle that will jump around, then the usual methods to temporarily kill a mummy are as good as permanent death for that game. They won\u2019t be coming back to the table if you kill them in this time and that\u2019s all you\u2019re playing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how. The cult may summon the mummy back tomorrow. The mummy's touchstone, or a ghost or something, or whatever other decree trigger is present, could even be involved on the very scene or an adjacent scene and immediately summon the mummy back up with a full tank of sekhem. Sure, its no picnic for the mummy, but to the outside world, you have an absolute madman with a full tank of Sekhem ready to party hard again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T15:12:41-08:00","id":1349931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349911#post1349911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, on the Master's Tools quote I have this quote to add <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> (I looked up the quote to see where it was coming from and I have to say it is a very interesting, thought provoking, philosophic idea.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Where you're tripping up is that literally any Sekhem you get that isn't the last bit from your own life is taken from somebody else. Dreams of Avarice was plain about this. You can't beat the tyrants who built you on stolen power by stealing that power for yourself - just because it's not theirs doesn't mean it's yours to take.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T15:30:37-08:00","id":1349937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349902#post1349902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dont get this. Just because the tools were owned by the master at one time doesn't mean that in my hands they cant be used against him. The tools are tools and are not bound in loyalty.<br /> <br /> I guess its a way of looking at the world but I don't see it this way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Imagine people living under INGSOC in 1984. What use will the tools of mass surveillance, oppression, doublethink, crime/right think, etc. be in dismantling INGSOC and bringing about a more equitable and open society?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T16:12:09-08:00","id":1349944,"title":"","content":"Perhaps the better question would be, how can the underlying technology, knowledge, and organization be leveraged to dismantle INGSOC and construct a more equitable society. Also, nothing assumes that the Arisen would inherently pursue a more equitable society. Some may simply wish to sit on the throne.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2096-willywonka","name":"willywonka","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T16:20:09-08:00","id":1349946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349931#post1349931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where you're tripping up is that literally any Sekhem you get that isn't the last bit from your own life is taken from somebody else. Dreams of Avarice was plain about this. You can't beat the tyrants who built you on stolen power by stealing that power for yourself - just because it's not theirs doesn't mean it's yours to take.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Power is a chain you wrap around yourself&quot; has always been a theme of Mummy, one of it's main ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T17:33:30-08:00","id":1349951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349921#post1349921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can someone involved in the game please clarify this?</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't write on the relevant sections, so am not in a position to give an authoritative answer anyway, but I would expect the writers who did are more likely to be open to giving you a clarifying answer once the Storytelling part of the manuscript is out.<br /> <br /> As a writer, it's always a fine line to tread when talking about topics that may be relevant to content that hasn't yet been previewed. I'd dearly like to talk more about Judge emanations and <i>benbenet</i> but I should really wait til Chapter 5 gets previewed next week :P<br /> <br /> If nothing else, I'll be happy to mull over the topic of the hypothetical you've posed with you once the Storytelling chapter is out. That alright with you? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T17:59:30-08:00","id":1349959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So after seeing a statement on the Rite of Investment I am less enthused by it than I originally thought but eh it's something.</div> </div> </div> </div>What statement?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T18:56:16-08:00","id":1349965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349951#post1349951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't write on the relevant sections, so am not in a position to give an authoritative answer anyway, but I would expect the writers who did are more likely to be open to giving you a clarifying answer once the Storytelling part of the manuscript is out.<br /> <br /> As a writer, it's always a fine line to tread when talking about topics that may be relevant to content that hasn't yet been previewed. I'd dearly like to talk more about Judge emanations and <i>benbenet</i> but I should really wait til Chapter 5 gets previewed next week :P<br /> <br /> If nothing else, I'll be happy to mull over the topic of the hypothetical you've posed with you once the Storytelling chapter is out. That alright with you? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. I\u2019ll be happy to wait if it\u2019s something that\u2019s coming. I was just feeling frustrated like I was supposed to have a better grasp on how the Arisen relationship with time works based on what we\u2019ve already seen than I do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T19:59:47-08:00","id":1349966,"title":"","content":"Reading the relic section is painful. I know the reason- word count and that goddamn 2nd edition mandate that the core rules be regurgitated over and over with every setting book. First edition we got relics with a interesting, atmospheric story behind them that created plot hooks and added to the lovecraftian feel of the game. Here we have one line descriptions of the object, the power, and the curse. The relics themselves aren't BAD for what they are, but I feel like the writers are being hamstrung. The little bitty bits were a big part of what made Mummy so great, off hand references to strange inhuman bloodlines or Ochre Masked Fiends alluding to cosmic horror hiding behind the veneer of gothic egypt. I'm concerned the more limited page count is really selling the game's potential short.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T20:25:03-08:00","id":1349967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349966#post1349966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading the relic section is painful. I know the reason- word count and that goddamn 2nd edition mandate that the core rules be regurgitated over and over with every setting book. First edition we got relics with a interesting, atmospheric story behind them that created plot hooks and added to the lovecraftian feel of the game. Here we have one line descriptions of the object, the power, and the curse. The relics themselves aren't BAD for what they are, but I feel like the writers are being hamstrung. The little bitty bits were a big part of what made Mummy so great, off hand references to strange inhuman bloodlines or Ochre Masked Fiends alluding to cosmic horror hiding behind the veneer of gothic egypt. I'm concerned the more limited page count is really selling the game's potential short.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or, maybe they decided to prioritize the ability to make your own over paragraphs and paragraphs of stuff that really didn't matter, and that means rather simple stuff to start with. Especially with Vestiges, which were...pure fluff. Now they ain't.<br /> <br /> Fluff is easy, and doesn't really need magic items to have their own fluff in a book that needs to do other things first. Especially since it's been exchanged for something more interesting, that the spontaneous enchantment of items as vestiges happens all the time, and often because of profoundly dark things; that's Lovecraftian in a way a thousand Blasphemous Depictions really couldn't match (&quot;ha, you thought you were <i>safe </i>from all this mystical crap - nope, humanity brings wild magic with it, and curses are inherent&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T23:15:29-08:00","id":1349985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349921#post1349921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone involved in the game please clarify this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not yet, sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T00:05:22-08:00","id":1349987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349882#post1349882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That only removes artforms from the world's artistic paradigms. It's an incredibly blunt hammer, when what you need is the soft and insistent shaping of mummies and cults providing consistent artistic, imperial, and cultural pressure over centuries and millennia.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is the crux of the misunderstanding, I think: no, the Judges do not want their servants to rediscover Memory and a sense of self. The Shan'iatu, in creating and encoding the Rite of Return, recognized that a <i>certain amount </i>of Memory <i>could be </i>situationally preferable to the raw might of Sekhem, especially when it comes to that all-important human interaction that is necessary for shaping artistic paradigms in the mold of Irem. They didn't anticipate Apotheosis; they knew that any recovered Memory would be eroded by the waves of Sekhem after the conclusion of the Descent. But the rising and falling pattern of Memory is a feature of the Arisen, not a bug.<br /> <br /> The Arisen are thinking slaves kept in rising and falling states of ignorance for eternity, not perfect automatons, and that's by design.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I mentioned earlier, my impression from 1e was not that Memory was intentional on anyone's part, but that it was simply not possible for the Rite to <i>not</i> provide a way out. Remember the fundamental laws of magic in the Mummy setting, and that they are built on Sutek's sacrifice to ensure beings can evade doom in Ammut's maw through their own Will. Of course the Rite can't entirely erase a Mummy's Memory, the very laws of existence itself mandate that they must have a chance to be free.<br /> <br /> All this stuff about the Shan'iatu wanting a certain amount of Memory present doesn't ring a bell to me, sorry. Is there some chapter or quote I can read about it? Mummy has always mapped to the binary of Memory=freedom/rebellion while Sekhem=slavery/power, and the idea of the Shan'iatu embracing a happy medium is new to me. The closest I can recall is them being taken aback that Ammut might use the Shuankhsen as an investment instead of a one-off payment. The arts and template of Irem has always seemed hard coded into civilisation itself, Mummies acting as stewards of it has always seemed more in the vein of making it more likely that they'll be nearby when a relic is made than necessary to perpetuate the existence of those arts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T07:55:19-08:00","id":1350015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1349862#post1349862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can Wanderer's Clay assume the form of complex items? Can it be reinvoked to make a different object or is it fixed once used? (I recall there were one(ish)-use regia like that wine that could only be recovered by pressing it out of a body.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Wanderer\u2019s Clay can\u2019t be used to make particularly complex items. You could mold it into the shape of a revolver, but it wouldn\u2019t function as one. It isn\u2019t a one use item, though. You can activate the Relic again to mold it into something else. An Iremite assassin might have molded it into a simple bracelet to walk into a place \u201cunarmed\u201d, then reactivated it to make a knife so she could slay her target.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T08:47:38-08:00","id":1350017,"title":"","content":"I just want to know if I'm understanding this correctly, but the Su-menent's purpose is to preserve the dead right? like maintain the mythology of death and memory of the people who once lived?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T11:43:39-08:00","id":1350073,"title":"","content":"I feel like this book might be a useful read for Mummies: <a href=\"https://www.howtoinventeverything.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.howtoinventeverything.com/</a><br /> <br /> Along with just general engineering textbooks and things, maybe work very hard on learning how gear driven babbage engines and calculators work. <br /> <br /> I kind of want to have the antikythera mechanism show up in a Mummy game as an item of power or something. Maybe do a bit of light crossover with the God Machine or Mage.<br /> <br /> If it isn\u2019t discussed in the Storyteller section, you might want to include a note about making sure everyone is on the same page as regards \u201cchanging history.\u201d I like the OOPARTS sidebar, but, once you know what you\u2019re doing, there are a lot of technical advances you can make fairly quickly. A Mummy that remembered enough about the future could give their Cult enough of an edge that they might be able to seriously change history. And if that\u2019s what people want, it\u2019s fine. But when half the players want to enjoy intrigue in a historical setting and half want to build guns so their cults can go take over the Roman Empire, there\u2019s a potential problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T13:21:10-08:00","id":1350098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350073#post1350073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like this book might be a useful read for Mummies: <a href=\"https://www.howtoinventeverything.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.howtoinventeverything.com/</a><br /> <br /> Along with just general engineering textbooks and things, maybe work very hard on learning how gear driven babbage engines and calculators work.<br /> <br /> I kind of want to have the antikythera mechanism show up in a Mummy game as an item of power or something. Maybe do a bit of light crossover with the God Machine or Mage.<br /> <br /> If it isn\u2019t discussed in the Storyteller section, you might want to include a note about making sure everyone is on the same page as regards \u201cchanging history.\u201d I like the OOPARTS sidebar, but, once you know what you\u2019re doing, there are a lot of technical advances you can make fairly quickly. A Mummy that remembered enough about the future could give their Cult enough of an edge that they might be able to seriously change history. And if that\u2019s what people want, it\u2019s fine. But when half the players want to enjoy intrigue in a historical setting and half want to build guns so their cults can go take over the Roman Empire, there\u2019s a potential problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>To say nothing of those mummies who have knowledge from the future relative to our own time.<br /> <br /> I suppose that might be one source of plot drama, attempting to change a bad future that only you know about and cannot provide any evidence for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T08:15:14-08:00","id":1350238,"title":"","content":"The new tease has BYOBG, Build Your Own Bad Guy. I like the way you can mix and match animal heads, bodies, and limbs to get different effects. Not sure what the essence cost means yet, but I'm sure that'll be revealed. (I'm guessing the essence cost of summoning one is equal to the highest of the pieces, but who knows.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T12:05:22-08:00","id":1350280,"title":"","content":"I saw the new tease and a part of me wondered if player mummies can create them as well. I mean yes, I understand that technically they are horrors, but really they would be epic and awesome tomb guardians and tomb servants. So I hope that a player can create them too, without having to give up a soul or sacrifice like a hundred people for one or something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T12:43:58-08:00","id":1350290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350280#post1350280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I saw the new tease and a part of me wondered if player mummies can create them as well. I mean yes, I understand that technically they are horrors, but really they would be epic and awesome tomb guardians and tomb servants. So I hope that a player can create them too, without having to give up a soul or sacrifice like a hundred people for one or something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm preeeetty sure it's not intended.... Saying that, if a player reeeeaally wanted something like that...?<br /> <br /> This is what I would do, and this is entirely house ruling, just to be clear.<br /> <br /> Iremic Sorcery/Magic/Whatever-You-Call-It is not a kind thing. Anything you want, <i>must </i>be paid for. You're either paying the cost up front, or <i>something else</i> is paying it for you, which means bad times down the road. Unfortunately, there's likely only one kind of coin that will suffice for payment. And so I'd likely go along the route of the Sadikh, requiring a person loyal to you willing to sacrifice themselves for the creation of the benevolent Amhkata. And honestly, I'd probably have that willing sacrifice actually <i>become </i>the Amhkata. I'm sure there are extra things that could be done to make stuff interesting and worthwhile as additional Tomb infrastructure, such as the body of the willing sacrifice needing to be interred within the Tomb of the Arisen, and so forth.<br /> <br /> But yeah. Something needs to be sacrificed, bare minimum. After that, there are the logistical issues of keeping the creature fed, etc.<br /> <br /> Edit: Yeah, I'd model it off of the rite for Sadikh, including hefty cost, probably pissing off the Judges a bit, etc. But probably also allow you to have more than one, while requiring a dedicated Relic to empower each Tomb Guardian that has to stay within the Tomb's Web. Not being able to interact with people like a Sadikh can is a pretty good disadvantage for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","user":"Paradim","date":". 11-22-2019, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T13:10:48-08:00","id":1350293,"title":"","content":"Basically, I'm right on board with anything that allows Cultists to serve their Arisen master beyond death. Whether as Sadikh, or ghosts, or even house ruling tomb guardian Amhkata, it's a pretty easy sell for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T18:06:46-08:00","id":1350359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350238#post1350238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The new tease has BYOBG, Build Your Own Bad Guy. I like the way you can mix and match animal heads, bodies, and limbs to get different effects. Not sure what the essence cost means yet, but I'm sure that'll be revealed. (I'm guessing the essence cost of summoning one is equal to the highest of the pieces, but who knows.)</div> </div> </div> </div>*idly points at First Edition doing the same thing*<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350280#post1350280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So I hope that a player can create them too, without having to give up a soul or sacrifice like a hundred people for one or something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chronicles in general is <i>not that</i>, but Mummy in particular is very much <i>not that</i>.<br /> <br /> Also, the Amkhata count as Lifeless, and it still rankles the Judges for the Arisen to treat the Lifeless without enmity, so while they <i>can</i> make it same as anyone else, it's counter-intuitive for their general goals.<br /> <br /> The Amkhata are <i>abominations</i>, the results of murdering the world and the tools of those who are okay with that. The Arisen may be monsters in both senses of the word, but even they have limits regarding one of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-22-2019, 09:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T00:49:56-08:00","id":1350599,"title":"","content":"So not gonna lie, who else is going to make a Pug headed Amkhat? Because I definitely am going to.<br /> <br /> Also while Abominations they may be, the Nameless Empire weaponized Amkhata for their benefit- so even if the Judges May disdain the existence of these Lifeless ( which they also use as servants mind you), I definitely envision guildhalls of the Su-Menent that focus on crafting these beasts for the purpose of furthering the Guild\u2019s mission of maintaining the necromantic legacy of Irem. They may be publicly seen as misguided or of poor form by the Guild proper, but they ultimately are endorsed by their peers behind closed doors much like how many Red Magicians were in first ed.<br /> <br /> After all, there are many uses such a creature can have, especially to those who are so closely tied to Death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 11-24-2019, 04:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T14:34:29-08:00","id":1350704,"title":"","content":"Update revealing the Blood Bathers and general fluff on the Endless (non-mummy immortals) today.<br /> <br /> Apparently Sekhem is the primary component in any would-be Elixir of Life; the presence of vessels and especially Arisen amplifies Endless abilities by quite a bit, and Bathers are essentially performing a Closed Rite that turns the Sekhem of their victims into youth for themselves (the example is noted to be grateful for her geriatric arthritis, because it's a warning shot she needs an infusion). Bathers can't leave their donors alive, though, sacrifice is needed for the symbolism to work. Which is fine by me, the rare bather who could just make do with a transfusion was so supernaturally crippled it honestly seemed more of an issue than just murder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T14:50:26-08:00","id":1350707,"title":"","content":"Looking forward to seeing how they handle my homeboys n' gals the Purified. As cool as body thieves are, I can't say no to a good chi-master. &lt;3<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T15:29:56-08:00","id":1350711,"title":"","content":"I think it was confirmed Purified won't be in the core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T17:12:06-08:00","id":1350735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350599#post1350599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So not gonna lie, who else is going to make a Pug headed Amkhat? Because I definitely am going to.<br /> <br /> Also while Abominations they may be, the Nameless Empire weaponized Amkhata for their benefit- so even if the Judges May disdain the existence of these Lifeless ( which they also use as servants mind you), I definitely envision guildhalls of the Su-Menent that focus on crafting these beasts for the purpose of furthering the Guild\u2019s mission of maintaining the necromantic legacy of Irem. They may be publicly seen as misguided or of poor form by the Guild proper, but they ultimately are endorsed by their peers behind closed doors much like how many Red Magicians were in first ed.<br /> <br /> After all, there are many uses such a creature can have, especially to those who are so closely tied to Death.</div> </div> </div> </div>.....I'm not finding any reference to Irem weaponizing these things or the Judges ever using them as servants, actually. Also, since I assume the rules for Amkhata are largely the same, their &quot;master&quot; must keep them fed once a week to keep them obedient and not go berserk and turn on them. They feed on Sekhem, which means you will be performing constantly raids searching for vessels or ordering assaults on fellow arisen to keep the beast on your side. So I don't really see their peers looking at them as misguided or of poor form so much as heretics and traitors that are playing russian roulette with the lives of their own cults as well as endangering all Arisen in the Nome by playing with blasphemous and forbidden forces they barely comprehend.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T17:25:21-08:00","id":1350737,"title":"","content":"Yeah, no where in Mummy will you find a reference to the Empire using the Amkhata. Again, they are abominations in the eyes of the Judges, and no one in Irem was gonna flirt with winning Frankenstein's game when the powers behind the nation were watching.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T18:17:41-08:00","id":1350745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350737#post1350737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, no where in Mummy will you find a reference to the Empire using the Amkhata. Again, they are abominations in the eyes of the Judges, and no one in Irem was gonna flirt with winning Frankenstein's game when the powers behind the nation were watching.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet the Rite of Return...?<br /> <br /> Yeah... &quot;We can't do this thing because higher ups are watching us&quot; sounds very unlike Chronicles of Darkness...<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, I know that &quot;Interacting with a Lifeless without obvious enmity.&quot; is a check for a Descent roll. But that seems kind of weird when Arisen explicitly have an Utterance that creates Lifeless Thralls in the preview text, and we know from 1st Edition that they had several other powers involving creating and commanding and otherwise making use of Lifeless.<br /> <br /> I'm not forcing my players to make constant checks for Descent rolls strictly because they're using powers the books lets them use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","user":"Paradim","date":". 11-24-2019, 09:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T18:22:10-08:00","id":1350746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350711#post1350711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it was confirmed Purified won't be in the core.</div> </div> </div> </div>My heart's canopic jar is broken. :'&lt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T19:00:46-08:00","id":1350750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350745#post1350745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And yet the Rite of Return...?<br /> <br /> Yeah... &quot;We can't do this thing because higher ups are watching us&quot; sounds very unlike Chronicles of Darkness...<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, I know that &quot;Interacting with a Lifeless without obvious enmity.&quot; is a check for a Descent roll. But that seems kind of weird when Arisen explicitly have an Utterance that creates Lifeless Thralls in the preview text, and we know from 1st Edition that they had several other powers involving creating and commanding and otherwise making use of Lifeless.<br /> <br /> I'm not forcing my players to make constant checks for Descent rolls strictly because they're using powers the books lets them use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, fair.<br /> <br /> Still though, nowhere in the text does it say the Nameless Empire used Amkhata, which says <i>something</i> about the way that culture looked at it.<br /> <br /> As for the Thralls, I think we've got a case of obvious exceptions being obvious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-24-2019, 10:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T19:01:03-08:00","id":1350751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350745#post1350745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet the Rite of Return...?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a world of difference between &quot;we snuck this big magic into the culmination of our pet project as scions of the powers that could ostensibly punish us&quot; and &quot;we had the humans make these things for war - you know, these things that we were charged to destroy as creations of the Devourer and, you know, the humans we were specifically tasked to teach the Law of the Judges to so that the world doesn't collapse because Ammut got impatient, and, you know, war, the art that we can already be one of two de facto mastering powers of by virtue of simply knowing things like tactics and metallurgy?&quot;<br /> <br /> The Shan'iatu played fast and loose with a lot of their little white mutiny, but the Shan'iatu were neither Arisen nor human nor placed to rely on any heavenly mandate that they weren't already stretching tissue-thin to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T19:13:24-08:00","id":1350752,"title":"","content":"I'm just not really seeing the big deal here. <br /> <br /> I mean... Having one of the Guilds be Death-Priest Necromancers seems kind of odd if you don't want to encourage making undead abominations as a solution to your problems. Plus, it would add to the horror and fear that the Nameless Empire was able to evoke.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T19:26:39-08:00","id":1350754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350750#post1350750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, fair.<br /> <br /> Still though, nowhere in the text does it say the Nameless Empire used Amkhata, which says <i>something</i> about the way that culture looked at it.<br /> <br /> As for the Thralls, I think we've got a case of obvious exceptions being obvious.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Like how common sense is rarely common, what you think is obvious, another person will completely miss. Stuff should be written with clarity in mind. While yes, if you try to make something idiot proof, the world just invents a better idiot.<br /> <br /> As it stands, this is a clear difference between Rules As Written and Rules As Intended, and I'm sure you've seen lots of problems in games from such differences whether in person, or argued about online. Wouldn't this be an opportune moment to clarify intent with what's written?<br /> <br /> (Just to be clear, I'm speaking strictly about how the rules as written state that interacting with Lifeless without enmity invoking Descent rolls, which would be a landmine for all interactions with Utterances that create Lifeless, which Arisen already have one of, and likely have more especially with an entire Guild about Necromancer Death-Priests. I'm not talking about Arisen using or creating Amkhata here.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T19:33:08-08:00","id":1350755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350752#post1350752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just not really seeing the big deal here.<br /> <br /> I mean... Having one of the Guilds be Death-Priest Necromancers seems kind of odd if you don't want to encourage making undead abominations as a solution to your problems. Plus, it would add to the horror and fear that the Nameless Empire was able to evoke.</div> </div> </div> </div>In their write-up it seems like they are more about properly treating the dead, burial duties and ceremonies of passing on. While they do create dead, it's pretty clearly not the mandate of the entire guild, with their undead seeming more of a mistake (like with the Guild of Healers).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T19:34:20-08:00","id":1350756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350752#post1350752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just not really seeing the big deal here.<br /> <br /> I mean... Having one of the Guilds be Death-Priest Necromancers seems kind of odd if you don't want to encourage making undead abominations as a solution to your problems. Plus, it would add to the horror and fear that the Nameless Empire was able to evoke.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Simple: Amkhata are a lot like other Lifeless, in that they are thralls of Ammut. Each one is essentially an independently sentient tooth of hers, much as how the Shuankshen are her priests.<br /> <br /> Judges may not care about more necromancy, but magic to conjure forth an avatar of their archenemy...yeah, they're going to be a bit skeptical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T20:05:08-08:00","id":1350758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350755#post1350755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In their write-up it seems like they are more about properly treating the dead, burial duties and ceremonies of passing on. While they do create dead, it's pretty clearly not the mandate of the entire guild, with their undead seeming more of a mistake (like with the Guild of Healers).</div> </div> </div> </div>To say nothing of how the ability of the Arisen to learn Utterances has always been a shaky metaphysical thing as far as their intended state goes \u2014 I haven't done a deep read of the entire line yet, but as far back as the corebook &quot;mummies were never meant to be able to do this&quot; was an in-universe theory, and by Dreams of Avarice that appeared to be borne out by the fact that the Litany of the Fivefold Soul mentions, almost offhand, the fact that in order to become Deathless every one of the Arisen had to be taught a specific Utterance that they forgot as the price of passage into Duat.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the matter of enmity for the Lifeless, considering that the 1e equivalent just says &quot;Shuankhsen&quot; and the same preview where the line appears uses it interchangeably in the paragraph on Bane Relics, I think it's safe to say that the Judges aren't going to strip the Sekhem from your bones for calling up feral zombies to eat the impious if you're not really mean to them, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T20:50:45-08:00","id":1350762,"title":"","content":"Not to mention the fact that few mummies would raise a corpse thrall to take them out to dinner and a movie. I'm pretty sure enslaving them for war or labor counts as enmity by the Judges' standards, and if you bring someone back to true life, they don't count as lifeless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T22:49:31-08:00","id":1350774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350758#post1350758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To say nothing of how the ability of the Arisen to learn Utterances has always been a shaky metaphysical thing as far as their intended state goes \u2014 I haven't done a deep read of the entire line yet, but as far back as the corebook &amp;quot;mummies were never meant to be able to do this&amp;quot; was an in-universe theory, and by Dreams of Avarice that appeared to be borne out by the fact that the Litany of the Fivefold Soul mentions, almost offhand, the fact that in order to become Deathless every one of the Arisen had to be taught a specific Utterance that they forgot as the price of passage into Duat.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the matter of enmity for the Lifeless, considering that the 1e equivalent just says &amp;quot;Shuankhsen&amp;quot; and the same preview where the line appears uses it interchangeably in the paragraph on Bane Relics, I think it's safe to say that the Judges aren't going to strip the Sekhem from your bones for calling up feral zombies to eat the impious if you're not really mean to them, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sothis Ascends really sure seemed like it implied they were a gift from Sutekh in the earliest Turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T22:59:52-08:00","id":1350775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350774#post1350774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sothis Ascends really sure seemed like it implied they were a gift from Sutekh in the earliest Turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am referring to the Utterance of Anpu's true name, the use and forgetting of which are essential to avoiding the third and fourth strayings from Deathlessness, well before the First Sothic Turn.<br /> <br /> The Arisen have the <i>capacity</i> to learn Utterances because it was required for them to become Deathless at all, and even with the involvement of the <i>sha</i> there's still little sign that exercising that retained capacity was in the Shan'iatu's plans to the degree that the role of the Su Menent in Irem could be described as &quot;necromancers who make undead abominations.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-25-2019, 02:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T05:08:08-08:00","id":1350794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350735#post1350735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> .....I'm not finding any reference to Irem weaponizing these things or the Judges ever using them as servants, actually. Also, since I assume the rules for Amkhata are largely the same, their &quot;master&quot; must keep them fed once a week to keep them obedient and not go berserk and turn on them. They feed on Sekhem, which means you will be performing constantly raids searching for vessels or ordering assaults on fellow arisen to keep the beast on your side. So I don't really see their peers looking at them as misguided or of poor form so much as heretics and traitors that are playing russian roulette with the lives of their own cults as well as endangering all Arisen in the Nome by playing with blasphemous and forbidden forces they barely comprehend.</div> </div> </div> </div>... Except there are references that Amkhata were used as weapons during the Days of Irem in the first edition Corebook, and the very preview even says that there are fewer servants of the Judges that are dreaded more than an Amkhat. Now that might change, but go back and read again before saying you can\u2019t find any reference please.<br /> <br /> Now would the majority of Arisen entertain the idea? Absolutely not, especially the ones who are extremely pious and/or dogmatic. But the ones who are desperate enough will, the disenfranchised arisen will. It is a blasphemy against their gods... but at the end of the day, the Use of Sekhem for any purpose that doesn\u2019t further the goal of ones judge is a blasphemy - yet mummies can and will do so if they think it is the right course of action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 11-25-2019, 08:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T06:08:31-08:00","id":1350802,"title":"","content":"Finally got around to reading on the updates to the Sadikh (don't look at me like that), and the only real comment that comes to mind is<br /> <br /> <i>here in the garden<br /> let's play a game</i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T06:17:50-08:00","id":1350805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350802#post1350802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally got around to reading on the updates to the Sadikh (don't look at me like that), and the only real comment that comes to mind is<br /> <br /> <i>here in the garden<br /> let's play a game</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ouch, my soul","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0