tainer\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350802#post1350802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally got around to reading on the updates to the Sadikh (don't look at me like that), and the only real comment that comes to mind is<br /> <br /> <i>here in the garden<br /> let's play a game</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Don't know if the saddest part is because I reconized the reference and completed in my mind with &quot;stand very still&quot; and the innocent &quot;this will be so muuch fun!&quot; that follows, or the fact that I'm still mysteriously drawn to and attached to Pink Diamond/Rose. Also never thought I could stablish a connection between steven universe and Mummy, that was genious","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25516-pinkhaunt","name":"PinkHaunt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25516_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T06:37:41-08:00","id":1350811,"title":"","content":"So, I really like how the system for building Amkhata is looking this time, but it trips me up something bad that the False Ka was not mentioned as one of the parts that make them up. I guess it's just listed separately? It made up some of the most memorable and freaky elements of Amkhata.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T07:36:16-08:00","id":1350819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350794#post1350794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Except there are references that Amkhata were used as weapons during the Days of Irem in the first edition Corebook</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;A briefcase nuke used by spiritual malcontents&quot; is not remotely the same thing as &quot;dedicated battlefield tech used by the military arm of a ruling empire.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T08:28:07-08:00","id":1350826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350819#post1350819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;A briefcase nuke used by spiritual malcontents&amp;quot; is not remotely the same thing as &amp;quot;dedicated battlefield tech used by the military arm of a ruling empire.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The entire empire was ruled by spiritual malcontents in the form of the Shan\u2019Iatu, there\u2019s no reason to believe that they didn\u2019t use them as battlefield attack animals as well.<br /> <br /> They were actively feeding the Devourer and used Lifeless as soldiers to begin with.. so why not use these insanely durable chimera like they used everything else? If you think that the Shan\u2019Iatu wouldn\u2019t spite Anpu or the Judges by using Amkhata as weapons, I\u2019m honestly surprised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T09:07:12-08:00","id":1350836,"title":"","content":"Here\u2019s an interview with one of the Mummy writers. Specifically me.<br /> <a href=\"https://307rpg.com/?p=67\" target=\"_blank\">https://307rpg.com/?p=67</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T10:08:10-08:00","id":1350844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350826#post1350826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you think that the Shan\u2019Iatu wouldn\u2019t spite Anpu or the Judges by using Amkhata as weapons, I\u2019m honestly surprised.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also mentions the Judges using Amkhata as weapons in the preview.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T10:13:13-08:00","id":1350845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350844#post1350844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also mentions the Judges using Amkhata as weapons in the preview.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, in a fashion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T10:22:35-08:00","id":1350847,"title":"","content":"FINALLY WE REACHED THE BOOK OF LASTING DEATH BY THE NAME OF THE JUDGES THANK YOU","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 11-25-2019, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T11:06:58-08:00","id":1350858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350844#post1350844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also mentions the Judges using Amkhata as weapons in the preview.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I must've missed that...<br /> <br /> Yeah, I think I'll definitely make use of Amkhata like that then. It fits very well with themes of self-justification like &quot;It's a necessary sacrifice when WE do it, but it's an atrocity when YOU do it&quot; that highlights hypocrisy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T11:21:34-08:00","id":1350860,"title":"","content":"Oh man, I really want the kickstarter to hit $62,000 for the Book of Lasting Breath expansion, but I'm kinda doubtful that's doable in nine days left....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T11:32:32-08:00","id":1350862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350860#post1350860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh man, I really want the kickstarter to hit $62,000 for the Book of Lasting Breath expansion, but I'm kinda doubtful that's doable in nine days left....</div> </div> </div> </div>Usually the last 48 hours sees a big jump in pledges as people who saved the project get notified. Doing 1/3 again as much is not unusual, which would put us in the $66k range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T11:55:29-08:00","id":1350866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350826#post1350826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The entire empire was ruled by spiritual malcontents in the form of the Shan\u2019Iatu,</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Arisen have been battling these monsters since the days of Irem, since the first mistake with a relic gave birth to an asp with a tiny bull\u2019s head. Sadly, not all who beheld the misbegotten were repulsed. There is always some warped soul who won\u2019t look away from the grotesque, but who instead takes delight in its deviance. In the early days, a few twisted beasts were built by jaded priests. <b>But their power soon caught the attention of spiritual misfits who saw in the by-blows of broken vessels a weapon they could raise against the Judges and, perhaps, a new and better way to blaspheme.</b> In their hubris, these degenerate clerics sought to steal the spark of life and the right of shaping from the gods themselves. </div> </div> </div>\u2026Yeah, sure that sounds like the temakh.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> there\u2019s no reason to believe that they didn\u2019t use them as battlefield attack animals as well. </div> </div> </div>Most of their soldiers were soldiers. Mortal soldiers. Who freak out and become less effective in the mere presence of an Amkhat. The Empire's necromancers <i>took the corpses back to work </i>more consistently than they used them as a fighting force.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They were actively feeding the Devourer and used Lifeless as soldiers to begin with.. so why not use these insanely durable chimera like they used everything else? If you think that the Shan\u2019Iatu wouldn\u2019t spite Anpu or the Judges by using Amkhata as weapons, I\u2019m honestly surprised. </div> </div> </div>The Shan'iatu's entire deal was that they were fucking around with the letter of their instructions, but the letter of their instructions still included keeping the Devourer in check. They <i>fed</i> the Devourer in one big event that ended with them immune to further repercussions than their failure to completely accomplish their goal. There's a tremendous difference between the temakh's scheming and <i>actively deliberately making things that serve the Devourer.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350844#post1350844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also mentions the Judges using Amkhata as weapons in the preview.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Judge's most feared messenger&quot; can mean all manner of things without context when you're talking about ancient beings of brutal justice perched on the roots of civilization. None of those things suggest sorcerous chimerae formed by mistake or exacting ritual were favored or necessary when dealing with most human societies circa 3800 BC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T13:06:35-08:00","id":1350894,"title":"","content":"reread Book of the Deceived again my friend, because they made numerous sacrifices to Ammut, they even had a ritual devoted to pick out choice morsels for Her. So I wouldn\u2019t be saying they were following the letter of their instructions that closely. Everything else, yeah that\u2019s fair to a point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T14:17:09-08:00","id":1350912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350894#post1350894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">reread Book of the Deceived again my friend, because they made numerous sacrifices to Ammut, they even had a ritual devoted to pick out choice morsels for Her. So I wouldn\u2019t be saying they were following the letter of their instructions that closely. Everything else, yeah that\u2019s fair to a point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotta 'pease Dark Lord Hippomamapocalypse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":974,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","user":"MrParaduo","date":". 11-25-2019, 07:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T15:01:16-08:00","id":1350916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350894#post1350894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">reread Book of the Deceived again my friend, because they made numerous sacrifices to Ammut, they even had a ritual devoted to pick out choice morsels for Her.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll note that by that point they had sought out an audience with the Devourer in a world where she could no longer directly speak with beings in the world; that the Shan'iatu who made Irem were all wounded by Ammut in that way that let her call to them; that by now the Shan'iatu had been given the Rite of Return after getting that audience through death and torture; that this tidbit about ritual comes up in the context of &quot;this priestess has a ritual instrument whose meaning is that the priestess points it at something she's going to sacrifice to the Devourer&quot;; and that this Shan'iatu in particular was one of the ones who met with the Herald of Ammut.<br /> <br /> The Shan'iatu were the only ones throwing Utterances around at the time of Irem, they were increasingly reclusive as they grew more mortal, and Amkhata are sufficiently unstable that making one using metal tools means it won't even listen to its creator. At that stage, an Amkhat is a liability rather than an asset. They're bombs, not tanks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So I wouldn\u2019t be saying they were following the letter of their instructions that closely. </div> </div> </div>The letter of the instructions for what they were supposed to teach humanity doesn't have much to do with what they get up to on their own time.<br /> <br /> <i>Still</i> doesn't make &quot;create a being that maintains itself by destroying relics and killing people indiscriminately&quot; a thing that doesn't go against the specific jobs they were given.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T15:52:01-08:00","id":1350918,"title":"","content":"Whatever happened in Irem, the game takes place well afterward, and if someone wants to have their guilds experimenting with Amkhata and the ST is okay with that then no big deal. Presumably there will be some rules to hurdle but that's for the table to work out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T16:13:37-08:00","id":1350919,"title":"","content":"What is the appeal of players having amkhata serve them? There's a dozen other stat blocks for ghosts, zombies, cthonic demons, and other innumerably custom horrors. I'm having playable-Heroes and playable-Alchemists flashbacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T16:21:46-08:00","id":1350923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350919#post1350919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the appeal of players having amkhata serve them? There's a dozen other stat blocks for ghosts, zombies, cthonic demons, and other innumerably custom horrors. I'm having playable-Heroes and playable-Alchemists flashbacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Splat specific servant? People've been asking for servants of creatures in their splats since they existed. Animal and supernatural ghouls, personal totems and spirits, Supernal and Abyssal familiars. Most of them have come through.<br /> <br /> It likely helps that Amkhata, at least in first edition, were basically 'Here's a near unkillable monster anyone can make and do what they want with providing they have the right bait.'<br /> <br /> Though in this case Korogra opened just explaining that they envision some guildmembers doing it behind closed doors. A better comparison for playable Heroes would be playable Shuankhsen, and for playable Alchemists the Faithful of Shulpae hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-25-2019, 07:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T16:29:18-08:00","id":1350925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350918#post1350918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whatever happened in Irem, the game takes place well afterward, and if someone wants to have their guilds experimenting with Amkhata and the ST is okay with that then no big deal. Presumably there will be some rules to hurdle but that's for the table to work out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody has been talking about what happened after Irem since the allusion to First Edition's briefcase nuke comparison.<br /> <br /> I don't care what people do in their own games, but the Amkhata being Things The Arisen Notionally Stand Against is hard-coded into their cultural background and metaphysics and I've seen enough cases of runaway fanon in this franchise that I want to firmly state that &quot;the Nameless Empire used Amkhata as weapons of war in a meaningful sense&quot; is headcanon in the vein of alteration rather than reinterpretation.<br /> <br /> This was a Bronze Age society with anachronisms of sorcerous origin, but what glimpses we've seen still mostly looked like a place where mundane people lived and the terrifying necromancy and god-magic had about the same place in the social landscape as it would in later eras. Their soldiers were primarily mortal folk fighting and killing other mortal folk by force of better arms and armor rather than ravening hordes of zombies and bestial mashups of divine mishap. If the armies of the Shan'iatu included Amkhata at any point, it was an aberrant circumstance rather than part of the standard battlefield practice. They're weapons of terror that you don't really need when your opposition hasn't figured out formations or alloys yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T17:08:39-08:00","id":1350928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350775#post1350775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am referring to the Utterance of Anpu's true name, the use and forgetting of which are essential to avoiding the third and fourth strayings from Deathlessness, well before the First Sothic Turn.<br /> <br /> The Arisen have the <i>capacity</i> to learn Utterances because it was required for them to become Deathless at all, and even with the involvement of the <i>sha</i> there's still little sign that exercising that retained capacity was in the Shan'iatu's plans to the degree that the role of the Su Menent in Irem could be described as &quot;necromancers who make undead abominations.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Speaking of the Sha...we never really got an explanation of where they came from, did we? From Sutekh, sure, but...who built them? Did Sutekh manifest an avatar? Did he have a cult working inside Irem? One that apparently had enough working knowledge of the Rite of Return to craft these amazing relics to activate at the same time the Arisen will wake up? AND have the combined secret knowledge of all the Guilds to build what amounts to a combination of all the relics operating in sync and with sentience? I feel like we have an unnamed Lost Guild or something more mysterious operating in the shadows, serving the agenda of Sutekh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T17:46:24-08:00","id":1350932,"title":"","content":"Considering how so many gods take the image of humans with animal heads I cant' see anything inherently culturally or societal that makes said beastmen automatically evil, not if the rules don't require such thing. So allowing for magic that lets someone take a form and add the physical traits of animals, well, I don't see how this is inherent evil necromancy. No matter what a random 1e paragraph said. <br /> <br /> Which is why I stand by what I hope - that the rules don't require something really really bad to make them possible and thus it could be used by player mummies to create a set of basically anthro servants or tomb guardians, if they want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T17:56:38-08:00","id":1350935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350919#post1350919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the appeal of players having amkhata serve them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Having a chimeric undead abomination as a Tomb Guardian sounds pretty awesome to me, honestly. If a player really enjoyed the idea of having their tomb guarded by some loyal Quetzacoatl-dragon-ish monster, and wanted help to make it something doable in a game I'm running, then believe me, my response isn't going to be being offended and shoot down the idea as BadWrongFun. I'm gonna have a shit-eating grin, riff off of the rules for making an official undead abomination servant, along with some handy Build-Your-Own-Monster rules, and tell my player to make sure their sacrificial knives are sharp, because this is gonna get bloody for what they want.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350919#post1350919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a dozen other stat blocks for ghosts, zombies, cthonic demons, and other innumerably custom horrors.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, why not another undead abomination? Options aren't a terrible thing. I see no reason to shut the idea down.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350919#post1350919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm having playable-Heroes and playable-Alchemists flashbacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hah, that's a bit hyperbolic! ^.^ No one has suggested <i>playing </i>an Amkhata ....yet. Hrmmmm.....<br /> <br /> But seriously, this is getting a little overblown. If the objection is that Amkhata are absolutely supposed to be restricted to being antagonists, that isn't difficult to overcome at all. Instead, there's a Rite of the Tomb Guardian that creates a Not-Amkhata, a thing kinda like an Amkhata but not quite because Arisen are powerful and awesome with divine/eldritch sorcery or whatever, which uses these specific rules for Amkhata that you're comfortable being in a player's hands, it costs having a dedicated Relic on hand that keeps the Not-Amkhata happy and if that Relic gets stolen or broken, then Terrible Things(tm) can happen (like maybe the Not-Amkhata goes out of control and turns into an actual Amkhata).<br /> <br /> This doesn't need to be put in the book. There are two sets of rules that will be available that can be easily riffed off of this if someone wanted to do it. And honestly, if a Storyteller was having trouble working it out, I'd think it would be perfectly acceptable for them to open a new thread asking people for help and folks around here would be able to give helpful advice on how to make it work for their game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T18:16:26-08:00","id":1350939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350932#post1350932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering how so many gods take the image of humans with animal heads</div> </div> </div> </div>That's symbolism, much like depictions of the Buddha with hundreds of arms. Things that work fine as artistic metaphor tend to be pretty fucked up when rendered literally.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I cant' see anything inherently culturally or societal that makes said beastmen automatically evil, not if the rules don't require such thing. </div> </div> </div>Nobody is talking about beastmen. These are things like bulls with the heads of falcons or jackals with the heads of snakes or, yes, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ammit\" target=\"_blank\">a hippopotamus with the legs of a lioness and the jaws of a crocodile.</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So allowing for magic that lets someone take a form and add the physical traits of animals, well, I don't see how this is inherent evil necromancy. No matter what a random 1e paragraph said. </div> </div> </div>They're literally made from dead animals and disaster, bro. They are ghost-adjacent spiritual fuckups that eat the stuff of manifest existence, the greatest of which was one of the Devourer's earliest attempts to jockey for more Sekhem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which is why I stand by what I hope - that the rules don't require something really really bad to make them possible and thus it could be used by player mummies to create a set of basically anthro servants or tomb guardians, if they want. </div> </div> </div>Again, their 1e precedent is &quot;these things don't manifest unless a relic breaks, and they store up time that they can spend in the material realm by breaking more vessels or killing people.&quot;<br /> <br /> None of them are going to be particularly anthropomorphic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T18:34:38-08:00","id":1350941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350939#post1350939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's symbolism, much like depictions of the Buddha with hundreds of arms. Things that work fine as artistic metaphor tend to be pretty fucked up when rendered literally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that difficult... I mean, Blessed is the God-King takes direct inspiration with making that symbolism very literal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T18:54:31-08:00","id":1350943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350941#post1350941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not that difficult... I mean, Blessed is the God-King takes direct inspiration with making that symbolism very literal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep!<br /> <br /> It's also <i>terrifying god-magic</i> that doesn't last very long and doesn't have any mechanical impact stemming from the use of that imagery, which is not the most compelling case to make for things that, again, are made by applying a blasphemous combination of taxidermy and necromancy towards the specific end of making something that eats Raw Life Force.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T19:25:28-08:00","id":1350950,"title":"","content":"If a society has a symbolism of something as a highly respected thing, and the powers that be exist and are real, then I can't see creatures or beings that make use of said symbolism as something that would be unexpected or thought of as wrong. I mean if gods exist, and walk about, then the bull-headed god isn't us imagining them that way but rather the god having that form and us writing it down.<br /> <br /> I'm just gonna note that the description and the rules don't say dead bodies, at least not in a blatent direct way. So when I looked at the nature of the idea all I saw was &quot;someone creating chimeric monsters&quot; and to that I say &quot;cool!&quot; I also thought 'tomb guardians' and hidden monsters in spaces that have laid untouched for centuries and such.<br /> <br /> I look forward to seeing how the minor groups of Immortals sense, control, or alter Sekhem to see how I may take what is here and twist things around a bit.<br /> <br /> PS. I like the comment 'dead animals and disaster&quot;. I think its a nice way of describing something bad. So thumbs up on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T19:30:26-08:00","id":1350951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350950#post1350950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just gonna note that the description and the rules don't say dead bodies, at least not in a blatent direct way.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you never read the first edition core then.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Like, clearly you didn't, because one of the best jokes in the book is on the subject.<br /> <br /> So people are kept straight on the subject<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pg. 183, The Lifeless, the Amkhata, Generation, from Mummy the Curse First Edition</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where do Amkhata come from? (Fortunately, it\u2019s not, \u201cWell son, when a jackal and a lion love one another very much\u2026\u201d) The lesser breed arises when Sekhem is wasted. Any time a relic with Sekhem is destroyed (not used up through use or drained for some other purpose, but physically ruined without first being emptied of Sekhem), there\u2019s a chance of a lesser Amkhat generating spontaneously. Largely, this is a matter for Storyteller fiat, though if a set of guidelines is desirable, the Storyteller can roll one die for each point of Sekhem that was in a relic. Any success generates a monster.<br /> <br /> Greater Amkhata are another matter entirely. Nothing that vile comes about by honest accident. <b>Using a blasphemous rite passed down through ages, a mortal gifted with even the rudiments of necromancy can build a monster that would make Dr. Frankenstein throw up his hands and say, \u201cI didn\u2019t know this was a competition, but you just won.\u201d</b></div> </div> </div> </div>For clarity, this ritual involves an inverted limestone pyramid at least twenty feet deep, marked with hieroglyphics in human blood equaling to a pint per roll of work on a 50 success task (So assuming average rolls, 2-3 successes per roll, comes out to 25 pints-17 pints, the average human body containing 10 pints), assembling the pieces of animals who represent the sacred to the Nameless Empire (with the animal pieces ideally being as fresh as possible, which usually means the necromancer in question murdered them and probably tortured them), and then perform the ritual over the thing inserting the False Ka and Sekhem, and behold, now you have a monster that eats Sekhem instead of sending it to the Judges.<br /> <br /> But yeah, tomb guardians and monster cats, and definitely not profanities against reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":".  Did you know how many pints of blood were in the average human being? I did not. 03-08-2022, 07:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T20:13:10-08:00","id":1350955,"title":"","content":"On your completely incorrect statement, not only have I read 1e but I also pledged for it on Kickstarter and own all 1e books. There are elements I like and there are elements I hate, which is why I have chosen to judge 2e based on 2e rather than take into consideration what was in 1e. The section we are talking about in 2e doesn't focus on them being undead besties, and so I won't automatically assume that. <br /> <br /> What I see is a being able to take animal parts and put them on other animal parts, which to me has a lot of interesting ST and player use, which is why I wondered if they could be used that way. <br /> <br /> All that said we aren't seeing this in the section of the book they are in, just kickstarter update and so the section itself might say that which you say as far as 1e is concerned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T20:13:13-08:00","id":1350956,"title":"","content":"If you want my personal opinion, what makes the Amkhata blasphemous is that they are effectively malformed, corrupted fetid half-formed souls. Consider that Sekhem is the essence of life and death itself, and that minor Amkhata are born from the destruction of vessels or similar distortions in Sekhem's flow. Consider likewise that most Amkhata are conjoined of two or more representations of sacred animals representing aspects of the human soul as understood in ancient Irem. So, Amkhata are the stillborn accidents of creation to create a proper human being, and greater Amkhata are deliberate acts of human beings attempting ape the sublime act of creation the gods alone can accomplish.Just my personal take on the subject, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T20:17:28-08:00","id":1350957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350955#post1350955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On your completely incorrect statement, not only have I read 1e but I also pledged for it on Kickstarter and own all 1e books.</div> </div> </div> </div>That <i>distinctly </i>is not better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T20:30:25-08:00","id":1350961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350935#post1350935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Having a chimeric undead abomination as a Tomb Guardian sounds pretty awesome to me, honestly. If a player really enjoyed the idea of having their tomb guarded by some loyal Quetzacoatl-dragon-ish monster, and wanted help to make it something doable in a game I'm running, then believe me, my response isn't going to be being offended and shoot down the idea as BadWrongFun. I'm gonna have a shit-eating grin, riff off of the rules for making an official undead abomination servant, along with some handy Build-Your-Own-Monster rules, and tell my player to make sure their sacrificial knives are sharp, because this is gonna get bloody for what they want.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Which is fine if that's what you want to do at your table, but realize it is a significant departure from the setting as written. I'd balk at having one of the major examples antagonists in the setting as a pet for the same reason I'd balk at giving a Mage summoning up abyssal entities or a werewolf getting a greater wound spirit as the pack totem. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T20:58:11-08:00","id":1350965,"title":"","content":"Anyways, so I caught up with the material today. Thoughts so far?<br /> <br /> By and large, Mummy is a lot more accessible now, and while I didn't realize how I liked the mechanical occultness of the systems and even the information drip (yeah, I suddenly realized that I actually had enjoyed the journey of discovering the truth about Mummy over multiple books, I'm as surprised as you), that accessibility can only be a good thing. There's some mechanics that answer things Mummy already did that I know long time Mummy fans know my opinion on, but meh, it works. While there's definite things to improve (Affinities and Utterances, though I wasn't as bothered by it as others, definitely need some more oomph, thank god for expanded materials), I enjoy the new version...with one exception.<br /> <br /> Mummy the Curse was a highly experimental game for the Chronicles franchise and as a roleplaying game on the whole , and I would personally argue it being revolutionary, or at least capable of it (seriously wouldn't have minded seeing more games take cues from it). It obviously ended up fairly niche, but I contend it ended up so for the right reasons.<br /> <br /> Now as a fan of that game who wanted nothing more than to see Curse in the Second Edition, this scratches the itch. I got a game I really like with a lot of neat additions and more openness lined up with the rest of the game in an incarnation I really like.<br /> <br /> But I am disappointed Curse wasn't quite as revolutionary in it's Second Edition form, that while it adds cool things, it doesn't really challenge conventions in the same way First Edition did.<br /> <br /> But that's a tall order for anyone, and I'm not going to let it stop me tipping my hat to everyone on the team for a job well done.<br /> <br /> Besides, we still have three chapters to go. I've still got room to be proven wrong, and I wouldn't be surprised to find out I'm wrong in some way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-26-2019, 12:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T21:21:43-08:00","id":1350967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350961#post1350961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is fine if that's what you want to do at your table, but realize it is a significant departure from the setting as written. I'd balk at having one of the major examples antagonists in the setting as a pet for the same reason I'd balk at giving a Mage summoning up abyssal entities or a werewolf getting a greater wound spirit as the pack totem.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Realize schmealize. I'm willing to use what is in the books to make the game fun for my players if they're willing to sell me on the idea, whether it's their Arisen characters having My Little Amkhatas (or Not-Amkhata, if that's a hang up), a Mage breaking reality with summoned abyssal entities, or a pack of werewolves under a wound spirit. Of those three examples, My Little Amkhata's is the <i>easiest </i>sell there for me.<br /> <br /> Words of Dead Fury is an Utterance in 1st Edition that arguably does something atrocious along the lines of the ritual for making a Greater Amkhata, considering it involves building a honey pot for ghosts for the deliberate purpose of feeding an undead shoggoth so it's easier to control, a monster that eats people it comes across <i>twice</i>. Arisen are quite capable of using their sorcery to summon and control some really terrible horrors.<br /> <br /> We also already have one ritual in the preview material that Arisen can perform that draws the displeasure of the Judges. This is not that significant of a departure from the setting as written and I've already expressed how it could be made to fit better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T21:25:46-08:00","id":1350968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350965#post1350965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I am disappointed Curse wasn't quite as revolutionary in it's Second Edition form, that while it adds cool things, it doesn't really challenge conventions in the same way First Edition did.<br /> <br /> But that's a tall order for anyone, and I'm not going to let it stop me tipping my hat to everyone on the team for a job well done.<br /> <br /> Besides, we still have three chapters to go. I've still got room to be proven wrong, and I wouldn't be surprised to find out I'm wrong in some way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm betting that a lot of work was put into making Duat more of a thing for Arisen, and that is the material we have yet to see. We've seen mentions before as to how what happens in Duat can affect an Arisen's next Descent. So I think we're going to be getting more information as to what Duat is, what Duat is like, and what can be found there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T21:42:25-08:00","id":1350970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350968#post1350968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm betting that a lot of work was put into making Duat more of a thing for Arisen, and that is the material we have yet to see. We've seen mentions before as to how what happens in Duat can affect an Arisen's next Descent. So I think we're going to be getting more information as to what Duat is, what Duat is like, and what can be found there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually looking forward to the whole adventure in Duat thing. I always thought the fact that mummies didn't adventure there in 1e was a missed opportunity, so I'm glad they fixed that. As is the idea that actions there might actually effect the next Descent. Which, come to think of it, maybe means that Duat is also sort of out of time, that is its a place where all times meet rather than being in one particular moment. hmmm That could be quite fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T21:53:43-08:00","id":1350972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350950#post1350950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a society has a symbolism of something as a highly respected thing, and the powers that be exist and are real, then I can't see creatures or beings that make use of said symbolism as something that would be unexpected or thought of as wrong. I mean if gods exist, and walk about, then the bull-headed god isn't us imagining them that way but rather the god having that form and us writing it down.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://anthrocentric.tumblr.com/post/162811174919/can-you-clear-up-the-animalhuman-egyptian-stuff\" target=\"_blank\">The god depicted as having the head of a bull is not thought of as being literally a person with the head of a bull</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm just gonna note that the description and the rules don't say dead bodies, at least not in a blatent direct way. </div> </div> </div>They were Lifeless whose ritually-created forms were made from dead animals in 1e and they're still Lifeless in 2e, where that term still means &quot;undead&quot; and this type of Lifeless in particular still occupies the same band of Twilight as ghosts. Odds are thin that making them on purpose isn't still a process that involves death and taxidermy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So when I looked at the nature of the idea all I saw was &quot;someone creating chimeric monsters&quot; and to that I say &quot;cool!&quot; I also thought 'tomb guardians' and hidden monsters in spaces that have laid untouched for centuries and such. </div> </div> </div>If you want tomb guardians without specific contrivances that make an Amkhat to act differently than they do, you'd be better served looking to Mage for this sort of thing. As it stands, most &quot;tomb guardian&quot; Amkhata are going to be hovering around a relic and waiting for it to break so they can act on the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T22:15:04-08:00","id":1350976,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar661_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"661\" data-vbnamecard=\"661\">LordHeru</a> Take personal note of what ideas you're thinking of and what you might want to accomplish. When the previews are finally finished so everyone has a better understanding of what the baseline is, if you need any help realizing your ideas on how the preview materials can serve you for what you're looking for, then a thread can be created specifically for that task. Then people who want to help can pitch in and the people who don't want to help can just ignore the thread or a moderator can be involved if necessary.<br /> <br /> I'd suggest creating the thread now, because I think this tangent isn't being very helpful currently, but it might be a little premature without more rules accessible regarding Amkhata.<br /> <br /> But I'd be willing to participate in such a thread and give suggestions as to what I would do in order to fulfill whatever parameters you want met.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T22:25:40-08:00","id":1350977,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar851_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"851\" data-vbnamecard=\"851\">Paradim</a> That's not a bad idea, though right now it was mostly a random thought I had rather than something that needed in-depth development and such. But I will keep that in mind, especially if or when further ideas come to me. <br /> <br /> Actually, speaking of that, I'm looking forward to the new update drop coming in a couple of hours. A new chapter becoming available is gonna be nice to see. Especially as Chapter 5 is where we see the immortal templates and other stuff, including I assume Sekhem Sorcerers. Which will probably lead to me having lots of thoughts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But yeah, thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T00:59:41-08:00","id":1350993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350935#post1350935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...then believe me, my response isn't going to be being offended and shoot down the idea as BadWrongFun.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's totally fair! I just don't think people should be surprised when certain ideas aren't published in official material, especially when it would conflict with the themes or setting of the game.<br /> <br /> It's like wanting Sekhem start at 1 and then increase as you buy it with experience: if that's more fun for your gaming group then you can do it because you can hack the game to be whatever you want, and I won't stop you, but I might <i>question</i> you and <i>defend the default</i>, but don't be surprised that it's not the official, published mechanic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T01:34:24-08:00","id":1350995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350993#post1350993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's totally fair! I just don't think people should be surprised when certain ideas aren't published in official material, especially when it would conflict with the themes or setting of the game.<br /> <br /> It's like wanting Sekhem start at 1 and then increase as you buy it with experience: if that's more fun for your gaming group then you can do it because you can hack the game to be whatever you want, and I won't stop you, but I might <i>question</i> you and <i>defend the default</i>, but don't be surprised that it's not the official, published mechanic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The default doesn't need defending. Questioning can actually be helpful in further refining ideas to make stuff more fleshed out and prepared for the table.<br /> <br /> Also, if you check back with everything I've said regarding this tangent, I've been very clear that I'm talking about houserules, things that I would want to do with the likely material, and how I can adapt what is available to my own purposes. I rather like preserving the themes of sacrifice in exchange for power, and so I would prefer having rituals creating such horrors to be bloody affairs involving dead animals, blood and a willing sacrifice.<br /> <br /> I generally encourage my players to enjoy having their characters do messed up stuff, emphasizing that their characters are monsters and to explore doing dark things for power. I take no control over their characters in a scene because I want the player to always have agency over what their character does, even when their character would have no agency over themselves. For example, if I have a player of a werewolf go into Death Rage, I'll present the player with two options: 1) They play their character as they want during the Death Rage and I will liberally bribe them with Beats for doing things the player wants to happen that will cause their character any grief. 2) I do a Cut-to-Black, then have a discussion with the player as to what scenarios they're comfortable their character waking up to and finding out what they've done. If the player doesn't want any of their character's friends hurt while the character is uncontrollable, then none of their character's friends get hurt. I'll engineer the scene to keep them safe.<br /> <br /> One of the things I love about Chronicles of Darkness games is being able to have a safe environment to share a story of horror, dark things, and taking the role of the monster. This is why I emphasize buy-in, both on a player being interested in an idea, and being able to sell me on the idea. Both parties need to be willing and consenting for it to work, which is why I generally stay away from &quot;surprise&quot; events. I dearly love the Beat system for being able to bribe players and reward them for complicating things for their characters, especially when showcasing their characters as monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T05:27:56-08:00","id":1351017,"title":"","content":"Well everything about the Judge's incarnations is awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T05:46:02-08:00","id":1351022,"title":"","content":"So the Swarm Headed are a Hunter in Darkness best \u201cfriend\u201d.<br /> <br /> Fricking swagger jacking the Hosts xD<br /> <br /> And the Sphinx change the game a bit, but this isn\u2019t unprecedented.. there was that one Fasad/Amkhat hybrid in first ed after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 11-26-2019, 08:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T06:27:16-08:00","id":1351027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351017#post1351017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well everything about the Judge's incarnations is awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad you like 'em! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T06:54:33-08:00","id":1351029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350961#post1350961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is fine if that's what you want to do at your table, but realize it is a significant departure from the setting as written. I'd balk at having one of the major examples antagonists in the setting as a pet for the same reason I'd balk at giving a Mage summoning up abyssal entities or a werewolf getting a greater wound spirit as the pack totem.</div> </div> </div> </div>But mages summoning Abyssal entities and werewolves taking wound spirits as Totems is not only fully possible but also something that happens in the setting. Often as antagonists rather than players, but nothing stops you from playing villains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T06:55:15-08:00","id":1351030,"title":"","content":"Question: if a body-thief becomes a sadhik, do they still have access to their ability to switch bodies?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T08:19:21-08:00","id":1351044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1350995#post1350995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The default doesn't need defending. Questioning can actually be helpful in further refining ideas to make stuff more fleshed out and prepared for the table.<br /> <br /> Also, if you check back with everything I've said regarding this tangent, I've been very clear that I'm talking about houserules, things that I would want to do with the likely material, and how I can adapt what is available to my own purposes. I rather like preserving the themes of sacrifice in exchange for power, and so I would prefer having rituals creating such horrors to be bloody affairs involving dead animals, blood and a willing sacrifice.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, if your talking house rules, that's great. I think the line about being offended by GoodBadFun or whatever it was could probably have been phrased better. Sounded like a crack at STs who preferred to keep the Amkhata as antagonists like they are portrayed in the setting. I think they work better as such and that it dilutes the horror if the PCs can make their own without major consequences, but I don't begrudge STs for doing so in their own games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T08:19:21-08:00","id":1351045,"title":"","content":"DOUBLE POST, NEVER MIND.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2244,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","user":"nothri","date":". 11-26-2019, 12:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T08:23:00-08:00","id":1351046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351029#post1351029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But mages summoning Abyssal entities and werewolves taking wound spirits as Totems is not only fully possible but also something that happens in the setting. Often as antagonists rather than players, but nothing stops you from playing villains.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I mean, a player is also free to go to a gas station, fill up a can, dump the contents on himself, and strike a match. Just because players have the ability to make these choices doesn't mean they aren't bad ideas that are likely to end badly for the PC. An Amkhata needs to be fed on a steady diet of Sekhem or it goes feral. Raising one is not sustainable under normal circumstances. Sooner or later you will run out of vessels, or fall back to Duat, and then its going to blow up in your face.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T09:33:58-08:00","id":1351059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351046#post1351046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, a player is also free to go to a gas station, fill up a can, dump the contents on himself, and strike a match. Just because players have the ability to make these choices doesn't mean they aren't bad ideas that are likely to end badly for the PC. An Amkhata needs to be fed on a steady diet of Sekhem or it goes feral. Raising one is not sustainable under normal circumstances. Sooner or later you will run out of vessels, or fall back to Duat, and then its going to blow up in your face.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which does not contradict my point. The opposite, in fact. Bad ideas (for the characters) are often good ideas (for the players) because they provide new sources of story and gameplay. Bad ideas have made for some of the most memorable and fun sessions I've ever had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T09:52:25-08:00","id":1351063,"title":"","content":"New preview is up: <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/339646881/mummy-the-curse-2nd-edition/posts/2694143\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects.../posts/2694143</a><br /> <br /> And wow. I freaking adore the benebenet - and all the potential boss forms with the Shuankshen's ability to turn into Titan Amkhat and the ability of a Judge to fuse with their emissaries for a short time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T10:56:52-08:00","id":1351070,"title":"","content":"Good news for those wanting amkhata minions/tomb guardians:<br /> 1. Amkhata are not called Lifeless<br /> 2. Arisen and shuanksen (sp?) are both mentioned as beings that may have amkhata serving them<br /> 3. &quot;Some Arisen have found ways to summon, capture, and tame the Menqi to serve as eternally loyal guardians of their resting places.&quot;<br /> 4. &quot;These destructive loners, volatile bruisers, and raging terrors of Twilight are the sorcerer\u2019s greatest servant, the immortal\u2019s most lethal weapon, the Judge\u2019s most feared messenger.&quot;<br /> <br /> Doesn't seem to be an indication that their use is forbidden to the Arisen or whatever anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T11:23:00-08:00","id":1351077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351044#post1351044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, if your talking house rules, that's great. I think the line about being offended by GoodBadFun or whatever it was could probably have been phrased better. Sounded like a crack at STs who preferred to keep the Amkhata as antagonists like they are portrayed in the setting. I think they work better as such and that it dilutes the horror if the PCs can make their own without major consequences, but I don't begrudge STs for doing so in their own games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I've been absolutely crystal clear and repeatedly, of only talking about house rules to achieve a specific goal that I want for my own games. I disagree that it dilutes the horror, instead it provides another avenue for a type of horror that the player got to bring on their character through their own choices.<br /> <br /> To clarify, the comment on BadWrongFun is about STs or players who complain about setting or rules changes that happen in someone else's game that they're not involved with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T11:23:37-08:00","id":1351078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351070#post1351070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good news for those wanting amkhata minions/tomb guardians:<br /> 1. Amkhata are not called Lifeless<br /> 2. Arisen and shuanksen (sp?) are both mentioned as beings that may have amkhata serving them<br /> 3. &quot;Some Arisen have found ways to summon, capture, and tame the Menqi to serve as eternally loyal guardians of their resting places.&quot;<br /> 4. &quot;These destructive loners, volatile bruisers, and raging terrors of Twilight are the sorcerer\u2019s greatest servant, the immortal\u2019s most lethal weapon, the Judge\u2019s most feared messenger.&quot;<br /> <br /> Doesn't seem to be an indication that their use is forbidden to the Arisen or whatever anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's interesting. ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T12:09:13-08:00","id":1351089,"title":"","content":"There is much potential in reading 2e from the perspective of 2e only and not automatically taking in what came before as still official! <br /> <br /> <br /> Chapter Five Thoughts<br /> <br /> * Amkhata - Like the fluff and like the mechanics. I see many uses for these rules so thumbs up on that. <br /> <br /> So Neter-Khertet is the mortal world right, I wish it said that rather than using this term. <br /> <br /> This section also gave me a thought - what is the difference between Essence and Sekhem. <br /> <br /> The Dread Powers are cool. They have lots of potential. <br /> <br /> * Ephemeral Dead - This is a good and useful section. <br /> <br /> * Shuankhsen - As monstrous foes this is very useful. <br /> <br /> But the part of this section that I like the most are its various Bane Rites. They are bits of interesting magic, and while bad are also quite mechanically useful. Some in fact I could see being useful with some fluff or whatnot manipulation. So yeah this section got me very interested. <br /> <br /> Also of interest are the Bane Affinities. Not so much because I want them used by characters but what they represent, the power they bring forth. <br /> <br /> That said Swarm Messenger is particularly cool. <br /> <br /> * The Judges - A very thematically interesting and useful section. Very interesting. <br /> <br /> So I should admit that on one hand I dislike the whole mummies are bound to the Judges element of Mummy. BUT, on the otherhand, this section has me going &quot;Oh boy, look at the Judges, wow, aren't they and their forces cool!&quot; So there is that. hehe<br /> <br /> Emanations are AWESOME. Like very very cool. Like full of so much fantastic potential from a campaign and setting potential. So yeah, this is really really nifty. <br /> <br /> And if Emenations aren't enough you then have Avatars. Which is AWESOME X2. There is something brilliant about beings of the underworld reaching through the layers of reality to 'directly' manifest there power in the world. Brilliant and utterly scary, and that is awesome! <br /> <br /> The various examples here are pretty cool to. They are each useful for particular campaign purposes, and that is nifty. <br /> <br /> THE IMMORTALS<br /> <br /> The format for this section is logical. The descriptions for the various groups make sense. That said, I wish there was more mechanical crunch - which in this case means POWERS - for the various Immortal types within each part. <br /> <br /> The Reborn are cool though the curse element doesn't work for me, though thankfully I can easily ignore that element and such. <br /> <br /> The Reborn having a potential for non-linear time is a nifty little added feature - for campaigns that what such a feature. <br /> <br /> I wish the Reborn society was described rather than saying something like &quot;the Reborn often find a way to meet.&quot; I think them having a society would have been cool. <br /> <br /> On other Immortals I really hope that when we see the Purified in 2e it is not decided to give them a curse. They didn't have that in 1e, and that was fine! <br /> <br /> Endless Micro-Template<br /> <br /> Okay, this is a brilliant way to go about it. So thumbs up on that. <br /> <br /> Gift of Years is AWESOME. I like the nature of it. I like how it is structured. (I do kind of wish that there is a potential for gaining 6+ dots in the merit for really really powerful Endless.) <br /> <br /> I like the fact that using this method a Reborn could gain things like Telepathy, Telekinesis, and on and on. Its a cool way to go about it. <br /> <br /> I also like how Gift of Years gives the character the Sekhem trait at 1 and that to increase it requires spending experience. That is awesome! <br /> <br /> On Endless Potency. When you use Sekhem to activate it do you loose the dot permanently, meaning the need to regain it by spending XP. Or does it recharge at some rate? I hope the later. I think it would be limiting to have to increase Sekhem again. <br /> <br /> Supernatural Resistance is cool too. <br /> <br /> I would have liked some sort of merits that grant access to Pillars. But that is not super hard for me to create on my own so yeah. <br /> <br /> *Sorcerers<br /> <br /> The fluff description of Sorcerers are cool. I like how Arisen think they are only from Irem and never to be brought again but the truth is they are wrong. <br /> <br /> Honestly, this is what I have been saying. The secrets of Sekhem manipulation were developed once and thus can be developed again. So this is nifty. <br /> <br /> On Sorcerous Rites I am not a fan of how things are limited to Resolve and Occult based on merit choices and would much rather you gain a number of free slots based on those while other slots can be purchased as merits. <br /> <br /> Open Rites. Lots of potential there. I especially LOVE the one called Creating a Vestige, hehe. <br /> <br /> Random question. Can an immortal via the Gift of Years merit be a Sekhem Sorceror. And if so would it be better to organize the supernatural merits they gain under the Gift of Years rules or the Open Rites rules. Or maybe both, depending on where the power best fits. (So Telepathy might be a supernatural merit under Gift of Years while Creating a Vestige or Amkhata summoning would be an Open Rite.)<br /> <br /> Vestige Creation. Yes. Yes. YES!!!! Love this section. <br /> <br /> On imprinting a Memory I could totally see many benefits to say having a Reborn do it. I mean they experienced many lives and may in fact have experiences that can be useful. <br /> <br /> On memory would something like Editic Memory or something else giving perfect memory provide a boost or benefit to the roll? <br /> <br /> Also, so on Sekhem use. If a character with Sekhem based on the Gift of Years merit uses his Sekhem then he wouldn't have to find a way to create Sekhem like someone else may right. He has an easy available source for it. <br /> <br /> The section on Creating Relics is cool. First, like I said before, I like how Vessel is the overarching term, Vestige is the simple version, and Relic is the more advanced version. Making it 'easy' for a sorceror to create a Vestige is really cool. BUT so is making there have various side effects. The whole Judges know about the purified Sekhem that now exists and so seeks to hunt it is very very interesting. <br /> <br /> Closed Rites. <br /> <br /> Okay. Honestly. I have to admit to not being a fan of them. At least not from the perspective of the powers being used by a Player Character. They sound/seem fine from a NPC magic user standpoint but not so much if they were being made available to a player. <br /> <br /> Additionally I am so very much not a fan of the Rule of Three element. Not a fan of such convoluted elements to casting. <br /> <br /> Last Dynasty International - A very interesting and fun enemy faction. Especially when one adds the difficulties to dealing with them due to lets say public good will. <br /> <br /> I'm imagining the PC discovering a facility and finding a number of Arisen tied down and being used for their Sekhem. Its a horrible discovery but one that would probably be an epic story within the campaign. <br /> <br /> The other groups have their fun potentials for various campaign ideas, so that is cool. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T12:11:27-08:00","id":1351090,"title":"","content":"Holy shit. The ritual to summon Amkhata only gets a dice penalty if &quot;Ammut or a Judge of Duat disapproves of the ritual&quot;. A hefty dice penalty of -5, but still. Only a modifier and not one that is always assumed. Remember guys, it's only blasphemy if the &quot;wrong&quot; people do it! This is &quot;justified&quot; as having an Arisen lead the summoning ritual adds a +3 dice modifier!<br /> <br /> And we've also got this line &quot;Mortals have long used Amkhata as devastating weapons of war, but this manifestation is impermanent.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T12:16:36-08:00","id":1351091,"title":"","content":"Soooo question on the Reborn. Do they have the whole same sanctity of experience thing that Arisen have? Do they get to keep the experience achievements from a past life in order to better improve in the current one or do they have to do it all again. I do admit that in some ways having them have to do it again isn't that bad - experinece is gained easier (this being a game) and with them having good memory of their past lives it won't be hard for them to regain say telepathy or telekinesis or vestige crafting. While a normal human would have to undertake long rituals and uncover secret occult lore, they know its possible, they know the paths that the soul require to unlock it, and they can do so 'easily.'<br /> <br /> But yeah, I am trying to imagine say a Reborn campaign and how would such things work.<br /> <br /> That said, the whole mention of how some reborn are said to have some ability to effect when and where their next lives will be to me says their is potential for them having a non-linear experience too. WHICH IS AWESOME!!!!<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> Just had a thought.<br /> <br /> A character with Gift of Years merit automatically has a Sekhem Trait, which as part of its basic effects grant supernatural potency. So in that case why would they gain the Supernatural Potency merit. <br /> <br /> Also, what exactly does an immortal with the Gift of Years merit granting Sekhem gain as part of that trait. Which of the sekhem features carry over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 11-26-2019, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T12:41:42-08:00","id":1351096,"title":"","content":"Amkhata can have opposable thumbs. Nothing can stop them now. Humanity is doomed. I see why Ammut is winning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T12:48:42-08:00","id":1351097,"title":"","content":"Weird... I thought we weren't having rules for Ghosts in the 2nd Edition core book for Mummy...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T13:04:43-08:00","id":1351099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351097#post1351097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weird... I thought we weren't having rules for Ghosts in the 2nd Edition core book for Mummy...?</div> </div> </div> </div>I changed my mind and made a cut elsewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T13:10:02-08:00","id":1351100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351099#post1351099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I changed my mind and made a cut elsewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, understood! I hope we'll get to see that cut sometime in the future, still. ^.^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T13:10:46-08:00","id":1351102,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar661_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"661\" data-vbnamecard=\"661\">LordHeru</a> Neter-Khertet refers to Twilight. Specifically, the frequency of deathly Twilight as it is experienced by mummies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T13:13:05-08:00","id":1351103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351102#post1351102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar661_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"661\" data-vbnamecard=\"661\">LordHeru</a> Neter-Khertet refers to Twilight. Specifically, the frequency of deathly Twilight as it is experienced by mummies.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Is Neter-Khertet a different frequency than that experienced by ghosts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T13:21:52-08:00","id":1351104,"title":"","content":"Yes, like how there is a Frequency for the God-Machine\u2019s Infrastructure and angels or the one for spirits. It\u2019s multilayered psuedo reality stacked on top of our physical plane, but it stops just before you get to actual parallel realms like the Shadow or Underworld.<br /> <br /> Think of it as different radio channels, but radio channels that have \u201cliving\u201d things infesting the white noise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 11-26-2019, 04:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T13:25:10-08:00","id":1351105,"title":"","content":"Technically, Neter-Khertet IS ghostly Twilight. Mummies experience it a bit differently, though, even in 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T13:25:56-08:00","id":1351106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351099#post1351099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I changed my mind and made a cut elsewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Probably for the best, given how Judge avatars are ephemeral entities, as are Amkhat. As well as how key ghosts are to the Anshem.<br /> <br /> Also, can I say it's hilarious how JRPG final bosses are now a minor splat?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T13:26:22-08:00","id":1351107,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"309\" data-vbnamecard=\"309\">White Oak Dragon</a> gotcha. Interesting. hehe<br /> <br /> So basically those beings are slightly out of phase with the material world but are able to come to the mortal plane when bothered. Makes sense.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Also i think adding rules for ghosts in a game about beings that are around the underworld make sense. <br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> Also still very much looking forward to more info and discussion on the Reborn, they fascinate me. They also have a lot of fun Dark Era using potential if the line about choosing a past or future point life gets used in a chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 11-26-2019, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T13:29:14-08:00","id":1351108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351105#post1351105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically, Neter-Khertet IS ghostly Twilight. Mummies experience it a bit differently, though, even in 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll admit, I find that kind of confusing...<br /> <br /> I'll have to read things extra carefully.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T13:33:05-08:00","id":1351109,"title":"","content":"Also while I enjoy the Shuanksen, their relationship with Sekhem May need to be returned to the old system in my game, because losing a Dot Of Sekhem a day unless they are constantly murdering and eating at least one person every day untenable in a modern setting, never mind actually maintaining a cult longer than a week or two before the Shuanksen fucks over its own power base before they can really do any major damage.<br /> <br /> That may be the intention to show how damned and desperate the Bane Mummies have to be... but it just devolves them from an actually frightening enemy to a blood mad super zombie that might be able to use one Bane Ritual in a descent if they are lucky.. and if they are REALLY lucky it might fulfill their goal before they are obliterated by the tide of Arisen, cultists, hunters, and whoever the fuck else calls that city home.<br /> <br /> But as they are now, I\u2019m disappointed by their reduced ability to be a long term opponent in favor of being a scary undead Slasher villain that at best causes a huge amount of trouble for a short time instead of being a constant source of fear or dread during ones descent.<br /> <br /> Sorry for venting...It\u2019s just sad that they are pretty much just human shaped Amkhata- literally in some cases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 11-26-2019, 04:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T13:34:16-08:00","id":1351110,"title":"","content":"So I have to admit to not really seeing what super benefit having Sekhem does for the Endless. Especially as it doesn't have its own power point pool or way to be refreshed beyond experience and such. <br /> <br /> A part of me wishes that Sekhem points (Which would obviously have to gain a recharge and point pool mechanic) could be used instead of Willpower by the Endless to activate their supernatural merit based powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T13:48:29-08:00","id":1351111,"title":"","content":"Rite of Eternal Chains is... interesting....<br /> <br /> &quot;Success: A Fasad is created. You can see through their eyes as a Reflexive action, and dismiss or conjure them from wisps of mystical air as an Instant Action.&quot;<br /> <br /> Are Fasad the Shuanksen's pokemon? ^.^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T13:50:41-08:00","id":1351112,"title":"","content":"\u201cI choose you, Rotten Larry!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c Kiiiiilll... Meeeee!\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T14:07:58-08:00","id":1351115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351109#post1351109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also while I enjoy the Shuanksen, their relationship with Sekhem May need to be returned to the old system in my game, because losing a Dot Of Sekhem a day unless they are constantly murdering and eating at least one person every day untenable in a modern setting, never mind actually maintaining a cult longer than a week or two before the Shuanksen fucks over its own power base before they can really do any major damage.<br /> <br /> That may be the intention to show how damned and desperate the Bane Mummies have to be... but it just devolves them from an actually frightening enemy to a blood mad super zombie that might be able to use one Bane Ritual in a descent if they are lucky.. and if they are REALLY lucky it might fulfill their goal before they are obliterated by the tide of Arisen, cultists, hunters, and whoever the fuck else calls that city home.<br /> <br /> But as they are now, I\u2019m disappointed by their reduced ability to be a long term opponent in favor of being a scary undead Slasher villain that at best causes a huge amount of trouble for a short time instead of being a constant source of fear or dread during ones descent.<br /> <br /> Sorry for venting...It\u2019s just sad that they are pretty much just human shaped Amkhata- literally in some cases.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, they're supposed to be masterminds; they have cults for a reason.<br /> <br /> One a week or month is appropriately thematic for the cannibal goddess' chosen, but one a day? Yeah, no, they're not much they can do apart from look for their next meal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T14:07:58-08:00","id":1351116,"title":"","content":"[DOBLE POST HAS BEEN SACRIFICED TO DUAT. THANK YOU FOR YOUR COOPERATION.]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013