[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T14:50:59-08:00","id":1351130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351128#post1351128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did I miss info about the Fiends? I thought it would be in this chapter...</div> </div> </div> </div>The fiends are in Chapter 7, in the Duat section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T14:57:13-08:00","id":1351132,"title":"","content":"Upon going over it again two thoughts come to me. <br /> <br /> 1 is Mummy gameline specific - if the lesser immortals are playable then a bit more structure on their character creation is needed. Especially insofar as how Sekhem works with them. <br /> <br /> 2 is a general thematic idea - which is that the non-linear nature of mummy would be PERFECT for a Trinity Continuum game based on high powered time and dimension hopping Talents. This particular thought then had me thinking I hope at some point in the future those who wrote the non-linear nature of mummy get to write an article or a section or some material using said idea in a Trinity setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T15:12:32-08:00","id":1351138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351104#post1351104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, like how there is a Frequency for the God-Machine\u2019s Infrastructure and angels or the one for spirits. It\u2019s multilayered psuedo reality stacked on top of our physical plane, but it stops just before you get to actual parallel realms like the Shadow or Underworld.<br /> <br /> Think of it as different radio channels, but radio channels that have \u201cliving\u201d things infesting the white noise.</div> </div> </div> </div>What gets me is that the Amkhata are described as beasts that feed on \u201cghosts and spirits, to shades, to their own kind\u201d. Since ghosts and spirits have different \u201cfrequencies\u201d, how can the Amkhata feed on them? <br /> <br /> Perhaps the Duat \u201cchannel\u201d overlaps with both the spirit and ghost \u201cchannels\u201d?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T15:13:41-08:00","id":1351139,"title":"","content":"Kinda disappointed that there was no mention of the Harvesters among the Immortals- their origin story does tie to Egypt, after all, and they are extremely fitting IMO. Oh well, nothing that little homebrew can't mend.<br /> <br /> I still need to give some more in depth reading for this chapter, but most of it seems to be cool. While I would have wished for a more developed mechanics for the Immortals, space limitations and the thank that they are not the main players of this game does mean they get less room. Still, good chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T15:49:40-08:00","id":1351145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351138#post1351138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What gets me is that the Amkhata are described as beasts that feed on \u201cghosts and spirits, to shades, to their own kind\u201d. Since ghosts and spirits have different \u201cfrequencies\u201d, how can the Amkhata feed on them? <br /> <br /> Perhaps the Duat \u201cchannel\u201d overlaps with both the spirit and ghost \u201cchannels\u201d?</div> </div> </div> </div>Very possible. Perhaps the very Rite Of Return scrambled Neter-Kherit\u2019s \u201cfrequency\u201d as well as forever breaking time, causing it to more or less share the same broadband spectrum as ghosts and spirits, as it were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T16:39:08-08:00","id":1351157,"title":"","content":"So, we have antagonists. The manifestations of the Judges are <i>awesome</i>, in multiple meanings of the word, Bane powers enable some disturbingly large scale problems (though some seem a little mechanically off at the moment), and Amkhata are scary with how much more developed they are. But I am <i>immesurably disappointed</i> that the False Ka is no longer a thing.<br /> <br /> Each Part that makes up an Amkhat now means significantly more in terms of their traits, and they exist across a wide and useful gradient of power, but they can't really <i>bleed bees</i> or <i>spew miasmic fungus</i> from their wounds, and they don't have any particular Dread Powers to stand in for that, which is honestly a shame. The False Ka was a phenomenally distinct and creepy element of Amkhata in 1st edition, and I was looking forward to seeing what the new one would do with it, especially given some of the new Parts. Was there a notable reason to cut the concept?<br /> <br /> (Overall, these are fantastic foes, though.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 11-26-2019, 08:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T16:51:59-08:00","id":1351161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351157#post1351157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, we have antagonists. The manifestations of the Judges are <i>awesome</i>, in multiple meanings of the word, Bane Rites enable some disturbingly large scale problems (though some seem a little mechanically off at the moment), and Amkhata are scary with how much more developed they are. But I am <i>immesurably disappointed</i> that the False Ka is no longer a thing.<br /> <br /> Each Part that makes up an Amkhat now means significantly more in terms of their traits, and they exist across a wide and useful gradient of power, but they can't really <i>bleed bees</i> or <i>spew miasmic fungus</i> from their wounds, and they don't have any particular Dread Powers to stand in for that, which is honestly a shame. The False Ka was a phenomenally distinct and creepy element of Amkhata in 1st edition, and I was looking forward to seeing what the new one would do with it, especially given some of the new Parts. Was there a notable reason to cut the concept?<br /> <br /> (Overall, these are fantastic foes, though.)</div> </div> </div> </div> I think it's as simple as Amkhata exist on all frequencies, like Changeling Helldivers on a Helldive to twilight. <br /> <br /> I do wander if Amkhata can feed on Angels, Helldivers, and Werewolves it finds in Twilight? Is it just Emphereal beings in twilight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T16:59:16-08:00","id":1351164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351139#post1351139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kinda disappointed that there was no mention of the Harvesters among the Immortals- their origin story does tie to Egypt, after all, and they are extremely fitting IMO. Oh well, nothing that little homebrew can't mend.<br /> <br /> I still need to give some more in depth reading for this chapter, but most of it seems to be cool. While I would have wished for a more developed mechanics for the Immortals, space limitations and the thank that they are not the main players of this game does mean they get less room. Still, good chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You might be able to do Harvesters as a subset of Blood Bathers or Eternals. Harvesters Blood Bathing ritual invovles bathing their ritual weapon in blood instead of their bodies and it requires the blood of immortals. <br /> <br /> Or the weapon is a special eternal relic who curse is that it decays if it doesn't kill another immortal every so often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T17:00:13-08:00","id":1351165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351130#post1351130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The fiends are in Chapter 7, in the Duat section.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh thanks! It's weird though as they are anatongists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T17:12:03-08:00","id":1351167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351107#post1351107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> gotcha. Interesting. hehe<br /> <br /> So basically those beings are slightly out of phase with the material world but are able to come to the mortal plane when bothered. Makes sense.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Also i think adding rules for ghosts in a game about beings that are around the underworld make sense. <br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> Also still very much looking forward to more info and discussion on the Reborn, they fascinate me. They also have a lot of fun Dark Era using potential if the line about choosing a past or future point life gets used in a chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div> How about this, the Reborn can easily be created by Mages and Changelings. Mages have a spell that can grant Supernatural merits, like the Merit that makes a human Endless, and Changelings can use Oniernomancy to grant Supernatural Merits (a lot of work). Arguable this means Changelings and Mages can make Endless and Sorcerers or Endless Sorcerers. They can do this with any Template (or Supernatural power) granted byba Merit, like Psychic Vampires, Infected, The Plain, Endless, ect...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T17:29:17-08:00","id":1351170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351167#post1351167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How about this, the Reborn can easily be created by Mages and Changelings. Mages have a spell that can grant Supernatural merits, like the Merit that makes a human Endless, and Changelings can use Oniernomancy to grant Supernatural Merits (a lot of work). Arguable this means Changelings and Mages can make Endless and Sorcerers or Endless Sorcerers. They can do this with any Template (or Supernatural power) granted byba Merit, like Psychic Vampires, Infected, The Plain, Endless, ect...</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea of a Mage (I like and own Mage so I have some knowledge that, in comparison to Changeling which I don't have any experience with) using their powers on a person to basically empower slash enrich their soul into an Endless state that can access supernatural power intrigues me. What makes it interesting is creating a power system out of the supernatural merit system is a pretty fun and useful one. <br /> <br /> I like the idea of an immortal (most likely Reborn) Sekhem Sorcerer, and I think there is a lot of potential for that. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T17:46:03-08:00","id":1351175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351167#post1351167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How about this, the Reborn can easily be created by Mages and Changelings. Mages have a spell that can grant Supernatural merits, like the Merit that makes a human Endless, and Changelings can use Oniernomancy to grant Supernatural Merits (a lot of work). Arguable this means Changelings and Mages can make Endless and Sorcerers or Endless Sorcerers. They can do this with any Template (or Supernatural power) granted byba Merit, like Psychic Vampires, Infected, The Plain, Endless, ect...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wouldn't that all go away if the spell ends?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T17:47:03-08:00","id":1351176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351170#post1351170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The idea of a Mage (I like and own Mage so I have some knowledge that, in comparison to Changeling which I don't have any experience with) using their powers on a person to basically empower slash enrich their soul into an Endless state that can access supernatural power intrigues me. What makes it interesting is creating a power system out of the supernatural merit system is a pretty fun and useful one. <br /> <br /> I like the idea of an immortal (most likely Reborn) Sekhem Sorcerer, and I think there is a lot of potential for that. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div> I think Eternals and Blood Bathers and Magical Body Snatchers are more likely to be Sorcerers as Reborn, they all study the occult to become immortals. <br /> <br /> And another potential source of Immortals could be the True Fae themselves, and they are more likely to do that then Changelings and none Lich mages. <br /> <br /> One twisted thing a Mage could do is replace a humans mind with a Duplicate of the Mages and then turn them into Reborn. That gives the Mages mind a kind of Immortality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T17:52:49-08:00","id":1351179,"title":"","content":"For an Eternal with a damaged, but not destroyed Eternal Relic, if you repair the Relic, does that restore the Eternal? <br /> <br /> Also is it just me or are Eternals better off seeking help from Changelings, Demons, and Mages who can put their Relic outside the reach of Arisen, Lifeless, Amakhata, other Immortals, and most Sorcerers? A Changelings has no use for Sekhem, but can place the Relic in it's Hollow where a Relic hunting Mummy and other predators can't reach it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T17:57:32-08:00","id":1351181,"title":"","content":"Can say Changelings and other splats take the Sorcerer merits? I'm pretty sure they can still conduct open rites without them, like almost everyone else can, just curious. <br /> <br /> I think a Autumn Court Sorcerer creating Vestiges and using other Open rites solves an issue that some folks had with the 2e Autumn Courts. <br /> <br /> Of all the Splatbook linked Splats Sorcerers and Endless are the most useful to other gamelines IMHO. <br /> <br /> For example I can see Sorcerers learning the keys to a Hedge Gate as an Open Rite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T18:10:06-08:00","id":1351188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351181#post1351181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can say Changelings and other splats take the Sorcerer merits?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're explicitly Supernatural Merits, which can only be taken by mortals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351175#post1351175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't that all go away if the spell ends?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, and oneiromancy can only grant Supernatural Merits for the duration of a story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T18:21:35-08:00","id":1351192,"title":"","content":"The section on Shuankhsen manages to be both great (frankly, Bane Rites are much closer to what 2e Utterances should be like, even if Bane Rites and Affinities do suffer a little from the same problem of there just not being many of them) and kind of frustrating. As mentioned, forcing Shuankhsen to be relentless, non-stop murderers hurts their impact. It's also weird that their stats are capped at 5 when they have 10 Sekhem to play with. The sample Shuankhsen from 1e, with her Intelligence 6 that she couldn't use until she had hunted down and devoured the Sekhem of an Arisen or two, was a great concept and I'm not sure why that limitation is in place. I also just think the Sekhem 10 component feels... kind of off. These were the fuel for the Rite, it seems a bit strange that they came back with as much power within them as the principle beneficiaries.<br /> <br /> Those are all pretty minor quibbles though. The mechanics are stranger. There's chunks of the Bane Rite section that feel like they're meant to invoke some kind of flavour, but I'm hazy on the context. For example, the Rite of the Lost Cause has a different impact on the Shuankhsen's Cult based on their Remnant, but those effects are phrased as &quot;emotional bouts&quot;. That suggests to me that the effects are temporary, but we don't really have a time frame for when they trigger (presumably when the Rite is performed?) or how long they last for. On top of that, the &quot;emotional&quot; bouts experienced by the Cultists include &quot;Flesh-eaten, rotting vessels of death&quot;, which isn't precisely an emotional state. And why does Ren seemingly turn the Shuankhsen's own Cult against them? And the Rite also grants the Shuankhsen a Bane Rite or Affinity, but only once? That feels unnecessary, every Shuankhsen has this Rite, just add another starting Rite or Affinity to their total if you want them to have an extra one.<br /> <br /> Then there's the Bane Relic Rite, which reduces the &quot;Sekhem&quot; of a Relic to 1. Technically, Relics don't have a Sekhem rating, they have a dot rating which translates to Sekhem when consumed. What impact does reducing a Bane Relic's Sekhem to 1 actually have on the Relic? Is its power reduced to be on par with a Rank 1 Relic now? Does the Relic's rating also change to 1? (That would have the amusing side effect of making the Relic easier to find with Kepher by reducing the Scope of the investigation, and conversely makes it unfortunate if the Rite achieves an Exceptional Success on a relic a Shuankhsen is trying to use as bait.)<br /> <br /> Also, why does each Bane Rite have a &quot;Cult&quot; section? Is this meant to provide an indication of the kinds of cultists drawn in by the Bane Rite? It feels a little superfluous, not having any mechanical benefit that I can see. More problematically, the section is just... there, appearing without introduction or context several Bane Rites into the section, which makes it a tad hard to parse initially to determine what the reader is meant to make of those paragraphs.<br /> <br /> And I may have missed something, but I don't understand the relationship between Bane Rites and Affinities. When do you choose a Bane Rite in relation to a Bane Affinity, and why does the Remnant involved need to not match? Is it trying to say that a Shuankhsen with Sekhem Clot can't use Rite of the Storm?<br /> <br /> There's a lot of evocative language in this section, but sometimes the actual mechanics appear to be on the hazy side. I feel like a lot of the time I'm missing core rules that weren't detailed in the document. Maybe I'm just struggling because the broken up PDF format makes it a little awkward to flip back and forward between the relevant sections, but there are other niggles like Body Snatcher (is the ability to use it right before losing your last dot of Sekhem meant to allow the Shuankhsen to immediately then start a new Descent in a new body?), Schism of Flesh having a &quot;Curse&quot; in addition to the &quot;Decay&quot; of other Affinities (and that &quot;Curse&quot; being the cost of Beats, which isn't super relevant for what will typically be an NPC), and Swarm Messenger being really clunky (you need to have a Fasad present to use it? You attack with it, but the attack is a contested roll instead of just treating the target's Sheut as armour? Why does it give people a Tilt that will kill just about anyone within a minute, but the Tilt lasts a week? And why is this Decay the only one that both doesn't effect the Shuankhsen, and may well be beneficial to them?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T18:41:17-08:00","id":1351196,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Shuankshen section needs another editing pass. I think Schism of Flesh doesn't even have an &quot;activation&quot; mode, just a Curse <i>and </i>a Decay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T18:58:59-08:00","id":1351198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351175#post1351175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Wouldn't that all go away if the spell ends?</div> </div> </div> </div> Which is why you now hang it on your supernatural friend, of course they can be killed by supernatural dispelling it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T19:01:06-08:00","id":1351199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351188#post1351188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're explicitly Supernatural Merits, which can only be taken by mortals.<br /> <br /> Yep, and oneiromancy can only grant Supernatural Merits for the duration of a story.</div> </div> </div> </div> That is a completely indeterminate time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T19:03:44-08:00","id":1351200,"title":"","content":"I like to know what Shades are, although I'm guessing we will learn more about them in the Duat Chapter like Duat Fiends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T19:42:28-08:00","id":1351204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351199#post1351199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is a completely indeterminate time.</div> </div> </div> </div>The same &quot;completely indeterminate time&quot; that limits how often a cult can take cult actions without strain and how frequently vessel in a mummy's Lifeweb can be used for the Call, which also doesn't change the fact that oneiromancy <i>requires the target to meet the Merit's prerequisites and needs an appropriate action within the dreamscape</i>.<br /> <br /> Much like Bargain being listed as a Manifestation in Geist doesn't imply that mages can create Bound by giving it to a ghost through powerful Death spells, Mummy's Endless mechanically requiring a particular Supernatural Merit to represent their experience and safety net doesn't make them viable direct outcomes for Changeling's Dream Assailant Condition when the latter book references the list of Supernatural Merits in the ChroD corebook. The narrative doesn't support it as a natural outcome for those powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T20:14:00-08:00","id":1351208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351196#post1351196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the Shuankshen section needs another editing pass. I think Schism of Flesh doesn't even have an &quot;activation&quot; mode, just a Curse <i>and </i>a Decay.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not just Shuankhsen either. The Amkhat section could really use some more clarity on a few subjects (such as whether Natural Weaponry stacks on top of the natural weaponry provided by their body parts, or whether those body parts that provide attacks are meant to sound like they provide extra attacks in a single combat turn the way they did in 1e, a mechanic 2e has otherwise done away with). And the Judges section has some irregularities too. The mechanic that is meant to cause Arisen to descend faster in the presence of an Emanation actually does the opposite as written, applying a -2 penalty to the Sekhem roll and thus making it <i>less</i> likely that the Arisen will lose Sekhem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T20:20:50-08:00","id":1351210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351204#post1351204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The same &amp;quot;completely indeterminate time&amp;quot; that limits how often a cult can take cult actions without strain and how frequently vessel in a mummy's Lifeweb can be used for the Call, which also doesn't change the fact that oneiromancy <i>requires the target to meet the Merit's prerequisites and needs an appropriate action within the dreamscape</i>.<br /> <br /> Much like Bargain being listed as a Manifestation in Geist doesn't imply that mages can create Bound by giving it to a ghost through powerful Death spells, Mummy's Endless mechanically requiring a particular Supernatural Merit to represent their experience and safety net doesn't make them viable direct outcomes for Changeling's Dream Assailant Condition when the latter book references the list of Supernatural Merits in the ChroD corebook. The narrative doesn't support it as a natural outcome for those powers.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't agree. For example the Social Merits from Gift of Years granted by a Changelings, would linked to the Changeling. <br /> <br /> For example a Changeling fears that a dangerous stalker going after their boyfriend/girlfriend is a serious threat to their survival so the Changeling turns them into an Eternal by killing them or one of their Eidolons in the dream and stuffing their death into an object they Physically brought into the Dream, that becomes the Relic. They gain the Gift of Years Merit at one dot, which grants them Allies \u2022 the Changeling that made them an Eternal, that can be used to get the Changeling to hide their Eternal Relic in their Hollow. <br /> <br /> I mean these aren't the first immortals that Changelings can create, Psychic Vampires are. <br /> <br /> And Sorcerers are even easier for Changelings to create, just have the Changeling teach the rites to the Eidilons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T20:46:25-08:00","id":1351214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351210#post1351210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean these aren't the first immortals that Changelings can create, Psychic Vampires are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't agree, because Merit-based templates have a bigger impact on a character than temporary access to telekinesis or clairvoyance or omen-reading and nothing you do in a dream is going to substitute for being born to or having contact with the necessary external factors for psychic vampirism.<br /> <br /> You're welcome to do whatever you want in your own game, but the games are not made under the assumption that strained application of crossover mechanics from books published separate from the mechanic you're leveraging is going to work, much less be the norm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T20:49:17-08:00","id":1351215,"title":"","content":"I'm... honestly sorely disappointed by the lack of good content for Immortals. That was... literally the reason I supported this Kickstarter, and now I regret it. Psi Vamp has more detail and unique stuff than Immortals, who actually, by the way, ripped off one of Psi Vamp's merits. I feel ripped off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25382-tzauri","name":"Tzauri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T20:54:33-08:00","id":1351216,"title":"","content":"Looking just at the manuscript, there's some confusion concerning Sorcerers. On the one hand, we're told that a Sorcerer can only learn so many Rites (Resolve, or Resolve + Occult) \u2014 though it does suggest that you can stretch this limit by deliberately failing Breaking Points involving supernatural phenomena. And it definitely said that Open Rites count toward these limits. The first bit of confusion is that #2 says that you get one extra slot per level in Sorcerous Knowledge, but that you can't have more levels of Sorcerous Knowledge than you have does in Occult. But #4 says that everyone has a number of slots equivalent to Resolve, and that Sorcerous Knowledge gives you additional slots equal to Occult. Some clarity would be nice. <br /> <br /> And it also says that anyone can perform Open Rites. As well, Preview #2 speaks of Open Rite Mastery, a term which doesn't appear in later previews. That's two different approaches as to how to handle Open Rites. <br /> <br /> Which one is right? <br /> <br /> My preference would be for Open Rite Mastery, where said Mastery gives you more flexibility and reliability with the Open Rite instead of a virtual guarantee that if you deviate from the stated procedure even slightly, Bad Things Will Happen. One advantage of this is that you don't need to dedicate any of your slots to Open Rites if you don't want to, and you don't even have to have any slots to use them, which is consistent with the complete lack of \u201cRite Slots\u201d in the Chronicles of Darkness Rulebook; but you still get some benefit from putting an Open Rite into a slot (i.e., taking the time to master it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T21:27:09-08:00","id":1351219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tzauri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351215#post1351215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm... honestly sorely disappointed by the lack of good content for Immortals. That was... literally the reason I supported this Kickstarter, and now I regret it. Psi Vamp has more detail and unique stuff than Immortals, who actually, by the way, ripped off one of Psi Vamp's merits. I feel ripped off.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know that you can still back out, right? <br /> <br /> I agree with the sentiment, though: there's a virtual lack of crunch in the Immortals section. There should be at least as much crunch for Blood Bathers and Body Thieves as there is in Dark Eras Companion or World of Darkness: Immortals. And there should be as much crunch for the Eternals and the Reborn as there should be for the Blood Bathers and Body Thieves. <br /> <br /> If there's no room for it in the core book, you should put it in the Companion. <br /> <br /> Also: could you throw World of Darkness: Immortals into the Scroll of Fading Memories, preferably updated with a Rules Appendix that updates the rules to 2e standards (similar to the Rules Appendix that appeared in God-Machine Chronicle, but only covering the stuff that's specific to World of Darkness: Immortals)? That would be the next best thing to actually doing a second edition of it, and would nicely address my concerns about a lack of material for the Immortals: most of the necessary fluff is already there, save only for the connections between these the carrots Immortals and the Arisen; and even the mechanics aren't too far removed from 2e standards. It might even encourage some people who otherwise wouldn't have to take the Add-On. <br /> <br /> And finally: could the Blood Bather and Magical Body Thief rituals (and, if you go the route of updating WoD:I to 2e standards, the ritual for becoming a Purified) be presented in the context of Sorcerous Rites?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T21:30:22-08:00","id":1351220,"title":"","content":"To be honest, if there's one thing that makes me particularly cranky it's the existence of so many example Avatars. I mean, they aren't a problem in and of themselves and they're well written and evocative, but there's approximately half as many pages dedicated to providing sample Manifestations as there are dedicated to providing Utterances. Given that the Shuankhsen, for example, get precisely <i>one</i> sample character, that seems truly excessive. I've been tempering my disappointment with some aspects of the text (the fact that so few Judges are presented in detail for character creation ironically being one of them) by trying to be understanding about word count limitations, but good grief that is a lot of this chapter spent on sample versions of one particular antagonist class. It seems just excessive in comparison to the other antagonists in the chapter, and a part of me can't help but think of all those missing Affinities and Utterances we could have had instead. Sure, we hit some stretch goals to get some more and the developers are taking another crack at the existing ones, but it would have been nice to get a bit more word count on the player side of things without all that rigmarole, and I would be happy sacrificing basically all of the <i>eight</i> Avatars to get there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T21:30:56-08:00","id":1351221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351216#post1351216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking just at the manuscript, there's some confusion concerning Sorcerers. On the one hand, we're told that a Sorcerer can only learn so many Rites (Resolve, or Resolve + Occult) \u2014 though it does suggest that you can stretch this limit by deliberately failing Breaking Points involving supernatural phenomena. And it definitely said that Open Rites count toward these limits. The first bit of confusion is that #2 says that you get one extra slot per level in Sorcerous Knowledge, but that you can't have more levels of Sorcerous Knowledge than you have does in Occult. But #4 says that everyone has a number of slots equivalent to Resolve, and that Sorcerous Knowledge gives you additional slots equal to Occult. Some clarity would be nice. <br /> <br /> And it also says that anyone can perform Open Rites. As well, Preview #2 speaks of Open Rite Mastery, a term which doesn't appear in later previews. That's two different approaches as to how to handle Open Rites. <br /> <br /> Which one is right? <br /> <br /> My preference would be for Open Rite Mastery, where said Mastery gives you more flexibility and reliability with the Open Rite instead of a virtual guarantee that if you deviate from the stated procedure even slightly, Bad Things Will Happen. One advantage of this is that you don't need to dedicate any of your slots to Open Rites if you don't want to, and you don't even have to have any slots to use them, which is consistent with the complete lack of \u201cRite Slots\u201d in the Chronicles of Darkness Rulebook; but you still get some benefit from putting an Open Rite into a slot (i.e., taking the time to master it).</div> </div> </div> </div>It does look like a little clarification is needed.<br /> The Ritual Sorcerer Merit gives slots equal to Resolve. Sorcerous Knowledge gives an additional slot per dot, limited by your Occult dots.<br /> The mechanics for Open Rite Mastery are contained in chapter 5, but it seems the Mastery term was left out, which is something that needs to be fixed.<br /> Anybody can attempt Open Rites, no slots necessary. Placing an Open Rite in a slot gives Mastery over it, which grants added benefits when using it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T21:51:49-08:00","id":1351223,"title":"","content":"Interesting that Irem would recognize a deity solely dedicated to punishing slavers (An-Hotep) as one of their patron gods... given that the entire empire was built on mass slavery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T23:18:28-08:00","id":1351231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351223#post1351223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting that Irem would recognize a deity solely dedicated to punishing slavers (An-Hotep) as one of their patron gods... given that the entire empire was built on mass slavery.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't be surprised if the hypocrisy is part of the point. That whole thing of, &quot;It's not a bad thing if WE do it.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T23:48:50-08:00","id":1351233,"title":"","content":"I just skimmed the new update, so was I misunderstanding that manifestations of the Judges basically use the rules for Amkata?<br /> <br /> If so, is that simply a useful mechanical shorthand or does it imply a deeper relationship between the two?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T23:57:51-08:00","id":1351235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351164#post1351164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You might be able to do Harvesters as a subset of Blood Bathers or Eternals. Harvesters Blood Bathing ritual invovles bathing their ritual weapon in blood instead of their bodies and it requires the blood of immortals.<br /> <br /> Or the weapon is a special eternal relic who curse is that it decays if it doesn't kill another immortal every so often.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh, they should be their own thing IMO. Their &quot;immortal hunter&quot; is niche is unique enough for it. They aren't bound to their Scythe like the Eternal, and have a different play style than Blood Bathers.<br /> <br /> And in general, I agree that the Immortals content was very limited- I hoped were were going to get an appendix about them, where they are presented as supporting characters (like the Absent of Geist, or Ghouls or something in that line). They didn't get enough of unique merits, IMO, and while I'm not outright against the Endless template some things feel a bit clanky in it. It is weird that the mechanics for the Endless show up at the end instead of at the begining, which got me confused when reading the section, and the fact that each other &quot;non core&quot; immortal got maybe a line or two (when two of the immortals, Wardens and Harvesters, were dropped), felt unfulfilling. 2e Immortals got me really excited towards Mummy, and that feels more like a band aid than what I expected.<br /> <br /> I'm still backing the Kickstarter because I want Minor Guilds material, but Immortals should have deserved more wordcount IMO, both mechanically and setting wise, and some more unique mechanics/tricks for them. Like, if I had to chose between a reprint of a ghost section and more Endless wordcount, I would have preferred to see more about Immortals. Just my opinion on the subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 11-27-2019, 03:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T00:51:36-08:00","id":1351236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351220#post1351220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, if there's one thing that makes me particularly cranky it's the existence of so many example Avatars. I mean, they aren't a problem in and of themselves and they're well written and evocative, but there's approximately half as many pages dedicated to providing sample Manifestations as there are dedicated to providing Utterances. Given that the Shuankhsen, for example, get precisely <i>one</i> sample character, that seems truly excessive. I've been tempering my disappointment with some aspects of the text (the fact that so few Judges are presented in detail for character creation ironically being one of them) by trying to be understanding about word count limitations, but good grief that is a lot of this chapter spent on sample versions of one particular antagonist class. It seems just excessive in comparison to the other antagonists in the chapter, and a part of me can't help but think of all those missing Affinities and Utterances we could have had instead. Sure, we hit some stretch goals to get some more and the developers are taking another crack at the existing ones, but it would have been nice to get a bit more word count on the player side of things without all that rigmarole, and I would be happy sacrificing basically all of the <i>eight</i> Avatars to get there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, I think they went a little too overboard with the Avatars and Emanations for the Judges. They are extremely cool, don\u2019t get me wrong.. but this seems to suggest that the Judges will be regular opponents, and that shouldn\u2019t be the case. If the Meret is encountering and fighting their own Gods more than their actual enemies like the Amkhata, Shuanksen, and rival cults/ LDI liquidation specialists.... Something is terribly, terribly wrong in the universe if the Judges have to manifest that often in opposition to the goals of your group.<br /> <br /> I understand the excitement with showing off the Idigam- Judges , but I think two or three examples would have sufficed, giving us maybe two more Shuanksen instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 11-27-2019, 03:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T04:45:39-08:00","id":1351257,"title":"","content":"Okay, so... I know this is an in-progress manuscript still, but honestly, it's slowly losing me the more we see of it. Two particular things with regards to the most recent preview: antagonists' mechanics don't always support their fluff or even appear to fully make sense<span style=\"color:#EE82EE\"><b>*</b></span>, and parts of the supporting cast getting limited crunch and singular examples while one particular antagonist category spends <i>ten pages </i>on examples <i>alone</i>.<br /> <br /> Mummy 1e was the first Kickstarter I ever backed so I'm seeing this out at least until the final bit of the preview drops, but between the conflict and the heavy financial crunch of the holiday season being imminent, I dunno if I can personally justify keeping my pledge in place.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#EE82EE\"><b>* </b></span>Two Shuankhsen-centered examples, because they're the most on my mind right now:<br /> 1) the Shuankhsen now hemorrhage Sekhem at an absurd rate compared to 1e, making them weirdly <i>very </i>immediate antagonists in a way they (and most other &quot;cracked mirror&quot; antagonists up to this point) haven't been prior. I'm not even sure how one would be able to pull together a coherent and cohesive cult in one or even many Descents, at least without chowing hearts like they're hot pockets. Unless they can still inflict Sybaris that is, and they very well might... my reading comprehension feels a bit shot lately.<br /> 2) Schism of Flesh, despite being meant for Storyteller characters - who last I checked don't by default track experience, unless Mummy's doing things differently? - references beat loss as a part of its core mechanics. I don't know if the intent is for Arisen to have the option available to pick Bane Affinities up like they could in 1e, and if so it makes sense for this to be here, but it weirdly stands out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":3946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","user":"Sconce","date":". 11-27-2019, 07:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T05:06:08-08:00","id":1351261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351196#post1351196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the Shuankshen section needs another editing pass. I think Schism of Flesh doesn't even have an &quot;activation&quot; mode, just a Curse <i>and </i>a Decay.</div> </div> </div> </div>And there is no mention of what triggers Decay or what Decay is vs. Curse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T06:18:05-08:00","id":1351269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351236#post1351236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree, I think they went a little too overboard with the Avatars and Emanations for the Judges. They are extremely cool, don\u2019t get me wrong.. but this seems to suggest that the Judges will be regular opponents, and that shouldn\u2019t be the case. If the Meret is encountering and fighting their own Gods more than their actual enemies like the Amkhata, Shuanksen, and rival cults/ LDI liquidation specialists.... Something is terribly, terribly wrong in the universe if the Judges have to manifest that often in opposition to the goals of your group.<br /> <br /> I understand the excitement with showing off the Idigam- Judges , but I think two or three examples would have sufficed, giving us maybe two more Shuanksen instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's just as much a stealth update to the list of Judges, too; we only got seven expounded on, the avatars are a list of other Judges and why they don't have a lot of mummies/why they often end up finding benbenets. <br /> <br /> I do think a couple can be dropped, if it means more crunch in the Endless section or more Shuankshen. I like what we have for the Endless, given how there's actually more Merits than in here (see the player section), but yeah, a couple notes over how an immortality ritual works would help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T06:20:50-08:00","id":1351271,"title":"","content":"As someone who hasn't read Mummy 1e or Immortals, I'm happy with the ratio of content, but I can see how others would more Endless content.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T07:07:45-08:00","id":1351278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351261#post1351261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And there is no mention of what triggers Decay or what Decay is vs. Curse.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> OK so I'm not the only one who was wondering <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> yeah I think it makes the preview a little confusing, possibly due to the addition of ephemeral being rules (which in all other games are in the general rules chapter, not the antagonist one).<br /> <br /> Haven't had time to read the whole thing, but Amkhata and Shuankhsen are solid antagonists. Looking forward to reading the rest of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T09:20:36-08:00","id":1351298,"title":"","content":"I too, while really liking the emanations and avatars of the Judges, think that there are too many of them and not enough mechanical rules and storytelling application for the Immortals. This lack for me is frustrating as it leaves open certain things that need answers to - like how Sekhem applies to the lesser immortal templates and also how experience growth works for say the Reborn as they die and are reborn. Heck, I even wish the Reborn had their own society listed, that way they could have something that sort of works for them rather than a simple paragraph saying they often organize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T10:36:43-08:00","id":1351314,"title":"","content":"Antagonists aside, Are we getting a dedicated Vessels chapter like in first ed, Matthew? \ud83d\ude03","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T10:43:02-08:00","id":1351316,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m away from a decent keyboard, so I\u2019ll probably write further comments this weekend when I have a chance. That said, I see two overarching issues to be addressed. <br /> <br /> 1. While affinity and utterance mechanics received a much needed cleanup, the new mechanics, particularly in the immortals chapter, are just not fully developed and don\u2019t reflect functional systems for some really great ideas. <br /> <br /> 2. At least some of this is a consequence of intermittent use of copy/paste (see sorcerer merits and arisen damage for examples). <br /> <br /> However, many of the rules just don\u2019t work, or don\u2019t make sense. Non-linear time is great, but when did arisen learn 3 utterances prior to their first descent? 1E addressed this in Sothis Ascends, but that explanation is now out the window for 2E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2096-willywonka","name":"willywonka","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T11:37:38-08:00","id":1351329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>willywonka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351316#post1351316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> However, many of the rules just don\u2019t work, or don\u2019t make sense. Non-linear time is great, but when did arisen learn 3 utterances prior to their first descent? 1E addressed this in Sothis Ascends, but that explanation is now out the window for 2E.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I remember...why not?<br /> <br /> Utterances are a deliberate capability of the Arisen, it makes sense that the Rite included some capability with the basics. Especially Dreams of Dead Gods, which is the core Utterance that allows them to build cults and direct from a distance.<br /> <br /> But, moving on; if the final draft is going to have some new rules for the Endless, I'd like a suggestion for Oddity Body Thieves. I've always liked the idea of Death.com, the mind-stealing website and the prisoners who can escape into its victims, and my first Thief character idea is a chemist of the Brown Acid who accidentally discovered the capacity for permanent transfer when he jumped into the body of a soulless person, and now hunts soul eaters, both to find new backup bodies and because he's thoroughly disgusted and appalled by the idea; he considers destroying the person who ate his current body's life to be a fair transaction for having moved in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T11:56:18-08:00","id":1351335,"title":"","content":"Leliel, utterances are learned, rather than innate. That hasn\u2019t changed so far. Sothis Ascends goes to some lengths to show they first arise without any utterances and introduces some mechanics by which they are learned during the first Sothic Turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2096-willywonka","name":"willywonka","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T12:01:18-08:00","id":1351336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>willywonka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351335#post1351335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leliel, utterances are learned, rather than innate. That hasn\u2019t changed so far. Sothis Ascends goes to some lengths to show they first arise without any utterances and introduces some mechanics by which they are learned during the first Sothic Turn.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I still don't see why some can't be innate by lore. Dreams of Avarice outright says a successful subject of the Rite did some Utterances to even reach Duat in the process of becoming Arisen, and the Judges want mummies to be more reliant on them, they being a reason to keep Sekhem up, which involves them doing their duties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T12:05:33-08:00","id":1351337,"title":"","content":"The more I think about the subject, I start to understand what doesn't clicks fully for me in the Endless section. I'm not even sure that it is the wordcount (not that I would ever have complains about more wordcount for Immortals). It is the presentation.<br /> <br /> If the presentation were to start talking about the Endless as a template- that is, as a singular subset of beings- and focus around how the Endless in general work with and against mummies, and then gives a small subsection about each of the dominant Immortal types and their behavior (perhaps in a splat like way, which may be their goal as we don't have art yet), then would give us a good chunk of mechanics for &quot;how to make any immortal you want&quot; with some special tricks unique to each Immortal splat (like a &quot;defining merit&quot; or something like that), and then continue to present a sample character for each of the dominant splats, I think it would have felt better for me. I could have got that the Endless are a big thing, and that there are many methods of Immortality, of which those with the greatest ties for Mummy have been explored in depth. Now, it feels like they tries to squeeze seven supernatural beings (and dropping a two) which are barely connected to each other into a single mechanical system, which doesn't really work for them all (the Purified are basically a Major Template in 1e, for example). <br /> <br /> What I am trying to say is that it feels like the writers tried their best at squeezing the whole Immortals book into less than a chapter and gave some very loose rules at the end of the section, with dedicating a few lines to a chosen Immortal types. Perhaps instead they should have went with a more cohesive presentation, where the Endless are a singular phenomena of people who manipulate Sekhem to extend their lives, like vampirism, or even the Paths of Awakening, or something similar of that concept (an X splat, so to speak). Just my two cents on the subject. Besides, the main reason that I think about it is because Immortals is my favorite CofD book (followed by Inferno and Hunter: the Vigil tied, and Witchfinders in the third place), so I assume if someone was not a big fan of 1e, they probably care less about the subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T12:32:16-08:00","id":1351342,"title":"","content":"Something I was hoping would be covered in the Body Thieves section is what happens when you end up in an unfamiliar body. There are roleplaying aspects to consider, but also some mechanical issues: is there a period of adjustment while you familiarize yourself with your new form? Do you just swap out your physical attributes for your new host's physical attributes? If the host has biological mental conditions (but not Conditions), what happens with your mental attributes? That sort of thing. <br /> <br /> Such rules would also be applicable when an Arisen takes over a cultist, though in that case I could also see a case for the Mummy having access to some \u201clateral character development\u201d, trading in Attribute dots where her original form was weaker than her new form in exchange for more rapid development of an Attribute where her original form was stronger than her new form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T13:03:53-08:00","id":1351346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351336#post1351336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I still don't see why some can't be innate by lore. Dreams of Avarice outright says a successful subject of the Rite did some Utterances to even reach Duat in the process of becoming Arisen, and the Judges want mummies to be more reliant on them, they being a reason to keep Sekhem up, which involves them doing their duties.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can be. My point is the book doesn\u2019t appear to reconcile the issue, and I presented it as an issue to resolve in revision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2096-willywonka","name":"willywonka","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T13:41:51-08:00","id":1351354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351337#post1351337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could have got that the Endless are a big thing, and that there are many methods of Immortality, of which those with the greatest ties for Mummy have been explored in depth. Now, it feels like they tries to squeeze seven supernatural beings (and dropping a two) which are barely connected to each other into a single mechanical system, which doesn't really work for them all (the Purified are basically a Major Template in 1e, for example).<br /> <br /> What I am trying to say is that it feels like the writers tried their best at squeezing the whole Immortals book into less than a chapter and gave some very loose rules at the end of the section, with dedicating a few lines to a chosen Immortal types. Perhaps instead they should have went with a more cohesive presentation, where the Endless are a singular phenomena of people who manipulate Sekhem to extend their lives, like vampirism, or even the Paths of Awakening, or something similar of that concept (an X splat, so to speak). Just my two cents on the subject. Besides, the main reason that I think about it is because Immortals is my favorite CofD book (followed by Inferno and Hunter: the Vigil tied, and Witchfinders in the third place), so I assume if someone was not a big fan of 1e, they probably care less about the subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm very concerned about this treatment, noted by Lostlight and others. So far I'm keeping my powder dry regarding Mummy 2e--albeit noting non-linear time storytelling as an intriguing hook. But 1e Immortals (especially Purified) are, along with skinchangers, some of my favorites of the entire CofD expanse. Perhaps because they are relate-able in ways that other full-splats struggle with.<br /> <br /> The association of Immortals (Endless?) with Arisen doesn't bother me at all: you could view the emergence of myriad forms of immortality as a side-effect of the Rite, but a muddled and half-hearted treatment is not a draw. So far I've kept my limited powder dry on this kickstarter, and it looks like a proper treatment may still need 2e homebrewed conversions.<br /> <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T14:00:23-08:00","id":1351355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351354#post1351354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The association of Immortals (Endless?) with Arisen doesn't bother me at all: you could view the emergence of myriad forms of immortality as a side-effect of the Rite, but a muddled and half-hearted treatment is not a draw. So far I've kept my limited powder dry on this kickstarter, and it looks like a proper treatment may still need 2e homebrewed conversions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to clarify to make sure you get the correct impression (not saying you didn't, but I assume that there are other Immortal fans who may or may not back the Kickstarter according to how Immortals are presented in 2e)<br /> <br /> The section (which is less than a chapter, that includes also all kinds of antagonists and allies to the Arisen) details that the Endless are a collective name that the Arisen use for Immortals who are neither Deathless or Lifeless, and that they are connected to Sekhem by the virtue of having immortality (Sekhem is pure lifeforce, more or less, after all). It then proceeds to present a writeup for the Blood Bathers, Body Thieves, Eternals and Reborn, without mechanics but with some mechanics-like fluff (like describing the features of the Bathing Ritual, or the Talents of Body Thieves, which do get mechanics for their talents). Each section is followed by a sample character, which is weird because we are yet to know the mechanics for the template, and as such gives the feeling that each immortal is a different splat on its own, with its own mechanics. Then it gives a few very short lines for Patchwork People, Purified and Visitors (which changes more or less nothing for the first two and making the Purified to stand out even more due to their connection to the Shadow, and basically the Visitor's description from the Dark Eras companion). It then concludes to give a description of the Endless Micro Template, with three merits to support it, where one is reprinted from Hurt Locker (Supernatural Resistance). Endless also have Sekhem rating due to their defining merit.<br /> <br /> As such, it gives a very unclear feeling about the Immortals- if the Endless are the same Template, why each is treated as a different creature earlier? How do I deal with things like the Purified in the Endless Micro Template? Are they a cohesive group of beings, each representing the powers of Sekhem and Immortality differently, or each are a special beast which has its own ways to use Sekhem, and the Endless Template is like the Horror rules- a general system for all kinds of unrelated creatures? How far Sekhem interact with their immortality? It is clear for some (like Bathers and Eternal), and less clear for others (like Mental Body Thieves or the Reborn).<br /> <br /> That's my review of it- it is not a bad or flawed execution, only that it feels a bit lacking for me as an Immortals fan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T14:13:16-08:00","id":1351357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351337#post1351337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The more I think about the subject, I start to understand what doesn't clicks fully for me in the Endless section. I'm not even sure that it is the wordcount (not that I would ever have complains about more wordcount for Immortals). It is the presentation.<br /> <br /> If the presentation were to start talking about the Endless as a template- that is, as a singular subset of beings- and focus around how the Endless in general work with and against mummies, and then gives a small subsection about each of the dominant Immortal types and their behavior (perhaps in a splat like way, which may be their goal as we don't have art yet), then would give us a good chunk of mechanics for &quot;how to make any immortal you want&quot; with some special tricks unique to each Immortal splat (like a &quot;defining merit&quot; or something like that), and then continue to present a sample character for each of the dominant splats, I think it would have felt better for me. I could have got that the Endless are a big thing, and that there are many methods of Immortality, of which those with the greatest ties for Mummy have been explored in depth. Now, it feels like they tries to squeeze seven supernatural beings (and dropping a two) which are barely connected to each other into a single mechanical system, which doesn't really work for them all (the Purified are basically a Major Template in 1e, for example).<br /> <br /> What I am trying to say is that it feels like the writers tried their best at squeezing the whole Immortals book into less than a chapter and gave some very loose rules at the end of the section, with dedicating a few lines to a chosen Immortal types. Perhaps instead they should have went with a more cohesive presentation, where the Endless are a singular phenomena of people who manipulate Sekhem to extend their lives, like vampirism, or even the Paths of Awakening, or something similar of that concept (an X splat, so to speak). Just my two cents on the subject. Besides, the main reason that I think about it is because Immortals is my favorite CofD book (followed by Inferno and Hunter: the Vigil tied, and Witchfinders in the third place), so I assume if someone was not a big fan of 1e, they probably care less about the subject.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am so glad to see this. I was thinking I was alone in thinking the inclusion of Immortals in Mummy is a mistake. They have nothing to do with Mummies, have no connection to Irem and worst of all, eat a bunch of word count.<br /> <br /> Now, I am a big fan of the Immortals book in 1e and would really like a new 2e version of it, but not in Mummy. I want the Mummy book to be about <i>Mummy </i>and those directly connected to them. I'd rather they make Sekhem Sourcerer's awesome in order to spice up the Cults and leave Cults with only 3 tiers. This would still allow the types of Chronicles with multiple PCs but only one Mummy while allowing all PCs to feel important.<br /> <br /> So much of the current manuscript could use more word count that having Immortals in the corebook of Mummy is a waste. It would be a great expansion book for Mummy though, where their connection to Mummies can be really fleshed out and how their integration in cults work.<br /> <br /> It is probably too late, but I thought I'd voice my opinion anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2611-guiskj","name":"guiskj","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2611_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T14:28:09-08:00","id":1351359,"title":"","content":"Actually, I'm curious as to exactly how much homebrewing would be needed. After Chapter 5 came out, I broke open my copy of WoD:I again to review things. And you know what? Mechanically, there really isn't much there that needs changing. We've already got Blood Bather and Body Thief updates in Dark Eras Companion, and the \u201cLesser Immortals\u201d (Visitors, Patchwork People, Wardens, Reborn, Eternals, and Harvesters) really don't have much in the way of mechanics for the 1e\u21922e change to trip over; so I focused mainly on the Purified. And you know what? I only found three things that need updating, and two of them are debatable: <br /> <br /> First, there are several references to the Purified being able to interact with both ghosts and spirits in Twilight; but in 1e, that was standard: <i>anyone</i> who could interact with Twilight could interact with ghosts, spirits, <i>qashmallim</i>, and virtually anything else that might be lurking in Twilight. So a 2e update of the Purified would need to clarify this point: do the Purified interact with ghosts, spirits, both, or everything in Twilight? (My personal preference would be \u201cghosts and spirits\u201d \u2014 the former because of their human nature, the latter because of what becoming Purified did to them; but I can see arguments for several of the options.) Incidentally, this is the same issue that needs to be addressed with the Amkhata. <br /> <br /> The second thing is Integrity. A major difference between 1e and 2e is that Morality wasn't challenged by witnessing the supernatural; Integrity is. Are the Endless (not just the Purified) immunized from that? Frankly, it's an issue that ghouls, wolf-bloods, Proximi, fae-touched, and other \u201clesser template humans\u201d share: they're now immersed in the supernatural world; are they going to inevitably and rapidly be broken by it? (That said, I think that's something that ought to have been addressed in the Chronicles of Darkness rulebook, not here.)<br /> <br /> The final thing that needs updating is the experience costs: specifically for Chi, Siddhi, and Spirit Numina. <br /> <br /> Oh: and some of the Siddhi make reference to \u201cNumina\u201d when they should reference \u201cManifestations and Numina\u201d. <br /> <br /> Really, that's about it. <br /> <br /> And with that in mind, I think what I'd really like to see would be a \u201cv1.1\u201d of <b>Immortals</b> that leaves the vast majority of the book intact and only makes those tiny changes that are needed to make it compatible with the 2e rules. <i>Maybe</i> rebrand it as a Mummy supplement, adding some information about how each kind of Immortal interacts with the Deathless; if not, just change its name from \u201cWorld of Darkness: Immortals\u201d to \u201cChronicles of Darkness: Immortals\u201d, toss it into the Scroll of Fading Memories, et voil\u00e0!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-27-2019, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T14:37:57-08:00","id":1351363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guiskj</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351357#post1351357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I am so glad to see this. I was thinking I was alone in thinking the inclusion of Immortals in Mummy is a mistake. They have nothing to do with Mummies, have no connection to Irem and worst of all, eat a bunch of word count.<br /> <br /> Now, I am a big fan of the Immortals book in 1e and would really like a new 2e version of it, but not in Mummy. I want the Mummy book to be about <i>Mummy </i>and those directly connected to them. I'd rather they make Sekhem Sourcerer's awesome in order to spice up the Cults and leave Cults with only 3 tiers. This would still allow the types of Chronicles with multiple PCs but only one Mummy while allowing all PCs to feel important.<br /> <br /> So much of the current manuscript could use more word count that having Immortals in the corebook of Mummy is a waste. It would be a great expansion book for Mummy though, where their connection to Mummies can be really fleshed out and how their integration in cults work.<br /> <br /> It is probably too late, but I thought I'd voice my opinion anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the recasting of the more predatory Endless as beings who extend their lives by consuming Sekhem, I think they fit into Mummy quite well; and the new pyramidal structure of the Arisen's Cults, with a whole level dedicated to immortals who help provide continuity to said colts while the Deathless sleep, gives them a critical role in MtC Chronicles: when you jump between eras, the Immortals are the only other characters in the Chronicle that can be recurring characters. <br /> <br /> So I don't want them pulled out of the MtC core book; I just want the Immortals book to be updated for use with 2e gamesters such as MtC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T14:59:08-08:00","id":1351366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351363#post1351363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the recasting of the more predatory Endless as beings who extend their lives by consuming Sekhem, I think they fit into Mummy quite well; and the new pyramidal structure of the Arisen's Cults, with a whole level dedicated to immortals who help provide continuity to said colts while the Deathless sleep, gives them a critical role in MtC Chronicles: when you jump between eras, the Immortals are the only other characters in the Chronicle that can be recurring characters.<br /> <br /> So I don't want them pulled out of the MtC core book; I just want the Immortals book to be updated for use with 2e gamesters such as MtC.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Quite. They also do something no other thing can: give living memory of time in henet, since eventually even a Sadikh falls asleep. That, combined with how many of them are even harder to kill than the companions...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T15:00:15-08:00","id":1351368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351363#post1351363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the recasting of the more predatory Endless as beings who extend their lives by consuming Sekhem, I think they fit into Mummy quite well; and the new pyramidal structure of the Arisen's Cults, with a whole level dedicated to immortals who help provide continuity to said colts while the Deathless sleep, gives them a critical role in MtC Chronicles: when you jump between eras, the Immortals are the only other characters in the Chronicle that can be recurring characters.<br /> <br /> So I don't want them pulled out of the MtC core book; I just want the Immortals book to be updated for use with 2e gamesters such as MtC.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's fair. I think Immortals can work really well with Mummies, that was never in debate. My point was more that the core book should focus on the Arisen and their closest supporting/antagonistic cast that reinforce their connection with Irem and the Judges. Immortals have nothing to do with either.<br /> <br /> Now, I think Immortals could fit <b>very</b> well in a supplement. It is just that putting them in the core book forces them to not get their just word count, and worst of all, robs word count that could be dedicated to fleshing-out <i>Mummies</i> and their mythos more, which is vastly more important for a core book about Mummies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2611,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2611-guiskj","user":"guiskj","date":". 11-27-2019, 08:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2611-guiskj","name":"guiskj","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2611_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T16:28:19-08:00","id":1351379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351029#post1351029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But mages summoning Abyssal entities and werewolves taking wound spirits as Totems is not only fully possible but also something that happens in the setting. Often as antagonists rather than players, but nothing stops you from playing villains.</div> </div> </div> </div>So my thought would be if you want an amkat familiar then play a Shuankhsen. It\u2019d also be an interesting game if your PC wanted to purposely serve Ammut and become Shuankhsen.<br /> <br /> Back to the Mage example, I think of it like this: a Pentacle Mage trafficking with the Abyss can happen, but it\u2019s a slippery slope where there\u2019s a lot going on against them like Mage society ostracizing them and taking hits to Wisdom. So yeah, if you want an amkat familiar then you gotta deal with the Guilds shunning or executing you, and the Judges punishing you. I stopped don\u2019t think it should be a \u201cnormal enough\u201d thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T17:11:34-08:00","id":1351382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351379#post1351379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So my thought would be if you want an amkat familiar then play a Shuankhsen. It\u2019d also be an interesting game if your PC wanted to purposely serve Ammut and become Shuankhsen.<br /> <br /> Back to the Mage example, I think of it like this: a Pentacle Mage trafficking with the Abyss can happen, but it\u2019s a slippery slope where there\u2019s a lot going on against them like Mage society ostracizing them and taking hits to Wisdom. So yeah, if you want an amkat familiar then you gotta deal with the Guilds shunning or executing you, and the Judges punishing you. I stopped don\u2019t think it should be a \u201cnormal enough\u201d thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Doesn't look comparable to what is presented in the preview material...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T19:48:26-08:00","id":1351397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is how I feel right now about the core. It feels s little bloated and a little like These Other Cool Things.....plusyougetmummies:the Curse on top of everything else I disliked about the 2nd preview.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not sure I agree with that entirely. 1E made a big deal about the importance of the cult, but didn\u2019t give us much to do with it save as a merit-based resource. 2E has gone a long way toward addressing this, which I think is why there are so many cult components in each chapter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2096-willywonka","name":"willywonka","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T20:00:30-08:00","id":1351401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>willywonka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351397#post1351397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m not sure I agree with that entirely. 1E made a big deal about the importance of the cult, but didn\u2019t give us much to do with it save as a merit-based resource. 2E has gone a long way toward addressing this, which I think is why there are so many cult components in each chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah. Honestly, this is what the cult should feel like; they are part of a mummy's legend, partially the very purpose the Arisen exist for, so they can preserve Irem's cultural memes forever. It also nails why the Arisen awakening is such a horrific prospect: &quot;You can kill the prophet, but you can't kill the god!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T22:03:47-08:00","id":1351411,"title":"","content":"And again, Immortals are an essential component of a mummy's cult, which is why the core book needs to at least talk about them, to highlight just how important they are. It would be like Werewolf the Forsaken (2e) talking about the Packs without mentioning the Wolf-bloods that form the bridge between the Uratha and the mortal members of the Pack. <br /> <br /> And just like WtF doesn't just talk about the wolf-bloods, it also provides rules for playing them, so too must MtC not just talk about the Endless who keep the Cult on track over the centuries; it needs to provide rules for playing them. <br /> <br /> That said, I <i>do</i> agree with <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2611-guiskj\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2611_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2611\" data-vbnamecard=\"2611\">guiskj</a> this far: I'd rather the section on the Endless be as concise as possible, to leave more room for other stuff. I've come around to the opinion that the section on the Endless should be as bare-bones as possible, with just enough fluff to give the reader an idea of what they are and how they fit into the world of MtC and just enough crunch to make them playable (for the sake of the cult). A more detailed treatment of them can be provided by a separate book (preferably a v1.1 of the existing Immortals book, which already does nearly everything we'd need an Endless supplement to do and mainly needs some minor tinkering, some significant rebranding, and a PR push that says \u201cthis is something that MtC fans will want to use\u201d).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T23:10:58-08:00","id":1351420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351411#post1351411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And again, Immortals are an essential component of a mummy's cult, which is why the core book needs to at least talk about them, to highlight just how important they are. It would be like Werewolf the Forsaken (2e) talking about the Packs without mentioning the Wolf-bloods that form the bridge between the Uratha and the mortal members of the Pack. <br /> <br /> And just like WtF doesn't just talk about the wolf-bloods, it also provides rules for playing them, so too must MtC not just talk about the Endless who keep the Cult on track over the centuries; it needs to provide rules for playing them. <br /> <br /> That said, I <i>do</i> agree with <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> and <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> this far: I'd rather the section on the Endless be as concise as possible, to leave more room for other stuff. I've come around to the opinion that the section on the Endless should be as bare-bones as possible, with just enough fluff to give the reader an idea of what they are and how they fit into the world of MtC and just enough crunch to make them playable (for the sake of the cult). A more detailed treatment of them can be provided by a separate book (preferably a v1.1 of the existing Immortals book, which already does nearly everything we'd need an Endless supplement to do and mainly needs some minor tinkering, some significant rebranding, and a PR push that says \u201cthis is something that MtC fans will want to use\u201d).</div> </div> </div> </div>You make good points. Though I would equate Sekhem sorcerers to wolfblooded, not Immortals. But even if we were to draw the parallel, there would be an inherent difficulty to, say, do Wolfblooded correctly in Werewolf's core if there were 5+ different flavours of Wolfblooded, like there are for Immortals.<br /> <br /> More than that, the part I have the most difficulty with is the fact that Immortals have nothing to do with Mummy. They are being ret-conned into a forced connection with Sehkem, but that is what that it feels to me, a forced connection.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, there are a bunch of other parts of the core book that could use more word count...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2611-guiskj","name":"guiskj","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2611_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T23:37:55-08:00","id":1351421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351411#post1351411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And again, Immortals are an essential component of a mummy's cult, which is why the core book needs to at least talk about them, to highlight just how important they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of can't help but feel, as it relates to the current conversation, the misconception of this statement is part of the problem-because, <i>no</i>, Immortals aren't important to the cult, they just help out in regards to it's high regards.<br /> <br /> Immortals were introduced as a concurrent point of interest for characters who don't experience death easily and can experience multiple points of interests along the historical axis along as a means of exploring various other long held issues. First Edition, though, proved the game works quite well without them.<br /> <br /> In <i>theory</i> this is a fine theory to approach the concept of Mummy, particularly since Mummy itself was not especially popular as was Immortals in terms of wide trends. Put two mildly popular things that have longevity together and also share similar themes and conflicts along the parallel lines of both, go forward.<br /> <br /> The Problem is that Mummy has been a little lacking on what Mummy fans and Would Be Mummy fans have been looking for in terms of Mummy, and when confronted with the alternative just aren't satisfied.<br /> <br /> Personally, I can't speak to the latter as I have not yet caught up on the material and still trust it's not a big issue-but as someone who wanted Mummy and didn't want any <i>any</i> of the immortals in my Mummy Core and must look for positives in that notion regardless, the notion that the Endless <i>do not</i> deliver a satisfactory update on experience is somewhat alarming. One I take with a grain of salt, because I frequently find fans blowing things out of proportion, but alarm all the same. Fortunately, the sluggishness of the former hasn't slowed me down much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-28-2019, 02:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T06:48:45-08:00","id":1351467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351421#post1351421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of can't help but feel, as it relates to the current conversation, the misconception of this statement is part of the problem-because, <i>no</i>, Immortals aren't important to the cult, they just help out in regards to it's high regards.<br /> <br /> Immortals were introduced as a concurrent point of interest for characters who don't experience death easily and can experience multiple points of interests along the historical axis along as a means of exploring various other long held issues. First Edition, though, proved the game works quite well without them.<br /> <br /> In <i>theory</i> this is a fine theory to approach the concept of Mummy, particularly since Mummy itself was not especially popular as was Immortals in terms of wide trends. Put two mildly popular things that have longevity together and also share similar themes and conflicts along the parallel lines of both, go forward.<br /> <br /> The Problem is that Mummy has been a little lacking on what Mummy fans and Would Be Mummy fans have been looking for in terms of Mummy, and when confronted with the alternative just aren't satisfied.<br /> <br /> Personally, I can't speak to the latter as I have not yet caught up on the material and still trust it's not a big issue-but as someone who wanted Mummy and didn't want any <i>any</i> of the immortals in my Mummy Core and must look for positives in that notion regardless, the notion that the Endless <i>do not</i> deliver a satisfactory update on experience is somewhat alarming. One I take with a grain of salt, because I frequently find fans blowing things out of proportion, but alarm all the same. Fortunately, the sluggishness of the former hasn't slowed me down much.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI'm only going off of the what's expressed here, and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a>'s comments in particular are helpful for this, so thank you.<br /> <br /> But I agree with the above: Immortals can and should be their own thing, though I think there is much utility in highlighting how from Risen's perspective an &quot;Eternal&quot; who runs on sekhem can be very handy to anchor their cult while away. From the immortal's perspective they may not have much cross-line understanding on how they actually work as a supernaturally-empowered being. They know they're unnaturally long-lived. They know they either did, participated or must continue to do something for that long life. And that's about it. <br /> <br /> Anything else they'll pick up from running into other supernaturals--full splats, in particular, and mummies are good candidates to <i>find them </i>and brand them with their own worldview. Mummies are fellow travelers, so to speak. So are vampires. And spirits.<br /> <br /> I don't mind anchoring Endless with sekhem as their power resource, give them a supernatural tolerance merit, and then run the rest of their powers as horrors. That's &quot;clean&quot;. The rest of the types of immortals could be given a short paragraph--essentially &quot;ideas on how this manifests&quot; and then the section could move on to mechanics and cult roles. <br /> <br /> Endless thus, from a mummy's perspective, represent linear memory to the Risen's asynchronous time-memory. That's not insignificant to the product. <br /> <br /> I do hope that they receive greater treatment in another book. Not by giving them half a dozen power stats (Chi? What?), but by elaborating on their common sub-type powers and providing mechanics for them as well as &quot;this is what it means&quot; text. A good method would be to treat powers as either or both of merits and horrors, and make use of the Conditions and Tilts system.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T07:09:45-08:00","id":1351472,"title":"","content":"I, personally, have little issue with Immortals showing up in the Core book- a lot of the book does well to integrate them into Mummy's setting, talking about how they interact with Investments, or the Eternal's Relic or things like that. My issue is that their own section in the book in a bit weird and underwhelming. Again, I want to state that I don't think it is bad- but it feels a bit confusing and lacking coherence. The ideas are interesting, the presentation is unsatisfying for my taste. I appreciate the effort of trying to update an whole book which was dedicated towards detailing around nine supernatural beings into less than a chapter, but it may have been too ambitious to be done. The fact that they are trying to connect the Immortals to Mummy from one side and stay true to their 1e presentation could be understood, but it feels too conservative, confusing and inconsistent when you read it the first time. Again, it is not a bad section, but just unsatisfying for me as Immortals fan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T10:22:22-08:00","id":1351505,"title":"","content":"I'm not opposed to Immortals being tied into Mummy either, it's just the sort of stuff I expected to be in, like, a Night Horrors book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T11:41:50-08:00","id":1351516,"title":"","content":"In terms of tying them more to Mummy, I think that their various rituals should be recast as Sekhem Sorcery Rites. If you don't want to require any of the Sorcery Merits, make them Open Rites. But especially with the Blood Bathers and Body Thieves, the rites they use feel perfectly in keeping with what we know of Sekhem Sorcery. <br /> <br /> One place to trim word count is to cut out those Endless who <i>don't</i> use rituals to become what they are: the Mental Body Thieves, the spontaneous Reborn, etc. It's not that they don't exist; it's just that they'd be addressed elsewhere. <br /> <br /> The Endless Micro-Template bothers me. One of the points of Micro-Templates is that all of their benefits are in the Merits: they don't give you a power stat. As well, the fact that you only get to treat it as Supernatural Resistance if you take an additional Merit to enable that feels clumsy. If you're going to give the Endless a Sekhem rating, just make them a lesser template like ghouls, wolf-bloods, et al. Better, don't give them a Sekhem rating: they don't need it, and the suggestion of tying their Rituals into Sorcery already connects them with Mummy's metaphysics well enough. Either way, I don't see a point in the Micro-Template.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T11:56:36-08:00","id":1351520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351516#post1351516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As well, the fact that you only get to treat it as Supernatural Resistance if you take an additional Merit to enable that feels clumsy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Per the Kickstarter comments, the Merit is supposed to stack with the Sekhem rating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T12:19:41-08:00","id":1351523,"title":"","content":"Ah. So it's not so much about enabling Supernatural Resistance as it is about extending its upper limit from 5 to 10. That's better; but it still feels clumsy and unnecessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-28-2019, 03:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T13:34:32-08:00","id":1351532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351516#post1351516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of tying them more to Mummy, I think that their various rituals should be recast as Sekhem Sorcery Rites. If you don't want to require any of the Sorcery Merits, make them Open Rites. But especially with the Blood Bathers and Body Thieves, the rites they use feel perfectly in keeping with what we know of Sekhem Sorcery. <br /> <br /> One place to trim word count is to cut out those Endless who <i>don't</i> use rituals to become what they are: the Mental Body Thieves, the spontaneous Reborn, etc. It's not that they don't exist; it's just that they'd be addressed elsewhere. <br /> <br /> The Endless Micro-Template bothers me. One of the points of Micro-Templates is that all of their benefits are in the Merits: they don't give you a power stat. As well, the fact that you only get to treat it as Supernatural Resistance if you take an additional Merit to enable that feels clumsy. If you're going to give the Endless a Sekhem rating, just make them a lesser template like ghouls, wolf-bloods, et al. Better, don't give them a Sekhem rating: they don't need it, and the suggestion of tying their Rituals into Sorcery already connects them with Mummy's metaphysics well enough. Either way, I don't see a point in the Micro-Template.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can get behind this, it's a good suggestion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2611-guiskj","name":"guiskj","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2611_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T15:02:08-08:00","id":1351548,"title":"","content":"I agree that the immortality-specific rituals of each Endless need to be more formalized, but I don't think they necessarily need to be Open Rites, both for distinction and as to not unintentionally skew perception of the current line-up of Rites. As said, some aren't even based on rituals, but I wouldn't say that's the strongest reasoning for removing them either. Of the Other Immortals in the core book, the ones presented in detail are all those who have the <i>most flawed</i> immortalities, and each foil and contrast the Arisen in different ways because of this.<br /> <br /> The Endless micro-template is non-standard, but it's clearly more like a common <i>s</i><i>ub-template</i> to these characters' supernatural gimmick. Gift of Years has pretty distinct benefits that suit the nature of these immortals, and that's in addition to access to a plethora of Supernatural Merits and a handful of Timeless Merits from Chapter 3. Supernatural Resistance as intended might be a little redundant, but there is pretty comprehensible value in the way the other merits are handled.<br /> <br /> As tie-ins and supporting characters in Mummy, it also makes sense for the Endless to have Sekhem, as there are multiple mechanics and antagonists that interact with the trait in particular ways, and it strengthens Endless associations to the main cast and the game as a whole if they can be targeted or endangered in the same ways as Mummies and their lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 11-28-2019, 07:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T16:23:56-08:00","id":1351555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351505#post1351505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not opposed to Immortals being tied into Mummy either, it's just the sort of stuff I expected to be in, like, a Night Horrors book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that makes sense. Night Horrors after all should have the wordcount for such a thing, that a core book doesn't. I just more or less want to make sure that people don't mistakenly think that &quot;Mummy ruined Immortals FOREVER&quot;- because it didn't. It is not a bad section, just lacking IMO for the reasons I have stated in my posts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T20:01:38-08:00","id":1351573,"title":"","content":"One of the things I wished that the lesser immortals had was access to merits that increased their healing rates. I say this so that campaigns don't derailed by unfun deaths or long term damage that other groups might be easily able to ignore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T20:21:21-08:00","id":1351576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351573#post1351573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the things I wished that the lesser immortals had was access to merits that increased their healing rates. I say this so that campaigns don't derailed by unfun deaths or long term damage that other groups might be easily able to ignore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Go back and read Fount of Vitality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T20:26:59-08:00","id":1351577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351576#post1351576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Go back and read Fount of Vitality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh cool. Thanks. I can see why I missed it though, it being the whole very last sentence, but yeah, taking this merit and gaining the healing rate of a Deathless is awesome. So that is cool. It is also well within the capability of immortal, including Reborn, character to get. So that is nice. <br /> <br /> Honestly, one of these days I plan on going through the merit list in both the general rule and the endless rules to see what particular features and powers that an immortal could gain access to, plus what exact capabilities that enables.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T20:31:50-08:00","id":1351578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351379#post1351379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So my thought would be if you want an amkat familiar then play a Shuankhsen. It\u2019d also be an interesting game if your PC wanted to purposely serve Ammut and become Shuankhsen.<br /> <br /> Back to the Mage example, I think of it like this: a Pentacle Mage trafficking with the Abyss can happen, but it\u2019s a slippery slope where there\u2019s a lot going on against them like Mage society ostracizing them and taking hits to Wisdom. So yeah, if you want an amkat familiar then you gotta deal with the Guilds shunning or executing you, and the Judges punishing you. I stopped don\u2019t think it should be a \u201cnormal enough\u201d thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds like a 1e understanding of Amkhata. 2e mentions Arisen summoning them up or using them as tomb guardians and Judges sending them as punishment, with no remarks on them being Lifeless or something that will get you excommunicated or whatever. They are clearly enormously dangerous and disturbing entities, but they aren't in the vein of the Lifeless or Ammut worship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T20:41:53-08:00","id":1351580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351578#post1351578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds like a 1e understanding of Amkhata. 2e mentions Arisen summoning them up or using them as tomb guardians and Judges sending them as punishment, with no remarks on them being Lifeless or something that will get you excommunicated or whatever. They are clearly enormously dangerous and disturbing entities, but they aren't in the vein of the Lifeless or Ammut worship.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Shuankhsen have a Bane Affinity that turns them into one, their summoning ritual explicitly relies on blasphemous symbolism in the same way that Bane Relics are defiled forms of guild relics, and even the most successful summoning only results in the creature obeying you as long as you feed it a steady supply of Sekhem from broken relics or human sacrifice. They occupy ghostly Twilight, the list of possible parts includes all the traditional bits associated with the form of the Devourer, and Shuankhsen are mummies as surely as the Arisen are.<br /> <br /> Even and especially for the servants of beings as hypocritical as the Judges can be, <i>this is not normal.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T21:32:33-08:00","id":1351586,"title":"","content":"While the rules for immortals are mostly &quot;rules? we don't need no stinkin' rules&quot; them being able to have Pillars and Sekhem, and from cryptic comments on the KS, the ability to use them to some extent is definitely exciting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T21:39:24-08:00","id":1351587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351580#post1351580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Shuankhsen have a Bane Affinity that turns them into one, their summoning ritual explicitly relies on blasphemous symbolism in the same way that Bane Relics are defiled forms of guild relics, and even the most successful summoning only results in the creature obeying you as long as you feed it a steady supply of Sekhem from broken relics or human sacrifice. They occupy ghostly Twilight, the list of possible parts includes all the traditional bits associated with the form of the Devourer, and Shuankhsen are mummies as surely as the Arisen are.<br /> <br /> Even and especially for the servants of beings as hypocritical as the Judges can be, <i>this is not normal.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Some Judges will likely give a damn (ones against crimes against the sacred and slaughter for example), but the idea that the Judges are blanket against it is a boring 1eism. Like, it even mentions that both Arisen and Judges call upon them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T22:20:53-08:00","id":1351591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351587#post1351587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some Judges will likely give a damn (ones against crimes against the sacred and slaughter for example), but the idea that the Judges are blanket against it is a boring 1eism. Like, it even mentions that both Arisen and Judges call upon them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It says that some Arisen have figured out how to use a particular type of Amkhat as tomb guardians and mentions the Judges offhand in the description of another particular type of Amkhat. This does not overwrite the fact that they're life-eating creatures who are made through explicitly blasphemous, heretical, and corrupt practices, and who the Judges will specifically reward you for destroying.<br /> <br /> I don't particularly care what you do with them in your game and I'm not saying they're never used by the Arisen, but the entire presentation of the Amkhata aside from literally two minor mentions angles their presentation towards &quot;these are fucked-up things that the Arisen have a cultural taboo against deliberately supporting for the same reasons that the Devourer lets her mummies take their forms.&quot;<br /> <br /> The mention of some mummies keeping Amkhata as tomb guardians has approximately the same weight as the fact that &quot;Statue of the Devourer&quot; and &quot;Unholy Fountain&quot; and &quot;Sacrifice Altar&quot; are sample Tomb Traps. A lion with the head of a cobra guarding the tomb of one of the Deathless at the bare minimum shares a vibe with the &quot;this ancient temple of a benign or austere religious collective secretly keeps a demon bound to its halls as a high-risk security feature&quot; trope, if not something more sinister yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-29-2019, 01:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T22:49:08-08:00","id":1351595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351591#post1351591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This does not overwrite the fact that they're life-eating creatures who are made through explicitly blasphemous, heretical, and corrupt practices, and who the Judges will specifically reward you for destroying.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's breaking a relic. &quot;All Amkhata are birthed this way, either by accident or ritual, formed piecemeal by parts and appendages of whichever sacred creatures lay dead nearby.&quot; As well as &quot;When Sekhem is spilled and there are no extant Amkhata to suck up the energy, a new and confused chimeric abomination is born.&quot; The occult ritual is a means of replicating, or maybe directing, something that happens well enough on it's own when a vessel gets broken.<br /> <br /> Though, I'll note that the text immediately contradicts itself, after stating &quot;All Amkhata are birthed this way&quot;, the book then goes to show that, no actually, not all Amkhata are birthed that way with the sidebar titled &quot;Amkhata Breeding?&quot;, where it describes Amkhata reproducing through mitosis in Neter-Khertet.<br /> <br /> See, here's the thing... We've got a lot of description of how a summoning ritual to create an Amkhata has blasphemy and sacrifice in it. But we also have the dice modifiers expressly mentioning what the dice penalty is if a Judge disapproves of the ritual being used. From what you're saying, this dice penalty would always apply. But the text does not make that explicit. Instead, it is provided as an optional dice modifier. Something that may or may not apply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T22:58:59-08:00","id":1351597,"title":"","content":".... Oh hey, the Manifestation of Bestu, &quot;The Writhing Eyes'&quot; Avatar, as well as &quot;The Screaming Flock&quot; Avatar and &quot;The Shadow Judge&quot; Avatar, all know the Utterance &quot;Words of Dead Fury&quot;.<br /> <br /> Hoo boy.<br /> <br /> Edit: On a side note, I am friggin in love with the descriptions of the Avatars. These things are absolutely horrifying in amazing ways and keep making me think of Mythos weirdness. I love it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","user":"Paradim","date":". 11-29-2019, 02:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T22:59:38-08:00","id":1351598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351591#post1351591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't particularly care what you do with them in your game and I'm not saying they're never used by the Arisen, but the entire presentation of the Amkhata aside from literally two minor mentions angles their presentation towards &quot;these are fucked-up things that the Arisen have a cultural taboo against deliberately supporting for the same reasons that the Devourer lets her mummies take their forms.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Not seeing the cultural taboo part, sounds like a 1eism. Definitely not seeing even the vaguest implication that mummies should be excommunicated or whatever for using them either.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T23:09:36-08:00","id":1351601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351598#post1351598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not seeing the cultural taboo part, sounds like a 1eism.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am uncertain what you think words like &quot;rogue sorcerers,&quot; &quot;blasphemous symbolism,&quot; &quot;unhallowed architecture,&quot; &quot;profane reversal,&quot; &quot;irreverence toward the sacred,&quot; &quot;abhorrent nests,&quot; and so on are supposed to convey about a being's place in a culture if not &quot;this is a Bad Thing.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Definitely not seeing even the vaguest implication that mummies should be excommunicated or whatever for using them either. </div> </div> </div>You are literally the only one talking about &quot;excommunication or whatever.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T00:14:16-08:00","id":1351606,"title":"","content":"Huh... Judges create Amkhata too...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T06:10:09-08:00","id":1351633,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/339646881/mummy-the-curse-2nd-edition/posts/2697667\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects.../posts/2697667</a><br /> <br /> Halifax is revealed as another signature setting!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T15:55:52-08:00","id":1351730,"title":"","content":"I can't help but think of starting a game in the modern day where the characters as a backstory undergo - either by choice or by pick - a ritual that basically enhances their soul, making them one of the Reborn. Not that they knew this at the exact moment. Especially since the moment the blinding light of the ritual faded they themselves incarnated in a body some 10k years ago, though they are thankfully together. Events happen that will see them gain some unique abilities and learn magic. One of their number, an NPC, will also suddenly disappear. Time and adventure will occur, and eventually they will die (from either violence or natural causes, at say the ripe old age of say 30, since its 10k in the past). They close their eyes and then when the open them again they are somewhere else a few centuries later in a different but very similar body. After a bit of time to figure things out they soon start to notice signs that they are being chased by something - which leads to the start of the appearance of some sort of big bad. <br /> <br /> For multiple campaign arcs all they can unlock is the powers gained via Supernatural Merits. At some point - maybe when things are getting a bit stale and the players are starting to want MORE - something will occur, maybe when the group reach Sekhem 5, which will lead to a certain breakthrough which will cause them to gain Pillars, which will unlock the greater magics of Affinites and Utterances. (I could see allowing the players to move XP about, removing dots in supernatural merits for dots in Pillars and Affinities, though thematic connections still probably need to be maintained). <br /> <br /> Anyway, it was just a thought I had while thinking on the mummy chapters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T17:38:08-08:00","id":1351745,"title":"","content":"Do the Reborn go through their cycles of reincarnation nonlinearly like the Arisen do? I was under the impression that their reincarnations are linear in time. <br /> <br /> Thematically, the Reborn and the Body Thieves still me as the Immortals most closely related to the Arisen, thematically (aside from the Purified, of course). The Reborn echo the \u201cmultiple lives\u201d aspect of the Arisen (but without the continuity of having the same body between lives), while the Body Thieves are basically doing the same sort of thing that an Arisen does when it takes over the life of one of its cultists. There are differences, of course; but play up the similarities, and those particular kinds of immortals will feel less tacked on. <br /> <br /> Eternals also have the bit that what <i>makes</i> them eternal is a mystical item: if it had a Curse associated with it, it would nearly fit into the array of mystical items that the Arisen deal with. <br /> <br /> As such, the Blood Bathers strike me as the odd men out \u2014 though the cruelty inherent in their brand of immortality, and the fact that the metaphysical explanation for it involves extracting \u201clife energy\u201d from their victims, might suffice to link them to Mummy's metaphysics. <br /> <br /> As for the others: while I'd like to see the Wardens as a Storyteller Character option (having a Warden guard your tomb over the millennia that you sleep would be immensely useful), I find myself having some difficulty tying them into Mummy's metaphysics: MtC doesn't really have anything in it about connecting to places. The Harvesters could be rephrased in terms of \u201charvesting Sekhem\u201d, at least where the Arisen are concerned: they wouldn't be able to destroy an Arisen; but they could drain her Sekhem and literally cut short her Descent, sending her back to Duat until her next one. This would make them fearsome enemies, even if not really all that powerful. <br /> <br /> As for the Purified: it's mentioned in Immortals that the first Purified came from ancient Egypt and China. Downplay or eliminate the \u201cEgypt\u201d part and say that the Purified have their origins in ancient China in the same way that the Arisen have their origins in the Nameless Empire, and the Purified become an example of the \u201cnon-egyptian mummies\u201d that some sectors of the fans have clamored for. Which, in addition to how much space it takes to present them, is plenty of reason to keep them out of MtC's core book. But I'm glad they're at least acknowledged. I could easily see them being presented as an alternate take on MtC's metaphysics: Sekhem and Chi are conceptually very similar, and might arguably be thought of as different approaches to the same thing: it's all just \u201clife force\u201d in the end. Unlike the other Immortals who are generally thought of as fundamentally inferior to the Arisen, I could see the Arisen viewing the Purified as distant relatives. <br /> <br /> Finally, the Patchwork People: back when Immortals first came out, I got a strong \u201cPromethean\u201d vibe from them, almost as if their artificial hearts had a spark of Azoth in it keeping them alive. These days, I'd be more inclined to associate them with Deviant. Either way, they're not really a MtC thing. To be fair, I also tend to think of Blood Bathers as more of a Vampire thing than a Mummy thing, and would tend to prefer that their 2e update take place somewhere in that line than in Mummy. But that's just me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T17:53:28-08:00","id":1351748,"title":"","content":"On the Reborn, the standard is that the lives they experience is linear. BUT, and this is a really cool line, there is a sentence which says some myths exist to indicate some masters of the Reborn seem to be able to choose to send their 'souls' backward or forward in time. This, as far as I read it, is more an adventure seed and storytelling possibility then an actual rule. So the way I see it the standard is linear but the potential for non-linear existence is possible, if a ST wants to allow it. <br /> <br /> On the Purified, I really like your stance. The idea that Sekhem and Chi are basically alternate names for Lifeforce Energy is really cool to me. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T18:09:31-08:00","id":1351750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351745#post1351745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do the Reborn go through their cycles of reincarnation nonlinearly like the Arisen do? I was under the impression that their reincarnations are linear in time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of them do: &quot;Rarer still are the Reborn who claim they can send their consciousness forward or backward in time, controlling when they next emerge into the world. They'd have interesting notes to compare with the Deathless on living lives out of order, if the enmity between them weren't so great.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T18:21:19-08:00","id":1351754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351748#post1351748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the Purified, I really like your stance. The idea that Sekhem and Chi are basically alternate names for Lifeforce Energy is really cool to me. </div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say that they <i>are</i>; only that they <i>might be</i>. That way, those like you can say that they are without contradicting the published material; while those like ArcaneArts can say that they aren't, <i>also</i> without contacting the published material. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351750#post1351750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of them do: &quot;Rarer still are the Reborn who claim they can send their consciousness forward or backward in time, controlling when they next emerge into the world. They'd have interesting notes to compare with the Deathless on living lives out of order, if the enmity between them weren't so great.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. In that regard, I could see the Reborn having something akin to a Sorcery Rite that lets them choose: those who know the Rite can access nonlinear time; those who don't, can't. In my games, I might even allow a temporary usage of it before death: conduct the ritual (which I imagine would involve items and symbolic representations emblematic of the time period you want to visit), and you enter a slumber during which your soul trades times with another of your incarnations, <i>Quantum Leap</i>-style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T18:32:32-08:00","id":1351757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351745#post1351745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eternals also have the bit that what <i>makes</i> them eternal is a mystical item: if it had a Curse associated with it, it would nearly fit into the array of mystical items that the Arisen deal with.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is actually the case that these items are Relics and work like them, save that their Powers and Curse ares centered on and suited to their creator. Eternal Relics are described as such in Chapter 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T20:06:02-08:00","id":1351771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351757#post1351757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is actually the case that these items are Relics and work like them, save that their Powers and Curse ares centered on and suited to their creator. Eternal Relics are described as such in Chapter 4.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given their inspiration, I'm surprised that the Eternals are just as likely to die from mortal causes as the Reborn. Even the Tenacious Eternity merit only adds Durability to their Relic; no mention of any Dorian Grey 'push fatal injuries into the painting' tricks for all their claims of phylacteries.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also where did Shades come from? Not bashing anything in the manuscript but the first hint of them is in the Antagonist chapter. Are they the 'other' souls we encounter in Duat? I know we won't see the fiends until we get the storytelling chapter...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 11-29-2019, 11:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T20:16:22-08:00","id":1351775,"title":"","content":"So I was wondering something, can other immortals have Cults dedicated to them. Could a Reborn have a cult? Or are Cults in a mechanical sense something strictly mummy.<br /> <br /> I was also thinking of some of my issues with the way the immortals in said chapter are organized, and I wish the template section had the same character creation rules format as say the Psiads or Superiors from Trinity. Yes, I know they are two gamelines but the format of templates are roughly the equivalent, as is the nature of character creation. Having the template be organized thusly allows for a much easier flow on character creation.<br /> <br /> So I do understand that this is a holiday weekend for those in America, but I do hope that the writers and developers are reading this and thinking about what we are saying when it comes to the immortals stuff. Especially because what there is is really freaken cool, it just needs some clarification and editing to be made pretty perfect.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Oh, I just noticed something. <br /> <br /> Gift of Years merit says &quot;dot of Sekhem&quot;. <br /> <br /> Endless Potency merit says &quot;point of Sekhem&quot;.<br /> <br /> Now I know in some ways this is being nitpicky but at the same time in CoD rules there is a difference between a DOT of something and a POINT of something. The former is a permanent growth and the later is sort of an energy that can be used but recharges. This is really important in Sekhem as there are no Sekhem points. <br /> <br /> As a personal thought I could see having it so the lesser immortals have Sekhem dots and Sekhem points, with the later gained by experience and the former coming with some sort of recharge. As they can go up to Sekhem 5, they can't have more than 5 points at one time, and that is only for the greatest of immortals. <br /> <br /> Then we have the Arisen, beings so potent that their understanding of Sekhem is deep enough that they realize its fivefold, and thus instead of them having Sekhem points they have instead Pillars, in both dot and point format. <br /> <br /> Same energy, but different understandings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 11-29-2019, 11:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T20:17:42-08:00","id":1351778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351771#post1351771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given their inspiration, I'm surprised that the Eternals are just as likely to die from mortal causes as the Reborn. Even the Tenacious Eternity merit only adds Durability to their Relic; no mention of any Dorian Grey 'push fatal injuries into the painting' tricks for all their claims of phylacteries.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also where did Shades come from? Not bashing anything in the manuscript but the first hint of them is in the Antagonist chapter. Are they the 'other' souls we encounter in Duat? I know we won't see the fiends until we get the storytelling chapter...</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s where the shades are, too. When I put in the ephemeral rules, I slipped some in for shades as well while I was at it.<br /> Edit: And the Eternals literally can\u2019t die unless their anchor is destroyed. The preview says they can\u2019t be killed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","user":"White Oak Dragon","date":". 11-29-2019, 11:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T21:10:55-08:00","id":1351783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351778#post1351778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That\u2019s where the shades are, too. When I put in the ephemeral rules, I slipped some in for shades as well while I was at it.<br /> Edit: And the Eternals literally can\u2019t die unless their anchor is destroyed. The preview says they can\u2019t be killed.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think it should be made clear that eventually they will heal completely from even the most crippling injury as well, because yeah shotting an Eternal in the head won't kill them, but it would leave them brain damaged and if you cut off an eternals legs and cut up their eyes, it doesn't kill them, but without Asiren support, they also don't regenerate their body parts and they stay maimed for eternity and I don't think that is what you intended. Just add something like &quot;can never been be killed and always makes a full recovery&quot; would solve that. Even Eternals that don't have a pillar invested in them should make full recoveries from any injury as long as their relic is in good shape, even if they still only heal at a human rate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T21:33:46-08:00","id":1351786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351587#post1351587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Some Judges will likely give a damn (ones against crimes against the sacred and slaughter for example), but the idea that the Judges are blanket against it is a boring 1eism. Like, it even mentions that both Arisen and Judges call upon them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Personally, I'm bored by the fact that an eldritch abomination that bleeds scorpions and shatters the mind of mortals has been downgraded to an occult pokemon statted up with the boilerplate Rank/Essence/Bane/Ban chart that every other immaterial being and their dog just has to have in 2nd edition. More and more I'm convinced that I'll just be mining 2nd edition for any good ideas I can convert back to 1st edition (you know, the good edition) and leave the downgraded setting for the rest of you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T21:53:04-08:00","id":1351788,"title":"","content":"I would like to say that the notion behind Sekhem Incantations is a very good and potentially sad set of hooks for dealing with a benbenet \u2014 drawing on the fear and shame of an avatar's mortal core to deny it some of its potency feels like a nice means of running the gamut of do-we-feel-good-about-doing-this for manifestations ranging from sorcerous bastards with a cutththroat eye for power to well-meaning people driven into a dark place by a bad situation and the attention of a primordial demon-god. It's definitely the sort of thing that suggests the Arisen feel some ways about these encounters when they remember them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T03:36:36-08:00","id":1351830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351771#post1351771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given their inspiration, I'm surprised that the Eternals are just as likely to die from mortal causes as the Reborn. Even the Tenacious Eternity merit only adds Durability to their Relic; no mention of any Dorian Grey 'push fatal injuries into the painting' tricks for all their claims of phylacteries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dorian Grey's portrait ages in his place and takes on the consequences of his sins (i.e. the effects of drug use). The whole transferring actual injuries comes from much later adaptations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T06:18:01-08:00","id":1351852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351786#post1351786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Personally, I'm bored by the fact that an eldritch abomination that bleeds scorpions and shatters the mind of mortals has been downgraded to an occult pokemon statted up with the boilerplate Rank/Essence/Bane/Ban chart that every other immaterial being and their dog just has to have in 2nd edition. More and more I'm convinced that I'll just be mining 2nd edition for any good ideas I can convert back to 1st edition (you know, the good edition) and leave the downgraded setting for the rest of you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. Meanwhile, everyone who understands that game mechanics are needed to actually do things in a relatively rules heavy system will enjoy the fact that Judges are active in the world and also remember that they were never invulnerable, just unreachable.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm skeptical that you know what &quot;avatar&quot; means; the form a benbenet assumes is literally only a small portion of their patron. The real Judge is the emanation, you know the <i>environment. </i>You oppose the Judges. You <i>fight </i>the <i>benbenet, </i>who is either a person or a sacred artifact. You know, like in Call of Cthulhu, which is based on the concept of eldritch abominations. Really, if anything it confirms just how vast the Judges are; it's only a moderate effort for them to anoint a person so that they become a demigod, and once there, the very rules of existence change to the Judge's specifications. The assessor of Ma'at is <i>here, </i>and you will play by <i>its </i>rules. Mummies are unique in that the Incantations allow them to <i>briefly </i>change the rules to something more fair when the benbenet gets serious. <br /> <br /> Also, all of this is ignoring a very pertinent detail; Dreams of Avarice is still canon. It is still a book that exists in-universe, and it's the most accurate and detailed view of Iremite creation mythology. In Iremite myth, the very fact that people can be content is an act of <i>successful rebellion, </i>a gift from Sutekh becoming sick of his siblings caring more about their own survival than actually creating justice. Not being able to oppose the Judges at all is noncanonical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T09:32:17-08:00","id":1351878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351775#post1351775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I was wondering something, can other immortals have Cults dedicated to them. Could a Reborn have a cult? Or are Cults in a mechanical sense something strictly mummy.<br /> <br /> I was also thinking of some of my issues with the way the immortals in said chapter are organized, and I wish the template section had the same character creation rules format as say the Psiads or Superiors from Trinity. Yes, I know they are two gamelines but the format of templates are roughly the equivalent, as is the nature of character creation. Having the template be organized thusly allows for a much easier flow on character creation.<br /> <br /> So I do understand that this is a holiday weekend for those in America, but I do hope that the writers and developers are reading this and thinking about what we are saying when it comes to the immortals stuff. Especially because what there is is really freaken cool, it just needs some clarification and editing to be made pretty perfect.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Oh, I just noticed something. <br /> <br /> Gift of Years merit says &amp;quot;dot of Sekhem&amp;quot;. <br /> <br /> Endless Potency merit says &amp;quot;point of Sekhem&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> Now I know in some ways this is being nitpicky but at the same time in CoD rules there is a difference between a DOT of something and a POINT of something. The former is a permanent growth and the later is sort of an energy that can be used but recharges. This is really important in Sekhem as there are no Sekhem points. <br /> <br /> As a personal thought I could see having it so the lesser immortals have Sekhem dots and Sekhem points, with the later gained by experience and the former coming with some sort of recharge. As they can go up to Sekhem 5, they can't have more than 5 points at one time, and that is only for the greatest of immortals. <br /> <br /> Then we have the Arisen, beings so potent that their understanding of Sekhem is deep enough that they realize its fivefold, and thus instead of them having Sekhem points they have instead Pillars, in both dot and point format. <br /> <br /> Same energy, but different understandings.</div> </div> </div> </div> I noticed that too. It could be clearer how that works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T09:46:50-08:00","id":1351880,"title":"","content":"Especially since it's possible to invest Pillars into cultists (including Endless cultists).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T13:36:12-08:00","id":1351910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351852#post1351852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay. Meanwhile, everyone who understands that game mechanics are needed to actually do things in a relatively rules heavy system will enjoy the fact that Judges are active in the world and also remember that they were never invulnerable, just unreachable.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm skeptical that you know what &quot;avatar&quot; means; the form a benbenet assumes is literally only a small portion of their patron. The real Judge is the emanation, you know the <i>environment. </i>You oppose the Judges. You <i>fight </i>the <i>benbenet, </i>who is either a person or a sacred artifact. You know, like in Call of Cthulhu, which is based on the concept of eldritch abominations. Really, if anything it confirms just how vast the Judges are; it's only a moderate effort for them to anoint a person so that they become a demigod, and once there, the very rules of existence change to the Judge's specifications. The assessor of Ma'at is <i>here, </i>and you will play by <i>its </i>rules. Mummies are unique in that the Incantations allow them to <i>briefly </i>change the rules to something more fair when the benbenet gets serious.<br /> <br /> Also, all of this is ignoring a very pertinent detail; Dreams of Avarice is still canon. It is still a book that exists in-universe, and it's the most accurate and detailed view of Iremite creation mythology. In Iremite myth, the very fact that people can be content is an act of <i>successful rebellion, </i>a gift from Sutekh becoming sick of his siblings caring more about their own survival than actually creating justice. Not being able to oppose the Judges at all is noncanonical.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The post you were quoting looks like it is referring to Amkhata.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23896-mirthless","name":"Mirthless","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T14:28:59-08:00","id":1351915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351852#post1351852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay. Meanwhile, everyone who understands that game mechanics are needed to actually do things in a relatively rules heavy system will enjoy the fact that Judges are active in the world and also remember that they were never invulnerable, just unreachable.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm skeptical that you know what &quot;avatar&quot; means; the form a benbenet assumes is literally only a small portion of their patron. The real Judge is the emanation, you know the <i>environment. </i>You oppose the Judges. You <i>fight </i>the <i>benbenet, </i>who is either a person or a sacred artifact. You know, like in Call of Cthulhu, which is based on the concept of eldritch abominations. Really, if anything it confirms just how vast the Judges are; it's only a moderate effort for them to anoint a person so that they become a demigod, and once there, the very rules of existence change to the Judge's specifications. The assessor of Ma'at is <i>here, </i>and you will play by <i>its </i>rules. Mummies are unique in that the Incantations allow them to <i>briefly </i>change the rules to something more fair when the benbenet gets serious.<br /> <br /> Also, all of this is ignoring a very pertinent detail; Dreams of Avarice is still canon. It is still a book that exists in-universe, and it's the most accurate and detailed view of Iremite creation mythology. In Iremite myth, the very fact that people can be content is an act of <i>successful rebellion, </i>a gift from Sutekh becoming sick of his siblings caring more about their own survival than actually creating justice. Not being able to oppose the Judges at all is noncanonical.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Soooo, on the one hand I feel like you make a very good and passionate argument with several excellent points against anyone who doesn't like the Judges being made manifest or whatever it is you were theoretically arguing against. On the other I am highly bemused you've gone to all this trouble to make this well crafted argument in response to a comment that was never about the Judges manifesting and indeed you are entirely preaching to the choir. I'm a fan of the 42 assholes showing up in the real world with all the psuedo apocalyptic trimming of the original story Call of Cthulhu. I was saying that I prefer the first edition version of the Amkhata better than second and will probably stick to that edition given other issues I have with Second Edition overall (never been a big fan of tilts or conditions for example).The bennet and avatar concepts are pretty much guaranteed to be converted for my game as its arguably the best addition to the new setting with immortals coming in a decent second.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T16:15:29-08:00","id":1351929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351775#post1351775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I was wondering something, can other immortals have Cults dedicated to them. Could a Reborn have a cult? Or are Cults in a mechanical sense something strictly mummy.<br /> <br /> I was also thinking of some of my issues with the way the immortals in said chapter are organized, and I wish the template section had the same character creation rules format as say the Psiads or Superiors from Trinity. Yes, I know they are two gamelines but the format of templates are roughly the equivalent, as is the nature of character creation. Having the template be organized thusly allows for a much easier flow on character creation.<br /> <br /> So I do understand that this is a holiday weekend for those in America, but I do hope that the writers and developers are reading this and thinking about what we are saying when it comes to the immortals stuff. Especially because what there is is really freaken cool, it just needs some clarification and editing to be made pretty perfect.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> *SNIP*</div> </div> </div> </div>In answer to the question voiced in the very first line; yes. All the Timeless gain access to the Timeless merits and Cult is considered a Timeless merit. It does imply that it is Mummy only with the description, but unlike Artisan's Aptitude, it does run off anything in the Arisen template. It also has clear benefits to Immortals (unlike Dead Flesh) and is arguably a social merit. Certainly if the Unchained and the Begotten can have cultists, Blood Bathers and Reborn can have them too.<br /> <br /> Plus, if an Immortal can contribute merit dots to the Arisen's cult it makes them more valuable as recruits (at the cost of them potentially hi-jacking the cult).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 11-30-2019, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-02T02:07:02-08:00","id":1352126,"title":"","content":"So, I'm not on the Kickstarter, I've been a bit skeptical about 2e for a while and I don't want to pay for it until I'm sure it's something I want to read, but I've been keeping up with these forum posts and would it be fair to say that a problem with the book so far is how cramped it is? It feels like every time a chapter is released there will be an array of comments along the lines of &quot;it would have been better if they went into more detail/added more content&quot; and I'm starting to get a picture of a book that's trying to do too many things at once and can't quite force all the various things they want into the limited page count they have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-02T02:33:03-08:00","id":1352128,"title":"","content":"If you want to know, you can pledge long enough to get the files, then cancel your pledge if you don't like what you see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-02T02:41:26-08:00","id":1352129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352128#post1352128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to know, you can pledge long enough to get the files, then cancel your pledge if you don't like what you see.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, at this point you only have three days to go through all the previews and form an opinion before deciding whether to support the book or not. I really do understand wanting to ask others first who've had time to analyse the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-02T11:57:34-08:00","id":1352193,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about a Closed Rite that can be used by a group of immortals (say the Reborn) to basically snap their immortal soul's enlightenment to another life in either the past or the future. The idea is that the present is a sort of home base location, or rather a home body location, while the past or future lives are basically adventure and mini campaign arc locations. the idea would be that something is needed and so the group conduct the ritual, snap to the past or move to the future, adventure for a bit, gain the knowledge or resources, and then snap back to the present. The future could give knowledge while the past could give the Cult something that they needed. (Example, they return to the present having completed an adventure in the past and are met an hour later by a courier with a message from a bank which says that at this date and time they are to reveal the contents of the vault. Contents which are needed to complete a particular task.) <br /> <br /> Of course, to add a sense of urgency or large scale issue, another group could also have access to the secret rite as well. Which leads to the two groups time jumping. <br /> <br /> Now, after writing this out I do have to say in themes (since its not really about horror or curses) this might fit better using the Trinity Continuum rules than the CoD rules, but that said the idea came to me from thinking about the Reborn. But even more I like the low key nature of the powers that the players would have in such a game, with it being the Supernatural Merits rather than the more world shaping powers of the Arisen, or Vampires, Werewolves, or Mages. (That said, again, I could see if the campaign goes long enough the players would unlock something that would awaken within their Sekhem the Pillars, which would then lead to the presence of maybe Affinities or Utterances. Though that would be late game epic level adventuring.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T04:06:33-08:00","id":1352329,"title":"","content":"The last backer preview is out! Come visit not-so-sunny Duat in chapter 7, or any of our other lovely settings in chapter 6!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T05:44:03-08:00","id":1352343,"title":"","content":"Mummy 1st was always a game of Fighting Time.<br /> <br /> Mummy 2nd is still that game, and one of Fighting Eternity* as well.<br /> <br /> *Sempiternity, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T06:07:16-08:00","id":1352345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352329#post1352329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The last backer preview is out! Come visit not-so-sunny Duat in chapter 7, or any of our other lovely settings in chapter 6!</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't right now. My daily Descent is over, and I must sleep for a time. (Ironic, considering that the Arisen visit Duat between Descents; but I won't be able to find out what their time in Duat is like right away, because I must visit my own kind of \u201cDuat\u201d now.) I'll check it out when my next Descent begins, probably in about six to eight hours. In the meantime, I'm out of Sekhem. Goodnight!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T06:17:21-08:00","id":1352347,"title":"","content":"I am very intrigued by Antarctica being named Second Irem. Much like ice and snow, the ideas begin to crystallize, fufufufufu. &gt;83","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T06:44:03-08:00","id":1352351,"title":"","content":"Annnnd now I want to play a fiend of Duat or a friend to them. Anpu knows they need one (that isn't a suffering sponge).<br /> <br /> I do think I know what Duat lacks as a Lower Depth, though; Mercy. The only end to pain you can have is part of a transaction or by offloading it. Judges don't see it as a problem, of course, and Ammut's point of view starts to sound awfully plausible the more you fail (my headcanon is that being &quot;condemned to Duat&quot; is really not being worthy enough to ascend to A'aru yet, but not accepting the Devourer's dubious mercy - so long as you don't volunteer to be lunch, you're technically still not classified as Ammut Chow yet, because you're showing the will to keep trying).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T06:49:06-08:00","id":1352352,"title":"","content":"Still skimming and reading more bits carefully one at a time, but DUAT JOURNEYS, complete with a whole managerie of Fiends, as well as temporal shenanigans for all Mummies, are extremely exciting. I dearly love the section of the chapter dedicated to chronicle-defining story hooks, but it is <i>very strange</i> that Apotheosis doesn't have a full entry here, and kind of sad too. We can gleam the elements of the Apotheosis narrative in several places, but that there isn't a dedicated section to it is somewhat dissonant with the build-up to Apotheosis in the Starfall sections of the Guild write-ups.<br /> <br /> The locations also seem to have some fascinating bits. I like that most of them seem to go into the history of the place, because that's actually pertinent to the Arisen; you could play through potentially any point, or multiple points, of these settings' recorded time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T07:22:51-08:00","id":1352358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352352#post1352352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still skimming and reading more bits carefully one at a time, but DUAT JOURNEYS, complete with a whole managerie of Fiends, as well as temporal shenanigans for all Mummies, are extremely exciting. I dearly love the section of the chapter dedicated to chronicle-defining story hooks, but it is <i>very strange</i> that Apotheosis doesn't have a full entry here, and kind of sad too. We can gleam the elements of the Apotheosis narrative in several places, but that there isn't a dedicated section to it is somewhat dissonant with the build-up to Apotheosis in the Starfall sections of the Guild write-ups.<br /> <br /> The locations also seem to have some fascinating bits. I like that most of them seem to go into the history of the place, because that's actually pertinent to the Arisen; you could play through potentially any point, or multiple points, of these settings' recorded time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apotheosis lacks a dedicated entry because we decided that it would need more space than we could give it to do it any justice. I thought about trying to cram the basics into a smaller space, but it just didn\u2019t seem fair to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T07:24:29-08:00","id":1352359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352358#post1352358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Apotheosis lacks a dedicated entry because we decided that it would need more space than we could give it to do it any justice. I thought about trying to cram the basics into a smaller space, but it just didn\u2019t seem fair to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a sensible answer, thank you. The lack of it hurts, but I hope we can see it in a future supplement or the companion!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T07:41:35-08:00","id":1352362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352359#post1352359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a sensible answer, thank you. The lack of it hurts, but I hope we can see it in a future supplement or the companion!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Me too, believe me!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T10:07:01-08:00","id":1352376,"title":"","content":"So am I the only one who is concerned that Second Irem likely was touched by the Contagion? Also don\u2019t mind me, I\u2019m just happy to see more justification for Amkhata domestication xD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T10:14:05-08:00","id":1352378,"title":"","content":"As I said on the kickstarter itself while we may not have rules for Apotheosis we do have mention of the potential of a sixth Pillar. The presence of that as a possibility opens up soooooo many potential setting and campaign elements that is quite cool. <br /> <br /> I mean imagine the idea that instead of having the standard five or the special sixth the various immortal groups might have their own special Pillars, that is quite cool to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T11:07:29-08:00","id":1352390,"title":"","content":"I dig the Cuzco setting. Lots of interesting stuff going on there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They are particularly interested in the development of penguin-based Amkhata. </div> </div> </div>Oh my god. . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T11:48:29-08:00","id":1352402,"title":"","content":"The thing that confuses me is that we get this long sidebar telling us that Apotheosis is bad and wrong because it's anticipated that mummies seeking power for themselves (not what apotheosis was in 1e) is part of the cosmic cycle, just as the Shaniatu sought power beyond their station, but then there's no support for this notion later in the book.<br /> <br /> I think the writers missed what Apotheosis was in 1e. It wasn't accumulating power or &quot;tearing down the master's house with the master's tools.&quot; Apotheosis was about an artistic class abandoning the cycle of exploitation and the power it gave them. They rebuild their identity and have to refrain from hurting their cultists (since that threatens memory in 1e) and in return are freed from the Judges' control and gain control of their own labor, represented (imo) by their ability to create relics again. They lose access to top tier Utterances, and their activities are heavily circumscribed by the fact that losing memory sends them immediately into a death cycle.<br /> <br /> The change I would suggest would be to make the book's perspective on Apotheosis to be a thing that's debated among arisen, instead of the reader being told what is the right or wrong way to rebel by the authorial voice in the sidebar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T12:17:31-08:00","id":1352404,"title":"","content":"My thoughts. <br /> <br /> Chapter Six<br /> ------------<br /> <br /> The intro paragraph is pretty epic. I especially like the sentence that starts the second paragraph, the one which begins with &quot;They crawl from tombs an crypts..&quot; Its very poetic. <br /> <br /> Historical Adventurers is a nice sidebar, thumbs up on what it represents. <br /> <br /> Cuzco, Peru - Oooh, how interesting. I mean the fact that there are Iremite mummies here from the first sothic turn is nifty. Lots of potential. <br /> <br /> Denmark - I wouldn't have thought of this place as a central to the mummy myth, so the information in this part is fascianting. So thumbs up. <br /> <br /> Halifax, Canada - For some reason I misstyped this as Hekufax, which amused me considering Heku is magic. Anyway, having Canada be the location for mummy intrigue is kind of brilliant. Especially the whole &quot;no one knows who you can trust, maybe not even yourself!&quot; I like that. <br /> <br /> Necromancer - In terms of the mummy setting and rules what exactly is a necromancer? <br /> <br /> Also yay on the Saboteur saving relics from the evi judges. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That said I love hearing things like &quot;Relic architecture&quot; and &quot;Sekhem-collecting network&quot;. <br /> <br /> Antartica - Oh this is cool. A part of Irem in a land of snow and ice, so cool. I also really like how Antartica is a place in a lot of CoD splats that has some mythic potential, its really cool. <br /> <br /> I LOVE how Irem came to this continent and established a base, outpost, or even city. Its really cool. <br /> <br /> South Africa - The whole rebel movement idea related to Irem interests me. Especially as what might have been 'bad' from Irem's perspective might honestly be 'good' from our own. And that leads to potential campaign seeds. <br /> <br /> New Zealand - Some interesting material here. <br /> <br /> Hong Kong - One one hand I am not sure I would use this, but on the other haand it makes PERFECT sense as a potential mummy campaign location. So for that reason I am glad its here. <br /> <br /> All in all Chapter Six is a good one. The way its organized, the location it covers, and the way things are presented are fun. I don't need the mateiral now, but I do think come certain campaign ideas the material present would be very very useful. <br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> Chapter Seven<br /> --------------<br /> <br /> I have been looking forward to this chapter quite a bit. <br /> <br /> The intro is well done. Nice advice. Everything from Tips to Sharing is informative. <br /> <br /> I'm not sure if the safety guidelines sidebar is necessary but its not bad that it is there. <br /> <br /> Troupes and Pyramids - The the idea of using something world epic as a starting point for group unity, and then having that resonate through history due to the non-linear nature of things sounds interesting to me. <br /> <br /> But even more so does the whole idea of a number of mummy Cults coming together over the years. The nifty thing about this is that the new united cult is going to be different then the sum of its parts. Which might also explain certain differences and variaties in terms or departments or whatnot. I like that. Its cool. <br /> <br /> Heck, there is nothing that says certain parts of the old cults might not have been abosrbed or when they were there were elemenets kept secret. Which is fun. <br /> <br /> The whole thing about non-mummies in a game is amusing when it is mentioned that a mortal could be the grandson or grandfather of a character. I also like the element of letting the player keep the XP gained from other characters, even as things get rearranged and such. In this I can easily see the Reborn coming into play, and that could be fun. <br /> <br /> The Truly Epic Chronicle sounds fun. hehe<br /> <br /> Neter-Khertet<br /> <br /> This is a very interesting place. I like the elements of it - the two mountains, the storm, the caves, the nature of the land. Its very eerie but its also interesting and has some potential. <br /> <br /> I wonder if something could be 'built' here by a mummy, leading them to have some sort of base of operations in the space between. hmm<br /> <br /> Death Cycles<br /> <br /> Okay so technically the above doesn't work, but, nothing says that they can't find some other way to get into twilight to allow such a thing. <br /> <br /> That said the rules for resurrection are interesting and I like how 'simple' it is. This is especially useful as it allows for a relatively quick return to the adventure going on in the land of the living, and that is important. <br /> <br /> Duat<br /> <br /> I like the idea thought I have to admit the whole Law of Suffering has me going &quot;yeah no.&quot; So there is that. <br /> <br /> Fiends are interesting. I like how they are the native 'life' of Duat. Very fun. As is the fact that they can find a wya to enter the world, which leads them to becoming Amkhata.<br /> <br /> The Seven Gates<br /> <br /> This stuff is cool. I am not entirely sure how I would want to use it, but its cool, that I am very sure on. I like the potential of it. <br /> <br /> Sooo don't trink from the cup of Anpu, gotcha. <br /> <br /> Okay. So upon ending every Descent they descend into Duat where they face the Trials. Upon success they wait a bit in the timeless place that is there before arising again for the next Descent. <br /> <br /> Here is what I don't get, if the potential for failure is really there then that means mummies aren't truly forever, which makes no sense to me. Which is why I think I might go with the idea that failure is not really real in the whole &quot;you will be permanently removed&quot; sense but rather failure leaves the Judges or the Devourer with an easier time modifying the mummy. Which is why you don't want to fail. <br /> <br /> Oh wait, just got to Penalties. lol. I see we actually were thinking the same thing. So yeah nice. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Escaping the Cycle<br /> <br /> First, as a random thought, are the blessed fields of starry A'aru real. Like I mean are they somewhere that someone could actually go to. Or are they a promise that has no true bearing. I'm just curious. <br /> <br /> Apotheois is cool and so is Reward. Now I want to find a way for my mummy to get those stats. <br /> <br /> Secret Name. Woah, what would shifting allegiance to Anpu actually entail. Hmm<br /> <br /> As random thing, if one stops having to go through Duat and instead only has to face a death cycle does that mean they never get to city the black and red city? Which is probably a good thing but I am curious. <br /> <br /> Storytelling Timelesseness<br /> <br /> Nice start, but this is particularly potent &quot;None<br /> but the Judges can permanently alter the Arisen, and even they face limitations.&quot;<br /> <br /> Adrift in Endless Waters - I love this section. So cool. Time as a river and time as a wheel is both really cool. hehe<br /> <br /> The Churning Maelstrom - If I thought I liked the previous section this one had me grinning and going &quot;f-in awesome!!&quot; So yeah this is brilliant. Love it. <br /> <br /> Different Flows - AWESOME stuff. This is some great material, some great options. <br /> <br /> So yeah, this stuff is cool. Very very cool. <br /> <br /> Tales through the Sandglass<br /> <br /> Nice start. Good information. <br /> <br /> Biker Fiends from Duat - I don't mind the idea though turning a good biker gang bad is not fun for me, especially as there is nothing that can be done to save them. So yeah not for me. <br /> <br /> The Shadow of Sothis - This is cool. I also like the whole mystery behidn the relic and why it works and how it works and how it keeps on coming back even though it should be gone. So yeah that's cool. <br /> <br /> Far From Home - Woah. Wow. Just wow. So much fun potential for a campaign start. That said, I really hope that a mummy could wake up and act in other ways than simply bloodshed. Imagine a mummy waking up and immediately making those around them obedient or something. That could be fun. Still, as it is written, tjhis is brilliant. <br /> <br /> Children of Irem - The idea of the Deathless having a child is kind of intriguing. Its also a potential fun campaign variant. <br /> <br /> The Darkest Turn - There can be only one! Also, while nicely written, this one ain't for me. <br /> <br /> Memory Broker - I don't get this. It eats memory, but so what as far as the mummies are concerned since they don't have much they remember. Eating memory is more useful as a curse for a being that remembers everything. Honestly, I think having the 'monster' unlock the mummy's memories would be more interesting, especially if the horror of the bargain was great. That said as the horror of being a monster is not something I care to dwell on in roleplaying this eleement is not gonna be really dwelled on by me. <br /> <br /> Mortal Power - This could be interesting. Lots of potential here. <br /> <br /> First and Foremost - I honestly reject the claim of this section (as related to the horror of memory) and so don't really see it as a potential campaign point. BUT, that said, the idea of the 'failures' and the 'testers' of what would be the Rite of Return are still around is an intriguing idea, one that has potential to be used and played around with.<br /> <br /> Build-a-Beast - This is cool. This is a nifty campaign idea. This could be something a saga is built around. <br /> <br /> The More You Know - This is a perfectly designed campaign idea. Which side do you support, which side do you fight, what happens if both are right or wrong and something else goes on. So yeah, this is very cool. <br /> <br /> Mummies on Mars - Firstly, love the name. This is cool. What a nice set up. Its also quite believable in terms of design. I also like how there is something for those both on Mars and on Earth, so that is cool. <br /> <br /> Duat Falls - Everything about this except that the Rite of Return might fail (to me its a one time act that is now foundational with no chance of being stopped) is brilliant. Stop the Judges. Free yourself by just simply not listening to them. Over power them and take the city and make it yours. So yeah, goo stuff. I also like the whole meret thing going to Duat together and facing the judges as one. So yeah good stuff. <br /> <br /> A Glimpse of the End - See this is cool in the sense that if you have it be a Descent early in a chronicle then you can have the players seek to fight against it over its length and span. So while I don't consider it the true future it would be a perfect &quot;Oh shit, things are bad, lets fix it&quot; element. <br /> <br /> Begins Again - Oooh yes, this is cool. Very very cool. So cool in fact I want to think more on it, to analyze the potential, to dwell on the interesting saga it can have. So yeah, very cool.<br /> <br /> This is a cool part of the chapter. It has a lot of potential interesting elements and story notes. I like the format, a few paragraphs and then bulleted ideas. I like the nature of it. <br /> <br /> Good stuff. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T12:18:11-08:00","id":1352405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352402#post1352402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The change I would suggest would be to make the book's perspective on Apotheosis to be a thing that's debated among arisen, instead of the reader being told what is the right or wrong way to rebel by the authorial voice in the sidebar.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2026 wasn't what that sidebar was saying.<br /> <br /> A major point of emphasis in this edition has been the fact that pursuing Memory often <i>hurts</i> \u2014 that the Arisen often have to confront the fact that they have done some <i>awful stuff</i> that they want to deny. The &quot;Apotheotic Movement&quot; sidebar is talking about all forms of pursuing freedom from the Judges' mastery, not just the mechanical state of Apotheosis, and pursuing that means gaining Memory and discovering all the things you've been made to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T12:27:34-08:00","id":1352407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352405#post1352405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2026 wasn't what that sidebar was saying.<br /> <br /> A major point of emphasis in this edition has been the fact that pursuing Memory often <i>hurts</i> \u2014 that the Arisen often have to confront the fact that they have done some <i>awful stuff</i> that they want to deny. The &quot;Apotheotic Movement&quot; sidebar is talking about all forms of pursuing freedom from the Judges' mastery, not just the mechanical state of Apotheosis, and pursuing that means gaining Memory and discovering all the things you've been made to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm referring to this:<br /> <br /> &quot;But this is no true threat. It is part of the formula. As civilizations rise, they too attempt to achieve godhood, a placement in the eye of the pyramid, to gaze over all the world and aim it towards new destinies.&quot;<br /> <br /> Neall Price on the KS responded to questions about this view of Apotheosis by saying &quot;It's detailed a bit later, but it boils down to this: you cannot tear down the master's house with the master's tools. Gaining more power will never break your chains.&quot;<br /> <br /> Not only was this not detailed later (as far as I can tell), but it mischaracterizes 1e's Apotheosis without replacing it with anything new in the ST chapter. I wonder if a recharacterized Apotheosis was dropped due to wordcount limits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":61,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","user":"Octavo","date":". 12-03-2019, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T12:39:33-08:00","id":1352408,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar61_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"61\" data-vbnamecard=\"61\">Octavo</a> amusingly enough it also talks about how the Judges aren't as dominant and in control of the Arisen as they seem to pretend to be. That they have limits to what they can do to a mummy, which is why they do as much as they can to keep the mummies thinking they have to obey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T12:46:10-08:00","id":1352409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352407#post1352407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm referring to this:<br /> <br /> &quot;But this is no true threat. It is part of the formula. As civilizations rise, they too attempt to achieve godhood, a placement in the eye of the pyramid, to gaze over all the world and aim it towards new destinies.&quot;<br /> <br /> Neall Price on the KS responded to questions about this view of Apotheosis by saying &quot;It's detailed a bit later, but it boils down to this: you cannot tear down the master's house with the master's tools. Gaining more power will never break your chains.&quot;<br /> <br /> Not only was this not detailed later (as far as I can tell), but it mischaracterizes 1e's Apotheosis without replacing it with anything new in the ST chapter. I wonder if a recharacterized Apotheosis was dropped due to wordcount limits.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A) It was, this was made explicit earlier in the thread.<br /> <br /> B) That is still not what the sidebar or what the writers are saying. The post-Apotheosis 2E rule explicitly notes that Apotheosis is about becoming willingly unable to be a Sekhem capacitor in return for being free from Duat and the Judges forever, spending the rest of your henet cycles kicking back cold ones in Twilight. The &quot;master's tools&quot; is stealing Sekhem for the Judges or trying to retain all of the Rite of Return's power. By continuing to benefit from that system, you are complicit in your own entrapment - in other words, that sidebar's snarking at people who want to have power without responsibility, and think Apotheosis is the way there; all that's doing is repeating the Shan'iatu's mistakes. Which is, in fact, what 1E Apotheosis explicitly was; <i>Dreams of Avarice</i> made it explicit that you can chose the Judges' power or you can chose eternal humanity, not both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T12:52:32-08:00","id":1352410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352409#post1352409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> A) It was, this was made explicit earlier in the thread.<br /> <br /> B) That is still not what the sidebar or what the writers are saying. The post-Apotheosis 2E rule explicitly notes that Apotheosis is about becoming willingly unable to be a Sekhem capacitor in return for being free from Duat and the Judges forever, spending the rest of your henet cycles kicking back cold ones in Twilight. The &quot;master's tools&quot; is stealing Sekhem for the Judges or trying to retain all of the Rite of Return's power. By continuing to benefit from that system, you are complicit in your own entrapment - in other words, that sidebar's snarking at people who want to have power without responsibility, and think Apotheosis is the way there; all that's doing is repeating the Shan'iatu's mistakes. Which is, in fact, what 1E Apotheosis explicitly was; <i>Dreams of Avarice</i> made it explicit that you can chose the Judges' power or you can chose eternal humanity, not both.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sidebar really did not get that across, at least to me. I'm glad that was the writers' intentions though!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T13:01:49-08:00","id":1352412,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar661_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"661\" data-vbnamecard=\"661\">LordHeru</a> Of all the typos in all the timelines, Hekufax is by far and away the most appropriate! I am very glad you enjoy it! I was super pleased when I realized I could draw some of my favourite 1e aspects into the setting. The Su-Menent are the Necromancers in Mummy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T13:06:00-08:00","id":1352415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1351786#post1351786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'm bored by the fact that an eldritch abomination that bleeds scorpions and shatters the mind of mortals has been downgraded to an occult pokemon</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Eldritch pokemon that will inevitably break free and cause chaos&quot; is pretty much how I'd describe either version, only in this one, the Judges aren't going to pearl clutch over their use. These guys also seem a lot stronger. ymmv","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T13:08:56-08:00","id":1352416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352412#post1352412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar661_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"661\" data-vbnamecard=\"661\">LordHeru</a> Of all the typos in all the timelines, Hekufax is by far and away the most appropriate! I am very glad you enjoy it! I was super pleased when I realized I could draw some of my favourite 1e aspects into the setting. The Su-Menent are the Necromancers in Mummy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I giggled at Hekufax, it was pretty fun. <br /> <br /> And also yeah, the two chapters were brilliant. At the lowest there were some &quot;no, but&quot; with the 'but' being me thinking of side ways to use it but that was very much overshadowed by &quot;yes&quot; and &quot;yes, and&quot; so that was cool. I had fun going over it. The two chapters are brilliant. There are so many interesting plot elements and story seeds (I love story seeds, so the bulleted story seeds in both chapters were brilliant to me) that I could see half a dozen chronicles. I will also add that the non-linear nature of things was totally satysfying, so that was great to see. <br /> <br /> Ooooh, of course Necromancer represents the guild, duh. lol. I should have realized that but for some reason my mind went to &quot;what template are they&quot; lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T13:20:01-08:00","id":1352419,"title":"","content":"Sooo as a random idea for the immortals (especially the Reborn but the others as well) I was thinking of using the Eidetic Memory, Advanced Merit from Beast. This idea then led me to wondering if there are other merits, both template based and supernatural, that might fit for the immortals. Which is why I am posting this, to see if anyone else has any thoughts on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T13:30:10-08:00","id":1352421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which is, in fact, what 1E Apotheosis explicitly was; Dreams of Avarice made it explicit that you can chose the Judges' power or you can chose eternal humanity, not both. </div> </div> </div>Well\u2026 kind of. In 1e, an Arisen who achieves Apotheosis has maxed out all of his Pillars, has a high Memory, and has replaced his Sekhem with his Memory for most purposes (the most significant exception being access to the bulk of one's Utterances) and with Willpower and the aforementioned maxed-out Pillars for self-healing purposes (both being resources that are much easier to recover than Sekhem is). On top of that, he's invisible to the supernatural world (having reclaimed his True Name) and can move Sekhem <i>into</i> things, letting him <i>make</i> relics. The only power you actually sacrifice with Apotheosis is the higher levels of your Utterances and Relics. <br /> <br /> That's still really powerful. <br /> <br /> But yeah; thematically, the intent is that power and freedom are mutually exclusive. I read the passages in the manuscript about Apotheosis along the lines of \u201cwe don't really need to worry about mummies selling Apotheosis, because it's against their nature to give up power.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T13:58:54-08:00","id":1352427,"title":"","content":"Okay. I want to make sure I get something. <br /> <br /> At character creation an Arisen has Memory 3. The first scene its 0 but then afterward it goes to 3. This means they have a basic identity and a rough memory of one previous descent. This all makes sense to me. <br /> <br /> But here is where my question lies. So then the descent ends, that is they die. Another descent occurs. Do they start the next with Memory 3, or do they begin with Memory 2. With the reduction being explained as them drinking from the cup in Duat. Does it matter if a death cycle or trip to Duat occurs? <br /> <br /> I also can't help but notice that unlike the sanctity of experience there doesn't seem to be any sanctity of remembrance experience. This is telling because memory can be eaten by judges and gods and lost because of other reasons. <br /> <br /> Additionally how easy should it be to get remembrance experience? Should enough beats be gained to equal at least one point each descent? <br /> <br /> I ask for others thoughts on this as I personally dislike the whole memory issue and would much prefer characters with Memory 10 and the eidetic memory merits so yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T14:12:34-08:00","id":1352432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352427#post1352427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay. I want to make sure I get something. <br /> <br /> At character creation an Arisen has Memory 3. The first scene its 0 but then afterward it goes to 3. This means they have a basic identity and a rough memory of one previous descent. This all makes sense to me. <br /> <br /> But here is where my question lies. So then the descent ends, that is they die. Another descent occurs. Do they start the next with Memory 3, or do they begin with Memory 2. With the reduction being explained as them drinking from the cup in Duat. Does it matter if a death cycle or trip to Duat occurs? <br /> <br /> I also can't help but notice that unlike the sanctity of experience there doesn't seem to be any sanctity of remembrance experience. This is telling because memory can be eaten by judges and gods and lost because of other reasons. <br /> <br /> Additionally how easy should it be to get remembrance experience? Should enough beats be gained to equal at least one point each descent? <br /> <br /> I ask for others thoughts on this as I personally dislike the whole memory issue and would much prefer characters with Memory 10 and the eidetic memory merits so yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reminisce Experiences are not protected. Doing so would render threats to Memory meaningless. If you don\u2019t like Arisen Memory issues, you can freely ignore them for your games, but doing so does alter the Arisen experience considerably. I believe you were saying that you were going to be tweaking things for your games anyway, though, so it probably wouldn\u2019t be an issue for your table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T14:24:18-08:00","id":1352435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352432#post1352432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Reminisce Experiences are not protected. Doing so would render threats to Memory meaningless. If you don\u2019t like Arisen Memory issues, you can freely ignore them for your games, but doing so does alter the Arisen experience considerably. I believe you were saying that you were going to be tweaking things for your games anyway, though, so it probably wouldn\u2019t be an issue for your table.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotcha on the not protected thing. And yeah that makes sense. That said, was my general set up accurate as far as official ruling goes? I like to make sure I get the way things are before I start making changes. <br /> <br /> Basically does Memory loose a point every Descent or would it stay around 3 if the whole Duat trials aren't played through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T14:24:25-08:00","id":1352436,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say that removing the Memory issues is \u201ctweaking\u201d; more like \u201cradically overhauling\u201d. It would be like playing Vampire without Humanity issues. <br /> <br /> But if it works for you, great!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T14:28:47-08:00","id":1352438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352436#post1352436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't say that removing the Memory issues is \u201ctweaking\u201d; more like \u201cradically overhauling\u201d. It would be like playing Vampire without Humanity issues.<br /> <br /> But if it works for you, great!</div> </div> </div> </div>Its funny that you would say that, as humanity issues was never something I cared about either. (Espeically in the previous edition, I disliked humanity as morality and such.) (That said I also have to admit to not focusing deeply on the nuances of 2e vampires as there were some changes that I didn't like right off the bat. But honestly that is neither here nor there, hehe)<br /> <br /> But anyway, I honestly like fully figuring out rules before making changes. Which is why I wanted to get a full on sense of how 2e handled memory before I go and change things. <br /> <br /> I do have to admit, as a note, that memory is one of those reasons I sort of latched onto the Reborn as a template group. <br /> <br /> But I also have to make it clear, and I think my recent posts prove this, that there is much, very much, in 2e mummy that I like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T14:39:45-08:00","id":1352441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352427#post1352427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ask for others thoughts on this as I personally dislike the whole memory issue and would much prefer characters with Memory 10 and the eidetic memory merits so yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it explicitly states you can explicitly avoid drinking Anpu's Bottled Lethe Juice. PCs, I would typically expect to avoid it, but it gives justification why NPCs don't have as good of an idea of what's going on and works as an idea of why the PC might not know what's going on (besides nonlinear time).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T14:40:40-08:00","id":1352443,"title":"","content":"So, a sum up of the first read of the last preview (I may have missed some things, due to me being extremely tired right now)-<br /> <br /> I do really enjoy Peru and Denmark as Mummy settings. Johannesburg is also a good one. Still kinda disappointed that Cairo or Jerusalem are not in the list, but nevermind that. Antarctica is creepy- I like it being represented as an ever hungry realm, filled with rage and desire for vengeance. In a way, it makes me think about it less as Irem and more as Duat on the face of Earth. While I have no complains about the setting, I'm kinda conflicted by the fact that for a continent with practically no one in it it has already showed up three times as an example setting. Sure, each time was a very evocative and interesting presentation, but when it first showed up in Promethean I've thought for myself &quot;wow!&quot;. When it showed up in the third time I've thought to myself &quot;again?&quot;. I kinda hope that unless we will get an &quot;Antarctic Adventures&quot; supplement, that it won't be used again as an example setting, but that the wordcount would be devoted to a place yet to be explored in CofD.<br /> <br /> The presentation of Duat was really cool, IMO. I'm still confused why things like Shades and Fiends don't show up in the antagonists section, but in the Storytelling chapter. I'm a bit disappointed that unless I missed it (and again, I'm tired, so don't send the Judges after me if I'm wrong), I don't think I've seen any mention for the Shan'iatu being confined to feast upon vinegar and ash, nor any mention of the Heretic in relation for Apotheosis. Just things I've thought could have been cool. In general I must admit that 2e feels a bit less &quot;mythic&quot; than 1e, as the multitude of divinities outside the Judges takes a much lesser place in the setting. Some people may prefer it this way, but I must say I miss it.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how I feel about the &quot;Ocean of Time&quot;. It is an evocative image, sure, but it feels a bit foreign to me. My brain for some reason keeps equating &quot;Sea = Ammut&quot; (probably something from Dreams of Avarice), and it just makes me feel weird. When I think about non-linear time, my mind turns more towards sands and winds, less towards seas and currents. Blame my syntheses for this :P<br /> <br /> Anyway, on a more relevant note, I can;t say that non-linear time ever made me feel too excited: I'm ok with it, but that's more or less it. I assume that for me it makes the game feel less... ancient, I think? Like, I'm not sure I feel the weight of ages as much as I felt in 1e. The fact that time becomes meaningless turns it, IMO, that the weight of millennia feels less heavy, if non existent. Again, personal flavor thing. The example scenarios were nice, however, even if some of them are not my cup of tea. Again, nothing bad, just preference.<br /> <br /> As for the methods for &quot;escape&quot; presented in the section- like many others, of course I would have preferred to see more about Apotheosis. The concept of becoming a servant of Anpu is intriguing, but needs further development. The Neru are also a cool concept, and I really like the idea of the Judges offering their mummies even extra power in guise of tightening the chains even harder. The concept of usurping the Judges doesn't really captures my attention, on the other hand. It feels that the only thing coming out of it will be that the usurper would become the same tyrant. <br /> <br /> I did enjoyed the crossover mentions- not sure how I feel about the Judges forcing Paradox upon mages, especially as it is said &quot;as if they were Annunaki&quot;. The Annunaki, after all, aren't aware enough to knowingly force Paradox- it is the Abyss, which isn't exactly the same thing. Just something that stings my eye a bit. The Judges forcing Paradoxes feels a bit too much about one gameline sticking its fingers in another, and while I'm far from being against crossovers, the fact that the Judge personally mess with your magic is a bit weird. On the other hand, the Judges do personally hate you, so it makes sense.<br /> <br /> So all in all, a nice conclusion for Mummy. I would still want to understand what could actually threaten a mummy outside of failing their Judge so much that they let Shezmu to crush them into wine and feed the Devourer. Also, if I understand correctly, killing a mummy in a way that would not allow them to progress through the timeline would cause the mummy to practically &quot;swim' to another &quot;current&quot; and reborn in a timeline where they could continue their existence regularly? I understand that the Arisen ignore the regular paradoxes of time, but I assume they do so by forcing a path of their own through the sea of time, jumping between timelines in a way that for someone from the same timeline would believe to be non linear, but that there is a trajectory when looking in the whole multiverse. I still don't really get how existing in whole times in the same time is related to non linear time- that concept is actually very well grounded in linear timeline, where an object could exist in all places and all times simultaneously, and that our own sense of time is an illusion of self. It is, in fact, a very deterministic concept- everything was decided, the trajectory is already formed, it is only your mind which can't grasp it. If your mind could exist simultaneously across all the points in time and space, it would have known both its beginning and end. Unless by saying &quot;existing simultaneously in all times&quot; refers to existing simultaneously in all timelines, which is different and makes sense in the context of mummies as &quot;islands of stability&quot; in the endless sea of timelines. A convergent point towards all different possibilities flow. Was it the intention?<br /> <br /> Anyway, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"156\" data-vbnamecard=\"156\">Bunyip</a>, you mentioned to help me to understand what is the meaning of temporal death versus permanent death to mummies, and what could exactly completely destroy one for all eternity (unless the only way is &quot;failing so much that even your Judge will just throw you to Ammut's maw&quot;), and I redeem that offer. Did I got it more or less right, or is there something that I have missed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T14:48:32-08:00","id":1352448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352435#post1352435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gotcha on the not protected thing. And yeah that makes sense. That said, was my general set up accurate as far as official ruling goes? I like to make sure I get the way things are before I start making changes. <br /> <br /> Basically does Memory loose a point every Descent or would it stay around 3 if the whole Duat trials aren't played through.</div> </div> </div> </div>We probably need to give Memory effects between Descents another pass to make sure everything is clear. That said, since gaining a dot of Memory is a potential benefit from the Trials of Duat, it can be boosted up by one to compensate for a lost dot from Anpu\u2019s cup. You could even justify that benefit as Anpu giving them a drink that didn\u2019t strip their memories, for whatever enigmatic reason he might have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T14:49:45-08:00","id":1352449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352432#post1352432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reminisce Experiences are not protected. Doing so would render threats to Memory meaningless. If you don\u2019t like Arisen Memory issues, you can freely ignore them for your games, but doing so does alter the Arisen experience considerably. I believe you were saying that you were going to be tweaking things for your games anyway, though, so it probably wouldn\u2019t be an issue for your table.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would it hurt having Reminisce Experiences just be refunded as regular Experiences? It really fucking sucks when you've spent time amassing enough XP to advance your character only for it to go up in smoke. I know that losing a dot doesn't negate the playing experience you had while collecting the Beats, but it can still make you feel like you've lost progress. Especially in a game like Mummy where you're actively encouraged to increase your Memory instead of Vampire or CofD where you're more focused on not losing Humanity/Integrity.<br /> \u200b<br /> My group has long house ruled that you regain all XP for any traits you lose, not just Merits, which made losing those traits actually fun instead of something that's outright undesirable both in- and out-of-game. It doesn't affect me since we've already house ruled the game that way (and I still don't know if I'll get to even play Mummy), but I'm seriously recommending doing something similar as a standard rule. I think Mummy is the best game for it, too, due to how much of a setback Memory loss is and that using different XP currencies makes it so you can refund the XP without some players immediately putting it right back into Memory again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T14:58:42-08:00","id":1352452,"title":"","content":"Also<br /> <br /> Narwhals (Amkhata)swimming in the ocean, causing a commotion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T15:03:16-08:00","id":1352455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352443#post1352443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda hope that unless we will get an &quot;Antarctic Adventures&quot; supplement, that it won't be used again as an example setting, but that the wordcount would be devoted to a place yet to be explored in CofD.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's shown up as a setting in the Contagion Chronicle and in the two splats premised around entropy and lifeless wastelands. I don't think there's much cause for concern.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The presentation of Duat was really cool, IMO. I'm still confused why things like Shades and Fiends don't show up in the antagonists section, but in the Storytelling chapter. I'm a bit disappointed that unless I missed it (and again, I'm tired, so don't send the Judges after me if I'm wrong), I don't think I've seen any mention for the Shan'iatu being confined to feast upon vinegar and ash, </div> </div> </div>Recall what the Shan'iatu were trying to become and how the agenda of the Judges is described in this edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not sure how I feel about the &quot;Ocean of Time&quot;. It is an evocative image, sure, but it feels a bit foreign to me. My brain for some reason keeps equating &quot;Sea = Ammut&quot; (probably something from Dreams of Avarice), and it just makes me feel weird. When I think about non-linear time, my mind turns more towards sands and winds, less towards seas and currents. Blame my syntheses for this :P </div> </div> </div>Ammut claims to hold the formless not-waters of Nu in her jaws and her mythological image includes two semiaquatic species, but she's mostly identified by the anatomical markers that get you called &quot;the Devourer.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T15:28:48-08:00","id":1352459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352449#post1352449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would it hurt having Reminisce Experiences just be refunded as regular Experiences? It really fucking sucks when you've spent time amassing enough XP to advance your character only for it to go up in smoke. I know that losing a dot doesn't negate the playing experience you had while collecting the Beats, but it can still make you feel like you've lost progress. Especially in a game like Mummy where you're actively encouraged to increase your Memory instead of Vampire or CofD where you're more focused on not losing Humanity/Integrity.<br /> \u200b<br /> My group has long house ruled that you regain all XP for any traits you lose, not just Merits, which made losing those traits actually fun instead of something that's outright undesirable both in- and out-of-game. It doesn't affect me since we've already house ruled the game that way (and I still don't know if I'll get to even play Mummy), but I'm seriously recommending doing something similar as a standard rule. I think Mummy is the best game for it, too, due to how much of a setback Memory loss is and that using different XP currencies makes it so you can refund the XP without some players immediately putting it right back into Memory again.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could absolutely do that for your games. It could prove a lot of bookkeeping if you try to track purchased Memory separately from that gained in other ways, but it could still be a nice thing to do for your players. It\u2019s a great house rule. I\u2019m not sure we\u2019ll make an official ruling on that for the core, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T15:45:15-08:00","id":1352460,"title":"","content":"The New Zealand entry needs a rewrite. The concept is fine, though it seems predicated on there being a lot more arisen than I\u2019d expect on a handful of isolated, barely populated islands, but it\u2019s main problem is that the writing is clunky and convoluted. <br /> <br /> Being one of the last places colonized by humans, early Polynesian settlers came by canoe in multiple waves between 1250 and 1300. These pioneers, under long isolation, developed the unique culture of the M\u0101ori people. <br /> <br /> Those sentences illustrate adequately, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2096-willywonka","name":"willywonka","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T15:46:36-08:00","id":1352461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352452#post1352452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also<br /> <br /> Narwhals (Amkhata)swimming in the ocean, causing a commotion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty big and pretty white they beat a polar bear in a fight~","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T15:57:23-08:00","id":1352462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352448#post1352448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, since gaining a dot of Memory is a potential benefit from the Trials of Duat, it can be boosted up by one to compensate for a lost dot from Anpu\u2019s cup.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh, interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T15:59:56-08:00","id":1352463,"title":"","content":"So... hmm... are mummies supposed to lose memory dots even when they only spend a scene reanimated, like when tomb robbers bust into their burial place?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T16:24:48-08:00","id":1352466,"title":"","content":"I think a cool Sorcerer merit would be something like Maker, which would provide some sort of bonus or enhancement to Vestige making. These aren't so much Relics, but they are a bit more advanced then normal vestiges.<br /> <br /> As an aside, the line in the newest update where it mentions Irem using the memory of starvation to produce relics that allow for food production is brilliant to me. It really says something about how magical workings work there. They used a negative to produce a positive.<br /> <br /> So, as a random question, I figure if a sorcerer has access to something like Eidetic Memory and or an equivalent supernatural merit or power that they might get a bonus to the Sealing a Vestige roll, even if the memory is old.<br /> <br /> Another question about creating a Vestige. What Dice Pool would you suggest be used to create them. The rules in the book say &quot;varies&quot; but it doesn't give any ideas. Now I am glad that it is not set in stone but some suggestions would be helpful I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 12-03-2019, 08:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T16:49:02-08:00","id":1352471,"title":"","content":"All jokes aside, I am very disappointed with the direction that Duat took, in that there was a detailed direction at all. One of the biggest pieces of mystique that Duat held is that it was impossible to remember what that dread realm was truly like other than the transparent afterimages afforded by Memory leaving an indistinct impression of the turmoil suffered without showing the image itself, leaving it entirely to the storyteller and the player\u2019s imagination. But now we have set tourist locations and attractions that give mechanical bonuses and penalties, even a cool potential prize in the form of a celestial sixth God-Pillar.. and no one ever understands why or how they get them because that chunk of their memory is always ripped away and is presumably lost permanently...<br /> <br /> Yeah I\u2019m upset by that, because it feels so much like a Dungeons and Dragons type of elemental plane where you have secret second adventures in rather than a terrifying nether realm that cannot be recalled for the sake of ones continued sanity.<br /> <br /> All in all, worst part of the chapter in my opinion, but every chapter has had its lows so I will admit while it\u2019s disappointing that the devs took this route, everything else that doesn\u2019t involve Duat as the central plot hook is really cool and interesting!<br /> <br /> Having said that, it does give me ideas regarding certain aspects like Affinities and Utterances using the new Pillar, so that is pretty fun! Some people likely love it, and that\u2019s no bad thing; if you like it you should use it for all it\u2019s worth. Me personally, I don\u2019t care for it save for a few pieces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 12-03-2019, 08:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T17:14:29-08:00","id":1352477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352471#post1352471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All jokes aside, I am very disappointed with the direction that Duat took, in that there was a detailed direction at all. One of the biggest pieces of mystique that Duat held is that it was impossible to remember what that dread realm was truly like other than the transparent afterimages afforded by Memory leaving an indistinct impression of the turmoil suffered without showing the image itself, leaving it entirely to the storyteller and the player\u2019s imagination. But now we have set tourist locations and attractions that give mechanical bonuses and penalties, even a cool potential prize in the form of a celestial sixth God-Pillar.. and no one ever understands why or how they get them because that chunk of their memory is always ripped away and is presumably lost permanently...<br /> <br /> Yeah I\u2019m upset by that, because it feels so much like a Dungeons and Dragons type of elemental plane where you have secret second adventures in rather than a terrifying nether realm that cannot be recalled for the sake of ones continued sanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting way of spelling &quot;Wraith: the Oblivion&quot; and &quot;Harrowing.&quot; Especially given how the advice is &quot;everybody gets to contribute what they want&quot;, so Duat is always going to be crazy-quilt, with only some guidelines on what is there. <br /> <br /> Presumably the fiends who follow you out remember perfectly well, and &quot;lost permanently&quot; is not exactly how I'd describe &quot;memories of Duat come back at high levels.&quot; Remember, Memory is the ability to recall, not the existence of actual memories.<br /> <br /> And &quot;prize&quot; is not how I'd describe that Pillar. More like &quot;most prized slave.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T17:14:29-08:00","id":1352478,"title":"","content":"[MORE DOUBLE POSTS HAVE JOURNEYED TO DUAT, WHERE THEY NOW GUIDE THE ENLIGHTENED ONE.]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T17:23:04-08:00","id":1352482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352471#post1352471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All jokes aside, I am very disappointed with the direction that Duat took, in that there was a detailed direction at all. One of the biggest pieces of mystique that Duat held is that it was impossible to remember what that dread realm was truly like other than the transparent afterimages afforded by Memory leaving an indistinct impression of the turmoil suffered without showing the image itself, leaving it entirely to the storyteller and the player\u2019s imagination.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a dread realm you reach by dying and searching out hidden geography in the dead skin of the living world, most prominently characterized by challenges drawn from your own mind to make you go through the thing that the Rite of Return was always specified to have made you go through.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But now we have set tourist locations and attractions that give mechanical bonuses and penalties, even a cool potential prize in the form of a celestial sixth God-Pillar.. and no one ever understands why or how they get them because that chunk of their memory is always ripped away and is presumably lost permanently... </div> </div> </div>One of those steps is literally based on the lifetime you led before the trip and five of the other six are based on tests of your fundamental character in ways that are personalized to each subject. In its most simplified form, the Trials of Duat are &quot;Know the Pillars of your soul and be rewarded for their strength&quot; and &quot;Explain yourself to your Judge and be ready for the consequences of a bad defense.&quot; If nobody understood how or why they were rewarded or punished by the Judges in even the most nebulous of terms, there'd be no Iremite culture in the Arisen's makeup at all besides what their cults managed to dig up. Scraps of the experience stick like sense memories because that's the way this setting works.<br /> <br /> There has literally always been a mythology about this place and the Trials of Duat do not do any more than affirm the basics of that mythology's consistent elements for the sake of a between-stories minigame that lends variety to the circumstances a character's next Descent might include. &quot;The Trials of Heart test the Pillar of your Heart, and may result in a reward for demonstrating mastery of your passion&quot; is not a tourist attraction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T17:32:01-08:00","id":1352483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352477#post1352477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's an interesting way of spelling &amp;quot;Wraith: the Oblivion&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;Harrowing.&amp;quot; Especially given how the advice is &amp;quot;everybody gets to contribute what they want&amp;quot;, so Duat is always going to be crazy-quilt, with only some guidelines on what is there. <br /> <br /> Presumably the fiends who follow you out remember perfectly well, and &amp;quot;lost permanently&amp;quot; is not exactly how I'd describe &amp;quot;memories of Duat come back at high levels.&amp;quot; Remember, Memory is the ability to recall, not the existence of actual memories.<br /> <br /> And &amp;quot;prize&amp;quot; is not how I'd describe that Pillar. More like &amp;quot;most prized slave.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve learned from letting players play the geister of their fellow players that this sort of thing is really cool on paper, but just causes unneeded drama and friction when implemented. I personally would/will run the trials for the players in order to keep a train wreck from occurring because Joey had just suffered a bad break up ten minutes before the session starts, so he spitefully makes Charlie\u2019s Trial virtually impossible to complete to cope. Not every group will be like that, of course, but I\u2019ve DM\u2019d and played enough games to know that this sort of thing can get messy hilariously fast.<br /> <br /> And a prized slave can be treated quite lavishly indeed, that\u2019s what rewards are for after all, to make the slave want to perform.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T17:38:15-08:00","id":1352484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352483#post1352483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019ve learned from letting players play the geister of their fellow players that this sort of thing is really cool on paper, but just causes unneeded drama and friction when implemented. I personally would/will run the trials for the players in order to keep a train wreck from occurring because Joey had just suffered a bad break up ten minutes before the session starts, so he spitefully makes Charlie\u2019s Trial virtually impossible to complete to cope. Not every group will be like that, of course, but I\u2019ve DM\u2019d and played enough games to know that this sort of thing can get messy hilariously fast.<br /> <br /> And a prized slave can be treated quite lavishly indeed, that\u2019s what rewards are for after all, to make the slave want to perform.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, when it comes to the idea of players designing the trials for other players, what you describe is exactly what I was thinking when I read the section. So on this I totally support what you are saying and would never really give players the authority to control the trials for other players. <br /> <br /> While I do like Duat I do also have to say the idea of playing out the Trials every time a Descent happens is not what I would consider fun. That said, the idea of maybe having there be some sort of adventure inside Duat is cool to me. Like maybe mummies get access to an apartment in the city where certain things can be kept and secured between descents. Or something. <br /> <br /> (On the idea that the Judges would look through the apartments I could say that maybe the apartment itself is secured by the same potent protections of the Rite of Rebirth that make it impossible for the Judges to wave their hand and destroy the Arisen.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T17:39:59-08:00","id":1352487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352482#post1352482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a dread realm you reach by dying and searching out hidden geography in the dead skin of the living world, most prominently characterized by challenges drawn from your own mind to make you go through the thing that the Rite of Return was always specified to have made you go through.<br /> <br /> One of those steps is literally based on the lifetime you led before the trip and five of the other six are based on tests of your fundamental character in ways that are personalized to each subject. In its most simplified form, the Trials of Duat are &quot;Know the Pillars of your soul and be rewarded for their strength&quot; and &quot;Explain yourself to your Judge and be ready for the consequences of a bad defense.&quot; If nobody understood how or why they were rewarded or punished by the Judges in even the most nebulous of terms, there'd be no Iremite culture in the Arisen's makeup at all besides what their cults managed to dig up. Scraps of the experience stick like sense memories because that's the way this setting works.<br /> <br /> There has literally always been a mythology about this place and the Trials of Duat do not do any more than affirm the basics of that mythology's consistent elements for the sake of a between-stories minigame that lends variety to the circumstances a character's next Descent might include. &quot;The Trials of Heart test the Pillar of your Heart, and may result in a reward for demonstrating mastery of your passion&quot; is not a tourist attraction.</div> </div> </div> </div>And all of this could be imbued with a vision or spiritual visitation by the Judge during a Descent should one uphold/fail to uphold the values of their Decree or their Judge in the face of their current mission in the sunlit world , so no good sir, I do not find the process of playing around in Duat while the other players mess with each other\u2019s standing while in afterlife to be an acceptable justification for this section. It is a tourist attraction disguised as a moral, spiritual, and narrative threshold. <br /> <br /> If the Judges were a distant figure like they are presented in first edition, then this whole trial in Duat thing would be much more thematically fitting and interesting.<br /> <br /> But seeing as your Judge can literally come to your house and kick your door in now, the idea of having a whole section of the game where you prostrate yourself before your Judge in Duat is redundant and frankly comical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 12-03-2019, 08:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T17:56:40-08:00","id":1352491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352487#post1352487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And all of this could be imbued with a vision or spiritual visitation by the Judge during a Descent should one uphold/fail to uphold the values of their Decree or their Judge in the face of their current mission in the sunlit world ,</div> </div> </div> </div>We had that in First Edition in the form of Descent rolls. Making the Judges double as qashmallim in this way would be painfully dull.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> so no good sir, I do not find the process of playing around in Duat while the other players mess with each other\u2019s standing while in afterlife to be an acceptable justification for this section. It is a tourist attraction disguised as a moral, spiritual, and narrative threshold. </div> </div> </div>The most &quot;touristy&quot; part of Duat is literally the first layer where all the demons tend to escape from, where the Trial is &quot;get to the next gate, possibly overcoming literal demons along the way&quot; as a prelude to a negotiatory set of scenes where your character is supposed to struggle with their more metaphorical demons as part of the recurring stress-test of their immortal soul.<br /> <br /> The typical context in which this minigame is going to be happening is at the end of a story. You had to die and not have other pressing business in the sunlit lands to get here. Nothing about this is tourism when people can literally summon fiends from Duat without even needing to be a sorcerer \u2014 this edition deals with Duat as a marginally more accessible place even without the Trials or the loss of the Storyteller's Wall. They're a tourist attraction in the sense that your Keeper's garden being a place you can technically go to is a tourist attraction in Changeling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">But seeing as your Judge can literally come to your house and kick your door in now, the idea of having a whole section of the game where you prostrate yourself before your Judge in Duat is redundant and frankly comical.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Your Judge needs to possess a mortal and warp reality around themselves in blood-marked response to a violation of the Law to grant you direct audience with one of its avatars and that <i>still</i> isn't going to obliterate you the way a trial on the edge of reality can. There's stakes and prerequisites involved that you don't get from the Trials' direct incentives to consign relics to Duat regardless of what they do or are.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 12-03-2019, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T20:05:13-08:00","id":1352507,"title":"","content":"It hasn't gone so far as to openly say, but I can honestly say I can't imagine a game I wouldn't implement it in, so I actually have meaningful headcanon now.<br /> <br /> The Underworld is totally Ammut's gullet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T20:54:01-08:00","id":1352509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352507#post1352507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It hasn't gone so far as to openly say, but I can honestly say I can't imagine a game I wouldn't implement it in, so I actually have meaningful headcanon now.<br /> <br /> The Underworld is totally Ammut's gullet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bet it gets really, really freaking annoying to her when the Arisen go in and try to cross a river:<br /> <br /> &quot;Ah, hell, Ashfoot's playing traffic cop again. Welp, time for another month of allergies...&quot;<br /> <br /> As for Duat, my full-throated defense of it indicates how much I love it as a stage for climatic psychodrama. I'm thinking of ways for other gamelines to visit it for Contagion Chronicles and other crossovers, and how one proves that one is worth being guided back out by Anpu - or failing that, how to not be completely <i>or </i>eternally yoked to a Judge, lest you start trying to negotiate with someone who traditionally <i>starts off </i>with an offer of euthanasia before she starts dealing honestly with you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T21:07:56-08:00","id":1352511,"title":"","content":"Maybe I am missing something but I see no benefit to making Duat anything other then its own realm. To me making it the interior body of a god or primordial would reduce the very interesting and potential adventurous nature of it. Duat is something that is as real as any other place under or above or sideways to the world for all that its existence is as special as it is due to the nature of the Rite of Return and its time twisting and reality effecting nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T21:18:04-08:00","id":1352512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352511#post1352511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I am missing something but I see no benefit to making Duat anything other then its own realm.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/down-in-the-dark-geist-the-sin-eaters/\" target=\"_blank\">Nobody in the above posts is talking about Duat</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 12-04-2019, 12:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T21:23:50-08:00","id":1352515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352512#post1352512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/down-in-the-dark-geist-the-sin-eaters/\" target=\"_blank\">Nobody in the above posts is talking about Duat</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, okay, fine then. I saw underworld and figured they meant Duat since that is what is mummy related.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T21:38:25-08:00","id":1352516,"title":"","content":"Tangentially, on the matter of crossover cosmology and Weird Time Shit\u2026<br /> <br /> Well, I think we now have a solid guess at where all that water came from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 12-04-2019, 01:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T00:14:29-08:00","id":1352544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352484#post1352484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I do like Duat I do also have to say the idea of playing out the Trials every time a Descent happens is not what I would consider fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same. That's a minimum of seven scenes (my sessions are like 5 scenes) focused on one character. There are a lot of cool concepts that look like they're going to utterly derail things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T00:52:34-08:00","id":1352551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352491#post1352491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We had that in First Edition in the form of Descent rolls. Making the Judges double as qashmallim in this way would be painfully dull.<br /> <br /> The most &quot;touristy&quot; part of Duat is literally the first layer where all the demons tend to escape from, where the Trial is &quot;get to the next gate, possibly overcoming literal demons along the way&quot; as a prelude to a negotiatory set of scenes where your character is supposed to struggle with their more metaphorical demons as part of the recurring stress-test of their immortal soul.<br /> <br /> The typical context in which this minigame is going to be happening is at the end of a story. You had to die and not have other pressing business in the sunlit lands to get here. Nothing about this is tourism when people can literally summon fiends from Duat without even needing to be a sorcerer \u2014 this edition deals with Duat as a marginally more accessible place even without the Trials or the loss of the Storyteller's Wall. They're a tourist attraction in the sense that your Keeper's garden being a place you can technically go to is a tourist attraction in Changeling.<br /> <br /> Your Judge needs to possess a mortal and warp reality around themselves in blood-marked response to a violation of the Law to grant you direct audience with one of its avatars and that <i>still</i> isn't going to obliterate you the way a trial on the edge of reality can. There's stakes and prerequisites involved that you don't get from the Trials' direct incentives to consign relics to Duat regardless of what they do or are.[/FONT]</div> </div> </div> </div>The Descent rolls can convey that, yes. My interpretation of a Descent roll that it was the metaphysical equivalent of your parent yelling at you for leaving a mess in the kitchen after you ate without cleaning it up, unpleasant and can incentivize you to maybe clean it up, but it\u2019s not what I would describe as a punishment rather than a warning/ potential game of chance.<br /> <br /> Funnily enough, the demon infested soul ghetto that is the first layer was actually interesting to me because it felt more of a ... I suppose fair way to challenge a Mummy rather than letting player two write out and dictate how a several hour character focused minigame plays out to me. It can be okay as an endgame event, but I don\u2019t think everyone wants to go through it in rapid succession, or multiple times in a single story if multiple mummies Descend at different times<br /> <br /> And you are right about that, but the way the preview worded it has it sound like manifestation seems easy enough that several judges can find the time to fuck with and fight over a single mummy for petty shits and giggles","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 12-04-2019, 04:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T02:47:36-08:00","id":1352564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352443#post1352443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>, you mentioned to help me to understand what is the meaning of temporal death versus permanent death to mummies, and what could exactly completely destroy one for all eternity (unless the only way is &amp;quot;failing so much that even your Judge will just throw you to Ammut's maw&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, and I redeem that offer. Did I got it more or less right, or is there something that I have missed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Will do this weekend. Operating on just phone at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T02:57:41-08:00","id":1352565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352516#post1352516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tangentially, on the matter of crossover cosmology and Weird Time Shit\u2026<br /> <br /> Well, I think we now have a solid guess at where all that water came from.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am tired and may have missed it. Please clarify, as it sounds interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T05:23:04-08:00","id":1352581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352483#post1352483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019ve learned from letting players play the geister of their fellow players</div> </div> </div> </div>And therein lies the problem. A geist is not a Shadow. A geist is fundamentally loyal to their partner unless something has gone drastically wrong. A geist does not need another player, just &quot;my geist feels that&quot;, and that's it.<br /> <br /> When you are designing a Trial of Duat, you are designing something that's fundamentally meant to <i>hurt</i> the person it is focused on; I would argue it's entirely thematic for a Trial to be made fundamentally impossible because a Judge was an ass that day. But really, if a player is designing a Trial that seems geared towards bullying the <i>other player, </i>that's when the ST needs to intervene; the issue is not the concept of the Trial, the issue is that it's being used as a tool of That Guy; That Guy will use any tool to make everyone else as miserable as he is.<br /> <br /> Really, in my experience, it's the exact opposite problem, and design things too easy; that's part of why there's a sidebar about entering Duat as a team.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T05:38:10-08:00","id":1352585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352516#post1352516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tangentially, on the matter of crossover cosmology and Weird Time Shit\u2026<br /> <br /> Well, I think we now have a solid guess at where all that water came from.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do love me a Green Grass, Running Waters reference that is also an accurate answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T07:39:24-08:00","id":1352600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352565#post1352565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am tired and may have missed it. Please clarify, as it sounds interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mummy's metaphor of choice for the flow of time is an ocean, and it characterizes deathly Twilight as very loosely desert-themed.<br /> <br /> Geist's presentation of the Underworld says that ghosts are not so much pulled there as blown in by a difference in pressure, which happens to be accompanied by a burst of &quot;water&quot; no matter how dry the living world is on the other side of the Gate.<br /> <br /> Demon specifies that entering the Underworld from a splinter timeline and leaving through a different Gate (or the same Gate after it's closed and reopened) returns you to the main flow of history even though ghosts ostensibly still enter the Underworld from splinters in the normal fashion.<br /> <br /> And Mummy's alternate currents may not necessarily have anything to do with death, but they <i>are</i> attached to Anchors\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T07:51:38-08:00","id":1352603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352581#post1352581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And therein lies the problem. A geist is not a Shadow. A geist is fundamentally loyal to their partner unless something has gone drastically wrong. A geist does not need another player, just &quot;my geist feels that&quot;, and that's it.<br /> <br /> When you are designing a Trial of Duat, you are designing something that's fundamentally meant to <i>hurt</i> the person it is focused on; I would argue it's entirely thematic for a Trial to be made fundamentally impossible because a Judge was an ass that day. But really, if a player is designing a Trial that seems geared towards bullying the <i>other player, </i>that's when the ST needs to intervene; the issue is not the concept of the Trial, the issue is that it's being used as a tool of That Guy; That Guy will use any tool to make everyone else as miserable as he is.<br /> <br /> Really, in my experience, it's the exact opposite problem, and design things too easy; that's part of why there's a sidebar about entering Duat as a team.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Geist is not fundamentally loyal, it can be downright exploitative and treasonous if it doesn\u2019t get its way, and can be incredibly unreliable or abusive if it thinks doing such things will get the human to do the things it needs to get done.<br /> <br /> And that\u2019s the fine line, a line I do not trust to other players if I can help it. If you like it that\u2019s great, let them do it.. but I will do things the old fashioned, safe way of paying attention to what the players characters are like before designing the trial <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I mean if the book needs to explain the importance of a Trigger Card.. well that\u2019s all you really need to know about how risky this can get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T13:02:30-08:00","id":1352667,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1686_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1686\" data-vbnamecard=\"1686\">Korogra</a> I make sure to explain the importance of a Trigger Card when I run D&amp;D for people. Because someday, someone might need it. I would hardly consider a basic eurofantsy setting to be that dangerous, but you never know.<br /> <br /> You are obviously more in touch with how your group will use the Trials and i'm not going to tell you how to play your game. I just ask that you consider them in the spirit they were written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T14:25:18-08:00","id":1352675,"title":"","content":"&quot;Some Affinities have effects requiring the expenditure of Willpower points to activate; these magics require a little more focus and intent on the part of the Arisen. <b>A mummy can spend any number of Willpower points on activating Affinities each turn without counting towards the usual one Willpower point per turn limitation.</b>&quot;<br /> <br /> Seriously? Of the five games that uses the new WP text, Mummy is the first one that didn't incorrectly say it was per turn instead of per action in its Kickstarter manuscript, but still manages to include references to that incorrect rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T14:31:16-08:00","id":1352676,"title":"","content":"I think this may be the first Kickstarter I've been involved in where it looks like we're not going to get through most of the planned Stretch Goals: we'll probably get the second part of the supplement, but at this point the Ka, Ren, and Sheut parts haven't even been posted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T14:59:08-08:00","id":1352679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352676#post1352676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this may be the first Kickstarter I've been involved in where it looks like we're not going to get through most of the planned Stretch Goals: we'll probably get the second part of the supplement, but at this point the Ka, Ren, and Sheut parts haven't even been posted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it really saddens me to see that. I assume that one of those chapter would have been an expansion for Immortals, such as the Purified and Visitors, and who knows what plans they had for the other two chapters. Oh well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T15:04:14-08:00","id":1352680,"title":"","content":"Let me caution that the Kickstarter isn't over quite yet; it's still possible (though admittedly unlikely) that a combination of a last-day surge and a tight spacing of the remaining planned Stretch Goals might still get them all out there and possibly even met. But while I'd be happy that they got satisfied, it would also feel a bit like cheating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T15:39:55-08:00","id":1352688,"title":"","content":"In some ways I can understand why this didn't get hit out of the ballpark. I mean Mummy the Curse is a niche game and not to everyone's interest. I do think that in time people who might not have liked some of the elements of 1e might look at 2e and find they like this new version. This very much includes the traditional book structure as compared to the the way they wrote 1e. <br /> <br /> I admit that besides the Sekhem going 10 to 1 this game has many things I do like in it, so while I was disappointed and yet still supported 1e, I find myself looking at 2e with much enjoyment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T16:42:50-08:00","id":1352696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352667#post1352667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1686_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1686\" data-vbnamecard=\"1686\">Korogra</a> I make sure to explain the importance of a Trigger Card when I run D&amp;D for people. Because someday, someone might need it. I would hardly consider a basic eurofantsy setting to be that dangerous, but you never know.<br /> <br /> You are obviously more in touch with how your group will use the Trials and i'm not going to tell you how to play your game. I just ask that you consider them in the spirit they were written.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me spare you some pain and point out that Korogra despises the idea of the trigger card outright, belittles those who defend it, and believes that any attitude less than assumed antagonism between game master and players is begging for trouble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T16:54:52-08:00","id":1352701,"title":"","content":"The previews are filled with cool concepts and all, but I'm not sold on actually playing it. It seems to me that in order to experience the cool stuff (multiple Descents, nonlinear time, the Trials of Duat, reaching high Memory, actually having your cults do meaningful stuff and not just be your alarm clock) you're going to have to play a relatively long campaign, but in doing so you also invite the headache of trying to coordinate all of that.<br /> If someone could convince me otherwise before the KS ends, that'd be great because right now I'm probably going to suggest to my group that we don't back it. I think that'd be the very first time we don't back a CofD KS aside from Contagion Chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T17:25:43-08:00","id":1352707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352701#post1352701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The previews are filled with cool concepts and all, but I'm not sold on actually playing it. It seems to me that in order to experience the cool stuff (multiple Descents, nonlinear time, the Trials of Duat, reaching high Memory, actually having your cults do meaningful stuff and not just be your alarm clock) you're going to have to play a relatively long campaign, but in doing so you also invite the headache of trying to coordinate all of that.<br /> If someone could convince me otherwise before the KS ends, that'd be great because right now I'm probably going to suggest to my group that we don't back it. I think that'd be the very first time we don't back a CofD KS aside from Contagion Chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Nonlinear time can also be covered by flashback vignette scenes, or incorporating other Arisen operating on a different timeflow (who may remember you even if you\u2019ve never met. <br /> <br /> 2. Your game can start in one Descent and bridge to another, with some focus on the Trials and adjusting to a the next Descent. Just focus on one transition rather than a long campaign. <br /> <br /> 3. The cult can do other things by being present as player characters, antagonists, dependents, or faithful plot devices of the death god. While you\u2019re asleep, they\u2019re you in the living world for all intents and purposes. You could even do a game without an Arisen except as a slumbering plot device for the cult member PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2096-willywonka","name":"willywonka","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T18:21:16-08:00","id":1352715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352701#post1352701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The previews are filled with cool concepts and all, but I'm not sold on actually playing it. It seems to me that in order to experience the cool stuff (multiple Descents, nonlinear time, the Trials of Duat, reaching high Memory, actually having your cults do meaningful stuff and not just be your alarm clock) you're going to have to play a relatively long campaign, but in doing so you also invite the headache of trying to coordinate all of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>How long of a campaign are you hoping to play? There are certainly ways to incorporate many aspects into shorter games.<br /> For example: Start your game off with a Descent already in progress, with whatever purpose for them to have been awakened you like (or even have it already accomplished). With a lower starting Sekhem, it\u2019s easier to draw (or violently force) the characters into Duat after giving them a chance to get a feel for the characters. Give them a chance for a great victory or defeat, then give them their Trials after the current Descent. Let them awaken in the past for the next one, now possessing all their mighty powers and ready to cause trouble for whatever poor bastards run afoul of them. If it\u2019s a defeat they experienced, you can even connect it to the \u2018future\u2019 by giving them the opportunity to shift the odds in their favor. Hell, you could even run an intense game for the characters, only to reveal that they\u2019ve been enduring their Trials the whole time. Those are just a couple thoughts off the top of my head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T18:34:16-08:00","id":1352719,"title":"","content":"Plus one could always have a session or two at starting experience levels before having a small break where you give the players some agreed upon amount of experience to represent various descents and growth periods off screen before coming back to the game at a bit higher level. <br /> <br /> Additionally, nothing says that one has to have Descent Rolls or Pillar Trials every single time. Sometimes you can simply say &quot;your Sekhem has gone to zero and you are now in the sleep of death&quot; or even more simply &quot;Your mummies have died.&quot; After that you can say, &quot;You open your eyes from a natural sleep in the next descent three days after awakening, your Sekhem is 8 and your peace is disturbed by the knocking at the doors.&quot; <br /> <br /> But yeah, certain elements can be covered at certain times but then ignored for a while if it is not fun again. This most especially includes things in Duat and also various alternate Descent points. I mean we got the interesting ideas of a dark future and also a long ago pre or early-Irem pasts, and both could totally lead to interesting campaign potentials. <br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> I have to say the idea of having the first Descent be in say 2012 or 2020 interests me quite a lot, especially if this modern life is considered a core past. Then having the next descent being in the far future could lead to the beginning of seeing a dark plot that needs to be solved. Then other descents could happen all around time effecting things. But also imagine having a Descent in January 2012, dying say by March, and then after a few descents awakening in May 2012. Its like &quot;woah, why is it only two months after the last time I was awake at this point.&quot; <br /> <br /> Which, to me, means campaign twists and turns and interesting plot seeds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T21:58:58-08:00","id":1352733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352667#post1352667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> I make sure to explain the importance of a Trigger Card when I run D&amp;D for people. Because someday, someone might need it. I would hardly consider a basic eurofantsy setting to be that dangerous, but you never know.<br /> <br /> You are obviously more in touch with how your group will use the Trials and i'm not going to tell you how to play your game. I just ask that you consider them in the spirit they were written.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I know, but these days people tend to get upset over things that seem trivial or get offended by what a player might say or do in character even if it is obviously not something the player actually would ever do <br /> <br /> And I will, no need to worry about that. I\u2019ve played with this group for nearly a decade, I\u2019ve gotten pretty good at judging what is and isn\u2019t safe to include in a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T23:41:25-08:00","id":1352759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352676#post1352676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this may be the first Kickstarter I've been involved in where it looks like we're not going to get through most of the planned Stretch Goals: we'll probably get the second part of the supplement, but at this point the Ka, Ren, and Sheut parts haven't even been posted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Minor update: The Ba threshold was passed at the 12-hours-remaining mark and Ka (add a section covering ghosts and spirits) is now on the list at 68K.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T23:51:42-08:00","id":1352761,"title":"","content":"Looks like they're sticking to 3K per stretch goal. Here's hoping we get enough of a last-minute burst to get there. <br /> <br /> On the upside, we already have access to material about ghosts and spirits in the Chronicles of Darkness Rulebook; so it won't be a huge loss if we don't get there. On the downside, we may never know what they had planned for Ren and Sheut.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T00:12:11-08:00","id":1352765,"title":"","content":"I actually do wish the Trials had a mechanical resolution (something like, &quot;roll relevant pillar, +1 if its in line with your balance, -1 if in line with your burden&quot;) come to think of it, due to that it may very well eat up a whole session, doesn't seem to give beats (can't tell) and the PC is unlikely to even be able to remember it and doesn't happen in objective time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T00:48:11-08:00","id":1352768,"title":"","content":"Perhaps as an optional rule for those gaming groups that don't have the time or inclination to roleplay it. For what it's worth, this strikes me as being analogous to the Quick and Dirty Combat rules, at least in intent: you have this challenge that you need to resolve; but playing it out will bog down the flow of the game more than you're willing to accept, the players aren't interested in playing through it, or they're just bored of it. So here's a quick way to resolve the challenge and get on with the things you want to get on with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T01:03:29-08:00","id":1352771,"title":"","content":"The issue with 'quick and dirty' Duat rules, is Duat is already the most optional part of the game, seeing as the general assumption is that the Arisen have no memory of it, ever, barring those exceptionial Deathless who are already in an endgame (Ankh or Apotheosis). Non-liner time is more baked in than playing in Duat.<br /> Furthermore, Dust is handled narratively, because it is not a matter of chance; it is the Descended's choices that are being Judged, not their luck. It might be better to just assume the character gets no punishment or blessing conditions for Duat, if people don't want to play through the Trials and the Judgement. Which could be done as one scene per trial, so it is possible for a solo session.<br /> <br /> Huh...going through Duat as the Arisen's player's Prelude would be interesting, especially if we don't discuss the preceding Descent beforehand. Not every time though. Maybe just once per campaign/chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T05:51:41-08:00","id":1352795,"title":"","content":"I have to say, the whole 'fluid time' concept is still something I'm massively disappointed with, to the point where I straight up do not think I'm interested in ever playing a Mummy game where that is the going assumption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T06:30:30-08:00","id":1352801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrBreaksIt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352795#post1352795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to say, the whole 'fluid time' concept is still something I'm massively disappointed with, to the point where I straight up do not think I'm interested in ever playing a Mummy game where that is the going assumption.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure nothing really breaks if you require all your descents to be in order. After all, that is a perfectly possible way for time to progress for your Mummy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T07:08:39-08:00","id":1352805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352801#post1352801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure nothing really breaks if you require all your descents to be in order. After all, that is a perfectly possible way for time to progress for your Mummy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. The Timeless aspect can be dialed up or down as much as someone likes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T07:47:50-08:00","id":1352809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352765#post1352765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually do wish the Trials had a mechanical resolution (something like, &amp;quot;roll relevant pillar, +1 if its in line with your balance, -1 if in line with your burden&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> come to think of it, due to that it may very well eat up a whole session, doesn't seem to give beats (can't tell) and the PC is unlikely to even be able to remember it and doesn't happen in objective time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing stops you from fading to black for the Trials. Interestingly enough, though, the mechanics you suggest are almost exactly how I would handle the Trials if I didn\u2019t want to run them but still wanted the resulting benefits and penalties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T10:47:48-08:00","id":1352831,"title":"","content":"(Pro tip: You know how these boards replace quotation marks with \u201c&amp;quot;\u201d when you quote someone? If you edit your post and save it without making any changes, it replaces the \u201c&amp;quot;\u201ds with quotation marks. This also has the effect of getting rid of the emoji that crops up from quoting something with \u201c&quot;)\u201d and fixing links that get broken in a quote. It would be nice if the board did it without intervention; but since it doesn't\u2026)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T11:09:40-08:00","id":1352836,"title":"","content":"Hey, everyone! We're getting Mummy 2e!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T11:41:10-08:00","id":1352841,"title":"","content":"Honestly, between both Aberrant and Mummy the Curse I really don't think I could do any more kickstarters this year. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> Humor aside I was rereading those story seeds at the end of the book and I honestly love them and what they represent. They are such a great series of potential adventure plots for a set of mummy characters. I could see a campaign with some of those descents within them creating an arc. So yeah, its quite fun. <br /> <br /> Especially as the group could also be full of Reborn, which gives them certain special traits that make things at the same time both mortal and not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T12:07:36-08:00","id":1352846,"title":"","content":"So I was thinking of allowing the Arisen to have something like a Sanctum Merit which would work like a residence merit but would give them a place in either Twilight or Duat. Yes, I know, this wouldn't work for every campaign, but I like the idea of the Arisen having a sort of forever residence somewhere in the City of Duat. Dots in the merit would probably give certain bonuses to Memory or Sekhem or ritual casting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T13:19:34-08:00","id":1352863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352846#post1352846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I was thinking of allowing the Arisen to have something like a Sanctum Merit which would work like a residence merit but would give them a place in either Twilight or Duat. Yes, I know, this wouldn't work for every campaign, but I like the idea of the Arisen having a sort of forever residence somewhere in the City of Duat. Dots in the merit would probably give certain bonuses to Memory or Sekhem or ritual casting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having something like that in Neter-Khertet sounds cool and plays a little with how it's more of a place for mummies rather than a state of being. Only problem being that the mummy either needs to die or stash their body someplace safe (like their Tomb), or gain a power that lets them bodily enter Neter-Khertet.<br /> <br /> For Duat, well, you'll have to rewrite the setting if it's going to have any effect in the game. Entering Duat means you've ended your Descent, and nothing you do affects the living world except through what you bring with you on your next Descent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T13:41:16-08:00","id":1352866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352863#post1352863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Having something like that in Neter-Khertet sounds cool and plays a little with how it's more of a place for mummies rather than a state of being. Only problem being that the mummy either needs to die or stash their body someplace safe (like their Tomb), or gain a power that lets them bodily enter Neter-Khertet.<br /> <br /> For Duat, well, you'll have to rewrite the setting if it's going to have any effect in the game. Entering Duat means you've ended your Descent, and nothing you do affects the living world except through what you bring with you on your next Descent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can I haz a base in both? hehe <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Your right on the interesting benefits of having a place in Neter-Khertet, which is Twilight right. I think having the ability to have a base of operations that is outside the wear and tear and worry about the mortal world could be useful. I could see an Affinity or an Utterance (if you want it to be difficult) for a mummy or even a sort of mortal Rite for an immortal or sorcerer that could be used. <br /> <br /> I do think something like this only really works for campaigns where the ST sort of protects the tombs and spiritual sites owned by the characters. Otherwise it might not be entirely useful or even necessary. <br /> <br /> On Duat, well there is a city and it does mention resting and stuff there till it becomes time for the next Descent. The place is entirely spiritual so I would figure that anything there would be manifested thought, emotion, or magic. If you want to decorate an apartment with say a picture that picture could represent a Memory. Accessing the apartment to me would mean something like coming out victorius in the Trials and not drinking from the cup of memory. Which is also why I was thinking that the benefits of having such a spiritual place would be represented in a bonus to Memory or Sekhem rolls, or maybe even having access to certain rites that could be found and used. Nothing physical, you wont be able to get a Relic from your Duat apartment, but rather it would be able to reinforce memory and such. <br /> <br /> I do know this isn't for everyone, but the moment I read you finish the trials and find yourself in a city I was like &quot;can I have an apartment plx&quot; which is why I brought it up here. hehe","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T15:47:17-08:00","id":1352884,"title":"","content":"So I was looking through the rules with my boyfriend and we came to realize that the game doesn't actually say how many touchstones a Mummy gets in second ed. We're presuming one, but there are a few spots it refers to a &quot;a Mummy's touchstones&quot;. There definitely isn't a merit to take extras that we can see. Just something we're wondering if anyone has clarity on and maybe something to clarify in the final draft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2989-violetdea","name":"violetdea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T15:58:30-08:00","id":1352886,"title":"","content":"During character creation it says Touchstone in singular, but it really should specify how many.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T16:23:39-08:00","id":1352890,"title":"","content":"Well we don't have the errata submission form yet, but unless there has been a change we will get a chance to point out any errors/mistakes like the Touchstone thing.<br /> <br /> A bit sad (and oddly, angry) we didn't get to 'Lasting Death: Ka'. It wasn't even the next goal. And Anpu knows we won't get the Purified until we get the Shadow/spirits in a Mummy book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T16:36:36-08:00","id":1352892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would not be surprised if things that the KS didn't give will end up showing up elsewhere at another time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just like how we got the Book of Going Westward, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T17:36:37-08:00","id":1352906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>violetdea</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352884#post1352884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I was looking through the rules with my boyfriend and we came to realize that the game doesn't actually say how many touchstones a Mummy gets in second ed. We're presuming one, but there are a few spots it refers to a &amp;quot;a Mummy's touchstones&amp;quot;. There definitely isn't a merit to take extras that we can see. Just something we're wondering if anyone has clarity on and maybe something to clarify in the final draft.</div> </div> </div> </div>damn it. I was just fine not getting that until you mentioned the Purified. just damn it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T17:37:41-08:00","id":1352907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes because the model of game lines in 2012 that were not Mage,Vampire, Werewolf are the same now and like how Dawkins said that Kickstarter is the only factour on what books get made, right. Totally just like how we got Book of Going Westward. How silly of me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Point is that the skepticism is not without merit. We have heard this song before, and disappointed by the dance that followed. Curse fans have been hurt before by such notions, let's be fair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T18:02:58-08:00","id":1352914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352907#post1352907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Point is that the skepticism is not without merit. We have heard this song before, and disappointed by the dance that followed. Curse fans have been hurt before by such notions, let's be fair.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I know folks held out hope for 7 years that we might get this content even though it didn't fund, but this time will be different because ???&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T18:16:27-08:00","id":1352922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1352914#post1352914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;I know folks held out hope for 7 years that we might get this content even though it didn't fund, but this time will be different because ???&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Now let's be counter-fair here: it <i>might</i> be different. A lot of the writers on the core <i>were</i> those fans who got scorned, and I think Matthew knows that the Book of Going Westward is a long held sore point for a fanbase that could be it's main source of revenue, and as such any notions of hopes should be fought for.<br /> <br /> I haven't seen any promises, which is good on the subject-but it's not <i>completely unreasonable</i> to see how it might play differently.<br /> <br /> You want a personal take, I honestly have just gotten to the point where I try to stop stressing about what I don't have and won't have and just deal with what I can get, deciding whether the prices paid are worth the product gotten. It ends up on the plan, it never ends up on the plan, at the end of the day, I don't care about unless it's actually within grasp.<br /> <br /> But I do get where both sides of this argument are coming from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T20:29:56-08:00","id":1352945,"title":"","content":"If it happens, great. If it doesn't, it is a shame but at least the rest of the gameline is great.<br /> <br /> I don't hold out much hope for expanding the...later Chronicles of Darkness lines. But that doesn't mean I will write them off. Who knows, maybe the book will sell enough that Onyx Path might ask it's writers for book pitches. I'd say it is WAY too early for that right now, at the very least it won't happen until the book is released and the stretch goal content is done.<br /> <br /> All we can right now is wait.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T16:31:00-08:00","id":1353177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except we really didn't as there wasn't very much said at all about that book after the original kickstarter so there was no song or dance, same with the Scroll of Ages hub. For that reason it 100% does not justify the attitude being expressed. So yes, let's in fact be fair. If it happens, it happens. If it doesn't it doesn't. But considering that this isn't 2012, and the material actually being discussed is more basic and central than others. The idea that it wont be explored later, when the developer has talked about doing that very thing and has reminded people to not think that a KS is the only avenue for book generation. And if people can't say so without being nasty about it, then there's no point discussing it because that sort of talk only exists to shut down conversation. The Kickstart JUST ended and one of the first things is trying to shut someone up for hoping we get a book dealing with ghosts and other ephemeral entities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Empathy. Please practice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T16:57:44-08:00","id":1353181,"title":"","content":"While we never got the Book of Going Westward... I kind of suspect we're beginning to see some of the material that might have been included with such a book. In particular, details of Duat, the Trials, the Shades/Fiends.... And I think it's a good sign that we're seeing these things because future supplements tend to expand upon previously presented material.<br /> <br /> I'm hopeful for what other supplements might have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T17:04:40-08:00","id":1353184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1353181#post1353181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While we never got the Book of Going Westward... I kind of suspect we're beginning to see some of the material that might have been included with such a book. In particular, details of Duat, the Trials, the Shades/Fiends.... And I think it's a good sign that we're seeing these things because future supplements tend to expand upon previously presented material.<br /> <br /> I'm hopeful for what other supplements might have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Me, I'm thinking we'll get Purified and/or Visitors in Night Horrors: [Something Related To Egypt/Immortal Pains], because they're stated to dislike Mummies, and they're excellent Out Of Context problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T17:10:35-08:00","id":1353186,"title":"","content":"Frankly, all that the failure to get through all the stretch goals means is that the stuff that would have been included in the stretch goal companion book will instead be published in books that we'll be buying separately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T17:10:55-08:00","id":1353187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1353177#post1353177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Empathy. Please practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hard to manage when a comparison is being made between a hypothetical bit of content for an edition with one explicitly planned supplement so far and a hypothetical bit of content for an edition that specifically held off on using the revised core system mechanics that were published two weeks after its corebook released.<br /> <br /> Cursed Necropolis: Rio was the last major funded stretch goal for the Mummy 1e KS, and it came out two and a half years ago. Mummy 2e formally hit the development cycle fifteen months later. The seven years Remi's talking about having held out hope through include such minor shifts in the state of things as:<br /> <br /> \u2022 The license holder changing.<br /> \u2022 The formalizing of the Revised Storytelling System's application into named Second Editions.<br /> \u2022 A lot of complicating factors in the writing and development crews for Onyx Path, including specifically concerns about the delivery of Dark Eras material for Mummy that had a much faster turnaround and failed to meet expectations the first time through.<br /> <br /> An expression of very mild optimism was being made about the capability of the team to make books with content that clearly exists, and the basic description of what the Book of Going Westward would entail appears to have been at least partially incorporated into Second Edition's presentation of the Judges. &quot;It wouldn't surprise me if some of the stuff we didn't get to in the Kickstarter shows up an unspecified amount of time later&quot; does not warrant snide remarks, and those snide remarks <i>definitely </i>don't warrant strident defense just because they come from a place of frustration.<br /> <br /> People are mad about things that didn't end up happening from a hundred-thousand-dollar Kickstarter campaign. That campaign was seven years ago for a line that finished delivering the things it got funding for less than three years ago through a very complicated stretch of time. People are capable of moving on, and probably should.<br /> <br /> <br /> In less contentious news, I finally looped back around to finishing reading the sample settings. Antarctica's wild.<br /> <br /> Also, I find myself wondering whether the first preview's discussion of the Pillars in relation to the Rite of Return wouldn't be better served being placed nearer in the book to the Trials of Duat, given their direct or near-direct relation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T17:16:23-08:00","id":1353188,"title":"","content":"For clarity, the Book of Going Westward did not influence our treatment of the Judges in 2nd Edition. That book never went further than pitch stage, and I never saw anything more than all of you did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T18:32:39-08:00","id":1353196,"title":"","content":"Is it possible to find out what some of the non-posted stretch goals would have been?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2096-willywonka","name":"willywonka","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T19:05:23-08:00","id":1353204,"title":"","content":"Unlikely; but I'm curious, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T20:38:40-08:00","id":1353233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>willywonka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1353196#post1353196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible to find out what some of the non-posted stretch goals would have been?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I\u2019m going to guess here that \u201cBa\u201d covering what it does was a tweak because of the somewhat slower than expected KS pace. I\u2019d bet money that new Utterances would have been \u201cRen\u201d, and \u201cBa\u201d would have been new Judges alone.<br /> <br /> we know what \u201cKa\u201d was going to be, so that only leaves \u201cSheut\u201d. Not positive how it fits with Sheut, but the other Immortals seems like the obvious missing topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T21:26:47-08:00","id":1353246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1353233#post1353233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I\u2019m going to guess here that \u201cBa\u201d covering what it does was a tweak because of the somewhat slower than expected KS pace. I\u2019d bet money that new Utterances would have been \u201cRen\u201d, and \u201cBa\u201d would have been new Judges alone.<br /> <br /> we know what \u201cKa\u201d was going to be, so that only leaves \u201cSheut\u201d. Not positive how it fits with Sheut, but the other Immortals seems like the obvious missing topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those do seem to be reasonable assumptions. <br /> <br /> Changing course a bit, I was running through the affinities again and realized that all of the affinities on page 107 of the 1e player's guide seem to be missing from 2e. While I realize several affinities are missing from the conversion, it does seem odd that an entire page of them clumped together are missing. I wonder if this was intentional. It's everything between Living Monolith and Radiant Lifeforce, and I don't see any similar gaps in the section.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2096-willywonka","name":"willywonka","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T01:45:03-08:00","id":1353287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1353233#post1353233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I\u2019m going to guess here that \u201cBa\u201d covering what it does was a tweak because of the somewhat slower than expected KS pace. I\u2019d bet money that new Utterances would have been \u201cRen\u201d, and \u201cBa\u201d would have been new Judges alone.<br /> <br /> we know what \u201cKa\u201d was going to be, so that only leaves \u201cSheut\u201d. Not positive how it fits with Sheut, but the other Immortals seems like the obvious missing topic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;Ba&quot; covered new Utterances. We don't know, nor may ever know, what &quot;Ren&quot; would have included. Might be for the best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T03:15:41-08:00","id":1353299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>willywonka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1353196#post1353196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible to find out what some of the non-posted stretch goals would have been?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, that wouldn't serve any positive purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T03:42:36-08:00","id":1353307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Night Horrors book for Mummy would be amazing!*<br /> <br /> *(As long as Deceived are given proper love)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Deceived are, technically, a Minor Guild, and we did got that stretch goal, so I assume we don't have to wait for a possible Night Horrors book to get them","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T05:10:05-08:00","id":1353317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1353307#post1353307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the Deceived are, technically, a Minor Guild, and we did got that stretch goal, so I assume we don't have to wait for a possible Night Horrors book to get them</div> </div> </div> </div>On that note, the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/maar-kherit-mummy-the-curse-2nd-edition/\" target=\"_blank\">Maar-Kherit</a> were shown in advance of the Kickstarter but that section is absent from the manuscript. So they may have been removed, in order to put the full details in the Book of Lasting Death.<br /> Ideally this would free up word count in the core rules to be used elsewhere, but that seems unlikely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T05:56:38-08:00","id":1353327,"title":"","content":"So, how does Sekhem limit your Pillars? The effective dot rating of your Pillars? How many Pillar points you can have? How many Pillars you have access to at all? Probably not the latter, but it doesn't say. The only text for that bullet point concerns how many Pillar points you can spend per turn (which is one, regardless of Sekhem rating).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T07:33:22-08:00","id":1353348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1353317#post1353317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On that note, the <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://theonyxpath.com/maar-kherit-mummy-the-curse-2nd-edition/&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Maar-Kherit</a> were shown in advance of the Kickstarter but that section is absent from the manuscript. So they may have been removed, in order to put the full details in the Book of Lasting Death.<br /> Ideally this would free up word count in the core rules to be used elsewhere, but that seems unlikely.</div> </div> </div> </div>They\u2019re still in there. They\u2019re in Preview 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T10:46:02-08:00","id":1353384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1353287#post1353287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> &quot;Ba&quot; covered new Utterances. We don't know, nor may ever know, what &quot;Ren&quot; would have included. Might be for the best.</div> </div> </div> </div>if you reread what I wrote, you will notice what I said was that the range of Ba we got reads like something pushed together because of the speed of the Kickstarter to make sure we got to some more Utterances. What I said was that I suspected the original intent was that Ba was going to be Judges and Ren Utterances, but they changed it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T13:07:14-08:00","id":1353409,"title":"","content":"So if non-Knowing/Unveiling Time/Fate Spells don't work on Mummies....do similarly aspected powers amongst other splats <i>also</i> not work? Like, if a demon tries to Stop an Arisen, does that instead just burn out?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T04:20:01-08:00","id":1353525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1353409#post1353409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if non-Knowing/Unveiling Time/Fate Spells don't work on Mummies....do similarly aspected powers amongst other splats <i>also</i> not work? Like, if a demon tries to Stop an Arisen, does that instead just burn out?</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s an interesting question. Most powers that try to change Fate/Time by imposing external rules on the mummy will fail. The scars left by the Rite of Return on both those concepts makes it impossible. However, mummies aren\u2019t immune to creatures that exploit loopholes in the universe\u2019s current rules, or use a more advanced understanding of those existing conditions to produce their effect. Mages are trying to impose their rules, and I\u2019d say things like Changelings do likewise. Neither should have much joy dictating a mummy\u2019s fate or time. OTOH, demons are just using the rules that exist, they just know them better than most creatures. Their time shiftings are more likely to work.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d say when in doubt, make a Clash of Wills and see what happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T07:47:33-08:00","id":1353543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1353525#post1353525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That\u2019s an interesting question. Most powers that try to change Fate/Time by imposing external rules on the mummy will fail. The scars left by the Rite of Return on both those concepts makes it impossible. However, mummies aren\u2019t immune to creatures that exploit loopholes in the universe\u2019s current rules, or use a more advanced understanding of those existing conditions to produce their effect. Mages are trying to impose their rules, and I\u2019d say things like Changelings do likewise. Neither should have much joy dictating a mummy\u2019s fate or time. OTOH, demons are just using the rules that exist, they just know them better than most creatures. Their time shiftings are more likely to work.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d say when in doubt, make a Clash of Wills and see what happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Decent logic, I had some of the shape of that when I finished chapter seven last night.<br /> <br /> Oh by the way, Chapter Seven is the best chapter in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T07:55:17-08:00","id":1353544,"title":"","content":"The only question is what to roll in such a CoW.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T08:13:01-08:00","id":1353546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1353544#post1353544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only question is what to roll in such a CoW.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whatever the individual CoW would call for. Each splat usually spells out what those rolls are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T08:32:16-08:00","id":1353550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1353546#post1353546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whatever the individual CoW would call for. Each splat usually spells out what those rolls are.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>The Arisen</i> in this context. It's a blanket immunity to time and fate effects not tied to any Pillar (or even Attribute) so there's no defined dice pool for the mummy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T12:12:43-08:00","id":1353598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Outside of that mage specific situation, I'd say just go with standard Clash pools. Maybe we'll see it brought up in the Contagion Companion?(forgive my mild speculation)<br /> <br /> In the mage specific situation I wouldn't use CoW personally.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was specifically about time and fate affecting supernatural powers other than those of mages- Regardless, the problem is that there <i>is no standard CoW dice pool</i> which we can default to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T12:58:04-08:00","id":1353609,"title":"","content":"Sekhem + Defining Pillar seems reasonable to me. A mummy\u2019s temporal anchorage is less inflexible as her Descent draws to a close and the Ocean prepares to draw her beneath its waves again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T13:37:08-08:00","id":1353624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems a weird thing to not have a pool for.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because CoW is only ever meant to be used with activated powers that are assumed to either be dot rated or connected to a dot rated trait. Afaik only beasts and ephemeral entities has dice pools to default to, and that's because beasts use Lair + highest Resistance Attribute for <i>all</i> their powers, and ephemeral entities just rolls Rank if they're not using an Influence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1353609#post1353609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sekhem + Defining Pillar seems reasonable to me. A mummy\u2019s temporal anchorage is less inflexible as her Descent draws to a close and the Ocean prepares to draw her beneath its waves again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Defining Pillar or highest Pillar makes sense to me. It just bothers me when CoWs are called for in situations they aren't designed to cover without providing the missing dice pool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 12-08-2019, 04:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T13:50:33-08:00","id":1353627,"title":"","content":"Is there any news on whether the 2ed core will include Seba? And how do Relics interact with other Supernaturals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T15:03:43-08:00","id":1353639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1353624#post1353624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's because CoW is only ever meant to be used with activated powers that are assumed to either be dot rated or connected to a dot rated trait. Afaik only beasts and ephemeral entities has dice pools to default to, and that's because beasts use Lair + highest Resistance Attribute for <i>all</i> their powers, and ephemeral entities just rolls Rank if they're not using an Influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>If memory serves, werewolves also have Primal Urge + Auspice Renown as the pool to use if they're not using a Gift Facet built on another Renown.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Defining Pillar or highest Pillar makes sense to me. </div> </div> </div>Defining Pillar specifically has to be your highest Pillar, so that works out either way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T15:22:22-08:00","id":1353641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1353639#post1353639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If memory serves, werewolves also have Primal Urge + Auspice Renown as the pool to use if they're not using a Gift Facet built on another Renown.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good catch. It's probably due to the number of innate werewolf abilities not tied to Renown. Great foresight from the dev/writer who added that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1353639#post1353639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Defining Pillar specifically has to be your highest Pillar, so that works out either way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. I got confused by the sidebar &quot;The Rite of Return when Arisen&quot; that mentions changing your &quot;main Pillar&quot; which I linked to your Defining Pillar. If you could change your Defining Pillar you could easily end up in situations where your Defining Pillar isn't your highest, but since you can't change your Defining Pillar I have literally no idea what &quot;main Pillar&quot; refers to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T16:26:16-08:00","id":1353652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1353627#post1353627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any news on whether the 2ed core will include Seba? And how do Relics interact with other Supernaturals?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are mentioned but not detailed. Likely waiting for the write up of the Deceived in a later book.<br /> <br /> As for how Vessels (Vestiges and Relics) interact with other supernaturals, no specifics are given. I assume they suffer the curses and reap the benefits as appropriate. Though Mage details are listed in the DEC (Princes of the Conquered Land chapter) and I see no reason to not use those rules there for now.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for Clash of Wills, it is listed on page 50 of Preview 3 and is listed as Sekhem + (highest Pillar required for the Affinity <b>or </b>their Utterence level). Which is less helpful for Clashes that aren't based around their own powers, but Sekhem + Defining Pillar works well defending the basic aspects of the template (things inherent to being Deathless/Arisen).<br /> <br /> I would argue that the Unchained's (demonic) Exploits aren't using the rules of reality but breaking them (or at least abusing them). It is what makes them different from Embeds and why they cause a Compromise roll, but Demon/Mummy relations are a bit outside the scope of this thread and I hope that it'll be covered in the Contagion stretch goal anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T16:38:34-08:00","id":1353655,"title":"","content":"I think it would be worth discussing what Mummy-related crossover issues you think ought to be addressed in the Contain Chronicle companion. In particular, new issues that arise from the second edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T17:59:39-08:00","id":1353666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1353655#post1353655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it would be worth discussing what Mummy-related crossover issues you think ought to be addressed in the Contain Chronicle companion. In particular, new issues that arise from the second edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, but I think that might be better as it's own thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T11:33:45-08:00","id":1354628,"title":"","content":"Random observation on my gradual closer readthrough of the preview manuscript, apologies if this has been raised already:<br /> <br /> The corebook for Mummy, the gameline with an emphasis on ancient history and stories that move between eras in history, has lists of sample ranged weapons and services that are overwhelmingly specific to the modern world. Different stats for different sizes of pistol or SMG might not be as good a use of book space as, say, a bow &amp; arrow, the same with &quot;rush plastic surgery&quot; versus obtaining medical reagants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T12:06:56-08:00","id":1354638,"title":"","content":"In the Right of Investment, it's mentioned that Mortals who are invested &quot;receive the benefits of their masters' decree.&quot; Does this just mean they gain the Affinity associated with the Arisen's decree, or is it something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2947-forgeeternal","name":"ForgeEternal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T12:27:25-08:00","id":1354647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1354628#post1354628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Random observation on my gradual closer readthrough of the preview manuscript, apologies if this has been raised already:<br /> <br /> The corebook for Mummy, the gameline with an emphasis on ancient history and stories that move between eras in history, has lists of sample ranged weapons and services that are overwhelmingly specific to the modern world. Different stats for different sizes of pistol or SMG might not be as good a use of book space as, say, a bow &amp; arrow, the same with &quot;rush plastic surgery&quot; versus obtaining medical reagants.</div> </div> </div> </div>The weapons (and armor) tables already do contain several historical examples or weapons that can stand in for historical examples. They even added javelins to the default list, meaning they have thought about historical weapons. The bow is basically the only thing missing (unless you want to go into culture specific weapons), and I'm glad it is because the bow rules (both sets of them) from Dark Eras were a lot of word count compared to any other weapons as well as just being disappointing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 12-12-2019, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T20:54:32-08:00","id":1355996,"title":"","content":"Still workin' my way through.<br /> <br /> The Endless Potency Merit available to immortals lets you spend &quot;a point of Sekhem&quot; to boost an Attribute for one scene.<br /> <br /> Am I correct in interpreting this to be a &quot;burn a dot, don't get it back until you spend 5 experiences to buy one like normal&quot; case? With a high Merit rating the boost can be quite high, so I can see the reasoning, but it's a fairly steep price even then, let alone if you had a low rating and were only getting +1 for a scene.<br /> <br /> <i>Edit:</i> Hang on. Does having Sekhem actually benefit or do anything for the Endless aside from a) buying and using Endless Potency, b) joining a scorpion cult and becoming invested, or c) prerequisites for two Timeless Merits? Do they get any of the other effects listed under the Sekhem trait in character creation, like kepher? They definitely don't get the major benefits without being invested, they can't raise it above 5 so Attribute maximums don't change, and it doesn't provide Supernatural Tolerance for them.<br /> <br /> Only tangentially related question: the names Deathless, Lifeless, Endless, and Timeless all recur through the book, and not all of them are clearly defined. I've got Deathless and Lifeless more or less down, with some haziness on what does and doesn't count as Lifeless. Am I correct in inferring that the Endless are immortals with the Gift of Ages, and the Timeless are... all immortals? just the Deathless and the Endless? Or just another name for the Deathless?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 12-20-2019, 12:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T03:46:43-08:00","id":1356032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1355996#post1355996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I correct in interpreting this to be a &quot;burn a dot, don't get it back until you spend 5 experiences to buy one like normal&quot; case?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're probably correct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1355996#post1355996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and it doesn't provide Supernatural Tolerance for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does, and stacks with the Supernatural Resistance Merit.<br /> <br /> <br /> Deathless: The Arisen<br /> Lifeless: Any undead who aren't Arisen<br /> Endless: Immortals<br /> Timeless: Never properly defined; at times it seem to refer to Arisen, Arisen and the Judges, Arisen and Immortals, something other than Arisen and Immortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T08:40:23-08:00","id":1356105,"title":"","content":"I've mostly been taking \u201cTimeless\u201d to mean \u201cthose with a non-linear connection to time\u201d. Primarily the Arisen; but it's possible that at least some of the Reborn are in that category, too. <br /> <br /> And while it hasn't been emphasized as heavily in Changeling 2e, I'm pretty sure that the Lost would also (marginally) qualify: when a changeling escapes Arcadia, the time period she returns to might be quite different than the one she left. Typically, this takes the form of \u201cI only spent a few weeks in my Durance, but years have passed in the human world\u201d (or vice versa); that is, there's still a default assumption that the changeling returns some time after her abduction. But I could see a few rare cases where a changeling might return to an entirely different era than the one she was taken from: say, a student of history who is so in love with the Elizabethian era that it's more real to her than the world around her. She gets taken to Arcadia and escapes\u2026 to the Elizabethian era. She would be one of the Timeless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T09:18:54-08:00","id":1356111,"title":"","content":"I wouldn\u2019t call a time-displaced changeling Timeless. Mummies are Timeless because they are not constrained by linear time moving from one Descent to the next. While Arcadia can displace the Lost, once they conclude their Durances they are confined to linear time once again. They cannot move freely from one era to the next as the Arisen do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T12:57:20-08:00","id":1356144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1355996#post1355996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still workin' my way through.<br /> <br /> The Endless Potency Merit available to immortals lets you spend &quot;a point of Sekhem&quot; to boost an Attribute for one scene.<br /> <br /> Am I correct in interpreting this to be a &quot;burn a dot, don't get it back until you spend 5 experiences to buy one like normal&quot; case? With a high Merit rating the boost can be quite high, so I can see the reasoning, but it's a fairly steep price even then, let alone if you had a low rating and were only getting +1 for a scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>Officially, yes, I think this is what they were going with. <br /> <br /> Unofficially I think that those who have Sekhem should also have Sekhem points. Mummies get that in the form of Pillar points while those without pillars simply have a number of points equal to their Sekhem. I think this is more fun and fair. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T13:12:46-08:00","id":1356146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1356144#post1356144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Officially, yes, I think this is what they were going with. <br /> <br /> Unofficially I think that those who have Sekhem should also have Sekhem points. Mummies get that in the form of Pillar points while those without pillars simply have a number of points equal to their Sekhem. I think this is more fun and fair. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You burn a dot for the effects. Sanctity of Experiences refunds them when that happens. You don\u2019t lose the invested Experiences, you just need to redirect them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T13:30:20-08:00","id":1356153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1356146#post1356146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You burn a dot for the effects. Sanctity of Experiences refunds them when that happens. You don\u2019t lose the invested Experiences, you just need to redirect them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't help any Immortals since Sanctity of Experiences, as written, specifically only applies to mummies.<br /> <br /> Edit: Hang on! Sanctity of Experience doesn't help mummies either. It only allows reshuffling traits you have, not refunding any Experiences from lost traits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 12-20-2019, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T14:37:52-08:00","id":1356164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1356153#post1356153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doesn't help any Immortals since Sanctity of Experiences, as written, specifically only applies to mummies.<br /> <br /> Edit: Hang on! Sanctity of Experience doesn't help mummies either. It only allows reshuffling traits you have, not refunding any Experiences from lost traits.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mummies don't pay for Sekhem","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T14:46:50-08:00","id":1356166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1356164#post1356164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mummies don't pay for Sekhem</div> </div> </div> </div>Point being, Sanctity of Experiences doesn't say it automatically refunds experiences lost to Sekhem expenditures, it's there to respec Attributes, Skills, Merits, and Pillars when you emerge in a new age. If it were meant to apply to immortals, and to their spending Sekhem on Endless Potency in the middle of an ongoing age, it should be edited to say that.<br /> <br /> It strikes me as an awkward solution, given it means the &quot;cost&quot; of using Endless Potency is to be forced to shuffle experiences on your sheet to other traits. I probably would have just given Endless Potency a per-chapter or per-story availability instead of a Sekhem cost, or kept the cost but had the text of the Merit add that the dot comes back after one story or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T15:32:47-08:00","id":1356181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1356166#post1356166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It strikes me as an awkward solution, given it means the &quot;cost&quot; of using Endless Potency is to be forced to shuffle experiences on your sheet to other traits.</div> </div> </div> </div>The cost is that your Sekhem goes down and can't go back up until the end of the chapter, which is how Sanctity of Merits works and ostensibly the basis for how spending Sekhem on Endless Potency is supposed to work.<br /> <br /> It's not ideal, but it's also not terribly complicated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T18:31:19-08:00","id":1356210,"title":"","content":"Which is why I think Sekhem for immortals should give points equal to its rating that can be used and recharged like most other point systems. What makes the Timeless so much more potent is that instead of a single Sekhem pool their potent Lifeforce has manifested as five (or six) distinct pools, one for each of their soul Pillars. <br /> <br /> I say their Sekhem points get restored by the dawning of a new day, meditation, and absorption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T14:02:03-08:00","id":1356689,"title":"","content":"Big question; can Shuankhsen steal Utterances like in first Ed, or are they reduced to Bane Rituals they don\u2019t have the ability to use effectively due to their shitty Sekhem mechanics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T20:36:29-08:00","id":1356746,"title":"","content":"Reframing an earlier observation because I remembered some helpful context: As currently written, the allocation rules for Pillar dots make it possible for the Disembodied Condition to produce a character with a Finesse or Resistance of 0, due to the lack of 1e's specification that only one Pillar may have zero dots in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T01:36:28-08:00","id":1356774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1356746#post1356746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reframing an earlier observation because I remembered some helpful context: As currently written, the allocation rules for Pillar dots make it possible for the Disembodied Condition to produce a character with a Finesse or Resistance of 0, due to the lack of 1e's specification that only one Pillar may have zero dots in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like it would cause nothing but trouble, though amusing trouble for one of the Deathless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T02:06:48-08:00","id":1356778,"title":"","content":"1e did have rules for not having any Attribute dots for the nine usual Attributes, but nothing like that has returned in 2e, much less for the three simplified Attributes.<br /> I'd just add &quot;to a minimum of one&quot; to the calculations of the simplified Attributes.<br /> <br /> Edit: Considering that it's not the usual dream form that is combined with Skills, I'd even add a base dot to all Attributes. It'd put their Attribute maximum to 12, the same as a Rank 4 ephemeral entity. That's pretty fitting considering they can reach an effective Rank of 5.<br /> (Speaking of which, there's a reference to the CofD book for ephemeral entities in the text for Judge avatars despite their rules being included in MtC.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 12-24-2019, 05:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T07:13:58-08:00","id":1356804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1356746#post1356746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reframing an earlier observation because I remembered some helpful context: As currently written, the allocation rules for Pillar dots make it possible for the Disembodied Condition to produce a character with a Finesse or Resistance of 0, due to the lack of 1e's specification that only one Pillar may have zero dots in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my fault. When I wrote the Condition, I hadn\u2019t realized that the limit of only one Pillar at 0 was no longer in place. Changing it to a minimum of 1 for each Attribute is a simple solution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-25T09:02:27-08:00","id":1356928,"title":"","content":"So upon even further thinking I can't help but think to myself it is the other true immortals, especially the Reborn, that I want to make a campaign about. The idea of them being basically normal humans but with special time traveling abilities really interests me. <br /> <br /> That said, i would add certain things. Like them having Sekhem points that they can use to activate their supernatural powers, in addition to still being able to use Willpower. Additionally, Sekhem (as a power stat) gets added to supernatural power dice pools, increasing their potency. <br /> <br /> I would also add the ability to learn or participate in a ceremonial ritual that would allow the Reborn to basically move themselves between the other lives, be they past or future or even a life in a sideways timeline. As part of this I would make this, modern, life something special - maybe having it so they were part of something - either by choice, force, or accident - that supercharged their soul. <br /> <br /> As an additional note, I could totally see taking some of the themes and campaign advice from Mummy and using it in a much less dark and horror nature in a variant Trinity Continuum game. <br /> <br /> All that said, basically, upon further analysis of Mummy the Curse 2e, I am glad I backed it. While some of the elements I disliked intensely from 1e are still there the changes, additions, and options that are presented make those elements a much lesser force, which I totally approve of. So yeah, Mummy the Curse 2e is pretty awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T01:34:53-08:00","id":1357482,"title":"","content":"So the Sekhem consumption is more &quot;player friendly&quot; now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-26T19:12:21-07:00","id":1376762,"title":"","content":"So...what's up with the sidebar that seems to exist solely to no-sell the abilities of one specific subcategory of playable characters from an entirely different gameline?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-26T20:15:54-07:00","id":1376774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1376762#post1376762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So...what's up with the sidebar that seems to exist solely to no-sell the abilities of one specific subcategory of playable characters from an entirely different gameline?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Mages doing Time Magic to Mummies is obvious. So it needs rules, and better the ones that limit Mages and creates a nice Mystery besides (because the reaction of an Acanthus is going to be &quot;holy fuck, Abyssal being&quot; or &quot;... COOL! And frustrating. But COOL!&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-26T20:48:17-07:00","id":1376777,"title":"","content":"I suppose I'd been hoping for something more interesting than a no-sell - like the magic having entirely unpredictable consequences, or affecting the Mummy at some other achronological time, or other more interesting outcomes.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of room for interesting mysteries where this interaction is, and that room being cut out and replaced with &quot;Nope, sorry, here's some Paradox&quot; is disappointing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 03-27-2020, 12:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T08:54:05-07:00","id":1376809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1376777#post1376777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose I'd been hoping for something more interesting than a no-sell - like the magic having entirely unpredictable consequences, or affecting the Mummy at some other achronological time, or other more interesting outcomes.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of room for interesting mysteries where this interaction is, and that room being cut out and replaced with &quot;Nope, sorry, here's some Paradox&quot; is disappointing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Metaphysically speaking I can't see why a mage's spells would behave like that. If it can affect a mummy, then when it affects the mummy in the timeline would at most be a matter of adding a Reach because it's more complex on a mummy. Furthermore, the only thing that is supposed to warp the effects of the spell (from an OOC perspective) is Paradox/the Abyss. Otherwise a spell should not have any unintended effects.<br /> A no-sell, on the other hand, is more thematic and even in line with the established rules of Mage. A mage can't mess with a mummy's timeline because the magic that already affects a mummy's timeline and destiny is simply too powerful and the mage can't win the CoW against the Rite of Return/Judges much like they can't against archmasters, or the God-Machine when casting certain spells on angels. The Paradox is a bit weird, though, even if we take the Judges of Duat's counter-interference at face value.<br /> I would've liked to see the souls of the arisen mentioned in the same sidebar, but at least it's brought up in Nameless and Accursed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T10:49:03-07:00","id":1376822,"title":"","content":"So, the writer shed some extra light on the intent of this in Discord, which made this click for me in a way that zeroing in on a blanket ban on specific practices did not. Paraphrasing - attempts to affect the Time, Fate, or Memory of a mummy will always fail; this totally makes sense to me and is super thematic. In light of that, the only real issue I have with the sidebar is the way it addresses the practices, since it creates edge cases that don't follow the intent.<br /> <br /> For example:<br /> 1) As written, an Acanthus can go back in time with Shifting Sands by a scene or so and 'kill' a Mummy. They would remain 'dead' in the present. This should not be possible, because that's messing with the personal Time of the Deathless.<br /> 2) As written, an Acanthus cannot use Warding Gesture to shield a Mummy ally from her own hostile AOE spells, because Shielding is a forbidden practice. This should be possible, because it's not messing with the personal Fate of the Deathless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":".  Clarity of language 03-27-2020, 07:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T13:00:39-07:00","id":1376844,"title":"","content":"Do we have any update on when we will get the updated manuscript with the additional Utterances and removed target number changing rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10272,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","user":"Daigotsu Max","date":". 03-27-2020, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T15:05:45-07:00","id":1376862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1376844#post1376844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we have any update on when we will get the updated manuscript with the additional Utterances and removed target number changing rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>Usually when the backer pdf is ready. OPP don\u2019t generally send out updated manuscripts after the Kickstarter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T21:27:37-07:00","id":1376899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1376777#post1376777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose I'd been hoping for something more interesting than a no-sell - like the magic having entirely unpredictable consequences[\u2026]<br /> <br /> There's a lot of room for interesting mysteries where this interaction is, and that room being cut out and replaced with &quot;Nope, sorry, here's some Paradox&quot; is disappointing.</div> </div> </div> </div>To reframe the things Tessie's already brought up, &quot;here's some Paradox&quot; <i>is</i> the magic having unpredictable consequences.<br /> <br /> Attempting to interfere with a mummy's Name at more than a cursory level doesn't work, and attempting to interact with it magically at all draws the influence of alien demon-gods made of pain and suffering just the same as if you'd exposed your Astral self to the raw currents of the world-soul and experienced a dreaming death \u2014 &quot;something powerful's got its tendrils in your magic, and that's represented with the same system as a normal Paradox&quot; goes clear back to 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T09:32:02-07:00","id":1376975,"title":"","content":"Well, the Book of Lasting Death is going to include an expansion on Minor Guilds, and the Deceived are included among them. As such, while a full glory 2e update for them is yet to be announced, nor does a Night Horrors book which could perhaps explore them in greater depth, I would imagine that most of their unique features will be detailed and updated in the supplement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T15:14:24-07:00","id":1377230,"title":"","content":"Just to be clear, since it does not say it's been cleared, we do have the chapter for new judges, affinities, and utterances right? We made the 63,000 thousand mark, but its unconfirmed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T16:43:15-07:00","id":1377238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1377230#post1377230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to be clear, since it does not say it's been cleared, we do have the chapter for new judges, affinities, and utterances right? We made the 63,000 thousand mark, but its unconfirmed</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I wrote some of the new Utterances myself for the Book of Lasting Death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T17:28:39-07:00","id":1377244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1377238#post1377238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. I wrote some of the new Utterances myself for the Book of Lasting Death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh ok, thanks! And I hope you had a fun time writing new Utterances!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T16:35:05-07:00","id":1378083,"title":"","content":"So I'm just wondering, what's the narrative reasons for the bonuses on Wayward cult? I understand the drawbacks, just not the bonuses","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key